[{"sha":"5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU3MTNkNWNmNTE4NzY3NGUwMTY5NDg1NjhmMTdhMTlkOWJhMDQ2YTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-30T15:34:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T15:34:03Z"},"message":"core-api: add Datadog APM (ddtrace + serverless-init) (#508)\n\n## What\nDatadog APM instrumentation for **core-api** (CAURA-0000 observability\nPOC).\n\n- Add `ddtrace>=4.10.6` to `core-api/pyproject.toml` (+ refreshed frozen\n`uv.lock`).\n- Instrument the image the single-container Cloud Run way:\n`datadog/serverless-init` becomes the entrypoint and runs the app under\n`ddtrace-run`, shipping spans to the in-process agent on localhost.\n\n## Why this shape\n- **No sidecar:** `datadog-ci cloud-run instrument` is incompatible with\nour VPC-connector services (it round-trips `vpc_access.connector` into a\nform the Cloud Run API rejects) **and** a live sidecar mutation would be\nwiped by the deploy pipeline. The in-image entrypoint survives\nredeploys.\n- Tracing stays **dormant** unless the deploy supplies\n`DD_API_KEY`/`DD_SITE`/`DD_SERVICE`/`DD_ENV`.\n\n## Verified\nImage builds; `ddtrace 4.10.6` imports; `ddtrace-run` +\n`/app/datadog-init` present.\n\n## Paired PR\nDeploy wiring (env + Secret Manager key + `service` label) lives in\n**caura-memclaw-enterprise** — link added below. Merge both for APM to\nactivate on `staging-memclaw-core-api`.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"46f0457757ec44ac41c3ff46f9f39766c46d01c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/46f0457757ec44ac41c3ff46f9f39766c46d01c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQ+HrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALa8QAH59sD/rZscXtMmHtuUPQknI\nXW874RuA7yZCu5dK97bwmW95EAzNmekec/KsfxAy12I1BduGbNOziuD9X87RGUsz\nCrXttBKQ2hUVXK4Igv/en/NUdgGvjiypQCi1IqTLDhmQMZMRJupqLKJWk4SC9ryR\nLo5qpXZZ042wGfiqWUxNT6l/DGwfw3DNx7Ac3hC6ENYeTzJX3l378V9n1I8wZENw\nuJNbmamD065gpyJyG/GkmDBefnYaVMZWjKOKGPtlbiieEVeO1GsaGjd96SfmtCy6\n06xeIaZdx79Nia9Gl9+FL1kYTmfreUOog2XwyLhX3wdQqjhiXNRDTvVOy4QETpZg\nBWDIdH1GLgaC5txwx5WD23xajQMYFg+SI9uQhZUaZtvFg/xg/Qx27lkwqfNbSs+1\nf7C2thl/QeZ8j1yIQkCxU1FMTGy7GKf3kjHugUom+rMr3xME5xKF81pgJlFnRmKj\n218f1/MIg9KuJcPe7LjOiWeCDK2UTSX7SdC0efVznyK2qATC8lr2QSwMxx5ck+Hp\nLDD+tefWOjnQdlqAnOG/DfL4mtiaCCMosxlnPlYIpyhBHg9JdzScS6DqDGRfFZnW\nUifWYP41rSb0m2QiaPvNwb/PsxlKHvY7ZQxyJW4NPSTi7EWY8D7gBwdoJBvnhWv8\nUuT9i6yUv8j9Dgm5/BSk\n=Aspp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 46f0457757ec44ac41c3ff46f9f39766c46d01c7\nparent 1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782833643 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782833643 +0300\n\ncore-api: add Datadog APM (ddtrace + serverless-init) (#508)\n\n## What\nDatadog APM instrumentation for **core-api** (CAURA-0000 observability\nPOC).\n\n- Add `ddtrace>=4.10.6` to `core-api/pyproject.toml` (+ refreshed frozen\n`uv.lock`).\n- Instrument the image the single-container Cloud Run way:\n`datadog/serverless-init` becomes the entrypoint and runs the app under\n`ddtrace-run`, shipping spans to the in-process agent on localhost.\n\n## Why this shape\n- **No sidecar:** `datadog-ci cloud-run instrument` is incompatible with\nour VPC-connector services (it round-trips `vpc_access.connector` into a\nform the Cloud Run API rejects) **and** a live sidecar mutation would be\nwiped by the deploy pipeline. The in-image entrypoint survives\nredeploys.\n- Tracing stays **dormant** unless the deploy supplies\n`DD_API_KEY`/`DD_SITE`/`DD_SERVICE`/`DD_ENV`.\n\n## Verified\nImage builds; `ddtrace 4.10.6` imports; `ddtrace-run` +\n`/app/datadog-init` present.\n\n## Paired PR\nDeploy wiring (env + Secret Manager key + `service` label) lives in\n**caura-memclaw-enterprise** — link added below. Merge both for APM to\nactivate on `staging-memclaw-core-api`.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-30T15:34:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d"}]},{"sha":"1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFiYzAwYzE0ZTJkZTY1M2YwMDZhYjUyMjZlMWMyMjYyNmI1ZjgyOWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-30T14:09:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T14:09:20Z"},"message":"feat(core-api,plugin): self-identify MCP writes when the verified id is reserved \"main\" (#507)\n\nFollow-up to #505 (reserved-`main` write guard). #505 reserved `main`,\nbut for the firehose creds the **escape hatch / plugin default couldn't\ntake effect** — this PR fixes that, de-collapsing them **without\nre-provisioning credentials**.\n\n## The gap this closes\n\nThe MCP write path resolved identity as `agent_id = _get_agent_id() or\nagent_id` — the gateway-injected `X-Agent-ID` (= credential\n`home_agent_id`) **always won over the body**. For the ~28 firehose\ncreds (`home_agent_id=\"main\"`), the body was ignored, so\n`MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID`, an explicit `agent_id` arg, and any plugin default\nwere all no-ops. Only re-provisioning the credential could de-collapse\nthem.\n\n## Change\n\n**Server** — new `agent_ids.effective_write_agent_id(verified, body)`:\nthe verified id wins **unless** it's a reserved placeholder\n(`main`/`mcp-agent`), in which case a non-placeholder **body** id is\nhonored (the install self-identifies). A *real* verified id is never\noverridden, so a properly-provisioned cred can't be spoofed via the\nbody. Applied to **`memclaw_write` only** (line 746); the ~8 read/manage\nresolution sites keep `_get_agent_id() or agent_id`, so **visibility\nscoping is unchanged**.\n\n**Plugin** — `memclaw_write` defaults `agent_id` to\n`main-${getInstallId()}` when `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` is unset.\n**Write-scoped at the dispatch, NOT in shared `enrichBody`**, so read\nscoping is unaffected. Plus `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` declared in\n`configSchema` (install prompt) + documented in `AGENT-INSTALL.md`.\n\n**Net:** `home_agent_id=\"main\"` creds (existing **and** future)\nde-collapse with no ops re-provisioning, and #505's reject/escape-hatch\nbecomes actionable for them.\n\n## Security note (please review this trade-off)\n\nThis loosens MCP write-identity resolution, so it deserves a deliberate\nlook — but it is bounded:\n- It applies **only when the verified id is a reserved placeholder** (a\ncred with no real assigned identity). A properly-provisioned cred\n(`home_agent_id != main`) still has the header win — **no new spoofing\nof real identities**.\n- It is **intra-tenant only** (`agent_id` is within-tenant scoping;\ntenant isolation is enforced separately).\n- It is **strictly tighter than the REST write path**, which already\ntrusts `body.agent_id` unconditionally today (`_write_memory_inner`,\nbind flag off by default). So this introduces no risk class that doesn't\nalready exist on REST.\n- It's **transitional** — once a cred is re-identified (`home_agent_id\n!= main`), the fallback never fires for it.\n\n## Tests\n- `tests/test_effective_write_agent_id.py` — 11 cases\n(real-id-wins/anti-spoof, `main`+body→body, both-placeholder→`main` so\nno `mcp-agent` collapse, tenant-key passthrough).\n- #505 guard tests (19) still green; `tsc` clean; plugin contract tests\n(34) green; ruff lint+format clean.\n\n## Roadmap impact\nMakes credential **re-identification (PR-3 / ops) optional cleanup**\nrather than the firehose fix; the enterprise provisioning guard becomes\ndefense-in-depth.\n\nRefs: `pr-plan-reserved-main-identity.md`,\n`roadmap-main-identity-fix.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a47600ba9367ad8cec8677f91da2020ae2b72ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a47600ba9367ad8cec8677f91da2020ae2b72ebb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQ84QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApFUQABOeuIulHGIk6LyrYjmb/bnQ\n2uEqR8nOX/BRBxOyqW1vi/AAQjlV2GE5mlkjKNTq8Hexwaw0yGP9yScMtqmYsqgZ\nnrwsYd5PN4A2gbH3ULYZ4ZKfLQvwvhP9icm4SkgPymWDOuWjBo2REF6diWYJJhDK\no3ooN92MmOJgTABbvLCL/BDdIUvqS9n7G5dziFXAnIrcWJt7j2zoGACxC5Q1ch8y\nDbpmdphdSYecUetYDXXK8IlXP6KtacPNX/ogh5c55JUzrT9tP7ijTv2TaIjpXxi+\n9h5GhMIexVlMfzD2j2OyiY4ttt5LrLZQAnMhYk+nNKeQHBw8UdAUNOJXJiVAIHxf\nP54iy0ObkJxNYPM5ZzHcffuqftPfK7cH+zKHMEX6bTRGEG4YTCcA9rcF+l2XaxUf\n6dHIIVHgIushRtdkBMH3f6gjjB3EQfszerXK3APu0HzXSJn4NdsN4kP7KuU7wyXX\nHmYwu3JsDCcMskVaM60QVaFk+6yfc8SHahO5M/mRPqiu/yItb+vIzicP6OoJwycD\nbSaMMIy7rML3egpPM77fRY6mXdc4lpmuRqz+Cs9wa3qbvWbzE24IkXnazHpjj7JD\nuGHhzneU8POptO5fAzaRIfzq5OTigGBBTpp8zad8sTj3pkIZ/2qJs840iW7sbrsz\n0jB/QdIj7yn+ewLju8KN\n=qXwc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a47600ba9367ad8cec8677f91da2020ae2b72ebb\nparent 9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782828560 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782828560 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api,plugin): self-identify MCP writes when the verified id is reserved \"main\" (#507)\n\nFollow-up to #505 (reserved-`main` write guard). #505 reserved `main`,\nbut for the firehose creds the **escape hatch / plugin default couldn't\ntake effect** — this PR fixes that, de-collapsing them **without\nre-provisioning credentials**.\n\n## The gap this closes\n\nThe MCP write path resolved identity as `agent_id = _get_agent_id() or\nagent_id` — the gateway-injected `X-Agent-ID` (= credential\n`home_agent_id`) **always won over the body**. For the ~28 firehose\ncreds (`home_agent_id=\"main\"`), the body was ignored, so\n`MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID`, an explicit `agent_id` arg, and any plugin default\nwere all no-ops. Only re-provisioning the credential could de-collapse\nthem.\n\n## Change\n\n**Server** — new `agent_ids.effective_write_agent_id(verified, body)`:\nthe verified id wins **unless** it's a reserved placeholder\n(`main`/`mcp-agent`), in which case a non-placeholder **body** id is\nhonored (the install self-identifies). A *real* verified id is never\noverridden, so a properly-provisioned cred can't be spoofed via the\nbody. Applied to **`memclaw_write` only** (line 746); the ~8 read/manage\nresolution sites keep `_get_agent_id() or agent_id`, so **visibility\nscoping is unchanged**.\n\n**Plugin** — `memclaw_write` defaults `agent_id` to\n`main-${getInstallId()}` when `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` is unset.\n**Write-scoped at the dispatch, NOT in shared `enrichBody`**, so read\nscoping is unaffected. Plus `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` declared in\n`configSchema` (install prompt) + documented in `AGENT-INSTALL.md`.\n\n**Net:** `home_agent_id=\"main\"` creds (existing **and** future)\nde-collapse with no ops re-provisioning, and #505's reject/escape-hatch\nbecomes actionable for them.\n\n## Security note (please review this trade-off)\n\nThis loosens MCP write-identity resolution, so it deserves a deliberate\nlook — but it is bounded:\n- It applies **only when the verified id is a reserved placeholder** (a\ncred with no real assigned identity). A properly-provisioned cred\n(`home_agent_id != main`) still has the header win — **no new spoofing\nof real identities**.\n- It is **intra-tenant only** (`agent_id` is within-tenant scoping;\ntenant isolation is enforced separately).\n- It is **strictly tighter than the REST write path**, which already\ntrusts `body.agent_id` unconditionally today (`_write_memory_inner`,\nbind flag off by default). So this introduces no risk class that doesn't\nalready exist on REST.\n- It's **transitional** — once a cred is re-identified (`home_agent_id\n!= main`), the fallback never fires for it.\n\n## Tests\n- `tests/test_effective_write_agent_id.py` — 11 cases\n(real-id-wins/anti-spoof, `main`+body→body, both-placeholder→`main` so\nno `mcp-agent` collapse, tenant-key passthrough).\n- #505 guard tests (19) still green; `tsc` clean; plugin contract tests\n(34) green; ruff lint+format clean.\n\n## Roadmap impact\nMakes credential **re-identification (PR-3 / ops) optional cleanup**\nrather than the firehose fix; the enterprise provisioning guard becomes\ndefense-in-depth.\n\nRefs: `pr-plan-reserved-main-identity.md`,\n`roadmap-main-identity-fix.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-30T14:09:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77"}]},{"sha":"9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDliMThiZDkxYTZhODE2YjZmYWI5MDdjNjQ0YTJlODZlYjNhOWZhNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-30T07:56:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T07:56:19Z"},"message":"feat(observability): sample below-floor near-misses on the /search recall log (#506)\n\n## What\nFollow-up to #503. The `/search` recall log is **returned-only** (to\nbound volume on the high-traffic auto path), which drops below-floor /\noutside-top-k **near-misses** — the exact signal needed to distinguish\n*just-missed* (the good memory was rank 7 at cosine 0.27) from *never\nclose* when validating claims like eToro's \"95% never recalled\".\n\nAdds a per-tenant knob\n**`observability.search_recall_near_miss_sample_rate`** (0.0–1.0,\ndefault **0.0**):\n- `0.0` (default) → unchanged: returned-only.\n- `>0` → keep near-misses on that random fraction of `/search` events,\ncapped at the same `_NEAR_MISS_LIMIT` (5) as `mcp_recall`.\n\nSo e.g. `0.01` keeps the just-missed distribution estimable on ~1% of\nsearch events without the full candidate-row volume. `mcp_recall` is\nunchanged (always full incl. near-misses).\n\n## Why\nOn the dominant path you could see *what was returned* but not *what\njust missed*. This restores that lens cheaply, behind a sampling rate,\nso it's safe to leave on for a busy tenant during a diagnostic window.\n\n## Per-memory certainty (note)\nSampled near-misses characterise the **marginal band** (cap = 5). For\nthe per-memory *\"is THIS memory ever close to any query?\"* question,\noffline replay against the logged queries remains the rigorous tool — no\nbulk near-miss firehose required.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/pipeline/test_log_recall_event.py`: added\n`test_search_keeps_near_misses_when_sampled` (rate=1.0 → near-misses\nkept); existing returned-only test now exercises the default rate=0.0.\nruff + format + mypy clean; 30 passing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebacec11d1f6391bca4f496330cee4f36f4b5a90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ebacec11d1f6391bca4f496330cee4f36f4b5a90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQ3ajCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHiIQAJLm8on8Vb6/a0GudBbCXWMB\nkxrfSl6vIWgxVI3DLBIBUWYMBH0xwOvfwK/4bVKiBCTqbjRzU/xMbVcEH6KqBr+Y\nKLtZj2fFZMkcGnnHIRrmGy/yJ6sJYe3TBvJ3uhV0n9i5boVm1bt4nTJekAA83mnP\nCguAMMs3AM2L0LrrI5FVPP41rcqekucuap0Bkjgo1rYTWfpfRsyeP5zJFpf80HbY\nFGc8xvl371wg9gc39RMciMVhR9MI3Drjiixygn/MQFLnwRl0rP3aokLSwogsC05G\n/mNt4gHhwoGDqztiYMge6GOcEfceUl730iZ0XqwqhbPrau16iNFu3KrOh+hpoPpp\nLBZ48IRHPeA50cjZsbU2pcEJ7Wu0sWnwhGak3aiOWFgJYbYMbMXRQcAHBs9Jk3sf\n2GC2um9prSdxakPs9gXlyZj/qwk6ZAmBhhh36x9LmJQg76pKDlmdysfHrfjFPUac\ntKGVW2ciFXX0bkTU3bzS36RlDR2t7ATWQv+4S6+KOO9OihCncFouafnD4ZT+CnVx\n4Q5nfPdIWeI1lcRPeCvn9+T8stffgMz7LtE9OJ1hu27qtdOPi+qlSP3v93LGq/b1\nZHotM5a7oMz85FrYrpLMVTEmj3sQZy4idTQ/IIrhk516+nybzjif2fNfy1bLlWC6\n4GKub7FCd2WGQFdxpLYs\n=QCz5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ebacec11d1f6391bca4f496330cee4f36f4b5a90\nparent 1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1782806179 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782806179 +0300\n\nfeat(observability): sample below-floor near-misses on the /search recall log (#506)\n\n## What\nFollow-up to #503. The `/search` recall log is **returned-only** (to\nbound volume on the high-traffic auto path), which drops below-floor /\noutside-top-k **near-misses** — the exact signal needed to distinguish\n*just-missed* (the good memory was rank 7 at cosine 0.27) from *never\nclose* when validating claims like eToro's \"95% never recalled\".\n\nAdds a per-tenant knob\n**`observability.search_recall_near_miss_sample_rate`** (0.0–1.0,\ndefault **0.0**):\n- `0.0` (default) → unchanged: returned-only.\n- `>0` → keep near-misses on that random fraction of `/search` events,\ncapped at the same `_NEAR_MISS_LIMIT` (5) as `mcp_recall`.\n\nSo e.g. `0.01` keeps the just-missed distribution estimable on ~1% of\nsearch events without the full candidate-row volume. `mcp_recall` is\nunchanged (always full incl. near-misses).\n\n## Why\nOn the dominant path you could see *what was returned* but not *what\njust missed*. This restores that lens cheaply, behind a sampling rate,\nso it's safe to leave on for a busy tenant during a diagnostic window.\n\n## Per-memory certainty (note)\nSampled near-misses characterise the **marginal band** (cap = 5). For\nthe per-memory *\"is THIS memory ever close to any query?\"* question,\noffline replay against the logged queries remains the rigorous tool — no\nbulk near-miss firehose required.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/pipeline/test_log_recall_event.py`: added\n`test_search_keeps_near_misses_when_sampled` (rate=1.0 → near-misses\nkept); existing returned-only test now exercises the default rate=0.0.\nruff + format + mypy clean; 30 passing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-30T07:56:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b"}]},{"sha":"1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFkMzEzZjk0ZDNkZjk1M2Q4M2YzN2YzN2UwNjhjZGQyZTNjNjUxNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-29T22:43:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T22:43:24Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): reserve agent_id \"main\" on the write path (Phase 1) (#505)\n\n## Why\n\nBare `agent_id=\"main\"` is the OpenClaw plugin's **unset default** —\nwithout a per-install `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID`, every install collapses onto\none shared identity (the eToro \"firehose\": ~52K memories, ≥15 installs\nunder one id). This PR reserves `main` on the write path so new writes\nstop refilling that bucket. It's the **delete-gate** for the bare-`main`\ncleanup and the first slice of the identity fix.\n\n## What (Phase 1 — behind a flag, default `warn`)\n\n- **`enforce_reserved_write_id`** (new `services/agent_identity.py`)\nenforced at the **`create_memory` / `create_memories_bulk` service\nboundary** — the single funnel for **REST, MCP and STM**.\n`data.agent_id` is the resolved *effective* id there, so:\n- a write supplying a **unique** `agent_id` (incl. the plugin's\n`main-<install_id>`) **passes** — the escape hatch;\n- only bare `main` is refused, with an **actionable 409** telling the\nagent how to set its identity (`MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` / per-call arg /\n`main-<install_id>` from `install.json`). The MCP write tool's existing\n`except HTTPException` surfaces the detail into its error envelope.\n- Reserved-id set **unified** in `core_api.agent_ids` (shared with the\nexisting `mcp-agent` gateway guard). `mcp-agent` stays\n**standalone-safe** (guarded conditionally there, not unconditionally\nhere).\n- `warn` mode logs `reserved_agent_write` (core-api has no metrics\nbackend → the log is the counter) so we confirm bare-`main` writes → ~0\nbefore flipping to `reject`.\n\n## Phase 2 (ships dark, `bind_write_identity_to_auth=false`)\n\nBinds a write's `agent_id` to the verified credential identity, ignoring\na body override (spoof hardening). Wired into both REST inner handlers\nbut **off**; enable only **after** the reserved-`main` credentials are\nre-identified (else it pins them back onto `main`).\n\n## Rollout\n\n`warn` → measure → flip `reserved_agent_id_policy=reject` (config, no\ndeploy) → run the bare-`main` delete → re-identify creds → flip\n`bind_write_identity_to_auth=true`. Instant rollback via the flags.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_agent_identity_guard.py` — 19 cases (policy ladder, escape\nhatch, `mcp-agent` standalone-safety, 409 guidance content, warn log).\nAll green locally.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\n1. **`mcp-agent` intentionally *not* unconditionally reserved** —\nstandalone uses it; only `main` is unconditional. (Softens the \"absorb\nboth\" suggestion to avoid a standalone regression.)\n2. Enforcement is at the **service boundary**, not the REST handlers, so\nthe MCP path (`memclaw_write → create_memory`) is covered — the gap the\ndesign review caught.\n\nRefs: design `pr-plan-reserved-main-identity.md`, sequencing\n`roadmap-main-identity-fix.md`. Companion: PR-2 (plugin default-id),\nenterprise provisioning guard, re-identify script.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a74f048be5f7b8e6bbf5e5b02b460310f9743c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9a74f048be5f7b8e6bbf5e5b02b460310f9743c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQvUMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZNkQAIb5x0Qv+C+u1d4iU8Xl2VAT\nFX7NrHmo7Eg9ItS8BiQgbft3Gh07W9xqY6C3JIBQoLCX2UVuDfn1JifEtjHvR1WV\n7nlcpx4a2WwXmmA5J1qfNpL0ufEVJ4+3aEjn9Jc4qjqAYmR6vDZk2KtkY+udAK4M\nGcvHv2QzkxonD5cX0zoyEvTz1y1+goooQ+OPWsSuAt6QIoLKlu/sSuSGUTw2opHz\nNGjBhthVw1JWlsMIUy+AB+Payg7noKCAEw3K6UgXoiA9NMKRTTPwWM0T6T92zww0\nxR8wfczN3cuazta29+BGGqvxChtRkDj4Q5iS9GxLgC5NAgtVISTeCqTyH0Qvv6u8\nCpBtEQgHGio85wdCDhBD49WG+9p/nZCQJKBSFBFs5ZnGmPkRqQTg8q2lhTzf2Bsh\nTj9aGbIjTv/M1BosCi5RQqeV0Hf5EB4u+VJKRSzCDb+ApBfxFF1a3RwuDnn2jfoG\nxrhtXH1KD+QG8pTbs6ztvlaqYWmBNFofQUgtApPLF6lZfjHgVasGQTtcjkBmUcky\nYHJVYE/9TGSQ6BxodbzO7PpzxPXOP6uyaSgr2YO4vPjNwFP5PCAPO1OymYbU0dVu\n7TS4TL+N6GjJzWg/dZNW4AoI1qi2CtenIRAeOmSkAyBO27OjSPS3cSp+3qicCVBV\naeZRstvANFwRVPB3C38e\n=KDZH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9a74f048be5f7b8e6bbf5e5b02b460310f9743c0\nparent cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782773004 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782773004 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): reserve agent_id \"main\" on the write path (Phase 1) (#505)\n\n## Why\n\nBare `agent_id=\"main\"` is the OpenClaw plugin's **unset default** —\nwithout a per-install `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID`, every install collapses onto\none shared identity (the eToro \"firehose\": ~52K memories, ≥15 installs\nunder one id). This PR reserves `main` on the write path so new writes\nstop refilling that bucket. It's the **delete-gate** for the bare-`main`\ncleanup and the first slice of the identity fix.\n\n## What (Phase 1 — behind a flag, default `warn`)\n\n- **`enforce_reserved_write_id`** (new `services/agent_identity.py`)\nenforced at the **`create_memory` / `create_memories_bulk` service\nboundary** — the single funnel for **REST, MCP and STM**.\n`data.agent_id` is the resolved *effective* id there, so:\n- a write supplying a **unique** `agent_id` (incl. the plugin's\n`main-<install_id>`) **passes** — the escape hatch;\n- only bare `main` is refused, with an **actionable 409** telling the\nagent how to set its identity (`MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` / per-call arg /\n`main-<install_id>` from `install.json`). The MCP write tool's existing\n`except HTTPException` surfaces the detail into its error envelope.\n- Reserved-id set **unified** in `core_api.agent_ids` (shared with the\nexisting `mcp-agent` gateway guard). `mcp-agent` stays\n**standalone-safe** (guarded conditionally there, not unconditionally\nhere).\n- `warn` mode logs `reserved_agent_write` (core-api has no metrics\nbackend → the log is the counter) so we confirm bare-`main` writes → ~0\nbefore flipping to `reject`.\n\n## Phase 2 (ships dark, `bind_write_identity_to_auth=false`)\n\nBinds a write's `agent_id` to the verified credential identity, ignoring\na body override (spoof hardening). Wired into both REST inner handlers\nbut **off**; enable only **after** the reserved-`main` credentials are\nre-identified (else it pins them back onto `main`).\n\n## Rollout\n\n`warn` → measure → flip `reserved_agent_id_policy=reject` (config, no\ndeploy) → run the bare-`main` delete → re-identify creds → flip\n`bind_write_identity_to_auth=true`. Instant rollback via the flags.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_agent_identity_guard.py` — 19 cases (policy ladder, escape\nhatch, `mcp-agent` standalone-safety, 409 guidance content, warn log).\nAll green locally.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\n1. **`mcp-agent` intentionally *not* unconditionally reserved** —\nstandalone uses it; only `main` is unconditional. (Softens the \"absorb\nboth\" suggestion to avoid a standalone regression.)\n2. Enforcement is at the **service boundary**, not the REST handlers, so\nthe MCP path (`memclaw_write → create_memory`) is covered — the gap the\ndesign review caught.\n\nRefs: design `pr-plan-reserved-main-identity.md`, sequencing\n`roadmap-main-identity-fix.md`. Companion: PR-2 (plugin default-id),\nenterprise provisioning guard, re-identify script.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T22:43:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2"}]},{"sha":"cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNmOGJmZTkxMTVmZWYxZDA0YzNjMTg2OGNhYWYzZmQ4NmU0NjU3YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-29T21:00:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T21:00:02Z"},"message":"docs(readme): add Skill Factory overview [slice 1] (#504)\n\nAdds a concise **Skill Factory** subsection to the README, in the\nMCP/skills area. Now that the feature is fully merged, the README\ndocumented only the narrow slices (direct `memclaw_doc` sharing, the\nstatic `/install-skill` one-liner) with no unified picture.\n\n## What it adds\nA `### Skill Factory` subsection covering the three pillars:\n- **Authoring** — agents *and* Forge (server-side distillation from\nfleet behavior).\n- **Governance** — the `candidate → staged → active` lifecycle, six\nauto-gates + Sentinel scan, Skills Inbox; agent writes land `staged`,\nnever instantly `active`.\n- **Delivery** — MCP pull vs OpenClaw-plugin push\n(`/api/v1/skills/installable` → disk → load path); active-only once\nenabled.\n\nPlus the opt-in flag (`skills_factory.enabled`, off by default) and\npointers to the existing deep-dive docs (`docs/mcp-skill-delivery.md`,\n`docs/operator-forge-cron.md`) and the full guide on the docs site.\n\nKept lean by design — the complete operator/developer guide lives in the\ndocs site (caura-memclaw-enterprise#677). No stale or invented\nmechanics: grounded in the merged code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a88475a17007397017185c067bc3cc554279b7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a88475a17007397017185c067bc3cc554279b7cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQtzSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgTkQAF1/dLOxvhal2NdHxcE0QLcN\nQQcaEDB5bUrugT1Ri+4zu1KAebj3HZaRhrptx9nYpQKH13vK6Jxl4ENR/DIWxwbP\niNqFO098aX5YcVaqxCcZNjbH7INh4oTEx81VaS9ddztivJXwFMqGzMglhclV4MzM\ngRc7apbPylBFqf0NeSaW/+0CmPmnEZErNP2U0EAKAtnVQc7XJ21qE/QtpoavyXG8\niQ9MjR7zojcJMvSbHwQMkY1lrIP6PD4wx7OUH+/gswzWJABYN/peYXVw/9dFBrsF\nz/hsYB/6U5vvRFaLkYbdHNefxy1q5hk4iDibvgGR/Yk1jlNYF1a+OtEDJgmPqNsW\nQrnZdM6dmYsiIdQVIvybg7kb5qhZacGnbtU9VYK2pFgHK+Wevbnx+XVLiQAMnCSD\n1UkhotuK/o7XGRIj6RbE207N9AvKJ2cxihgmN9HsC7UyOubogljjeIl0daV/d6SC\n7TLCQr2qNRVijiWku1iu9JY+zyakrduWfjhq3kXr6iItubLW79rMZXe9AdBmqHn8\nSkH0iH9mHmh4PQ4ftLYiCpEHHs1aJzIy4dsRFImMxWndgoOJrnsHzlKNmsp5AhZ4\nuDx8WUjnMGtxeCsxmHeaNdiUtJM2ek7rqeonP9docmvVtXBPNZvrGjJLynKcs76A\nnoaOFsIZIjPgjgwg2e4X\n=cTnW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a88475a17007397017185c067bc3cc554279b7cc\nparent f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782766802 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782766802 +0300\n\ndocs(readme): add Skill Factory overview [slice 1] (#504)\n\nAdds a concise **Skill Factory** subsection to the README, in the\nMCP/skills area. Now that the feature is fully merged, the README\ndocumented only the narrow slices (direct `memclaw_doc` sharing, the\nstatic `/install-skill` one-liner) with no unified picture.\n\n## What it adds\nA `### Skill Factory` subsection covering the three pillars:\n- **Authoring** — agents *and* Forge (server-side distillation from\nfleet behavior).\n- **Governance** — the `candidate → staged → active` lifecycle, six\nauto-gates + Sentinel scan, Skills Inbox; agent writes land `staged`,\nnever instantly `active`.\n- **Delivery** — MCP pull vs OpenClaw-plugin push\n(`/api/v1/skills/installable` → disk → load path); active-only once\nenabled.\n\nPlus the opt-in flag (`skills_factory.enabled`, off by default) and\npointers to the existing deep-dive docs (`docs/mcp-skill-delivery.md`,\n`docs/operator-forge-cron.md`) and the full guide on the docs site.\n\nKept lean by design — the complete operator/developer guide lives in the\ndocs site (caura-memclaw-enterprise#677). No stale or invented\nmechanics: grounded in the merged code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:00:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c"}]},{"sha":"f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY0MTFkYjI5ZWUzZjU4MjEzMDMxMjhmYjUyOTM2YjhiNmE4ODlkM2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-29T19:10:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T19:10:04Z"},"message":"feat(observability): log auto /search recalls behind a separate flag (#503)\n\n## What\nAdds a second, independent per-tenant flag\n**`observability.search_recall_logging_enabled`** (default off) that\nturns on recall logging for the high-volume automatic plugin\n**`/search`** path — separately from the existing\n`recall_logging_enabled` (which gates the agent-chosen `memclaw_recall`\ntool).\n\n`LogRecallEvent` now logs two modes through the one shared search\npipeline:\n| source | flag | what's logged |\n|---|---|---|\n| `mcp_recall` | `recall_logging_enabled` | full: returned candidates\n**+** below-floor near-misses |\n| `search` | `search_recall_logging_enabled` | **light**: returned\ncandidates only (id + `vec_sim` + `final_score`), no near-misses |\n\n`event.source` now reflects the real source instead of being hardcoded\nto `mcp_recall`.\n\n## Why\nWe want to study *why good memories aren't recalled* on the path that\nactually dominates real traffic — the auto `/search` (the MCP tool is\nrarely used). The light mode keeps write volume down on a busy path\nwhile still capturing which memories surfaced and their scores.\n\n## Operational note (volume)\n`/search` is high-volume (≈12.7k/day on a large tenant). This is\nintended to be enabled on **a couple of tenants for a short diagnostic\nwindow, then turned off** — no deploy needed to toggle (settings API).\nNear-misses are dropped for this path specifically to limit row growth.\nA retention/prune policy is advisable before any broad/long enablement.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/pipeline/test_log_recall_event.py` extended: search-flag-off\nskip, mcp-flag-off skip, unknown-source skip, mcp full\n(returned+near-misses), search light (returned-only). ruff + format +\nmypy clean; 28 passing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4141e934066e0ff3a930a8d0cea321d5b266e188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4141e934066e0ff3a930a8d0cea321d5b266e188"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQsMMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS4kQAIrpZZqdBDMmt1iBlt0+DAhf\nUzHTiqB4lb676edANsfL5m6Dj7M02ZGXIiG+mAIANpfxDaEhBXmp4zvcg4JwMjXL\n49jQ+kPLfMzEeGU4BuVIUCg5PjGa5JRs1dn5Oaz/Esg7oyK/bptS/hCeiq3TTLIm\nPnaRaUHI7bmpC5BEx+fcnunCnG3DA6NjcedAZLHDT2h7ICVr78RQKr+MdakO5S08\ndYM++w1iC3RBh37euuUPy2nNgLLOa/C1t0y5cqcqEWoiKY/uw8ejAeoW+ajqtkKe\n2K2gCjay7AZcKitcYiSzZReDela9ijaNCTKUlZJjpxoePJBBxbSijICTGpJU8Oae\nq8C2ZX2vAxA9O5FlKcL9J4t1FelzY0Brrcd/I+ODrSF/xTlbBCt8fMd5Zt22SUN4\nogNdcGNdUcpw/Ijmf8eff+hAFeolaRY5wIrXtdNJEFbM5GS0FHmmiODFMgbwJwjN\ntQ2MuVaOjgq6YadbnAwq0whv/DFCQsrF4zoFekfa+K3PMenNZb539cy9X1L6qF6K\ntAwNtl3taaTZ/pLQT6TOE6VNU3TolqUHJQZ+g4IwpOeVgrqBNc+aFhXdmnpj4/wm\nd8rJbvKslNkwxPizx/DG9ceFuUaIswX3ZB0Ftr0yL1/D8xBaJaMwPH+ADn3CgVWk\nI1d1BljvIjqxSM37XhxA\n=fxT0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4141e934066e0ff3a930a8d0cea321d5b266e188\nparent 3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1782760204 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782760204 +0300\n\nfeat(observability): log auto /search recalls behind a separate flag (#503)\n\n## What\nAdds a second, independent per-tenant flag\n**`observability.search_recall_logging_enabled`** (default off) that\nturns on recall logging for the high-volume automatic plugin\n**`/search`** path — separately from the existing\n`recall_logging_enabled` (which gates the agent-chosen `memclaw_recall`\ntool).\n\n`LogRecallEvent` now logs two modes through the one shared search\npipeline:\n| source | flag | what's logged |\n|---|---|---|\n| `mcp_recall` | `recall_logging_enabled` | full: returned candidates\n**+** below-floor near-misses |\n| `search` | `search_recall_logging_enabled` | **light**: returned\ncandidates only (id + `vec_sim` + `final_score`), no near-misses |\n\n`event.source` now reflects the real source instead of being hardcoded\nto `mcp_recall`.\n\n## Why\nWe want to study *why good memories aren't recalled* on the path that\nactually dominates real traffic — the auto `/search` (the MCP tool is\nrarely used). The light mode keeps write volume down on a busy path\nwhile still capturing which memories surfaced and their scores.\n\n## Operational note (volume)\n`/search` is high-volume (≈12.7k/day on a large tenant). This is\nintended to be enabled on **a couple of tenants for a short diagnostic\nwindow, then turned off** — no deploy needed to toggle (settings API).\nNear-misses are dropped for this path specifically to limit row growth.\nA retention/prune policy is advisable before any broad/long enablement.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/pipeline/test_log_recall_event.py` extended: search-flag-off\nskip, mcp-flag-off skip, unknown-source skip, mcp full\n(returned+near-misses), search light (returned-only). ruff + format +\nmypy clean; 28 passing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T19:10:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4"}]},{"sha":"3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNmMGNlOTk4NDExNWNkZjMzN2ZkMTE4NTRlYTExNjNjZDVlYzgyZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-29T08:52:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T08:52:11Z"},"message":"chore(fleet): reconcile plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.12.0 (#502)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **`2.9.0` → `2.12.0`** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`.\n\nThis constant is the fleet **auto-upgrade target / \"outdated\" floor**.\nOn each heartbeat, `routes/fleet.py::_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` queues a\n`deploy` command to this version for an eligible node — one that is `>=\nMIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0), has tenant auto-upgrade\nenabled, isn't in `KNOWN_BROKEN_DEPLOY_VERSIONS`, and has no deploy\nalready pending — when it reports a plugin `<` this floor. It's also the\n`is_plugin_outdated` threshold and is surfaced via `/api/v1/health`.\n\n## Why\nReconcile the floor to the current shipped plugin release\n(`plugin-v2.12.0`) so fleets self-upgrade and converge to 2.12.0.\n\n## Scope / impact\n- **`MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0) unchanged** — nodes below\nit (pre-manifest-aware: `0.98.x` / `2.0–2.5`) are still skipped and need\na one-time **manual reinstall**.\n- **No mechanism change** — the auto-upgrade logic just reads the\nconstant. The existing auto-upgrade suite (which monkeypatches the\nfloor) passes unchanged (59 tests green locally).\n- Eligible nodes (≥2.6.0) converge over their heartbeat cadence once a\ncore-api carrying this floor is deployed.\n\n## Test\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` — guards the invariant that the\nrecommended floor stays **≥** the auto-deploy eligibility floor (a\nmisconfig would queue deploys below the safe-to-self-deploy line), plus\nfloor-value-agnostic `is_plugin_outdated` semantics.\n\n## Deploy prereq\nConfirm `plugin@2.12.0` is published where on-prem nodes self-fetch it\nbefore deploying a core-api with this floor (so the queued `deploy`\ncommands can actually install). `plugin-v2.12.0` is cut, so this should\nalready hold.\n\n`ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on the changed\nsource.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d69e136655663b592ef279f773dec2a4170717f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d69e136655663b592ef279f773dec2a4170717f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQjI7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs5AQAIk+vnqRHY5kQkHU++Fok/Oo\nshZ6t/8ilQvkgaESdf41Io0ZcDuypY88iUAwsuUqDP3aEV4DRXLH9090p08IxgIg\nY0yKn+jPZ2XbVNS1ifLlp2xNu+Kh13KRnh/liDG6Mx4VAK9dNPZk7o8vo5hP3T34\n4bKMxGPzONtZBjDHbeDD3tT9g49Tz2+m0S8gWYjQjvIsKwrllqj4WgF0XznbIYok\nP6p/KpOZnaEAy+XNycYy/kQuZU0100TfWa2gtwqWywBtwn9uHzqPxedg8mbT1FZg\ngqhyY24WRFkef9d6m3KDdl7yqqo9pAqDc6sagmQKzNK1NzoySqZrfE6uESPBKO7R\nY6pzJd6EvKzk9GhU241KfsIvVJCgQ7drWca+ei8fx73t2Pdk3sWv/26z0JwdyapQ\nWTtwpm9IzcUVQo/AxE6cGMO+3stZGTv8ekYw5hGjjUzAMbVZL6TZeJRPh03nF7+5\n2EGhgx7HEjLL4qi2zRWHWhAXHGeHnHO9QMCoxe6K2sVh7C8pnBzdAV0eua4BW5WV\nUfStutco1Hi0nXHTUvkPmYr4c12qsaP3UoAw81/bizL+zP4Rg7a3eL6xx3OgY+hQ\nCRghL4pPqvCgII02+ESOcV9J//tX2nouT6syM/8aIo9dnWi2tx7AMhbrScHfwors\nRNp2+7051OSkiY4Rbbcl\n=YuXO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d69e136655663b592ef279f773dec2a4170717f4\nparent 77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782723131 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782723131 +0300\n\nchore(fleet): reconcile plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.12.0 (#502)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **`2.9.0` → `2.12.0`** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`.\n\nThis constant is the fleet **auto-upgrade target / \"outdated\" floor**.\nOn each heartbeat, `routes/fleet.py::_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` queues a\n`deploy` command to this version for an eligible node — one that is `>=\nMIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0), has tenant auto-upgrade\nenabled, isn't in `KNOWN_BROKEN_DEPLOY_VERSIONS`, and has no deploy\nalready pending — when it reports a plugin `<` this floor. It's also the\n`is_plugin_outdated` threshold and is surfaced via `/api/v1/health`.\n\n## Why\nReconcile the floor to the current shipped plugin release\n(`plugin-v2.12.0`) so fleets self-upgrade and converge to 2.12.0.\n\n## Scope / impact\n- **`MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` (2.6.0) unchanged** — nodes below\nit (pre-manifest-aware: `0.98.x` / `2.0–2.5`) are still skipped and need\na one-time **manual reinstall**.\n- **No mechanism change** — the auto-upgrade logic just reads the\nconstant. The existing auto-upgrade suite (which monkeypatches the\nfloor) passes unchanged (59 tests green locally).\n- Eligible nodes (≥2.6.0) converge over their heartbeat cadence once a\ncore-api carrying this floor is deployed.\n\n## Test\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` — guards the invariant that the\nrecommended floor stays **≥** the auto-deploy eligibility floor (a\nmisconfig would queue deploys below the safe-to-self-deploy line), plus\nfloor-value-agnostic `is_plugin_outdated` semantics.\n\n## Deploy prereq\nConfirm `plugin@2.12.0` is published where on-prem nodes self-fetch it\nbefore deploying a core-api with this floor (so the queued `deploy`\ncommands can actually install). `plugin-v2.12.0` is cut, so this should\nalready hold.\n\n`ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on the changed\nsource.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T08:52:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f0ce9984115cdf337fd11854ea1163cd5ec82f4/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8"}]},{"sha":"77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc3YmZjYmUyNjZmODA0YTgwOGI3NWU4OTVmNTZjMDA4OTVhNzFmZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-29T06:12:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T06:12:48Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): don't 422 the whole heartbeat on an oversized observability blob (#497)\n\n## Why\n\n`HeartbeatIn`'s `recall_metrics` (4 KB) and `reconcile` (8 KB)\nfield-validators **raised** when oversized. A raised `field_validator`\nfails the *entire* request model → FastAPI **422** → the heartbeat is\nrejected wholesale, dropping the node's **registration + command\nchannel** (auto-upgrade, remote ops) over one bloated **optional**\nobservability field.\n\n**eToro 2026-06-28:** a node whose (legacy, unfiltered) skill catalog\npushed the `reconcile` summary past 8 KB 422'd on *every* heartbeat →\nwent stale in the fleet view and uncommandable. Memory tooling was\nunaffected (different path) and the on-disk skill reconcile still ran\n(it happens client-side *before* the POST), so it was non-blocking for\nthe agent — but the fleet control channel was broken for that node.\n\n## Fix\nDegrade gracefully. A shared `_cap_or_drop()` helper replaces an\noversized blob with a small `{\"_truncated\": True, \"_original_bytes\": N}`\nmarker (and logs a warning) instead of raising — so the load-bearing\nheartbeat still lands; only the detailed snapshot for that tick is lost.\nStill bounds `nodes.metadata` growth.\n\nApplied to **both** caps (same bug class). It's unfixed on `main`, so\nthis affects all deployments.\n\n## Tests — `tests/test_fleet_heartbeat_oversized_caps.py`\n- oversized `reconcile` / `recall_metrics` → **dropped, not rejected**\n(no `ValidationError`, replaced with the marker)\n- normal blobs pass through unchanged\n- absent fields stay `None`\n\nVerified locally: 4/4 pass, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy`\nall clean.\n\n## Context / rollout\nNot urgent for eToro right now — the server skill catalog is empty\nthere, so summaries are small and heartbeats are landing fleet-wide; the\nobserved 422 was transient. This lands as **defense-in-depth** so a\nfuture catalog growth (or any large node) can't silently knock nodes off\nthe fleet command channel. Can ride a normal release; no redeploy\nrequired immediately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"092ce541c6a417ca6aa3a72f880e4112381d0c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/092ce541c6a417ca6aa3a72f880e4112381d0c3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQgzgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWYoQAGPklJaVuYNGSY+PpIiFeTBD\nDXd/msX1Zk840fPvsAg3NQZvtIPx9kAqO/Uz5PsYSd05gE6zvAB4PC8iksuCaJTg\n4dTJQslsRKLyMSIalYdmr/1AdtrIBc2Oti8N8XcJd2rqxpL2uqeIkmJwNDUJR5cn\no4f33Zh6ARwdPRJI6F94zj9klQ0ceHzDfNB8j3p3Rc091vx/HM7bB8lHtQaCsKqI\n/f1r2t66+gZCB9epWtqCAHVPuPrGP5n+iFMV5jFtLpPKVXs7FBLyvQGPr3ejUfYo\naAR8LNxq6KbiFNp9692sGyX2wJouSntfgUN0NDDqeWqLXCKRatTjHHI+QjwVkPDX\nxrTEWLMY+++YkS+rZkmel+LOV7WIJP/NcUkK0IVYE6xaZjuoV5e3qMXSrwaDJiYa\n28vcKg1lBmkF/AACE9GFPtZkQ9O6ZNY/bTdSjJ7g5ZnO6S3UCI3Gdqw3maLH6/AJ\ndVXVNvKW/CsuV9NgoKC9gO5aXeiD/OtMfenmbIg5fMdqkUL2Q60lt1RLcziRbboE\nGs7yTJE5VxQSeDRo/bAsQEXtYOCntDmVsN4jNJ/tk9RJsU2vhco3SFdWr/36Nl8k\nyd2yr/ONyr7uQgA/kbWgvLxVZAhNU8QSaKzJGSm2OyNK43Am+4uqNkErq0WPixym\n0RnIkfVq2xzY2zTfeHuZ\n=dTry\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 092ce541c6a417ca6aa3a72f880e4112381d0c3a\nparent 3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782713568 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782713568 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): don't 422 the whole heartbeat on an oversized observability blob (#497)\n\n## Why\n\n`HeartbeatIn`'s `recall_metrics` (4 KB) and `reconcile` (8 KB)\nfield-validators **raised** when oversized. A raised `field_validator`\nfails the *entire* request model → FastAPI **422** → the heartbeat is\nrejected wholesale, dropping the node's **registration + command\nchannel** (auto-upgrade, remote ops) over one bloated **optional**\nobservability field.\n\n**eToro 2026-06-28:** a node whose (legacy, unfiltered) skill catalog\npushed the `reconcile` summary past 8 KB 422'd on *every* heartbeat →\nwent stale in the fleet view and uncommandable. Memory tooling was\nunaffected (different path) and the on-disk skill reconcile still ran\n(it happens client-side *before* the POST), so it was non-blocking for\nthe agent — but the fleet control channel was broken for that node.\n\n## Fix\nDegrade gracefully. A shared `_cap_or_drop()` helper replaces an\noversized blob with a small `{\"_truncated\": True, \"_original_bytes\": N}`\nmarker (and logs a warning) instead of raising — so the load-bearing\nheartbeat still lands; only the detailed snapshot for that tick is lost.\nStill bounds `nodes.metadata` growth.\n\nApplied to **both** caps (same bug class). It's unfixed on `main`, so\nthis affects all deployments.\n\n## Tests — `tests/test_fleet_heartbeat_oversized_caps.py`\n- oversized `reconcile` / `recall_metrics` → **dropped, not rejected**\n(no `ValidationError`, replaced with the marker)\n- normal blobs pass through unchanged\n- absent fields stay `None`\n\nVerified locally: 4/4 pass, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy`\nall clean.\n\n## Context / rollout\nNot urgent for eToro right now — the server skill catalog is empty\nthere, so summaries are small and heartbeats are landing fleet-wide; the\nobserved 422 was transient. This lands as **defense-in-depth** so a\nfuture catalog growth (or any large node) can't silently knock nodes off\nthe fleet command channel. Can ride a normal release; no redeploy\nrequired immediately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T06:12:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3"}]},{"sha":"3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNmODkyMTg5Y2Y2Y2FhOThjYWIxYTgzOGFlNWIzZGZhYTE4MjkzYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-28T13:04:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T13:04:24Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): stop passing removed positional db to log_action on write path (#495)\n\n## Why (production regression — found on eToro v2.11.0 cutover)\n\n`#491` (delete core-api's direct DB pool; route all DB via core-storage)\nmade `audit_service.log_action` **fully keyword-only** by dropping its\n`db` parameter, and updated the `mcp_server` / `agents` / `documents`\ncall sites — **but missed the pipeline write path.**\n\n`write_memory_row.execute()` still passed `ctx.db` **positionally** to\nthe `audit_log` hook (wired directly to `log_action`), so on **every\nmemory create**:\n\n```\nTypeError: log_action() takes 0 positional arguments but 1 positional argument (and 6 keyword-only arguments) were given\n```\n\nThis is caught by the step's `try/except` and logged as `Audit hook\nfailed (non-critical)` — so **writes still persist, but no audit-log\nentry is recorded for memory creates.** Other audited actions (agents,\ndocuments, MCP) are unaffected (their call sites were updated by #491).\n\n**Still present on `main`** → affects all v2.18.0 deployments, including\nSaaS.\n\n## Fix\nDrop the positional `ctx.db` argument (the call is otherwise correct —\nkeyword-only). One line.\n\n## Tests — `tests/test_write_path_audit_signature_regression.py`\n- **unit:** asserts `log_action` stays fully keyword-only (no positional\n`db`) — guards the contract callers rely on. (Runs without a DB.)\n- **integration:** drives the real write pipeline and asserts the audit\nhook does **not** log `Audit hook failed`. The existing\n`test_mcp_write_db_none_regression` can't catch this — it only asserts\nthe row persists, which it does *despite* the swallowed audit failure.\n\nVerified locally: unit test passes, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`,\n`mypy` clean. (Integration test runs in CI — needs the pgvector DB.)\n\n## Rollout\nTargets `caura-memclaw`. eToro is live on v2.11.0 with this regression\n(memory-write audit gap since cutover); once merged we cut\n`backend-v2.18.1` → rebuild on-prem `v2.11.1` → redeploy eToro via the\ngated `upgrade.sh`. Service is otherwise healthy (pool fix working);\nrollback was rejected (would reintroduce the pool leak).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5b266a609ffd89c60b62731477b39d94ab14d75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c5b266a609ffd89c60b62731477b39d94ab14d75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQRvYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkBoQAKPGc/lkTV/+f3ZJMvj4lXxM\ntIfMDML45rp+gkA28pYEkqEPSiiA2wIgNLHOGJqF00vnPImDZNcdK0h+PVSaWPrx\n20S2Qpg0386xDige7gbwcydHIkomblSIh9InVal0MI7zk+3schdGU5L04sM/TjzT\nFU6acogfQzvbv2apA5YUkavaZoaB2TbeFdevzFZzWiYwMkyRUa3CHJYx1Rpafnsx\n/bG3+5De8i6wwWy+ykhaBIUCeqLRDFP86Dm8zxnEo9f6rxpevdHzKdvoAI817rtX\nKDhjWhsXkWrK6j0BYwKIw8JNzqu7OkWVvVJAIvdeWBmA2k2iS98V20Og0UBBK4vO\nDy9mdA9N35BJqicuoZ+w8DtLaWfX7mbX6Wl0l1XUCiB2ZlS2OritXqIVYrQ25mdW\nXUlvYE7XaxmRp+MINB8GD4CaG7oc0YHRi3hPronr1mQV5InBckhUMlMLLleE07kU\nUNv5F/fQH6wTW2szcuEBF1oM4w1Oq7H8hmwot82/t0wNoByzXDmSXR2aWiCg9khz\nyMpvsPHMHecpjkkcSslHuxgOCIjVvVvOQBE9Dt1jI2fL0ue+UstVcM8RAGPNXAQk\nXNoeuUjMB1oIkM+yP8dtM14Z/gjoWLbbgmnV7zIJDcuMly7KrhIlP7u6WjBt1yxd\nChavWKoIViHSdIMFGHX8\n=3OIo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5b266a609ffd89c60b62731477b39d94ab14d75\nparent 62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782651864 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782651864 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): stop passing removed positional db to log_action on write path (#495)\n\n## Why (production regression — found on eToro v2.11.0 cutover)\n\n`#491` (delete core-api's direct DB pool; route all DB via core-storage)\nmade `audit_service.log_action` **fully keyword-only** by dropping its\n`db` parameter, and updated the `mcp_server` / `agents` / `documents`\ncall sites — **but missed the pipeline write path.**\n\n`write_memory_row.execute()` still passed `ctx.db` **positionally** to\nthe `audit_log` hook (wired directly to `log_action`), so on **every\nmemory create**:\n\n```\nTypeError: log_action() takes 0 positional arguments but 1 positional argument (and 6 keyword-only arguments) were given\n```\n\nThis is caught by the step's `try/except` and logged as `Audit hook\nfailed (non-critical)` — so **writes still persist, but no audit-log\nentry is recorded for memory creates.** Other audited actions (agents,\ndocuments, MCP) are unaffected (their call sites were updated by #491).\n\n**Still present on `main`** → affects all v2.18.0 deployments, including\nSaaS.\n\n## Fix\nDrop the positional `ctx.db` argument (the call is otherwise correct —\nkeyword-only). One line.\n\n## Tests — `tests/test_write_path_audit_signature_regression.py`\n- **unit:** asserts `log_action` stays fully keyword-only (no positional\n`db`) — guards the contract callers rely on. (Runs without a DB.)\n- **integration:** drives the real write pipeline and asserts the audit\nhook does **not** log `Audit hook failed`. The existing\n`test_mcp_write_db_none_regression` can't catch this — it only asserts\nthe row persists, which it does *despite* the swallowed audit failure.\n\nVerified locally: unit test passes, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`,\n`mypy` clean. (Integration test runs in CI — needs the pgvector DB.)\n\n## Rollout\nTargets `caura-memclaw`. eToro is live on v2.11.0 with this regression\n(memory-write audit gap since cutover); once merged we cut\n`backend-v2.18.1` → rebuild on-prem `v2.11.1` → redeploy eToro via the\ngated `upgrade.sh`. Service is otherwise healthy (pool fix working);\nrollback was rejected (would reintroduce the pool leak).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T13:04:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804"}]},{"sha":"62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDYyY2VmYjdkNGZhMDQzZGQwNDk4ZTY0ZDUxNWM5NDZkZDM4M2I4MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T08:01:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T08:01:58Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#492)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.18.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.18.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.17.0...backend-v2.18.0)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skill:** curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance\n([#494](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/494))\n([d7bca1f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **core-api:** correct get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids return type to\nlist[dict]\n([#493](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/493))\n([3d208e3](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **core-api:** delete direct DB pool, route all DB access via\ncore-storage-api (Fix 2 final cleanup)\n([#491](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/491))\n([9e6d7f8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.12.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.12.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.11.0...plugin-v2.12.0)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skill:** curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance\n([#494](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/494))\n([d7bca1f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec41abfd4bdfb57a11c45da45b256a970d448467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ec41abfd4bdfb57a11c45da45b256a970d448467"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQNT2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACQIQABagi9j2OTN0s9ZurIGoiOqm\nRyEXul0/g2Kz3DIRjiDDovNQz7Sf4mNJ24DohUPfWMkYPqNobeVP2U9/Q4Kzpv4X\nO/tEWUAC2aW17bheOFyRW8UGZPizrgLT7BAYE6fHkpd4WlLv43o/dinABQENZ1rV\ndHw9O8fO1v1y4Jb40dYfl5Dz8JrYfo+Du6Qz6kaVx61Jro/x1yuj8COxDC+cQRsl\nZpuW60radg5wcSjM/+PvLFgyqlObach7Sq5fVubu+t4YdOB4Bd+x4fgUsWKdm5PP\nQMQ61D7TH0lZHmhfYjF7oub12iNtWPiHveMTIdRhEtB5C5CJEvJ4XhAwmmRwRDtV\njeZgXDzaK02oEqLdtefeRT6rOUiUV+R/YQjoGJLQBPIU/pOax8KV+H++h6lFa859\nRWgYRRff7E1oO0jcvgAjiCns8IYfi5pGM3kh1DttPJCNfde8fdbTFxsYvGA1OCeV\nXwjCDWQR3lzzkHksy5JBTI8gAW9+1x/SbqKv7BwepEzYstBVAZ6CP/MFHiYrMAyz\nKRmcsPQMWI2tRMrp0P2HTeudXq5DMeF0ZM/+1z8Cl0G311+dlpO1JxxXSjlCA2Oh\nxHN+srK778u9VZCxApDX5Sf5rscKzaJ2ORYtv9F1pqDG3DqnOqAu1GhLhhGMAcG6\nFAhqrRQebeIUIz5d2O9Q\n=XepE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ec41abfd4bdfb57a11c45da45b256a970d448467\nparent d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474\nauthor caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782633718 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782633718 +0300\n\nchore: release main (#492)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.18.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.18.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.17.0...backend-v2.18.0)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skill:** curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance\n([#494](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/494))\n([d7bca1f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **core-api:** correct get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids return type to\nlist[dict]\n([#493](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/493))\n([3d208e3](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **core-api:** delete direct DB pool, route all DB access via\ncore-storage-api (Fix 2 final cleanup)\n([#491](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/491))\n([9e6d7f8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.12.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.12.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.11.0...plugin-v2.12.0)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **skill:** curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance\n([#494](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/494))\n([d7bca1f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T08:01:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62cefb7d4fa043dd0498e64d515c946dd383b804/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474"}]},{"sha":"d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQ3YmNhMWY5ZTdhOWEzODI3OWQzZDQ4ZjhlNzE3NTA1MjQ3YmQ0NzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-25T11:42:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T11:42:24Z"},"message":"feat(skill): curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance (#494)\n\n## Summary\n\nReduce trivial / episodic memory writes. The every-turn agent guidance\npushed agents to write everything — in practice they logged tool calls\nand play-by-play as memories, polluting recall. This removes the \"always\nwrite\" pressure from the every-turn guidance and aligns the SKILL.md L1\ncadence with its own anti-noise rule.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nN/A (behavioral tuning observed in production agent usage).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n### What changed\n\n- **`AGENTS.md`** (`buildAgentsMd`, injected every turn): replaced the\ncompletion-contract mandate (*\"no silent completions — every meaningful\noutcome MUST produce a write. No write = not done.\"*) with a durability\nbar + an explicit *\"never write tool calls / command output /\nintermediate steps\"* line; flipped *\"If in doubt: write\"* → *\"If in\ndoubt, don't.\"*\n- **`prompt-section.ts`** (the leanest every-turn fragment): now states\n*\"write durable, reusable knowledge only — never tool calls,\nintermediate steps, or session-local logs.\"*\n- **`SKILL.md` §9**: L1 cadence is **per-task**, not per-turn —\nresolving its contradiction with §3 *\"Don't write the noise\"* and the\nAnti-patterns section.\n- **`educate.test.ts`**: updated the assertion that pinned the old `L1 —\nper turn` wording.\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n```\ncd plugin && npm test\n# tests 351 | pass 351 | fail 0\n```\n\nAlso verified `buildAgentsMd()` stays under the enforced 1700-char\nevery-turn slim budget (**1695 chars**).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read CONTRIBUTING.md\n- [x] I have added tests that cover my changes (updated the SKILL.md\ncadence assertion; AGENTS.md slim-budget test guards length)\n- [ ] `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` — **N/A** (TypeScript +\nMarkdown only; no Python touched)\n- [ ] `mypy` — **N/A** (no Python touched)\n- [ ] `pytest` — **N/A**; ran plugin suite instead: `npm test` (351\npass)\n- [x] I have updated relevant documentation (the SKILL.md skill doc is\npart of this change)\n- [x] CHANGELOG — auto-generated by release-please from the Conventional\nCommit; no manual edit (repo has no `Unreleased` section)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n- The high-leverage surface is the **every-turn** files (`AGENTS.md` +\n`prompt-section.ts`), not the on-demand `SKILL.md` — agents act on\nwhat's in context every turn.\n- The **`static/` (MCP/canonical) `SKILL.md` is intentionally\nunchanged**: it has no per-turn capture-cadence section and already\ncarries the §3 \"Don't write the noise\" + Anti-patterns guidance.\n- `dist/` is gitignored; only source + skill content is committed.\n- Branched from `origin/main` (the shipping skill version), not the\nin-flight feature branch the investigation started on.\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d34212edb200d1b5f9722014afabac28c7ad7c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8d34212edb200d1b5f9722014afabac28c7ad7c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPRQgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAviYQACCESTWXNE5xsUUiPnDj3l3d\nLYHRSuCT1AG6yqNUgCmaeMxUFr8HczULRZo6s7Ca29vl/tgOcNA1dmjcy2g/TGvF\nBqLGWfnuNC3gSIH7G861lmGzlWJPG1ug1rfk4WXBWNpBbm4Yk3iE6FttPg6Fawur\nCJ/7wuDX2FGqLTlYUfSKFS6ww+xulI2NpGeZf2K+PPXuYk2ZZKIYJfDGF0GkLjcp\nKlZkXPBFrWi/sUjdTn+hgZPEFaZBlcJ/V8HZdCuk/T0rKwTr1RqL6d/pCefT9G7D\ntpi7CPttGc4ZkVnGAWQydpQ0gkSEjg4HZGP/bcupbM5tNdAh9RmEKlXGAOd3pF0q\n8RdRU+q4GLaQCXRBY0Pv8oweR9JuGQb/WANvDrCgln409JcDqXIb7CwI9dNlxNyB\n4eQbFK0fuisrkpfjFrWs5k4n5QUdp4c74PmZaFEBo8cADrZSaOAuEZ16pFtjnTpM\nrJtViO6yLnAuUu1SwrMRxvSTuh0+TmTecWB2saGkrXCRyj8AMRRDZsFrb+JZAHbG\n6cHlMB0s75L7dBsXrES9uOTqVD4p38Bhw4cK9pyQaHD12u7r4alBac7m8FGETV+R\nvgb1/0WN+T5WxS9NcFReDqWGxA855S7A3qDm+8cySBqowgeYU9G56EWN6KeGCjFu\ns5w5t+DQIz0M4lBXabWX\n=lx5g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d34212edb200d1b5f9722014afabac28c7ad7c8\nparent 3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782387744 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782387744 +0300\n\nfeat(skill): curb trivial memory writes in agent guidance (#494)\n\n## Summary\n\nReduce trivial / episodic memory writes. The every-turn agent guidance\npushed agents to write everything — in practice they logged tool calls\nand play-by-play as memories, polluting recall. This removes the \"always\nwrite\" pressure from the every-turn guidance and aligns the SKILL.md L1\ncadence with its own anti-noise rule.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nN/A (behavioral tuning observed in production agent usage).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n### What changed\n\n- **`AGENTS.md`** (`buildAgentsMd`, injected every turn): replaced the\ncompletion-contract mandate (*\"no silent completions — every meaningful\noutcome MUST produce a write. No write = not done.\"*) with a durability\nbar + an explicit *\"never write tool calls / command output /\nintermediate steps\"* line; flipped *\"If in doubt: write\"* → *\"If in\ndoubt, don't.\"*\n- **`prompt-section.ts`** (the leanest every-turn fragment): now states\n*\"write durable, reusable knowledge only — never tool calls,\nintermediate steps, or session-local logs.\"*\n- **`SKILL.md` §9**: L1 cadence is **per-task**, not per-turn —\nresolving its contradiction with §3 *\"Don't write the noise\"* and the\nAnti-patterns section.\n- **`educate.test.ts`**: updated the assertion that pinned the old `L1 —\nper turn` wording.\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n```\ncd plugin && npm test\n# tests 351 | pass 351 | fail 0\n```\n\nAlso verified `buildAgentsMd()` stays under the enforced 1700-char\nevery-turn slim budget (**1695 chars**).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read CONTRIBUTING.md\n- [x] I have added tests that cover my changes (updated the SKILL.md\ncadence assertion; AGENTS.md slim-budget test guards length)\n- [ ] `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` — **N/A** (TypeScript +\nMarkdown only; no Python touched)\n- [ ] `mypy` — **N/A** (no Python touched)\n- [ ] `pytest` — **N/A**; ran plugin suite instead: `npm test` (351\npass)\n- [x] I have updated relevant documentation (the SKILL.md skill doc is\npart of this change)\n- [x] CHANGELOG — auto-generated by release-please from the Conventional\nCommit; no manual edit (repo has no `Unreleased` section)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n- The high-leverage surface is the **every-turn** files (`AGENTS.md` +\n`prompt-section.ts`), not the on-demand `SKILL.md` — agents act on\nwhat's in context every turn.\n- The **`static/` (MCP/canonical) `SKILL.md` is intentionally\nunchanged**: it has no per-turn capture-cadence section and already\ncarries the §3 \"Don't write the noise\" + Anti-patterns guidance.\n- `dist/` is gitignored; only source + skill content is committed.\n- Branched from `origin/main` (the shipping skill version), not the\nin-flight feature branch the investigation started on.\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T11:42:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7bca1f9e7a9a38279d3d48f8e717505247bd474/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79"}]},{"sha":"3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNkMjA4ZTM2MTU0YzgyMDcxYjBkMTA0MzEwN2E1ZmRhMGE2ODJhNzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-25T06:34:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T06:34:49Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): correct get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids return type to list[dict] (#493)\n\n## What\n\nCorrect a misleading return-type annotation on\n`CoreStorageClient.get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`.\n\nThe method was annotated `-> list[tuple]`, but the storage endpoint it\ncalls (`POST /entities/memory-ids-by-entity-ids`, see\n`core-storage-api/.../routers/entities.py`) returns `-> list[dict]` —\nrows of `{\"memory_id\", \"entity_id\", \"role\"}`. The sole consumer,\n`memory_service._entity_boost_pipeline`, already reads the result by key\n(`item[\"memory_id\"]` / `item[\"entity_id\"]`) and constructs tuples *from*\nthose dicts — which is likely how the `list[tuple]` annotation crept in.\n\n## Why it's safe\n\nAnnotation-only change — no runtime behaviour changes. The method\nalready returned dicts; this just makes the type hint match reality (and\nthe storage endpoint's own signature). `storage_client` is in core-api's\nmypy `ignore_errors` set, so this was never type-checked; the fix is\npurely for human readers. Spun out of the #491 review as a noted\nnon-blocking follow-up.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src, common) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api (182 files) — clean\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"3decc579dbf110c0f3f7d75a74c04661698ad854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3decc579dbf110c0f3f7d75a74c04661698ad854"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPMwJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6FUQAJuVXPI8B5md+fiow5Ne5qsR\n51IiX2POKktN+qeAJLcHF83uCbu5hKzgtDUU4S3tBDoa4CsVNfskgdf7O5naiBse\nc90IQTWIKiT08azfPFg/A7sfh1fjyY/5ne8PR2Scl2/R9VuIN+k9uLKYtQvPQbwu\n5Cvo/TfMKN2vz6xEUIFxF8h/BOAlEs/farEk+nSi0wBJ5tyAps3iDFTYlJc6CF2R\nbz+B2hhKxJJH4bHvlucAGfbV9ISNIYqyyTYQi9t4Pm0w+8Nu6nQE8WNNnR+ll3iD\n/Tkkz3Bni5NjJ7a8gjom/xqxfEZdW2ufyq5Y832aXSYrk3T7hSE+f/8p9xtn6fL8\nvTkJAPoJ+XB9k3O6W3Yemy5Egk81A3Z8iSx2K81aeQrtemYBzG8bV7FMTmmJIUB7\npGzrfI+oGYtZ5PaNQKkrFwHnf1S+qIZkwZGVfeu3zl5Y3nPiyLzGCaVBU41slq2W\nQEiwtBLt9P9LuCaiRdn/nRprjh6l4szH/7lVJtNAwHvpPdEaWUNBvjvCpUF/9bGk\norZ/JxXArCrCQgneXrbWg0r3qiSax0upU6sz1iEYgqjefpZbfHpOYp5IXLvM/WjX\nGHnWKZRgPvyawCiXiWUITSJYsULUI7LvoJtx3F43fmNsLUq92b9MwNgcgb4/2wD4\npi5hYsysqidK6ZE0Z7A9\n=DcjT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3decc579dbf110c0f3f7d75a74c04661698ad854\nparent 9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782369289 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782369289 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): correct get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids return type to list[dict] (#493)\n\n## What\n\nCorrect a misleading return-type annotation on\n`CoreStorageClient.get_memory_ids_by_entity_ids`.\n\nThe method was annotated `-> list[tuple]`, but the storage endpoint it\ncalls (`POST /entities/memory-ids-by-entity-ids`, see\n`core-storage-api/.../routers/entities.py`) returns `-> list[dict]` —\nrows of `{\"memory_id\", \"entity_id\", \"role\"}`. The sole consumer,\n`memory_service._entity_boost_pipeline`, already reads the result by key\n(`item[\"memory_id\"]` / `item[\"entity_id\"]`) and constructs tuples *from*\nthose dicts — which is likely how the `list[tuple]` annotation crept in.\n\n## Why it's safe\n\nAnnotation-only change — no runtime behaviour changes. The method\nalready returned dicts; this just makes the type hint match reality (and\nthe storage endpoint's own signature). `storage_client` is in core-api's\nmypy `ignore_errors` set, so this was never type-checked; the fix is\npurely for human readers. Spun out of the #491 review as a noted\nnon-blocking follow-up.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src, common) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api (182 files) — clean\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T06:34:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d208e36154c82071b0d1043107a5fda0a682a79/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592"}]},{"sha":"9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDllNmQ3ZjhmOTdkZTIwNDY5ZGY5MzA1YWY3NmVmZWYwODFhZDM1OTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-25T05:23:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:23:00Z"},"message":"refactor(core-api): delete direct DB pool, route all DB access via core-storage-api (Fix 2 final cleanup) (#491)\n\n## What\n\nFinal Fix-2 cleanup: **delete core-api's direct DB pool** and route\nevery remaining DB access through core-storage-api over HTTP. This\nfulfils the \"no direct DB outside core-storage-api\" invariant for\ncore-api. Last phase of the series — follows OSS #484 (PR1), OSS #485\n(PR2), OSS #486 (PR3a), all merged.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Delete `db/session.py` (engine / `async_session` / `get_db`) and all\nof `repositories/*`; delete `services/memory_stats.py`.\n- Relocate the tenant-context setters to `core_api/tenant_context.py`\n(`auth.py` updated) and `_relation_weight` to `constants.py`.\n- Remove the `on_recall` hook; recall paths call the storage client's\n`increment_recall` directly.\n- Reroute the remaining class-A consumers to storage-client methods:\nmemories list/stats/tenants, ingest doc-hash idempotency, crystallizer\nentity-coverage + audit-usage, insights queries, and evolve persistence.\nThese consumers now read storage **dict rows by key** (not ORM\nattributes).\n- Add storage-client methods `get_entity_coverage` / `get_audit_usage` /\n`find_prior_ingest_by_doc_hash` (the endpoints already landed in\n#484/#486).\n- Strip ~51 vestigial `db` params, 41 `Depends(get_db)`, dead\n`commit`/`rollback`, and `postgres_*` / `db_pool_size` /\n`db_max_overflow` / `database_url` from config; drop the now-deleted\n`db.session` / `repositories` entries from the mypy overrides.\n- Add `tests/test_no_direct_db_outside_storage.py` (AST guard) so a\ndirect DB pool can't be reintroduced into core-api.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public contract change — routes, response models, request schemas,\nand MCP tool schemas are unchanged. This is internal DB plumbing only;\nthe ~550 internal test updates are because they call internal functions\ndirectly.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src, common) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api (182 files) + core-storage-api (68 files) — clean\n- Full pytest (no `--timeout`, mirrors CI): **3669 passed, 0 failed**,\nno hangs\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"784d4ac2f74517c820e13aabd694b348b866bc9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/784d4ac2f74517c820e13aabd694b348b866bc9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPLs0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOM4QACZ8Tt7aENuHG+2UFS296RwV\nhiMElyJiCmBkNhf9o4wmXxWaB6hWOYbhCXcEeYWOxPkjBRiyVrOawZLUwaVqt8tg\nI0oVCJHCClMZVP8+0lQth5kumid1/zocALg8sid8jG/EPf+3FmjpXflSH7vJ1ZKV\ndVQWNeVB8j+cZpC8w92SUx0Hbnu+exKb5GUXUwU4WQAldN+nh+RQvkYcjqTlleYR\nq4W/nF1g3TMEpqtWhufqwo6llFgtBLeXI37IoWvs0BjqYrJzWkNvHHBK0B1kz3g5\nlfnr9MVe9jLn4W4pTYQ1FdK6TeRvzdUSR1yyEF+IIlA4XmB0zxtElu+QBFCsh8Pi\nME8l2nLHcjQe619oOINZKz1a+BOVIlCXKU77QsZXsa3lt4ZWM++m0CVc5pcXCxl3\nQ1c/ZDP49eglxUWqQUvX7KGohoFbG9XLhDApdNL0LfwVPmx7SkOacdbarwNmeI85\nTJJ9bCWeAn7DFsBy17MeYcUVLD7QUZUTPeLpWuw5RHDBN9EoCWRxkHiaM+snARP1\nZ+TY2hkHfZW3RbzGDqpN7XK2Z2sQWcdFK9WXltQy3oNK8/qoQFMncQdu3ZjngZ8T\niyP9DHkqjixVoAimF/S/5RxvwTeiaegq9BzCrHnrC3YIZeaZf8RpECmqb4vmG3N3\n01dggMTEiJgAD6B+AGIR\n=IWq6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 784d4ac2f74517c820e13aabd694b348b866bc9e\nparent d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782364980 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782364980 +0300\n\nrefactor(core-api): delete direct DB pool, route all DB access via core-storage-api (Fix 2 final cleanup) (#491)\n\n## What\n\nFinal Fix-2 cleanup: **delete core-api's direct DB pool** and route\nevery remaining DB access through core-storage-api over HTTP. This\nfulfils the \"no direct DB outside core-storage-api\" invariant for\ncore-api. Last phase of the series — follows OSS #484 (PR1), OSS #485\n(PR2), OSS #486 (PR3a), all merged.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Delete `db/session.py` (engine / `async_session` / `get_db`) and all\nof `repositories/*`; delete `services/memory_stats.py`.\n- Relocate the tenant-context setters to `core_api/tenant_context.py`\n(`auth.py` updated) and `_relation_weight` to `constants.py`.\n- Remove the `on_recall` hook; recall paths call the storage client's\n`increment_recall` directly.\n- Reroute the remaining class-A consumers to storage-client methods:\nmemories list/stats/tenants, ingest doc-hash idempotency, crystallizer\nentity-coverage + audit-usage, insights queries, and evolve persistence.\nThese consumers now read storage **dict rows by key** (not ORM\nattributes).\n- Add storage-client methods `get_entity_coverage` / `get_audit_usage` /\n`find_prior_ingest_by_doc_hash` (the endpoints already landed in\n#484/#486).\n- Strip ~51 vestigial `db` params, 41 `Depends(get_db)`, dead\n`commit`/`rollback`, and `postgres_*` / `db_pool_size` /\n`db_max_overflow` / `database_url` from config; drop the now-deleted\n`db.session` / `repositories` entries from the mypy overrides.\n- Add `tests/test_no_direct_db_outside_storage.py` (AST guard) so a\ndirect DB pool can't be reintroduced into core-api.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo public contract change — routes, response models, request schemas,\nand MCP tool schemas are unchanged. This is internal DB plumbing only;\nthe ~550 internal test updates are because they call internal functions\ndirectly.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src, common) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api (182 files) + core-storage-api (68 files) — clean\n- Full pytest (no `--timeout`, mirrors CI): **3669 passed, 0 failed**,\nno hangs\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:23:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e6d7f8f97de20469df9305af76efef081ad3592/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736"}]},{"sha":"d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQ3Y2ExN2NhMmNkNTVkMGEyOTMzZDZkNTNlYjVmYmJhZjM4ZTU3MzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-24T13:00:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T13:00:53Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#401)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.17.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.17.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.16.0...backend-v2.17.0)\n(2026-06-24)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **audit:** tamper-evident per-tenant hash chain for audit_log (eToro\ngovernance)\n([#397](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/397))\n([baaa493](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/baaa493cdc8a2bf71d031b0f457844d389c8f6c4))\n* **core-api:** cross-worker settings-cache invalidation (CAURA-571)\n([#418](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/418))\n([86bbe9e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654))\n* **core-api:** fast business/personal pre-gate before enrichment\n(opt-in) ([#403](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/403))\n([095c360](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6))\n* **core-api:** install-skill ?skill= selector + company-brain import\npath ([#483](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/483))\n([a2a764e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081))\n* **core-api:** route documents + fleet residuals through\ncore-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 3)\n([#431](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/431))\n([ad2a2d9](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346))\n* **core-api:** route mcp_server's 9 ready tools through\ncore-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 4)\n([#432](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/432))\n([dc0b674](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5))\n* **core-api:** route memory REST surface through core-storage-api (Fix\n2 Phase 2)\n([#429](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/429))\n([1e39c59](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247))\n* **core-api:** route organization_settings through core-storage-api\n(Fix 2 Phase 0)\n([#427](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/427))\n([4450ec0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583))\n* **core-api:** route tenant-discovery through core-storage-api (Fix 2\nPhase 1) ([#428](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/428))\n([f05f498](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562))\n* **core-storage-api:** crystallizer entity-coverage + audit-usage reads\n(Fix 2 final-cleanup PR3a)\n([#486](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/486))\n([0737b6a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf))\n* **core-storage-api:** recall/capability/ingest endpoints for Fix-2\nfinal cleanup (PR1)\n([#484](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/484))\n([d8b18d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410))\n* **core-storage-api:** route entity-linking pipeline through storage\n(Fix 2 Ph6)\n([#477](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/477))\n([74a18d7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39))\n* **core-storage-api:** route evolve through storage + delete\n_mcp_session (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR2)\n([#472](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/472))\n([44743e1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0))\n* **core-storage-api:** route insights_service through storage (Fix 2\nPh5b, PR1 — insights)\n([#471](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/471))\n([2655b84](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866))\n* **core-storage-api:** route the skill-factory pipeline through storage\n(Fix 2 Ph5a)\n([#470](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/470))\n([81e79be](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8))\n* **governance:** ingestion-boundary PII + business/personal gate\n(eToro) ([#398](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/398))\n([12860af](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/12860af951539ea2b097f2f2dd9ee7615b1c9464))\n* **plugin:** additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2)\n([#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/417))\n([3d970ef](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd))\n* **plugin:** auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path\n(PR3b) ([#425](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/425))\n([819a77f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa))\n* **plugin:** per-target reconcile observability (PR3a)\n([#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/424))\n([04120f2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334))\n* **recall:** opt-in logging of agent-chosen recalls\n([#480](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/480))\n([953ec33](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389))\n* **skills:** refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add\ncompany-brain\n([#482](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/482))\n([aa03c03](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **audit:** idempotent bulk flush via client_event_id — stop dropping\naudit rows\n([#407](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/407))\n([bf87e64](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb))\n* **core-api:** cut prod connect-timeout + rate-limit-Redis log noise\n([#426](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/426))\n([a082f3f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180))\n* **core-api:** harden business/personal pre-gate (timeout, audit truth,\nfail-closed, audit durability)\n([#416](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/416))\n([aa4be8e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931))\n* **core-api:** keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out\n(VPC-connector ConnectTimeout residual)\n([#434](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/434))\n([0ba51b4](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331))\n* **core-api:** per-tenant embed concurrency cap (noisy-neighbor-search)\n([#464](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/464))\n([043c02e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e))\n* **core-api:** re-route third-party loggers from the ASGI lifespan\nstartup ([#473](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/473))\n([8f8f39e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe))\n* **core-api:** resolve home fleet on omitted fleet_id for MCP writes\n([#465](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/465))\n([56db1f5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70))\n* **core-api:** route recall/capability writes through storage (Fix-2\ncleanup PR2)\n([#485](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/485))\n([592b231](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/592b231d395ff8787c9ad82c91a4b5262432b95d))\n* **core-api:** self-heal storage pool + cancellation-safe requests\n(CAURA-000)\n([#415](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/415))\n([5889e3f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9))\n* **core-api:** stamp version into image so /api/v1/version stops\nserving \"dev\" (CAURA-000)\n([#414](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/414))\n([4d1c486](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a))\n* **core-api:** surface write-pipeline step failures instead of masking\nas KeyError\n([#474](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/474))\n([5d359b2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476))\n* **core-storage-api:** 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding\nwrite ([#468](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/468))\n([bec8229](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373))\n* **core-storage-api:** 422 on missing/non-list embedding in\n/entities/set-embeddings\n([#478](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/478))\n([6268725](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270))\n* **core-storage-api:** followers skip the migration lock once schema is\nat head ([#487](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/487))\n([8a7ac37](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780))\n* **core-storage-api:** tenant-guard by-id memory UPDATEs\n([#467](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/467))\n([4248b4d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e))\n* **extraction:** re-fold split-off subject discriminators (A33)\n([#412](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/412))\n([ab0d2d6](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c))\n* **http-retry:** widen connection-phase retry to ride out storage cold\nstarts ([#406](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/406))\n([5bbede7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a))\n* **logging:** demote handler-less reroute 'no-op' to DEBUG (records\naren't lost)\n([#488](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/488))\n([9bdbe44](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791))\n* **prompts:** stop brace-escaping content before str.format\n([#404](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/404))\n([ba94a54](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604))\n* **rate-limit:** fail open on Redis outage instead of 500\n(view_rate_limit AttributeError)\n([#410](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/410))\n([53b467d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427))\n* **recall:** tighten recall-brief grounding to stop invented details\n([#489](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/489))\n([6794f3e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79))\n* **search:** dampen recall_boost so it can't hijack rankings (A26)\n([#411](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/411))\n([1de219c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0))\n* **search:** rank entity-lookup fan-out cap by query-match count (A30)\n([#409](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/409))\n([8f809c0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b))\n* **storage:** harden migration advisory-lock so a slow migration can't\ncrash booting writers\n([#408](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/408))\n([54cbe1a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1))\n\n\n### Performance\n\n* **core-api:** make document-ingest (kreuzberg) an opt-in extra to cut\ncold start\n([#469](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/469))\n([1f082d8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **core-api:** clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not\nrejected ([#481](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/481))\n([6938f08](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0))\n* **core-api:** document LLM free-form PII recall limit (recommend a\ncapable enrichment model)\n([#419](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/419))\n([36b1b30](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7))\n* point all memclaw.dev links to memclaw.net\n([#475](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/475))\n([a6f9ad1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **core-storage-api:** consolidate router validation guards into\n_validation\n([#479](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/479))\n([e9dd9ca](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f))\n* **plugin:** configurable skill-reconcile targets (PR1 — refactor +\nconfig plumbing)\n([#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/413))\n([57e5e96](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.11.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.11.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.10.1...plugin-v2.11.0)\n(2026-06-24)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2)\n([#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/417))\n([3d970ef](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd))\n* **plugin:** auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path\n(PR3b) ([#425](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/425))\n([819a77f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa))\n* **plugin:** per-target reconcile observability (PR3a)\n([#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/424))\n([04120f2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334))\n* **skills:** refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add\ncompany-brain\n([#482](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/482))\n([aa03c03](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **core-api:** clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not\nrejected ([#481](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-