api:** route memory REST surface through core-storage-api (Fix\n2 Phase 2)\n([#429](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/429))\n([1e39c59](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247))\n* **core-api:** route organization_settings through core-storage-api\n(Fix 2 Phase 0)\n([#427](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/427))\n([4450ec0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583))\n* **core-api:** route tenant-discovery through core-storage-api (Fix 2\nPhase 1) ([#428](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/428))\n([f05f498](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562))\n* **core-storage-api:** crystallizer entity-coverage + audit-usage reads\n(Fix 2 final-cleanup PR3a)\n([#486](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/486))\n([0737b6a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf))\n* **core-storage-api:** recall/capability/ingest endpoints for Fix-2\nfinal cleanup (PR1)\n([#484](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/484))\n([d8b18d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410))\n* **core-storage-api:** route entity-linking pipeline through storage\n(Fix 2 Ph6)\n([#477](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/477))\n([74a18d7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39))\n* **core-storage-api:** route evolve through storage + delete\n_mcp_session (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR2)\n([#472](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/472))\n([44743e1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0))\n* **core-storage-api:** route insights_service through storage (Fix 2\nPh5b, PR1 — insights)\n([#471](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/471))\n([2655b84](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866))\n* **core-storage-api:** route the skill-factory pipeline through storage\n(Fix 2 Ph5a)\n([#470](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/470))\n([81e79be](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8))\n* **governance:** ingestion-boundary PII + business/personal gate\n(eToro) ([#398](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/398))\n([12860af](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/12860af951539ea2b097f2f2dd9ee7615b1c9464))\n* **plugin:** additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2)\n([#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/417))\n([3d970ef](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd))\n* **plugin:** auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path\n(PR3b) ([#425](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/425))\n([819a77f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa))\n* **plugin:** per-target reconcile observability (PR3a)\n([#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/424))\n([04120f2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334))\n* **recall:** opt-in logging of agent-chosen recalls\n([#480](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/480))\n([953ec33](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389))\n* **skills:** refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add\ncompany-brain\n([#482](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/482))\n([aa03c03](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **audit:** idempotent bulk flush via client_event_id — stop dropping\naudit rows\n([#407](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/407))\n([bf87e64](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb))\n* **core-api:** cut prod connect-timeout + rate-limit-Redis log noise\n([#426](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/426))\n([a082f3f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180))\n* **core-api:** harden business/personal pre-gate (timeout, audit truth,\nfail-closed, audit durability)\n([#416](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/416))\n([aa4be8e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931))\n* **core-api:** keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out\n(VPC-connector ConnectTimeout residual)\n([#434](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/434))\n([0ba51b4](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331))\n* **core-api:** per-tenant embed concurrency cap (noisy-neighbor-search)\n([#464](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/464))\n([043c02e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e))\n* **core-api:** re-route third-party loggers from the ASGI lifespan\nstartup ([#473](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/473))\n([8f8f39e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe))\n* **core-api:** resolve home fleet on omitted fleet_id for MCP writes\n([#465](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/465))\n([56db1f5](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70))\n* **core-api:** route recall/capability writes through storage (Fix-2\ncleanup PR2)\n([#485](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/485))\n([592b231](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/592b231d395ff8787c9ad82c91a4b5262432b95d))\n* **core-api:** self-heal storage pool + cancellation-safe requests\n(CAURA-000)\n([#415](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/415))\n([5889e3f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9))\n* **core-api:** stamp version into image so /api/v1/version stops\nserving \"dev\" (CAURA-000)\n([#414](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/414))\n([4d1c486](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a))\n* **core-api:** surface write-pipeline step failures instead of masking\nas KeyError\n([#474](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/474))\n([5d359b2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476))\n* **core-storage-api:** 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding\nwrite ([#468](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/468))\n([bec8229](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373))\n* **core-storage-api:** 422 on missing/non-list embedding in\n/entities/set-embeddings\n([#478](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/478))\n([6268725](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270))\n* **core-storage-api:** followers skip the migration lock once schema is\nat head ([#487](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/487))\n([8a7ac37](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780))\n* **core-storage-api:** tenant-guard by-id memory UPDATEs\n([#467](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/467))\n([4248b4d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e))\n* **extraction:** re-fold split-off subject discriminators (A33)\n([#412](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/412))\n([ab0d2d6](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c))\n* **http-retry:** widen connection-phase retry to ride out storage cold\nstarts ([#406](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/406))\n([5bbede7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a))\n* **logging:** demote handler-less reroute 'no-op' to DEBUG (records\naren't lost)\n([#488](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/488))\n([9bdbe44](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791))\n* **prompts:** stop brace-escaping content before str.format\n([#404](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/404))\n([ba94a54](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604))\n* **rate-limit:** fail open on Redis outage instead of 500\n(view_rate_limit AttributeError)\n([#410](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/410))\n([53b467d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427))\n* **recall:** tighten recall-brief grounding to stop invented details\n([#489](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/489))\n([6794f3e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79))\n* **search:** dampen recall_boost so it can't hijack rankings (A26)\n([#411](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/411))\n([1de219c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0))\n* **search:** rank entity-lookup fan-out cap by query-match count (A30)\n([#409](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/409))\n([8f809c0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b))\n* **storage:** harden migration advisory-lock so a slow migration can't\ncrash booting writers\n([#408](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/408))\n([54cbe1a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1))\n\n\n### Performance\n\n* **core-api:** make document-ingest (kreuzberg) an opt-in extra to cut\ncold start\n([#469](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/469))\n([1f082d8](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **core-api:** clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not\nrejected ([#481](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/481))\n([6938f08](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0))\n* **core-api:** document LLM free-form PII recall limit (recommend a\ncapable enrichment model)\n([#419](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/419))\n([36b1b30](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7))\n* point all memclaw.dev links to memclaw.net\n([#475](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/475))\n([a6f9ad1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **core-storage-api:** consolidate router validation guards into\n_validation\n([#479](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/479))\n([e9dd9ca](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f))\n* **plugin:** configurable skill-reconcile targets (PR1 — refactor +\nconfig plumbing)\n([#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/413))\n([57e5e96](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.11.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.11.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.10.1...plugin-v2.11.0)\n(2026-06-24)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2)\n([#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/417))\n([3d970ef](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd))\n* **plugin:** auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path\n(PR3b) ([#425](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/425))\n([819a77f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa))\n* **plugin:** per-target reconcile observability (PR3a)\n([#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/424))\n([04120f2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334))\n* **skills:** refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add\ncompany-brain\n([#482](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/482))\n([aa03c03](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **core-api:** clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not\nrejected ([#481](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/481))\n([6938f08](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **plugin:** configurable skill-reconcile targets (PR1 — refactor +\nconfig plumbing)\n([#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/413))\n([57e5e96](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T13:00:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d7ca17ca2cd55d0a2933d6d53eb5fbbaf38e5736/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79"}]},{"sha":"6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY3OTRmM2U2MGQxNzdjZDdkNjAwNThlYmE3Yjc2NDEzMjZiZjRiNzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-24T11:08:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T11:08:44Z"},"message":"fix(recall): tighten recall-brief grounding to stop invented details (#489)\n\n## What\nStrengthen `RECALL_PROMPT` (recall-brief summarization) grounding.\n\n## Why\nNightly `recall-brief-ungrounded` (HIGH): the summary judge flagged an\nunsupported claim — *\"Project Zephyr is scheduled to be completed by\nSeptember 14, 2026\"* — a date present in **no** memory (tenant A: 4/5\ngrounded, mean 4.8). The prompt already had grounding rules, but the\nmodel still *completed* a missing date.\n\n## Change\n- Lead with: answer using **ONLY** the memories as source of truth — no\noutside/world knowledge.\n- Every name/date/number/title/identifier in the answer **must appear\nverbatim** in the memories; never invent/estimate/approximate/complete a\nmissing value (explicitly: don't supply a completion date if none is\nstated).\n- A detail the question asks for but the memories lack → say it's **not\nrecorded** rather than supplying one.\n\nPrompt-only; no logic/API-shape change. No unit test pins the prompt\ntext; grounding is judged by the nightly LLM judge (which caught this),\nso the next run re-measures.\n\n## Follow-up (not this PR)\nGate releases on a groundedness threshold — the nightly already computes\nthe score; making it a hard gate is @ran / test-automation side.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce9f74acf9f07d30e055b7c55366b68e9fdf1a11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ce9f74acf9f07d30e055b7c55366b68e9fdf1a11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO7q8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgwMQAEXzS+8Citmwl7ic4lUFNjWT\nfvXTdbT4Ra1aADnNOZ9PzVCm3B10rdbpVF45KxHroRKkvqhX4L5Y/r9uIKg5Pzgz\nAgOkN9enbZXDnqdjETaKziG9vwCCsCnQHsSidaFsW+Nqo2nj5clTfuqx8pqGhlcg\nhlBtR7R9QdoBICIg94jgwB0bIBYI6mZAI1l65MIOYj5HFLVG+1lQeoTJE1pwRyt5\nkN/kcfuy5q7HmYC1japJSoGiujzGoz8m/eorDUNkICJFwDmxCeMkJKpyyV1x+jOH\nKmfYwFV3/PQvo1kPL7InSAq/V0SsXX8xjROCt0EuGg6zkE6s4PW9ePPi7AWKSqY5\neY68zCu0TjZPknekeMrABXcNi8GYcAukQm5lTpt4Y58vtg9gfg2Vq+fYdyTXkvj3\n7DXbiPNPguyZpFKvp+wtQJ1rzFjFgyRFVwn56r7h5XzfcTLlxN0kLu/U6AyB36bS\n9eknzBzLKBbF8Z0aW8jJLEf76RLEThrNxTcsEHs/PZUDR2RX3DMdD3EvGD5euufF\n7ZeKsD34pxqCietdw+OiyQe4KPwzwXgosJUZvME4jDQFCc0bCw14oFwz56uhKMZE\n3NqnOquEt+tN90ZzJCl8moZWEHzqwjEnHJv+RYmb0VnTB3HAbWYF45mrP+X5mvC2\nnsVden3G2vdFuhiCnJ+w\n=bMta\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ce9f74acf9f07d30e055b7c55366b68e9fdf1a11\nparent 9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782299324 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782299324 +0300\n\nfix(recall): tighten recall-brief grounding to stop invented details (#489)\n\n## What\nStrengthen `RECALL_PROMPT` (recall-brief summarization) grounding.\n\n## Why\nNightly `recall-brief-ungrounded` (HIGH): the summary judge flagged an\nunsupported claim — *\"Project Zephyr is scheduled to be completed by\nSeptember 14, 2026\"* — a date present in **no** memory (tenant A: 4/5\ngrounded, mean 4.8). The prompt already had grounding rules, but the\nmodel still *completed* a missing date.\n\n## Change\n- Lead with: answer using **ONLY** the memories as source of truth — no\noutside/world knowledge.\n- Every name/date/number/title/identifier in the answer **must appear\nverbatim** in the memories; never invent/estimate/approximate/complete a\nmissing value (explicitly: don't supply a completion date if none is\nstated).\n- A detail the question asks for but the memories lack → say it's **not\nrecorded** rather than supplying one.\n\nPrompt-only; no logic/API-shape change. No unit test pins the prompt\ntext; grounding is judged by the nightly LLM judge (which caught this),\nso the next run re-measures.\n\n## Follow-up (not this PR)\nGate releases on a groundedness threshold — the nightly already computes\nthe score; making it a hard gate is @ran / test-automation side.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T11:08:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6794f3e60d177cd7d60058eba7b7641326bf4b79/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791"}]},{"sha":"9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDliZGJlNDRmMDVhYTNiMmU5MGUzMDliNjZjZGY4YmFkZGFkNWI3OTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-24T09:07:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T09:07:42Z"},"message":"fix(logging): demote handler-less reroute 'no-op' to DEBUG (records aren't lost) (#488)\n\n## What\n\n`common/structlog_config.py`'s `_route_third_party_to_root` emitted a\n**WARNING** (\"logger X has no own handlers at rerouting time; rerouting\nwas a no-op …\") whenever a listed third-party logger\n(`mcp`/`fastmcp`/`uvicorn.error`/`slowapi`) was handler-less +\n`propagate=True`. Demote it to **DEBUG** + reword.\n\n## Why\n\nThat state is **benign, not a routing failure**: a handler-less,\n`propagate=True` logger already flows to the root handler. **Verified in\nprod** — `mcp.server.streamable_http` / `uvicorn.error` records land in\nCloud Logging as structured JSON via propagation. So the WARNING was a\n**misleading false alarm**, firing ~once per instance start (~57/day for\n`fastmcp` in prod core-api), implying records wouldn't reach GCP when\nthey do. It nearly mis-led triage into thinking FastMCP tool-errors were\ninvisible (the very thing #473 was about — which is actually working).\n\n## Safety\n\nRouting behavior is unchanged — only the log level + message. The\nsnapshot/idempotency guard is untouched, and the empty state is still\n**not** snapshotted, so a later reroute can still act if a library ever\ninstalls its own handlers / sets `propagate=False`.\n\n## Test\n\nExisting 21 logging tests pass; adds\n`test_route_third_party_to_root_pristine_logger_no_warning` asserting a\npristine handler-less logger emits no WARNING. ruff + mypy clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"782880a8ced2de1f868c3183999a26565d6899de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/782880a8ced2de1f868c3183999a26565d6899de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO55eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAabwQAGrEV6xdx56KaGbDn/n/yQYr\nmHjRzDbwMsWTTsOiLX1ohYjNfdzxK9p/x5jNfu8D9CRUp8FAYQ45Fsb5C9bXozsl\naSO7bNn7ujcE856U/ZD5RJzWzbkP5Z/sDMpWTVNBl3Xdne6ulg1j94qheOybHSxb\nPkG6YbVRs90lwmPsbU2Nd710mUIVL0PgTtVRZYnghJoLJeCobcUryrBjFdFLKTS+\nwplUJO0I4tdZoYu1d1BKzMmKh1VlohsQYT5kZn9QuRFn5FRgtp9oQxtQhrwGs5QU\nYxuCotz1vMNNzM11v61zgNnxC9EoHmVXvcyOvdpHrrsqLTB1ofvQfGQsfcoK8T/q\n+SWp8GBBKsbKeTyBHFJBJ2TY83LVH3fWeqJ+mf7KSk4FyUwNdU3OY45yYQHssm+4\nP03r60pIIW6W+KNM3vyT2L8wPFXvGfhPWtwlPb3Nkyo1fGeo6T51I/acx+2gf30x\nBKqd0OgB+7eJTID11y08/SXR174mRlx40nTimv3QnjdWtrDWh8pMWRb3M9wkKYU0\nAKK86bJPHRYhDhW1iYiBTgOV/RL2dTgemphf38QFj36bsbjQARadoo5yurQdHPNC\nynApERBm3o2OoDx1Bn8oVjaNSIMlGBCbWVOyK+qqAwdbUHfYAM8WtzkSYR7BVCi6\nYW+kw+rv6pO3k9VwKfnH\n=gaWp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 782880a8ced2de1f868c3183999a26565d6899de\nparent 8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782292062 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782292062 +0300\n\nfix(logging): demote handler-less reroute 'no-op' to DEBUG (records aren't lost) (#488)\n\n## What\n\n`common/structlog_config.py`'s `_route_third_party_to_root` emitted a\n**WARNING** (\"logger X has no own handlers at rerouting time; rerouting\nwas a no-op …\") whenever a listed third-party logger\n(`mcp`/`fastmcp`/`uvicorn.error`/`slowapi`) was handler-less +\n`propagate=True`. Demote it to **DEBUG** + reword.\n\n## Why\n\nThat state is **benign, not a routing failure**: a handler-less,\n`propagate=True` logger already flows to the root handler. **Verified in\nprod** — `mcp.server.streamable_http` / `uvicorn.error` records land in\nCloud Logging as structured JSON via propagation. So the WARNING was a\n**misleading false alarm**, firing ~once per instance start (~57/day for\n`fastmcp` in prod core-api), implying records wouldn't reach GCP when\nthey do. It nearly mis-led triage into thinking FastMCP tool-errors were\ninvisible (the very thing #473 was about — which is actually working).\n\n## Safety\n\nRouting behavior is unchanged — only the log level + message. The\nsnapshot/idempotency guard is untouched, and the empty state is still\n**not** snapshotted, so a later reroute can still act if a library ever\ninstalls its own handlers / sets `propagate=False`.\n\n## Test\n\nExisting 21 logging tests pass; adds\n`test_route_third_party_to_root_pristine_logger_no_warning` asserting a\npristine handler-less logger emits no WARNING. ruff + mypy clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T09:07:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9bdbe44f05aa3b2e90e309b66cdf8baddad5b791/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780"}]},{"sha":"8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhhN2FjMzc1ODM0N2UwNDk2MGU5NDJkYzgxZTkwN2E0MjVkZjc3ODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-24T08:51:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T08:51:35Z"},"message":"fix(core-storage-api): followers skip the migration lock once schema is at head (#487)\n\n## Problem\n\ncore-storage-api runs alembic migrations on startup, serialized by a\nPostgres advisory lock: one replica (leader) migrates; the others\n(followers) **poll to acquire the lock, then run a redundant no-op\n`upgrade`**. During a multi-replica scale-up, that serialized `acquire →\nno-op → release` tail means tail replicas wait far longer than the\nleader's actual migration — long enough to blow the Cloud Run **240s\nstartup TCP probe** (`failureThreshold: 1`), so Cloud Run kills them.\n\n**Observed (prod 2026-06-24 02:04Z):**\n`prod-memclaw-core-storage-writer` — `Default STARTUP TCP probe failed …\nDEADLINE_EXCEEDED. The instance was not started.` Killed instances →\nbrief storage capacity dips → the `core-api → core-storage-api`\n`httpx.ConnectTimeout`s that raise + nack the `memclaw.memory.embedded`\npubsub handler (`consumer.py:184 → storage_client.get_memory`). This PR\naddresses the storage-startup root cause of that connect-timeout class.\n\n## Change\n\n`_schema_is_at_head(connection, head)` lets a non-leader replica start\nserving **as soon as the schema reaches head, without acquiring the\nlock**:\n- **Fast path** before the lock loop: if nothing is pending, return\nimmediately — no replica even contends on the lock (steady-state boot).\n- **Follower poll loop**: bail the moment the leader's migration lands,\nso all waiting followers unblock *together* instead of draining\none-at-a-time through the lock.\n\nUnchanged / preserved:\n- **Leader path** still acquires the advisory lock and runs the real\n`upgrade`/`stamp`.\n- **Fresh DB** (`current is None`) still falls through to the\nstamp/upgrade path under the lock.\n- `head` is computed **once** (constant per process), so the per-poll\nfollower check is a single `alembic_version` SELECT — not a\nmigrations-dir re-walk each poll.\n\n## Test\n\n`tests/test_init_schema_at_head.py` — unit-tests the predicate (at-head\n→ True; pending → False; fresh/`None` → False) by stubbing\n`MigrationContext` (no DB). `ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\n## Residual (by design)\n\nThis removes the **serialization** overhead, not the **per-migration\nruntime floor**: a single migration that runs longer than the\nstartup-probe deadline still kills followers (they legitimately can't\nserve until the schema is ready). That case requires raising the\nstartup-probe deadline or moving migrations off the boot path (the known\nlonger-term direction) — out of scope here.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"823cb007a8f28082d0ecf4caf6fc1160953d8589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/823cb007a8f28082d0ecf4caf6fc1160953d8589"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO5qXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR6QQAArZLn0FKEsOFdlVOvTtyYb3\nVIUL6n81DjglX8JkQilG0yjTiuWhTc3LAzJLXzXXFtN/lsXDB6mvK6VeGg+ct7jo\nf+PWg1Ri+tiYkRI7s0nt/TCO1geyi32XkDd+BZvXo2aO8X5FwsBNJak35xyy8xFz\nXXzT4huBk0bBoENijyIrh9vSFbi+LLKkOygqIPE91gIPoGlprauvW6wELnuQde6H\nLUL1Xxsz0ZHeppjPBXwDHTIATBw3xjRj3YDRvqfTAIxx9iFjZKb0H1KkhyowXfxV\nsd8g7NshmuEZxDeVQAuxW2BA1VPmi4EcJ5mbb6f2PF3cRQiGFM6l454all3x+EWX\nZf6SmnkzB0g82Mlq0HYvoK9rHf7QPQ0xpUMs1ZmyWVd/FvHjMGsXbfKaRjJKXjYE\nuspGXl8kYunyW2FC3YhEANKWclFbC9uvorq2l5ojX6Yf4xjGj88gl2PYKDQqQSqB\nMkLbuF1CIjpkPo2FX767JKPXp+4p404yjlhoGNVR9nQ2+XWPZSWQoUe2ewWWAZEc\ng+scajFlh1ZXr9aHdEAO5gt/yxKKetdsGf3bqdJX9PGVDW0rtI6SwZBx2uTqwIrQ\nR/QRW4XjeNMu6tV1hG12A5Mr936SQiVTclz7tW7udyGnkRiDDMept0o6kJ//s4FX\nMBxttyYZbYYOuVuupHPo\n=9SPH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 823cb007a8f28082d0ecf4caf6fc1160953d8589\nparent 0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782291095 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782291095 +0300\n\nfix(core-storage-api): followers skip the migration lock once schema is at head (#487)\n\n## Problem\n\ncore-storage-api runs alembic migrations on startup, serialized by a\nPostgres advisory lock: one replica (leader) migrates; the others\n(followers) **poll to acquire the lock, then run a redundant no-op\n`upgrade`**. During a multi-replica scale-up, that serialized `acquire →\nno-op → release` tail means tail replicas wait far longer than the\nleader's actual migration — long enough to blow the Cloud Run **240s\nstartup TCP probe** (`failureThreshold: 1`), so Cloud Run kills them.\n\n**Observed (prod 2026-06-24 02:04Z):**\n`prod-memclaw-core-storage-writer` — `Default STARTUP TCP probe failed …\nDEADLINE_EXCEEDED. The instance was not started.` Killed instances →\nbrief storage capacity dips → the `core-api → core-storage-api`\n`httpx.ConnectTimeout`s that raise + nack the `memclaw.memory.embedded`\npubsub handler (`consumer.py:184 → storage_client.get_memory`). This PR\naddresses the storage-startup root cause of that connect-timeout class.\n\n## Change\n\n`_schema_is_at_head(connection, head)` lets a non-leader replica start\nserving **as soon as the schema reaches head, without acquiring the\nlock**:\n- **Fast path** before the lock loop: if nothing is pending, return\nimmediately — no replica even contends on the lock (steady-state boot).\n- **Follower poll loop**: bail the moment the leader's migration lands,\nso all waiting followers unblock *together* instead of draining\none-at-a-time through the lock.\n\nUnchanged / preserved:\n- **Leader path** still acquires the advisory lock and runs the real\n`upgrade`/`stamp`.\n- **Fresh DB** (`current is None`) still falls through to the\nstamp/upgrade path under the lock.\n- `head` is computed **once** (constant per process), so the per-poll\nfollower check is a single `alembic_version` SELECT — not a\nmigrations-dir re-walk each poll.\n\n## Test\n\n`tests/test_init_schema_at_head.py` — unit-tests the predicate (at-head\n→ True; pending → False; fresh/`None` → False) by stubbing\n`MigrationContext` (no DB). `ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\n## Residual (by design)\n\nThis removes the **serialization** overhead, not the **per-migration\nruntime floor**: a single migration that runs longer than the\nstartup-probe deadline still kills followers (they legitimately can't\nserve until the schema is ready). That case requires raising the\nstartup-probe deadline or moving migrations off the boot path (the known\nlonger-term direction) — out of scope here.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T08:51:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8a7ac3758347e04960e942dc81e907a425df7780/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf"}]},{"sha":"0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA3MzdiNmEzZDEzNGRkMDNmM2NmM2VhMzE2MDExZDllZWU0ZGMyY2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-24T07:41:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T07:41:03Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): crystallizer entity-coverage + audit-usage reads (Fix 2 final-cleanup PR3a) (#486)\n\n## What\n\nAdditive **storage-only** step toward deleting core-api's direct DB pool\n(rule `6440b9a6`). Adds two read endpoints on the memories router that\nwill replace `crystallizer_service`'s last two service-level direct-DB\nsites — the cutover + pool deletion land in **PR3b** after this deploys.\n\n- `GET /memories/entity-coverage` → `{memories_with_entities}` —\ndistinct memories with ≥1 entity link; ports `_compute_health`'s\ncross-table `COUNT(DISTINCT mel.memory_id)` verbatim, scoped by\n`tenant_id` (+ optional `fleet_id`). The caller divides by total\nmemories for the pct.\n- `GET /memories/audit-usage` → `{agent_activity, peak_hours}` — ports\n`_compute_usage`'s two `audit_log` queries verbatim.\n**`search_write_ratio` is intentionally dropped** — its `usage_counters`\ntable does not exist in the OSS schema (verified: only referenced in\n`crystallizer_service.py`, no model/migration).\n\nBoth reads use `get_read_session` (replica). No core-api changes in this\nPR.\n\n## Why split\n\nMirrors the PR1→PR2 rhythm: this additive storage PR deploys first so\nPR3b's core-api cutover never calls an endpoint that isn't live yet.\n\n## Gates (local, clean-DB)\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3688 passed**, 3 skipped, 1 xfailed, 3 xpassed (+9 new\ncrystallizer-storage tests)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"dd0957b9ea0dc72e7862090d5fe179c471242597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/dd0957b9ea0dc72e7862090d5fe179c471242597"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO4oPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQpkQAF8c525cA34r37gJTKUGGq7g\nByvQXWJfq7ilGqBdlh9lDLuf7qAR5lSsU628LVmOFVdvqdKbghgX0Y7w+JpNweWq\nieNMgj0QMADA0AGMzJGy3jcndAwcr1wIYWYuTvxbn2nEKCH9mzequKcEujC8gfJI\nsy0E6J2CSP9bs7KmuA2GSPHYAtkYWxfHCarO8M3LvOxK8AU9BizNkInh00ETZkmj\nKCDvwEGAmnINz8XZ5UxHC76Xfio9iC0UWqUA4SVKICov/JDfYD+IDbdd3R8ydZNN\n24IdkfBULJdKl28u8W5vx8xLEpdbaax+8IgmM3Gy+yDMT3+T7Fc/nP8w17OpDDCw\ndk9ESVtLE0XpiUKbeEE9tcb4yGuBhQOD7WGSPTA8jT58Ge2HCLT/17XCTZEqDQcI\nUsfiC2tuPinS5GIGKBszTgZuAmBmI2DWLvqHCrYs7VFd8+59wfRZFYHMce90gYhh\nKPqZpTL+sifjgqEiepmfJcTFSrZ4mu6iJ3uym/HWW3kPP8T+afvfoQCP9pOpCJGq\nbLWpe0ERQMzb0xRN1UA5JPF9OuTCnGmMtN7AMiwa62eq/9XT4fj0wpW4l6e1pU58\n3ZfOlofZyzXU5IOh09MorViTeKWIyzZGcTgfHmjPIY1PAF1y2FTdwPBsQe34ijOg\nScahzX+incT7ScQCMvU6\n=Dbcy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd0957b9ea0dc72e7862090d5fe179c471242597\nparent a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782286863 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782286863 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): crystallizer entity-coverage + audit-usage reads (Fix 2 final-cleanup PR3a) (#486)\n\n## What\n\nAdditive **storage-only** step toward deleting core-api's direct DB pool\n(rule `6440b9a6`). Adds two read endpoints on the memories router that\nwill replace `crystallizer_service`'s last two service-level direct-DB\nsites — the cutover + pool deletion land in **PR3b** after this deploys.\n\n- `GET /memories/entity-coverage` → `{memories_with_entities}` —\ndistinct memories with ≥1 entity link; ports `_compute_health`'s\ncross-table `COUNT(DISTINCT mel.memory_id)` verbatim, scoped by\n`tenant_id` (+ optional `fleet_id`). The caller divides by total\nmemories for the pct.\n- `GET /memories/audit-usage` → `{agent_activity, peak_hours}` — ports\n`_compute_usage`'s two `audit_log` queries verbatim.\n**`search_write_ratio` is intentionally dropped** — its `usage_counters`\ntable does not exist in the OSS schema (verified: only referenced in\n`crystallizer_service.py`, no model/migration).\n\nBoth reads use `get_read_session` (replica). No core-api changes in this\nPR.\n\n## Why split\n\nMirrors the PR1→PR2 rhythm: this additive storage PR deploys first so\nPR3b's core-api cutover never calls an endpoint that isn't live yet.\n\n## Gates (local, clean-DB)\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3688 passed**, 3 skipped, 1 xfailed, 3 xpassed (+9 new\ncrystallizer-storage tests)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T07:41:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0737b6a3d134dd03f3cf3ea316011d9eee4dc2cf/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081"}]},{"sha":"a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGEyYTc2NGU4M2Y2ZjQyZDViZjgxMjJhZGViZWNiODYyMjcxNzAwODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T20:37:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:37:02Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): install-skill ?skill= selector + company-brain import path (#483)\n\n**PR-2** of the skills refresh (stacked on #482). Makes the new\n`company-brain` posture skill installable via the same one-liner as\n`memclaw`, plus docs.\n\n> Base is `claude/skills-canonical-refresh` (#482) — it adds\n`static/skills/company-brain/SKILL.md`, which this PR serves. Retarget\nto `main` once #482 merges.\n\n## Endpoint (`routes/plugin.py`)\n- `GET /install-skill` gains a **`skill`** query param (default\n`memclaw`), **allowlisted** to `{memclaw, company-brain}` → invalid\nvalue returns 400, so the value never reaches a filesystem path or the\ngenerated script.\n- The script generator threads the skill name through install dirs\n(`~/.claude/skills/<skill>`, `~/.agents/skills/<skill>`), the fetch URL\n(`/api/v1/skill/<skill>`), and the title. **For `skill=memclaw` the\noutput is byte-for-byte the original.**\n- New `GET /skill/{skill}` serving route (allowlisted) serves\n`static/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`; the explicit `/skill/memclaw` route is\nkept and matches first, so the default resolves through the unchanged\nhandler.\n\n## Default-unaffected guarantee (your hard requirement)\nNo `?skill=` ⇒ identical to today. Pinned by the pre-existing memclaw\ntests **plus** a new `test_default_skill_is_memclaw_and_unchanged`\n(title + memclaw paths + `/skill/memclaw` URL + **absence** of any\n`company-brain` string).\n\n## Docs (`README.md`)\n\"Install the skill\" → new **Optional: the Company Brain skill**\nsubsection + one-liner (`curl -s \".../install-skill?skill=company-brain\"\n| bash`), a `?skill=` Options row, and the endpoints reference updated.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py` +6 (default-unchanged guard;\ncompany-brain paths/url/title; invalid-skill 400; allowlist rejects\ntraversal-looking value; `/skill/company-brain` serves; unknown → 404).\n**16 pass; ruff check + format clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef650981af19cd20407c67a281bc41149ae092f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ef650981af19cd20407c67a281bc41149ae092f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOu5uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe3AQAABCcU8OIoX7hYJrH/2Zfktr\n1w4buNx47o87dBaW3hk4hj+kky/MY6YYseHPW6ZiwuQp++PQEVpoh3QIz4wcvEHx\nEygkxssyW/QYXUo26NcgM3ZSlFjoH9ifyXxpnNd3pjVQsIaNzmhWk57u7z1SxqeB\nDKcRDNPvR90GpJj0AtZ2GDUh5ab8k3KNB3jpp7noT0N0ffh3XSTUXzp4Hyh+t0fP\nSyg633szbXtF0CE0ExSfQXQeGrI811jV/aPtnqrYi/bbGu7oRSIElyaZBs4vV0Gv\nh249Vo6psL1b7uB0fy3VQIUPmNbibFoTjDhsEQrK3o+zlbvD/z5/d3Fojp4rGetn\nsdrbHooc6Fx5v50hlW0jiTbSg6xGSsWJZ4CwsoapQhx1Ie2LnYHh2biIJEccyR/2\nlxGbl61v3hiH8E2kBZUvM9dPyArDf9nlZIVyfvHM6Fcc3KKekJH/lszcpnyaydK8\nigQR96/xIavX9q5RWM5DHFBQlMRyqBvNPfae1ocqhDBNmylgkmbyeG+7zUI+n9/b\nLcKNPEGQyIVPZaZIoDVGF8MERG699opRtkiSnPfZU4KRdYcjrBeAHF8+X/sGrRay\n8BF2Ti7C6Pj0AL2oXHJMTsmlqOdvSG0kyP27iaB5TWbhPjkp5ExUCMQUT1GNIJod\ncuZjjrp6ALFnJ9ZGEiQi\n=lY4J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ef650981af19cd20407c67a281bc41149ae092f2\nparent 592b231d395ff8787c9ad82c91a4b5262432b95d\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782247022 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782247022 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): install-skill ?skill= selector + company-brain import path (#483)\n\n**PR-2** of the skills refresh (stacked on #482). Makes the new\n`company-brain` posture skill installable via the same one-liner as\n`memclaw`, plus docs.\n\n> Base is `claude/skills-canonical-refresh` (#482) — it adds\n`static/skills/company-brain/SKILL.md`, which this PR serves. Retarget\nto `main` once #482 merges.\n\n## Endpoint (`routes/plugin.py`)\n- `GET /install-skill` gains a **`skill`** query param (default\n`memclaw`), **allowlisted** to `{memclaw, company-brain}` → invalid\nvalue returns 400, so the value never reaches a filesystem path or the\ngenerated script.\n- The script generator threads the skill name through install dirs\n(`~/.claude/skills/<skill>`, `~/.agents/skills/<skill>`), the fetch URL\n(`/api/v1/skill/<skill>`), and the title. **For `skill=memclaw` the\noutput is byte-for-byte the original.**\n- New `GET /skill/{skill}` serving route (allowlisted) serves\n`static/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`; the explicit `/skill/memclaw` route is\nkept and matches first, so the default resolves through the unchanged\nhandler.\n\n## Default-unaffected guarantee (your hard requirement)\nNo `?skill=` ⇒ identical to today. Pinned by the pre-existing memclaw\ntests **plus** a new `test_default_skill_is_memclaw_and_unchanged`\n(title + memclaw paths + `/skill/memclaw` URL + **absence** of any\n`company-brain` string).\n\n## Docs (`README.md`)\n\"Install the skill\" → new **Optional: the Company Brain skill**\nsubsection + one-liner (`curl -s \".../install-skill?skill=company-brain\"\n| bash`), a `?skill=` Options row, and the endpoints reference updated.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py` +6 (default-unchanged guard;\ncompany-brain paths/url/title; invalid-skill 400; allowlist rejects\ntraversal-looking value; `/skill/company-brain` serves; unknown → 404).\n**16 pass; ruff check + format clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:37:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a2a764e83f6f42d5bf8122adebecb86227170081/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://githu