-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410"}]},{"sha":"d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQ4YjE4ZDA4OTNiYTJlMzQwMDYzMGQ5ZGVkMzI4Yjg3NTg5YzI0MTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T19:11:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:11:04Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): recall/capability/ingest endpoints for Fix-2 final cleanup (PR1) (#484)\n\n## Fix-2 final cleanup — PR1 of 3 (storage endpoints, additive)\n\nStorage-side groundwork for the last Fix-2 phase: deleting core-api's\ndirect DB pool (rule `6440b9a6`). Adds 4 endpoints + `PostgresService`\nmethods so the remaining core-api direct-DB sites can route through HTTP\nin PR2/PR3. **Storage-only — no core-api files touched, nothing\ndeleted.**\n\n### Endpoints (all under `/api/v1/storage`)\n- `POST /memories/increment-recall` — exposes the existing\n`memory_increment_recall` (by-id `recall_count` bump; the\n`track_recalls` hook target).\n- `POST /memories/recall-log` — `recall_event` + N `recall_candidate`\nrows in one txn (the recall-logging writer that currently bypasses\nstorage — that **rule regression is fixed in PR2**).\n- `POST /capability-usage` — cross-tenant / RLS-free adoption-counter\nbulk insert (`capability_usage`, migration 023).\n- `POST /memories/prior-ingest-by-doc-hash` — doc-hash idempotency\nlookup, SQL ported verbatim from `ingest_service` (writer session —\nreplica lag would re-ingest).\n\nEach endpoint validates its own contract and fails closed (422). The\ndoc-hash and recall SQL is ported faithfully from the current core-api\nimplementations.\n\n### Also\nRegisters `recall_log` + `capability_usage` models in\n`conftest._import_all_models` — the recall-logging feature added the\nmodels but not their registration, so `create_all` wasn't building\n`recall_event`/`recall_candidate` in the test schema.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3664 passed** on a clean (TRUNCATE'd) DB; +22 new tests\nin `test_fix2_cleanup_storage.py` (happy-path DB-effect assertions +\nfail-closed 422 cases for each endpoint)\n\n### Plan\nPR1 (this) deploys first. **PR2** rewires the 3 recall/capability\ncore-api sites through these endpoints (fixes the live `6440b9a6`\nregression). **PR3** migrates the REST/ingest sites, drops the\ncrystallizer enrichments, strips dead `get_db` params, and deletes\n`repositories/*` + `db/session.py`'s engine/pool + the `postgres_*`\nconfig.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"c36068e87c745fe22638bf371092538375effe4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c36068e87c745fe22638bf371092538375effe4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOtpICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnFEQAJpRX0SDKDrr8sWGh9+cKCQ7\nykuerXVssNjO4C5mFiS9XaXqSmxN7uSkQO3FPglwmiY6RbSbscpuJJjKs8qpkKP+\nQ+M7psql2QiR4izkV0w0bUoNC4eoe8MlOvvnloYJqWJW18hrxkvSAZ0BgCitPnNH\nrdpkeHbqveymMHsX8z0stwr88QkL/mkgif8Kq4MbnMg+aIxV5CfB/4kvtwWnNOhG\nwzAgsPrKfoo0F4MwJJvjd74OHhh1njLZ9XFrrc0fRru1fpSCNaXH9MM8gOaJu7I9\n19jwXuR49GjxHUttE4/cJqpf+sJjzRN2Fp9MQs1wrT4G+8taB5eKc0UTGUgAyjJf\n2NPVGAPqSwZUzxWPm2ZxJP+EV1Kxe71rMsqORszs4bOdduDhzSgGyhmNOZjtOy58\n64Hvq+wNEN+dxs6LebzKX2tHxoqvuxXn7vRyzqNVcPZ8C1Ft43Ygbe2l83VFVwJ3\nJ6MsqThAsSWuaLysqc7whRnI7qlE2muq3QEC0uFC3EIyMMHEYY0Q8wQ3yrrBnyfq\nBeXhw56/l7udd+L3FwI7KR24/MuXG45oVrsC/RhpKRJ2tgjxGOKAyHZQYmco5NJk\nQFF5FnFC6UgyW+GSL9WQAY+Y93Q1049XApBYfneZnXdCP8YKbmBDLZBmv6tE4ieR\np/ka9mllyu5y22PIALr1\n=9RMI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c36068e87c745fe22638bf371092538375effe4b\nparent aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782241864 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782241864 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): recall/capability/ingest endpoints for Fix-2 final cleanup (PR1) (#484)\n\n## Fix-2 final cleanup — PR1 of 3 (storage endpoints, additive)\n\nStorage-side groundwork for the last Fix-2 phase: deleting core-api's\ndirect DB pool (rule `6440b9a6`). Adds 4 endpoints + `PostgresService`\nmethods so the remaining core-api direct-DB sites can route through HTTP\nin PR2/PR3. **Storage-only — no core-api files touched, nothing\ndeleted.**\n\n### Endpoints (all under `/api/v1/storage`)\n- `POST /memories/increment-recall` — exposes the existing\n`memory_increment_recall` (by-id `recall_count` bump; the\n`track_recalls` hook target).\n- `POST /memories/recall-log` — `recall_event` + N `recall_candidate`\nrows in one txn (the recall-logging writer that currently bypasses\nstorage — that **rule regression is fixed in PR2**).\n- `POST /capability-usage` — cross-tenant / RLS-free adoption-counter\nbulk insert (`capability_usage`, migration 023).\n- `POST /memories/prior-ingest-by-doc-hash` — doc-hash idempotency\nlookup, SQL ported verbatim from `ingest_service` (writer session —\nreplica lag would re-ingest).\n\nEach endpoint validates its own contract and fails closed (422). The\ndoc-hash and recall SQL is ported faithfully from the current core-api\nimplementations.\n\n### Also\nRegisters `recall_log` + `capability_usage` models in\n`conftest._import_all_models` — the recall-logging feature added the\nmodels but not their registration, so `create_all` wasn't building\n`recall_event`/`recall_candidate` in the test schema.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3664 passed** on a clean (TRUNCATE'd) DB; +22 new tests\nin `test_fix2_cleanup_storage.py` (happy-path DB-effect assertions +\nfail-closed 422 cases for each endpoint)\n\n### Plan\nPR1 (this) deploys first. **PR2** rewires the 3 recall/capability\ncore-api sites through these endpoints (fixes the live `6440b9a6`\nregression). **PR3** migrates the REST/ingest sites, drops the\ncrystallizer enrichments, strips dead `get_db` params, and deletes\n`repositories/*` + `db/session.py`'s engine/pool + the `postgres_*`\nconfig.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:11:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d8b18d0893ba2e3400630d9ded328b87589c2410/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd"}]},{"sha":"aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGFhMDNjMDNjNDdhYWVlZjRkYTMzOTBkMmI4MTBhZTNiNDYwNDViZmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T17:48:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:48:57Z"},"message":"feat(skills): refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add company-brain (#482)\n\nLands the reviewed, optimized skill texts and re-pins the structural\ninvariant tests to the approved design. Skill-content only + their tests\n— no runtime/endpoint changes.\n\n## Skills\n\n- **`static/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md`** (direct-MCP canonical) —\nrewritten: stronger \"THE long-term memory\" framing; **`fleet_id`**\ncorrected to home-fleet-resolve-on-omit (post-#465) + the\nno-home-fleet/cross-fleet residual; precise enrichment timing (type+PII\n**inline**, entities+contradiction **async**); `evolve` failure →\n**private rule by default**; loop spine (orient most-binding-first →\nwrite → evolve), dedicated **\"How and when to write a memory\"**, **trust\nself-awareness**, **cross-store pointer-memory**. Per-tool signature\ncards dropped → lean **\"Behaviors the schema won't tell you\"**\n(signatures already live in the always-in-context MCP schemas). Host\nnormalised to **`memclaw.net`** (retires stale `.dev`).\n- **`plugin/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md`** (OpenClaw variant) — same spine +\nfixes, OpenClaw layers kept (`<keystone_rules>` auto-injection,\nMEMORY.md vs workspace files, L1/L2/L3, orchestrator/subagent, recall\nauto-gating, TOOLS.md). Preface now makes the **automatic baseline\nexplicit** (auto-recall, keystone inject, `MEMCLAW_AUTO_WRITE_TURNS`\nturn-summary) **and** that the agent must still use the tools\ndeliberately. `keystones_set` stays withheld (`plugin_exposed=false`);\n`memclaw_stats` documented.\n- **`static/skills/company-brain/SKILL.md`** (NEW) — concept-first\nposture skill layering on `memclaw`, deferring all mechanics to it.\n\n## Tests re-pinned (approved structural change)\n\nThe redesign deliberately changed section names, **dropped signature\ncards** (schema-deferral), softened MUST-walls, and renamed Prohibitions\n→ Anti-patterns. The invariant tests are updated to assert the **new**\nstructure while keeping every meaningful guarantee (frontmatter,\nno-openclaw/no-TOOLS.md in static, install paths, error codes, all tool\n*names*, cross-store, etc.), plus a regression guard that signature\ncards are **not** reintroduced.\n\n- `tests/test_direct_mcp_skill.py`\n- `plugin/src/educate.test.ts`\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.test.ts`\n\n**Validation:** 351 plugin tests pass; 10 direct-MCP-adapter invariants\npass.\n\n## Follow-up (PR-2, intentionally split)\n`company-brain` install path — an `?skill=` selector on\n`/api/v1/install-skill` (allowlist `{memclaw, company-brain}`, default\n`memclaw`) + endpoint tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d788fd6dbfd9627e183d61071fa46c024fb87692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d788fd6dbfd9627e183d61071fa46c024fb87692"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOscJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWvsQAJgHojSLa8SNrFGY8M7MdgtB\nkWlI6D8wfnGxkg5QtAkV+BgwN0r955FLuNehME2wn0LnTGwy+NGcRxeoGy5WuICl\nQ/5VC/wT1nTVHSniCkgd0CQcsT+j22GrH22KmNw/bhYr1X95mtq0u5hR2I8j4+eC\nGt5UpvROhBhv7sLQmaJjAgPUst2QPvjErjVUOAue5olR/FKQwNRjuGPcmZ+TDT3v\nFvkAfOhAgXC435fgNFjvRn9hUA41/E2YGJRvsEygFnbHZfXPQ3TnKJuuBTSH4ttm\nO6TJPog3hnQQ82WNX/Y1Ux57nm+RWtEngdST5NpRIRwnCt6zTufmKD0OCAb/fAOo\nuGsqrazwFFkjU9TXwZKyLlI0F6adeKkwflFbAYKZ/8pBpBgYe/Q6Uv5/e5Ijy7Se\noWBBiDp9lu8BQgkKGp4XtXpnsrP6w7dT5+nonO+FGK1lJ076TsIwh4cXbcL9THvY\niCUAxmHCFJch0oew/zs5eA6D8Lqu989AnB1l0lPCtOTba3n1JnPEd61AgEEbIvbT\nocjHePfHZZGNXCA1L/vNp+PD5Qi/7oSnGTceU1AoQszzsaiL4cvHsb+x1wWTcfu1\nzVMAhmJ/8w1gWlGnqbfchl3zipUQra91zKvMbzxnfNd9zl14BRe17WBFmXy7ra2X\nTvLQ0AG9+Etyw7gVycS6\n=JvEY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d788fd6dbfd9627e183d61071fa46c024fb87692\nparent 6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782236937 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782236937 +0300\n\nfeat(skills): refresh canonical + plugin memclaw skills, add company-brain (#482)\n\nLands the reviewed, optimized skill texts and re-pins the structural\ninvariant tests to the approved design. Skill-content only + their tests\n— no runtime/endpoint changes.\n\n## Skills\n\n- **`static/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md`** (direct-MCP canonical) —\nrewritten: stronger \"THE long-term memory\" framing; **`fleet_id`**\ncorrected to home-fleet-resolve-on-omit (post-#465) + the\nno-home-fleet/cross-fleet residual; precise enrichment timing (type+PII\n**inline**, entities+contradiction **async**); `evolve` failure →\n**private rule by default**; loop spine (orient most-binding-first →\nwrite → evolve), dedicated **\"How and when to write a memory\"**, **trust\nself-awareness**, **cross-store pointer-memory**. Per-tool signature\ncards dropped → lean **\"Behaviors the schema won't tell you\"**\n(signatures already live in the always-in-context MCP schemas). Host\nnormalised to **`memclaw.net`** (retires stale `.dev`).\n- **`plugin/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md`** (OpenClaw variant) — same spine +\nfixes, OpenClaw layers kept (`<keystone_rules>` auto-injection,\nMEMORY.md vs workspace files, L1/L2/L3, orchestrator/subagent, recall\nauto-gating, TOOLS.md). Preface now makes the **automatic baseline\nexplicit** (auto-recall, keystone inject, `MEMCLAW_AUTO_WRITE_TURNS`\nturn-summary) **and** that the agent must still use the tools\ndeliberately. `keystones_set` stays withheld (`plugin_exposed=false`);\n`memclaw_stats` documented.\n- **`static/skills/company-brain/SKILL.md`** (NEW) — concept-first\nposture skill layering on `memclaw`, deferring all mechanics to it.\n\n## Tests re-pinned (approved structural change)\n\nThe redesign deliberately changed section names, **dropped signature\ncards** (schema-deferral), softened MUST-walls, and renamed Prohibitions\n→ Anti-patterns. The invariant tests are updated to assert the **new**\nstructure while keeping every meaningful guarantee (frontmatter,\nno-openclaw/no-TOOLS.md in static, install paths, error codes, all tool\n*names*, cross-store, etc.), plus a regression guard that signature\ncards are **not** reintroduced.\n\n- `tests/test_direct_mcp_skill.py`\n- `plugin/src/educate.test.ts`\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.test.ts`\n\n**Validation:** 351 plugin tests pass; 10 direct-MCP-adapter invariants\npass.\n\n## Follow-up (PR-2, intentionally split)\n`company-brain` install path — an `?skill=` selector on\n`/api/v1/install-skill` (allowlist `{memclaw, company-brain}`, default\n`memclaw`) + endpoint tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T17:48:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa03c03c47aaeef4da3390d2b810ae3b46045bfd/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0"}]},{"sha":"6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY5MzhmMDhmZDUyZGQ5YTljOWVmZGIzZmJhNDJmN2IyMGM0YjY1ZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T14:05:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T14:05:41Z"},"message":"docs(core-api): clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not rejected (#481)\n\n## Why\nValidated follow-up **B6**. `memclaw_recall`'s `top_k` Field advertises\n`\"1-20.\"` but has **no `le=` validator** — values above 20 are silently\nclamped (`min(top_k, MAX_SEARCH_TOP_K=20)`, `mcp_server.py:608`), not\nrejected. The declared contract didn't match enforcement.\n\n## Change (doc-only)\n- `memclaw_recall` `top_k` description → `\"Max results, default 5.\nValues above 20 are capped to 20.\"` — states the actual soft-cap\nbehavior.\n- Updated the recall `top_k` entry in\n`tests/fixtures/tools_list_baseline_v1.json` so\n`test_v1_baseline_matches_live_registry` stays green (`memclaw_tune`'s\nidentical `\"1-20.\"` is a separate param, left as-is).\n\n**Chosen over** adding `le=20`, which would convert today's safe\nsoft-cap into a `422` for callers sending e.g. `top_k=30` — a behavior\nchange. No validation/behavior change here.\n\n## Validation\n`tests/test_mcp_token_budget.py` (live==baseline match + token ceiling)\nand `tests/test_tool_descriptions_regression.py` — 7/7 pass. `ruff check\ncore-api/src/` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26063a04a877020fb5a9fd87573e745fb080139a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/26063a04a877020fb5a9fd87573e745fb080139a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOpK1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlrcQAI49F/TI0dx4NXgabYOlSFEh\n9fNMzat9bFD8Q2H2LgoK7uckD7pZ0bq7k/QIozV/Rr2KOYM+SodK3D/aft6e8+Nj\nMtsTFj1xeRlt98vLFN66WMnbdy7h5Kl4H1AUcPnJD/xifI3Lpl39SYdzegycPTD0\nF8/88lj4pSQke7gj/hq1JEzhfqUngpYRGXt8u3WV46aexcLCmQepNxqI3CVjNYay\ndWl1YqjZRXF642evMR0fnzKw66SL3VJNT8g02/18LTgR/meENrLlnXJPiUwb4slE\nJ6A04sP6EuZstTdMRWcrptJQVrWvaDVqs3GxavE7eHPWdmYOAKd8L4bNY0SuiTCO\ngfCXjjHwBzevhu+wXw3nXcdq/EIIGVK6GVj4SGZkrT1EMi32pVyFqwEbu1ojNBXs\n4XvYP06RvkNZlenvqELNj0N20i0nLmMl7yAQ5I2FTgD7bB9HdD6+xBr3Z40/LcXY\nR3k7qbVLxvJ4/C8skxEg8R9BLJYsxR159HScKLWruTm6jx3IHQnZHheLF6j3wSuY\n1jQuwX94Hn1VpTRB1/nIbEeiEt7vR5ldQoOnnlHVuiwelMDpT1J9A/lGTd7Zu1O+\nsK7w+xoHJictNwZuYVNg6vJPZNWeivA+d2mXSyKxLM+Fdlf8Lb4RLiEJmv5bFhZH\nEwVW1EpOi5FGfCyYrxOs\n=AUCd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 26063a04a877020fb5a9fd87573e745fb080139a\nparent 62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782223541 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782223541 +0300\n\ndocs(core-api): clarify memclaw_recall top_k is soft-capped, not rejected (#481)\n\n## Why\nValidated follow-up **B6**. `memclaw_recall`'s `top_k` Field advertises\n`\"1-20.\"` but has **no `le=` validator** — values above 20 are silently\nclamped (`min(top_k, MAX_SEARCH_TOP_K=20)`, `mcp_server.py:608`), not\nrejected. The declared contract didn't match enforcement.\n\n## Change (doc-only)\n- `memclaw_recall` `top_k` description → `\"Max results, default 5.\nValues above 20 are capped to 20.\"` — states the actual soft-cap\nbehavior.\n- Updated the recall `top_k` entry in\n`tests/fixtures/tools_list_baseline_v1.json` so\n`test_v1_baseline_matches_live_registry` stays green (`memclaw_tune`'s\nidentical `\"1-20.\"` is a separate param, left as-is).\n\n**Chosen over** adding `le=20`, which would convert today's safe\nsoft-cap into a `422` for callers sending e.g. `top_k=30` — a behavior\nchange. No validation/behavior change here.\n\n## Validation\n`tests/test_mcp_token_budget.py` (live==baseline match + token ceiling)\nand `tests/test_tool_descriptions_regression.py` — 7/7 pass. `ruff check\ncore-api/src/` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T14:05:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6938f08fd52dd9a9c9efdb3fba42f7b20c4b65d0/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270"}]},{"sha":"62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDYyNjg3MjUzMDAwYTFmMGZiYjM3MjA2YzlmNTM4YWE3ZjNiZGMyNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T12:39:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T12:39:33Z"},"message":"fix(core-storage-api): 422 on missing/non-list embedding in /entities/set-embeddings (#478)\n\n## Fail-closed validation for `/entities/set-embeddings`\n\nSurfaced by the #477 (Fix 2 Ph6) round-2 review. The `set-embeddings`\nendpoint validated only each update's `id` (UUID format), not\n`embedding`. A request with a valid `id` but a **missing or non-list\n`embedding`** passed the 422 guard, then hit `u[\"embedding\"]` in\n`entity_set_embeddings` (`KeyError`) or bound a non-vector value to the\npgvector column — surfacing as a **500 instead of a clean 422**.\n\nFix: extend the existing per-item validation loop to require a list\n`embedding`, failing closed consistently with the surrounding guards\n(`tenant_id`, `updates`-is-list, `id`-is-UUID).\n\nReal-world impact is low — the typed client / backfill step always sends\n`{\"id\", \"embedding\"}` with a list — so this only hardens direct storage\ncallers, in keeping with the \"each endpoint validates its own contract\"\nstance from Ph5b/Ph6.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3635 passed** (clean DB); +2 new 422 tests\n(`test_set_embeddings_missing_embedding_422`,\n`test_set_embeddings_non_list_embedding_422`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"5969f3ddb10393b3b674520b62aed17a59156d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5969f3ddb10393b3b674520b62aed17a59156d0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOn6FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaYQQACxQUYkPFf9FoXX+WZtgGG2y\njjcuaCoa4XW4d3BdN/l4MsL2v/dOGkc80ureL1ZLpi5VaIu+PYt+WZhLCXAeVaa+\nagJCSoq+0eGkVvEzQA2n4iCMSNVhEebwZL6qvyFNSVA7inAu68OBo/XO/a2XrSiW\nen5ipLAnHIVFXhY8n183buiYAuMbdhdtPMBhEnYaVvX8WqLDWESCa6xwMFX65IcL\n7gNK2IWznybYOup/mTGUG2QCeHc1db13EDd3MiqBrc2u/PWHxP9avSUmFwfqrLJw\nFLVyFgIPeH92esc/IMVo06vCS1MQRIz76jPU7stjINlFZzlmESrnZH2tpjOMfvdD\nNH/DecNNcOdpge9rqYBAYRwgsDnl0h033vYTw0pziscVGcKWWw67pDC3ScIxea39\nAqlCxbcywVOJd9J3zZ2jkXC/zvXoHntMb2bnEsoxW5YyMaExNvoDfOGvdyKD3sPp\n8rt5ushR80+ERG1wGmrYEL1P5CxkosWPE2W0fl1m2DX9pIPimbSQG/gdLtuSSbgV\nnhbkI7CYEEr4nnaojLFackUWRKH8gLwE+xSIk4QUrvJBX66hJmUwUFkgY0HupEQO\nVWT54IROewUt2nojTIBI7+RUcjPYufws7huz/TMr2l7DnO9mK/7w3uL3ORL1ReKa\n6cH+GMduQm5ql9lSCn94\n=GeDU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5969f3ddb10393b3b674520b62aed17a59156d0d\nparent 953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782218373 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782218373 +0300\n\nfix(core-storage-api): 422 on missing/non-list embedding in /entities/set-embeddings (#478)\n\n## Fail-closed validation for `/entities/set-embeddings`\n\nSurfaced by the #477 (Fix 2 Ph6) round-2 review. The `set-embeddings`\nendpoint validated only each update's `id` (UUID format), not\n`embedding`. A request with a valid `id` but a **missing or non-list\n`embedding`** passed the 422 guard, then hit `u[\"embedding\"]` in\n`entity_set_embeddings` (`KeyError`) or bound a non-vector value to the\npgvector column — surfacing as a **500 instead of a clean 422**.\n\nFix: extend the existing per-item validation loop to require a list\n`embedding`, failing closed consistently with the surrounding guards\n(`tenant_id`, `updates`-is-list, `id`-is-UUID).\n\nReal-world impact is low — the typed client / backfill step always sends\n`{\"id\", \"embedding\"}` with a list — so this only hardens direct storage\ncallers, in keeping with the \"each endpoint validates its own contract\"\nstance from Ph5b/Ph6.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3635 passed** (clean DB); +2 new 422 tests\n(`test_set_embeddings_missing_embedding_422`,\n`test_set_embeddings_non_list_embedding_422`)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T12:39:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62687253000a1f0fbb37206c9f538aa7f3bdc270/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389"}]},{"sha":"953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDk1M2VjMzM2YzA1MmY4OGE5ZjYzMDM5NGM2ZGZhYzBlNjhkMGQzODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-23T11:58:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T11:58:46Z"},"message":"feat(recall): opt-in logging of agent-chosen recalls (#480)\n\n## What\n\nOpt-in, per-tenant logging of **agent-chosen recalls**\n(`memclaw_recall`) to two new tables, so we can finally answer **\"why\naren't good memories recalled?\"** — separating *no-demand* from\n*below-floor near-miss* from *outranked*. Today this is unanswerable:\nthere is no per-recall event log (`recall_count` is a bare counter).\n\n## How\n\n- **Migration 027** — `recall_event` (query + scope + strategy +\nresult_count) and `recall_candidate` (one row per memory considered:\nrank, `memory_id` **pointer**, raw `vec_sim` cosine, `final_score`,\n`recall_boost`, `returned`). Candidates store only `memory_id`; content\nis JOINed from `memories` on demand.\n- **`LogRecallEvent`** pipeline step logs the returned top-k **plus a\nfew near-misses below the similarity floor** — the signal that\ndistinguishes \"just missed the cutoff\" from \"never close.\"\n- **Gated two ways**, both cheap and evaluated before any DB work:\n1. `source == \"mcp_recall\"` — the plugin's automatic `/search` firehose\nis **never** logged.\n2. `observability.recall_logging_enabled` org setting (**default off**)\n— opt-in per tenant.\n- Writes run **fire-and-forget** in a background task like\n`TrackRecalls` — zero added request latency; failures are swallowed so\nlogging can never break a recall.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 3 unit tests (gating + candidate construction).\n- **Wet-tested end-to-end** on a full local stack: 1 / 100 / 1000 real\n`memclaw_recall` calls → 1104 events logged exactly, 0 errors;\nnear-misses + cosine scores + empty-result events all captured; a REST\n`/search` produced **zero** events (tool-only gating confirmed); ~1000\ncalls in 25s with no latency impact.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No behavior change to recall ranking/scoring — logging only.\n- Tenant isolation is app-level (consistent with the rest of the\nschema); `recall_event` carries `tenant_id`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"57523b01a6b4e1b99c59c5ae5fdc52d9852f89d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/57523b01a6b4e1b99c59c5ae5fdc52d9852f89d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOnT2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF8UQAFF7lInBuWiT3NGLgIEpJYAP\nruFgqY0h2p3pT7Q5vcztZ2W5MQBkWpbSm20B6N9Fgc4FngGCEFVG5tTazPUdHJMB\nRUCjK8FsQbnt4LNsTEYcMvr46Sc3e2WprspeID4bpIXxxfgvyaPp8sWEt09AG6YA\nqLdYUQ6ouNfvx412NorXVi1+MxndtW1DEbcABfaR32VzSRfaMvRzXLGIgIf4clDj\nuGoA6tS/h9BgVum4FsQzlTN38RPG9Oj2tSwY1uU3wMuy3wwpHRIbezF66oGsVceq\nvAlEbfWLcLlc+zMQCO2mS6XbKNjjm3hRwQjHu2RXgk/h49RK7JOVQIjlvQ5aRgjh\n+YHjhDQdZdpyckLbUQpJ5brgR0SIr4g3BCt+Zcve9KUBmO3Mgr3I2GhBhWXrJxyg\nxrnNavPRevDNiVOSoe3thVvGg/1u4/WNL1Bq2089MhXz+YksuUuKuVXoNLr8bwwX\nqyO2ijq49X6BKkr/zj9nxE/Vu+hpu7Hg2e6A74xBwUnj+19wGPrxyQnP7ZDMOUnj\n7YyJYjPj8c7mchqUDJdFJvIpx1MNVo9hci1uKgBdN5dVlbVf6bZdZBC3ye5hnr8V\nVstc+QiMAqqqDzPpeUb5w7FfvmrgWeMMRIx6NzAlYF95LRdQYnZE/mTLmd+uQ/25\n3xDlaBa/tMSoGTPre6KL\n=dUuZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57523b01a6b4e1b99c59c5ae5fdc52d9852f89d6\nparent e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1782215926 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782215926 +0300\n\nfeat(recall): opt-in logging of agent-chosen recalls (#480)\n\n## What\n\nOpt-in, per-tenant logging of **agent-chosen recalls**\n(`memclaw_recall`) to two new tables, so we can finally answer **\"why\naren't good memories recalled?\"** — separating *no-demand* from\n*below-floor near-miss* from *outranked*. Today this is unanswerable:\nthere is no per-recall event log (`recall_count` is a bare counter).\n\n## How\n\n- **Migration 027** — `recall_event` (query + scope + strategy +\nresult_count) and `recall_candidate` (one row per memory considered:\nrank, `memory_id` **pointer**, raw `vec_sim` cosine, `final_score`,\n`recall_boost`, `returned`). Candidates store only `memory_id`; content\nis JOINed from `memories` on demand.\n- **`LogRecallEvent`** pipeline step logs the returned top-k **plus a\nfew near-misses below the similarity floor** — the signal that\ndistinguishes \"just missed the cutoff\" from \"never close.\"\n- **Gated two ways**, both cheap and evaluated before any DB work:\n1. `source == \"mcp_recall\"` — the plugin's automatic `/search` firehose\nis **never** logged.\n2. `observability.recall_logging_enabled` org setting (**default off**)\n— opt-in per tenant.\n- Writes run **fire-and-forget** in a background task like\n`TrackRecalls` — zero added request latency; failures are swallowed so\nlogging can never break a recall.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 3 unit tests (gating + candidate construction).\n- **Wet-tested end-to-end** on a full local stack: 1 / 100 / 1000 real\n`memclaw_recall` calls → 1104 events logged exactly, 0 errors;\nnear-misses + cosine scores + empty-result events all captured; a REST\n`/search` produced **zero** events (tool-only gating confirmed); ~1000\ncalls in 25s with no latency impact.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No behavior change to recall ranking/scoring — logging only.\n- Tenant isolation is app-level (consistent with the rest of the\nschema); `recall_event` carries `tenant_id`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T11:58:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/953ec336c052f88a9f630394c6dfac0e68d0d389/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f"}]},{"sha":"e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU5ZGQ5Y2FhMThjMjkxNjMwZjdmMmQzOWFmOWE2Y2RkYzU0NjA4OGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T11:22:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T11:22:09Z"},"message":"refactor(core-storage-api): consolidate router validation guards into _validation (#479)\n\n## Consolidate the duplicated router validation guards\n\nThe fail-closed `_require(body, key)` guard was **byte-identical across\nfour routers** (`evolve`, `skill_factory`, `insights`, `entities`), and\n`entities` had added `_require_number` while `evolve` still hand-rolled\nthe same numeric check inline. This extracts both into\n`core_storage_api/routers/_validation.py` and imports them across the\nfour routers, replacing evolve's inline `isinstance(..., (int, float))`\nloop with `_require_number`.\n\nSurfaced during the Fix 2 Ph6 (#477) `/simplify` review (the duplication\nwas flagged as out-of-scope for that PR and spun off here).\n\n**Pure refactor** — no change to the happy path or the 422 detail\nmessages. One intentional tightening: evolve's `delta`/`floor`/`cap` now\ngo through `_require_number`, which rejects `bool` (a subclass of `int`\nthat was never a valid tuning value); the 422 message is unchanged.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-api + core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3633 passed** (clean DB), unchanged\n(behavior-preserving; existing evolve/entities numeric-422 tests\nexercise the shared guards)\n- Net −6 lines across the routers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"7186578e6edccfc16d4720c746beea46e0dec6a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7186578e6edccfc16d4720c746beea46e0dec6a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOmxhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHy8QADJQTCXU00NGZPrzCYcfy1fv\nbz8OKfundkCReFfF6qzpVUmjRzRFn1vbAni0k2MHtcJpeKBoEA5dkkpLngKrYxc3\n/RI51T81OaibxT29oSHjZ6iq4BkG0kiZ43T5MHP3rCw20KDjwBeHwy3aVf7EWFPF\nWgIcu8uIZvtaDPwYbZG6LZ1BRAfLRv/jTufG91SA50hsGWJR2IE9W17UNcTHYlaY\nVPB73akMqJ/28a33Dl+DRNhKQ9qvX+mNQ4Ngs5S7ulfl1efwOD6DmlROYs2yzTEd\n5K/ui22XfWBg/3I37HiGsYUsKiFGG1G+WGYgCIjtPqQ7wA+K9p3OyjoCgL4i6egD\nrTXRcywL5ruqs2F7RzInXO3bU+EbqxRePkG6uxgRO2zC2VzUDY6j7UdjO9j/ByJB\nDUfxNVUzkrflSpNMlK8ciSDhKMQOuoeSeR69kx7f5FvlHdl/UXPJTcCRrKejqps8\na4zqSfsCM9PxuEQyLEXJzlSXfKW4Gm7Of/Y8UWVmgEMSAyL7O/4yNhT/S7FOjxao\n2J5dSJekc6bQiv0XgPfSWLY04ICp2G2jrbf2LXG4grLYLwig3NaEGG8JevBoVNRV\nxiBq6qbcNs6ngrR6CYYhVU19fL7Gta4t3EBTq4/WxttklRfZAkqmVnCg5Jug9+Ue\n66DBZt1SX/JQtT5Ksoo9\n=LzFE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7186578e6edccfc16d4720c746beea46e0dec6a7\nparent 74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782213729 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782213729 +0300\n\nrefactor(core-storage-api): consolidate router validation guards into _validation (#479)\n\n## Consolidate the duplicated router validation guards\n\nThe fail-closed `_require(body, key)` guard was **byte-identical across\nfour routers** (`evolve`, `skill_factory`, `insights`, `entities`), and\n`entities` had added `_require_number` while `evolve` still hand-rolled\nthe same numeric check inline. This extracts both into\n`core_storage_api/routers/_validation.py` and imports them across the\nfour routers, replacing evolve's inline `isinstance(..., (int, float))`\nloop with `_require_number`.\n\nSurfaced during the Fix 2 Ph6 (#477) `/simplify` review (the duplication\nwas flagged as out-of-scope for that PR and spun off here).\n\n**Pure refactor** — no change to the happy path or the 422 detail\nmessages. One intentional tightening: evolve's `delta`/`floor`/`cap` now\ngo through `_require_number`, which rejects `bool` (a subclass of `int`\nthat was never a valid tuning value); the 422 message is unchanged.\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` — clean\n- `mypy` core-api + core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3633 passed** (clean DB), unchanged\n(behavior-preserving; existing evolve/entities numeric-422 tests\nexercise the shared guards)\n- Net −6 lines across the routers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T11:22:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e9dd9caa18c291630f7f2d39af9a6cddc546088f/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39"}]},{"sha":"74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc0YTE4ZDdjN2VjYmZkZjY0MzkyOWU3OGMwOGJlZWI1NGQ0NjFkMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T10:18:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T10:18:57Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): route entity-linking pipeline through storage (Fix 2 Ph6) (#477)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph6 — entity-linking pipeline → core-storage-api\n\nMoves all direct DB access in the entity-linking pipeline out of\ncore-api and behind `core-storage-api` HTTP (rule: no DB outside\ncore-storage-api), following the proven coarse \"run-op\" pattern (one\natomic storage call folds a multi-statement transaction). Removes 2 of\nthe 6 remaining `async_session()` sites in core-api; the other 4 are the\nfinal-cleanup phase.\n\n### New endpoints (on the existing `entities` router)\n- **`POST /entities/resolve`** — the whole `resolve_entities` step in\nONE `get_session()` txn: pgvector pair-find + union-find clustering +\nthe per-duplicate **SAVEPOINT** merge (`begin_nested()` per dupe), with\nthe pair-find/cluster-load reads on the *same write session*\n(read-your-writes). A SAVEPOINT can't cross an HTTP boundary, so the\nclustering+merge logic moves storage-side.\n- **`POST /entities/discover-cross-links`** — candidate-find + LATERAL\npgvector match + text-verify filter + bulk `ON CONFLICT` insert (single\nmulti-VALUES `RETURNING`, CAURA-686) in one txn. Targeted + batch modes.\n- **`POST /entities/infer-relations`** — co-occurrence scan +\nexisting-relation lookup + reinforce-vs-create split + batched\n`UPDATE`/`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT` in one txn.\n- **`POST /entities/list-null-embeddings`** + **`POST\n/entities/set-embeddings`** — the backfill read/write halves. The LLM\n`get_embedding` loop **stays in core-api** (storage has no\nembedding/provider chain and embedding needs per-tenant config), so\nbackfill is read → core-api embed loop → write (2 calls).\n\n### core-api side\nThe 4 entity-linking steps become DB-free (call the storage client);\n`lifecycle_audit.entity_link` and\n`entity_extraction_worker._discover_cross_links_for_memory` drop their\n`async_session` blocks. `db/session.py` and `PipelineContext.db` are\nuntouched (still used by the search pipeline — later cleanup).\n\n### Correctness notes\n- SQL ported **verbatim** — prod-fixed asyncpg quirks preserved\nbyte-for-byte: `ANY(CAST(:x AS uuid[]))`, `SET weight=:w` (not\n`LEAST(...)`, prod 2026-06-13), `update(Entity.__table__)` executemany\n(not `update(Entity)`, prod 2026-06-16), single multi-VALUES `RETURNING`\n(CAURA-686).\n- Every statement scopes `tenant_id` (resolve's link ops via `JOIN\nmemories`). New endpoints fail closed (422 on missing `tenant_id` /\nnon-numeric params / invalid UUID) — they validate their own contract\nrather than trusting core-api.\n- Behavior note: each step now commits in its own storage txn (vs the\nold single end-of-pipeline commit). This matches today's observable\nbehavior — `Pipeline.run` already swallows step errors and commits the\nprefix, and every step is idempotent (resolve re-merges, discover/infer\nare `ON CONFLICT`, backfill only fills NULLs).\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api + core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3628 passed** on a clean (TRUNCATE'd) DB; +21 from new\n`tests/test_ph6_entity_linking_storage.py` (resolve\nmerge/link-repoint/dupe-delete/tenant-isolation, discover\ntargeted+batch+text-verify, infer create+reinforce, backfill read/write,\nand fail-closed 422 cases). The 3 mock-`db` pipeline tests were\nrewritten to mock the storage client; the SQL-shape regression anchors\nmoved to the real-DB storage test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"1bd0953888332fc65df15630a9373a570c1c516c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1bd0953888332fc65df15630a9373a570c1c516c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOl2RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtygQAA2Vfln6YWcWW5br1gWb04CR\nqZIpFTeo2P65bwuYpr5Ech6Xi4W9rnzJ7ERplFo8auN+339cYYDU06iJjp4QvtVx\nO7AH7FfgYb9ZlQKQQUS352+pca1V74qW042jxBKXfboOT8+66F/oBoZ/qWkc04fo\nuo0fHXM15fGJVTOY5iRRy7LPCNwSPvSyJILd5FPCs9iDq3LX5LPtGFwmuE97VW3e\n8kWDmZi3k9Wq4/ulom7QNzwaVMqBaBS15mmKqpj+wCSmXNFYhLd/vP3zJPVMaYaI\ntpSQuMOr8TGEfPGrwLXRzjhH4A9Tf5aSUp8ahRSijT5TqMYKSNeTFH6IW+jyY8bA\n1LoEL/0khhUfrNPkvk0ibCUujQXdrtLcV7/Lgdii5VOWMnrNAlxN81T2CHu+wzOc\n9gYsupxfsnbnLV78X16X5DTV+Q6wsMsO4W8A/LOm4sJzpyQQgaZfCT0PI6xYNrFP\nxVfbdrZuD5oqd/9Ut5B+GzhWkU1V+cl+nIUfGDOdzCvdtQuuGwhkwMgAfLlQ9gza\n+K3FSn+Ovj7kyXo8aGMKWHHVh+hq/wq++WHQ6z6YVQ9AuOu+T4em9bRwciZf5OLu\nwfUFzqoJ3Z4yXqsQtH2POkJ5zUXxPKHX9qBx8Gz7Nj4CvCj6ePTtpflOQKAVtkIw\ncS+lnZQK/lTU+2CqXCzV\n=DBLe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1bd0953888332fc65df15630a9373a570c1c516c\nparent b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782209937 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782209937 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): route entity-linking pipeline through storage (Fix 2 Ph6) (#477)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph6 — entity-linking pipeline → core-storage-api\n\nMoves all direct DB access in the entity-linking pipeline out of\ncore-api and behind `core-storage-api` HTTP (rule: no DB outside\ncore-storage-api), following the proven coarse \"run-op\" pattern (one\natomic storage call folds a multi-statement transaction). Removes 2 of\nthe 6 remaining `async_session()` sites in core-api; the other 4 are the\nfinal-cleanup phase.\n\n### New endpoints (on the existing `entities` router)\n- **`POST /entities/resolve`** — the whole `resolve_entities` step in\nONE `get_session()` txn: pgvector pair-find + union-find clustering +\nthe per-duplicate **SAVEPOINT** merge (`begin_nested()` per dupe), with\nthe pair-find/cluster-load reads on the *same write session*\n(read-your-writes). A SAVEPOINT can't cross an HTTP boundary, so the\nclustering+merge logic moves storage-side.\n- **`POST /entities/discover-cross-links`** — candidate-find + LATERAL\npgvector match + text-verify filter + bulk `ON CONFLICT` insert (single\nmulti-VALUES `RETURNING`, CAURA-686) in one txn. Targeted + batch modes.\n- **`POST /entities/infer-relations`** — co-occurrence scan +\nexisting-relation lookup + reinforce-vs-create split + batched\n`UPDATE`/`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT` in one txn.\n- **`POST /entities/list-null-embeddings`** + **`POST\n/entities/set-embeddings`** — the backfill read/write halves. The LLM\n`get_embedding` loop **stays in core-api** (storage has no\nembedding/provider chain and embedding needs per-tenant config), so\nbackfill is read → core-api embed loop → write (2 calls).\n\n### core-api side\nThe 4 entity-linking steps become DB-free (call the storage client);\n`lifecycle_audit.entity_link` and\n`entity_extraction_worker._discover_cross_links_for_memory` drop their\n`async_session` blocks. `db/session.py` and `PipelineContext.db` are\nuntouched (still used by the search pipeline — later cleanup).\n\n### Correctness notes\n- SQL ported **verbatim** — prod-fixed asyncpg quirks preserved\nbyte-for-byte: `ANY(CAST(:x AS uuid[]))`, `SET weight=:w` (not\n`LEAST(...)`, prod 2026-06-13), `update(Entity.__table__)` executemany\n(not `update(Entity)`, prod 2026-06-16), single multi-VALUES `RETURNING`\n(CAURA-686).\n- Every statement scopes `tenant_id` (resolve's link ops via `JOIN\nmemories`). New endpoints fail closed (422 on missing `tenant_id` /\nnon-numeric params / invalid UUID) — they validate their own contract\nrather than trusting core-api.\n- Behavior note: each step now commits in its own storage txn (vs the\nold single end-of-pipeline commit). This matches today's observable\nbehavior — `Pipeline.run` already swallows step errors and commits the\nprefix, and every step is idempotent (resolve re-merges, discover/infer\nare `ON CONFLICT`, backfill only fills NULLs).\n\n### Verification\n- `ruff@0.15.4 check` + `format --check` (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src) — clean\n- `mypy` core-api + core-storage-api — clean\n- full suite — **3628 passed** on a clean (TRUNCATE'd) DB; +21 from new\n`tests/test_ph6_entity_linking_storage.py` (resolve\nmerge/link-repoint/dupe-delete/tenant-isolation, discover\ntargeted+batch+text-verify, infer create+reinforce, backfill read/write,\nand fail-closed 422 cases). The 3 mock-`db` pipeline tests were\nrewritten to mock the storage client; the SQL-shape regression anchors\nmoved to the real-DB storage test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T10:18:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/74a18d7c7ecbfdf643929e78c08beeb54d461d39/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115"}]},{"sha":"b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI1ZjI2YmNmOGIwZmQxYjg5ODY0Zjg4MjgxZGNiODQ0ODk0MjYxMTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T09:53:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T09:53:27Z"},"message":"test(core-api): cover the db=None MCP/STM write path in create_memory (#476)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an integration regression test\n(`tests/test_mcp_write_db_none_regression.py`) for the MCP / STM write\npath — `create_memory(db=None, ...)`, which is what `memclaw_write` runs\nvia `_no_db()`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe prod MCP-write regression (2026-06-23, loadtest\n`mcp-tool-broken-write` HIGH) had **no test coverage**. Before Fix 2\nPh5b PR2 (#472), four `write_fast` steps (`load_tenant_config`,\n`detect_near_duplicate`, `check_semantic_duplicate`, and\n`write_memory_row`'s audit hook) called `ctx.require_db`, which\n**raises** on `db=None`. The runner broke the failing step without\nre-raising, and `create_memory` then read the unset `ctx.data[\"memory\"]`\n→ `KeyError: 'memory'`, surfaced to MCP clients as `Error executing tool\nmemclaw_write: 'memory'`. #472 switched those steps to the nullable\n`ctx.db`; #474 made `create_memory` raise a clean 500 instead of masking\nthe failure.\n\nNothing guarded against a reintroduction: `test_mcp_write.py` mocks\n`create_memory`, and the `mcp_env` fixture patches `_no_db` to yield a\n`MagicMock` (not `None`) — so neither exercises the real `db=None`\npipeline.\n\n## What the test does\n\nDrives the **real** write pipeline with `db=None` against the\nintegration DB:\n- `test_create_memory_tolerates_db_none[fast|strong]` — parametrized;\n`fast` covers `load_tenant_config` + `detect_near_duplicate` +\n`write_memory_row`, `strong` additionally covers\n`check_semantic_duplicate` (all four switched `require_db` sites).\nAsserts a persisted `MemoryOut` and reads the row back from a separate\nsession.\n- `test_memclaw_write_mcp_handler_succeeds_with_no_db` — end-to-end\nthrough the real `memclaw_write` handler (real `_no_db()` yielding\n`None`, real\n`create_memory`/`enforce_fleet_write`/`check_and_increment`); only\nauth/identity is stubbed. Guards the `_no_db` wiring too.\n\nReintroducing a `require_db` in any write step makes these fail (the\nfailed step → clean 500 → no `MemoryOut`).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check`: clean\n- `pytest tests/test_mcp_write_db_none_regression.py`: 3 passed (against\nlocal PG + pgvector)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4960e5a699e27871661540790bab36c6aef596e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4960e5a699e27871661540790bab36c6aef596e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOleXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2MsQADJRL0fLekw44RIaVzFWB+pu\nlYKHuwzCoj5nWYz8L+sxSp0vEaBuK0A71xVpWEb8qU7Qw8BYI1JyJwTLcVbJzGRJ\neROW3+SJpec5owTNu2Mqp0TXvSIl/Ad9f+A9vKErSoBuisuiPJXFXG2MVmGt3SY7\nAlbHpXpZX69ljR18nAhVzqyyUTmO3nvXdjstT8WSfLU24wNirkSqRctjIoChCgux\nU4H8L/U0OlbCIgVuwZS4i7Uen7hVCwa4087tEQKOj8V23wqlak/wns2Qws12OVwf\nXQALWJNztnpd8B6TZoQHHtDan9jJC61jjMKu/TbiYJ/KapUePvR4tKn51RoWt/Ez\n4HhWh2rtSFNBQac6pOWzI2yuIXwUraNAT8ex2qoqR8T3mX2Qgivcadahwl7Db79H\nI7pkBBcf/S8V3RHOuH1D9Izz5DOXCJaQNnCka6gFjTBk+lHO9wsSfrp7oOXNPNI2\nHv4AULIb2toa7fjCW7UEgV8nQd/ZXHealjFWTVIAhXUDfKdyw96NUUV4bi1/596K\nuz2zVs1PO1mKaVmKagVzln1tTru6vl5cg5h16pobDgR4b0juPTiu5VHUoEG4SDln\nX3FmXhJJAS9E4EL3YYs6jx4dV1mB2Pd1+ZZGBA1wE/DsLT7N0swdtcUlpI8yoO+/\nihKwVpdy1XkAZyQ7bT/t\n=vQU8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4960e5a699e27871661540790bab36c6aef596e1\nparent a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782208407 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782208407 +0300\n\ntest(core-api): cover the db=None MCP/STM write path in create_memory (#476)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an integration regression test\n(`tests/test_mcp_write_db_none_regression.py`) for the MCP / STM write\npath — `create_memory(db=None, ...)`, which is what `memclaw_write` runs\nvia `_no_db()`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe prod MCP-write regression (2026-06-23, loadtest\n`mcp-tool-broken-write` HIGH) had **no test coverage**. Before Fix 2\nPh5b PR2 (#472), four `write_fast` steps (`load_tenant_config`,\n`detect_near_duplicate`, `check_semantic_duplicate`, and\n`write_memory_row`'s audit hook) called `ctx.require_db`, which\n**raises** on `db=None`. The runner broke the failing step without\nre-raising, and `create_memory` then read the unset `ctx.data[\"memory\"]`\n→ `KeyError: 'memory'`, surfaced to MCP clients as `Error executing tool\nmemclaw_write: 'memory'`. #472 switched those steps to the nullable\n`ctx.db`; #474 made `create_memory` raise a clean 500 instead of masking\nthe failure.\n\nNothing guarded against a reintroduction: `test_mcp_write.py` mocks\n`create_memory`, and the `mcp_env` fixture patches `_no_db` to yield a\n`MagicMock` (not `None`) — so neither exercises the real `db=None`\npipeline.\n\n## What the test does\n\nDrives the **real** write pipeline with `db=None` against the\nintegration DB:\n- `test_create_memory_tolerates_db_none[fast|strong]` — parametrized;\n`fast` covers `load_tenant_config` + `detect_near_duplicate` +\n`write_memory_row`, `strong` additionally covers\n`check_semantic_duplicate` (all four switched `require_db` sites).\nAsserts a persisted `MemoryOut` and reads the row back from a separate\nsession.\n- `test_memclaw_write_mcp_handler_succeeds_with_no_db` — end-to-end\nthrough the real `memclaw_write` handler (real `_no_db()` yielding\n`None`, real\n`create_memory`/`enforce_fleet_write`/`check_and_increment`); only\nauth/identity is stubbed. Guards the `_no_db` wiring too.\n\nReintroducing a `require_db` in any write step makes these fail (the\nfailed step → clean 500 → no `MemoryOut`).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check`: clean\n- `pytest tests/test_mcp_write_db_none_regression.py`: 3 passed (against\nlocal PG + pgvector)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T09:53:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b5f26bcf8b0fd1b89864f88281dcb84489426115/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222"}]},{"sha":"a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGE2ZjlhZDE1ODFiZDMwYzYwYTEyNWRlMTE1OWZmZTM5MThiZjMyMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T08:30:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T08:30:13Z"},"message":"docs: point all memclaw.dev links to memclaw.net (#475)\n\n## Why\n`memclaw.net` is the canonical host. This repoints every **user-facing\nlink** and **illustrative example URL** from `memclaw.dev` →\n`memclaw.net`.\n\n## Changed\n- **`docs/integration-without-plugin.md`** — all dev-facing API /\ndashboard / install / MCP URLs (12).\n- **`docs/plugin-upgrade.md`** — server-examples parenthetical.\n- **`core-api/.../routes/plugin.py`** — install-skill docstring +\n`api_url` Query description examples. **Comment-only** — the endpoint\nstays host-agnostic via `X-Forwarded-Host`\n(`_derive_api_url_from_request`); no logic change.\n- **`scripts/repro_contradictions_*.py`** — example `MEMCLAW_API_URL`\nenv in usage docstrings.\n\n## Deliberately NOT changed (and why)\nThese `.dev` references are **factual records / behavior-test data, not\nsite links** — rewriting them to `.net` would misrepresent what\nhappened:\n- `tests/test_enrichment_inline_timeout.py`,\n`tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`,\n`tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` — provenance docstrings\n(\"observed/wet-tested on memclaw.dev\" — where the prod incident actually\noccurred).\n- `tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py` — the forwarded-host **echo\ntest**: it sets `X-Forwarded-Host: memclaw.dev` and asserts the\ngenerated script echoes that host. `.dev` is deliberate fixture data\nproving the script isn't hardcoded to localhost.\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.ts:189` — a historical wet-test comment.\n\n(Happy to genericize those to \"in production\" in a follow-up if we want\nzero `.dev` in the tree — flagged separately.)\n\n## Out of scope\nThe shipped skill texts (`static/` + `plugin/` `SKILL.md`) are being\nupdated separately.\n\n## Validation\n`ruff check core-api/src/` clean; `tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py`\n9/9 pass (confirms the comment-only `plugin.py` edit didn't disturb the\nendpoint). No logic changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50d3eea1780c365930e80ca4c2d03e82bdae6482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/50d3eea1780c365930e80ca4c2d03e82bdae6482"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOkQVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKz0QAChi10fP6u2nPO1efMPsOXHH\nANI+o+gLPOqxUpOLzSAbZPdwz2FVefdGkOgvABidFYsuSjRhyb2vhs1SSV9MkUrp\nYSy9n6xsKHN28GqfCIw4B9WFslXpCg1fbVc7yBvgYf8jhsDDOECrN2pswaKTN7vc\nnw8uM4Y9+UjZMxthTb0wYodds5l+aTEHwiouknIJOj/7p0WQskQF+Cn4UdRmxoTE\neCVwsjwxZdYbUaE/8+eRE6e49jDS/pGILzxh9Ck32LZnD/36Ru+ARVaZ7raAkkzk\n/Y5+Y4+GQ5KQ2RHivpfPeQRgrJtv5mDuXTasQ8fd75Lu8+7O3Z2eH8zVjszMg2xC\nL0u8YeosfhI05HcCSfYjgMuzxAN5gf0ODH/SoTP9Jt9c1/PkHuHJapoRmu1IGBNF\ni259Sk8xbLJhIV8vYJVXk3tKwb7LPvXExMVmmvUYSyg40NmDoNyhE5M6GL67Px0U\n6Mnqzfej89OI8incKAnfdYyUi36f/wF93fZ28xhpxVsfP5az+m5nyJ90adWy0NOH\n8crX9fp3vDNapI1oNh3yp2kT7qkdOttbkpu/GlVeykwf6hNNqsi1Ya5d3DYFXLCy\n17dLKw7bC3AInPTVMoHxTQie6Fu10NRuS7c6roqK4qZ/KgF66sq4Lk4qRj0T8YUu\nmgQzcV2Wz8Lt8CyyzXWL\n=caMk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 50d3eea1780c365930e80ca4c2d03e82bdae6482\nparent 5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782203413 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782203413 +0300\n\ndocs: point all memclaw.dev links to memclaw.net (#475)\n\n## Why\n`memclaw.net` is the canonical host. This repoints every **user-facing\nlink** and **illustrative example URL** from `memclaw.dev` →\n`memclaw.net`.\n\n## Changed\n- **`docs/integration-without-plugin.md`** — all dev-facing API /\ndashboard / install / MCP URLs (12).\n- **`docs/plugin-upgrade.md`** — server-examples parenthetical.\n- **`core-api/.../routes/plugin.py`** — install-skill docstring +\n`api_url` Query description examples. **Comment-only** — the endpoint\nstays host-agnostic via `X-Forwarded-Host`\n(`_derive_api_url_from_request`); no logic change.\n- **`scripts/repro_contradictions_*.py`** — example `MEMCLAW_API_URL`\nenv in usage docstrings.\n\n## Deliberately NOT changed (and why)\nThese `.dev` references are **factual records / behavior-test data, not\nsite links** — rewriting them to `.net` would misrepresent what\nhappened:\n- `tests/test_enrichment_inline_timeout.py`,\n`tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`,\n`tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` — provenance docstrings\n(\"observed/wet-tested on memclaw.dev\" — where the prod incident actually\noccurred).\n- `tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py` — the forwarded-host **echo\ntest**: it sets `X-Forwarded-Host: memclaw.dev` and asserts the\ngenerated script echoes that host. `.dev` is deliberate fixture data\nproving the script isn't hardcoded to localhost.\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.ts:189` — a historical wet-test comment.\n\n(Happy to genericize those to \"in production\" in a follow-up if we want\nzero `.dev` in the tree — flagged separately.)\n\n## Out of scope\nThe shipped skill texts (`static/` + `plugin/` `SKILL.md`) are being\nupdated separately.\n\n## Validation\n`ruff check core-api/src/` clean; `tests/test_install_skill_endpoint.py`\n9/9 pass (confirms the comment-only `plugin.py` edit didn't disturb the\nendpoint). No logic changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T08:30:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a6f9ad1581bd30c60a125de1159ffe3918bf3222/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476"}]},{"sha":"5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVkMzU5YjI5MWE3MzQwMzgzYmFjOTVlOGRkODFlOTA4Yzk0YmY0NzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T07:44:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:44:25Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): surface write-pipeline step failures instead of masking as KeyError (#474)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a write-pipeline step raises a non-`HTTPException`, the runner\n(`pipeline/runner.py`) records `StepResult(FAILED)`, sets\n`result.failed=True`, and **`break`s without re-raising**.\n`create_memory` ignored `result.failed` and read `ctx.data[\"memory\"]`\ndirectly — but `WriteMemoryRow` never ran, so that read raised\n**`KeyError: 'memory'`**, masking the real cause.\n\nConcretely (the prod MCP-write regression): an MCP `memclaw_write` runs\nunder `_no_db()` (`db=None`); the `load_tenant_config` step raises\n*\"This pipeline step requires a DB session\"*, the runner breaks, and the\nclient saw the cryptic `Error executing tool memclaw_write: 'memory'`\nwith **no actionable error**. Prod log confirms:\n```\nwrite_fast.load_tenant_config: FAILED — This pipeline step requires a DB session.\nPipelineContext was built without one (STM path).\n```\n\n## What\n\nMirror the existing `_search_memories` pattern: after\n`pipeline.run(ctx)`, if `result.failed`, log the failing step's real\nerror and raise `HTTPException(500)` — so the real cause is logged and\nthe caller gets a clean error envelope instead of a `KeyError`.\n\n- **Success path unchanged** — `result.failed` is `False` on success;\nthe new block is skipped.\n- `_exc` is set so the `memory_write_latency` `finally` still records\n`success=False`.\n- Uses the same local `from core_api.pipeline.step import StepOutcome`\nimport the search path uses (this module imports pipeline symbols\nlocally throughout, to avoid an import cycle).\n\n## Scope\n\n**Masking fix only.** The underlying **trigger** — `load_tenant_config`\nrequiring a DB session on the MCP `_no_db()` write path (an incomplete\nstorage-routing migration; REST passes a real session, so it's\nunaffected) — is being fixed separately (ph5b storage-routing). With\nthis change, that failure (and any future write-step failure) surfaces\nas a clear 500 + logged cause instead of `'memory'`.\n\n**Follow-ups:** (1) the same `result.failed` guard should be applied to\nthe auto-chunk persist path (the second `ctx.data[\"memory\"]` read in\nthis file); (2) a unit test (`db=None` → `HTTPException(500)`, not\n`KeyError`) is recommended alongside the trigger fix — note the\nanalogous search-pipeline-failure handling is currently untested too.\n\n## Verification\n\n`ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓ (repo-pinned ruff 0.15.10),\n`mypy` ✓ on `core-api/src/core_api/services/memory_service.py`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"5b5cd54ed316a2d952b2400f4accc2381c9c0862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5b5cd54ed316a2d952b2400f4accc2381c9c0862"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjlZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS/IQAI2VTR3QM+XlJCAw2TGoGYws\n1c5Powa6pu3+WKH89I3y5evGpOfBMKfcqoQ9u/tX0K4xq92keA8S7ACNCIhxqWuC\nydGWGVD8DWb8pPltTYKfxVgqm5dcpe/S9EBcThcOY4BXf8UB89740QYj5LVWBtfH\nfiookiU+dSh77HsHq5vDmAI8/aVAI4mr5YezQgZIfHJd5yCY8u5mqnZcJRO/gbw+\nUh6og76RY/rA6Lj3GwKPFqm0sJLOtoD/b5kT4nELS4ySw7k4nT2+Lme9uMsrtAEg\ng1dBPSjwNgpUCC159qzQhJHZkFPfbgZ4bxnEXLi4cQOxO/fRQqW+Qe5gKvDIZ/ic\nMox+qF9c2ctLwO8TRdnctTkppPVHb4S+RFL2gWXOdLE02u32eYWi8VzAZrC990kL\n1lUG6ZKhhnA/MSNGWeRCsXXPKeUDWwT5cw6PE/xaMCTaBNBGE+yAsf8cnTrlDX+N\n79boHnntHsJVI4B/qEogfbXl2uCLonQRjTAFeqmHykguyBSr6iNI9hiE3WOQ/wCI\nVp71Xd1M+toNOA716ka+8E2L6/GepDSh0BZbKDTV4b7zioNX3tT2KAvSgDWfQDEY\nvL8JvKIgevurOB5G6Q3GyT222QaF0qWiuVlszhHEaVOjnJVfNdK/Qc6MQYJrB3cm\nP23ZO7Se+yF22JFYvrGD\n=b6CF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b5cd54ed316a2d952b2400f4accc2381c9c0862\nparent 8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782200665 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782200665 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): surface write-pipeline step failures instead of masking as KeyError (#474)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a write-pipeline step raises a non-`HTTPException`, the runner\n(`pipeline/runner.py`) records `StepResult(FAILED)`, sets\n`result.failed=True`, and **`break`s without re-raising**.\n`create_memory` ignored `result.failed` and read `ctx.data[\"memory\"]`\ndirectly — but `WriteMemoryRow` never ran, so that read raised\n**`KeyError: 'memory'`**, masking the real cause.\n\nConcretely (the prod MCP-write regression): an MCP `memclaw_write` runs\nunder `_no_db()` (`db=None`); the `load_tenant_config` step raises\n*\"This pipeline step requires a DB session\"*, the runner breaks, and the\nclient saw the cryptic `Error executing tool memclaw_write: 'memory'`\nwith **no actionable error**. Prod log confirms:\n```\nwrite_fast.load_tenant_config: FAILED — This pipeline step requires a DB session.\nPipelineContext was built without one (STM path).\n```\n\n## What\n\nMirror the existing `_search_memories` pattern: after\n`pipeline.run(ctx)`, if `result.failed`, log the failing step's real\nerror and raise `HTTPException(500)` — so the real cause is logged and\nthe caller gets a clean error envelope instead of a `KeyError`.\n\n- **Success path unchanged** — `result.failed` is `False` on success;\nthe new block is skipped.\n- `_exc` is set so the `memory_write_latency` `finally` still records\n`success=False`.\n- Uses the same local `from core_api.pipeline.step import StepOutcome`\nimport the search path uses (this module imports pipeline symbols\nlocally throughout, to avoid an import cycle).\n\n## Scope\n\n**Masking fix only.** The underlying **trigger** — `load_tenant_config`\nrequiring a DB session on the MCP `_no_db()` write path (an incomplete\nstorage-routing migration; REST passes a real session, so it's\nunaffected) — is being fixed separately (ph5b storage-routing). With\nthis change, that failure (and any future write-step failure) surfaces\nas a clear 500 + logged cause instead of `'memory'`.\n\n**Follow-ups:** (1) the same `result.failed` guard should be applied to\nthe auto-chunk persist path (the second `ctx.data[\"memory\"]` read in\nthis file); (2) a unit test (`db=None` → `HTTPException(500)`, not\n`KeyError`) is recommended alongside the trigger fix — note the\nanalogous search-pipeline-failure handling is currently untested too.\n\n## Verification\n\n`ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓ (repo-pinned ruff 0.15.10),\n`mypy` ✓ on `core-api/src/core_api/services/memory_service.py`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:44:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d359b291a7340383bac95e8dd81e908c94bf476/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe"}]},{"sha":"8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhmOGYzOWVmODUzNjBlMzdjMWFjYTUxMGZlYWI3NzBkZTliOTI2ZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T07:30:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:30:59Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): re-route third-party loggers from the ASGI lifespan startup (#473)\n\n## Why\n\n`configure_logging()` runs at import time (`app.py`) and calls\n`_route_third_party_to_root()` then — but `uvicorn` / `fastmcp` / `mcp`\n/ `slowapi` are imported **after** that call (slowapi + `mcp_server`\nfurther down in `app.py`, uvicorn by the server). So the import-time\npass **no-ops for those loggers** — it even logs the warning it was\nbuilt to emit:\n\n> `logger 'fastmcp' has no own handlers at rerouting time; rerouting was\na no-op (library may not be imported yet — call\n_route_third_party_to_root from an ASGI lifespan startup handler if this\nis a uvicorn-fronted service)`\n\nResult: those libraries' records never reach the JSON/GCP handler.\n**Most consequentially, FastMCP's `Error executing tool …` tool-error\nlines are invisible in prod** — an MCP tool that raises surfaces the\nerror to the client but leaves **no server-side log to debug from**.\n(Concretely: this is why a recently-surfaced MCP `memclaw_write` failure\nproduced a client-side `'memory'` error with nothing in Cloud Logging\nfrom FastMCP.)\n\n## What\n\nAdd an **idempotent** `_route_third_party_to_root()` call at the start\nof the ASGI **lifespan startup** — by then\n`uvicorn`/`fastmcp`/`mcp`/`slowapi` are imported, so the re-route\nactually takes. This is exactly what the no-op warning instructs. The\nimport-time call in `configure_logging()` is unchanged (still routes\neverything imported by then).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓ (repo-pinned ruff 0.15.10),\n`mypy` ✓ on `core-api/src/core_api/app.py`.\n- The routing function is already covered by `tests/test_logging.py`\n(incl. an idempotency test and a \"re-call after a handlerless no-op\nreroute\" test), so the second call is safe.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"32a21320add515e3bd33bd548338212e7d5e2bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/32a21320add515e3bd33bd548338212e7d5e2bc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjYzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARecQAJX8Zn+aS9yl/7ZxeVzV7DCo\n2qSxn+3i3bvItDjXiv4qUsVb2nRvKiuzn7QDpUVIRVcx8PN6kve3SHYVjP9KfJ93\n2rcGUCu9kOWrYt0QK77JveNipIzN3mbrJwZWhsxaErlODpoG//HWn7DfkT412Yx0\nx66gYAS7tc1ioI5D7TH9qK5ceocFHmnVLJCnoGyZkSRBYDPhfOUiJaoEhdn4IPkN\n17TNjaVky62Zdeiache0xSrZqFp1zrzmIz1MyDew0iiHi/Qm32TPx85tVhXH3lMH\n8smT2bvKCkcm6KLVe6liAoVhRb2scqP8eyG+gQ1eAykrgMGCHuaVLb3a8rkDkvzO\nMM5fSmHpF9qbFWoPvbmEzmiVm5v6uqqw+ZNB+HFf9d/7HEPiLu0dC+Q1bsgjjvKl\nNQqFq1h2REBCccXFxpVnBIJatu/CyDXlMKBOjQs59zrsn+RFdUrCfqC4lHe/nViK\nLwt/I9Z1xXu3x+uGfZnVR8mcvnRG4p1LkJeyp8wBWYgbXEfIlUJlO3fjDbc6v66s\nNOhnW5SZ/8lPDVArCDPVNdE/SEkZDMfZQJ+eCOvSXoOxoM5D94nLOzB+B1tEpSeq\nlMoKCwdFutU6QUm+1nXrwSpXWPAisx4ehVIWPnwjnRH3XZwV1lW2yGqxfHC4Clta\nj9qJTpolbS9zVhaF1kbD\n=BDz2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 32a21320add515e3bd33bd548338212e7d5e2bc4\nparent 44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782199859 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782199859 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): re-route third-party loggers from the ASGI lifespan startup (#473)\n\n## Why\n\n`configure_logging()` runs at import time (`app.py`) and calls\n`_route_third_party_to_root()` then — but `uvicorn` / `fastmcp` / `mcp`\n/ `slowapi` are imported **after** that call (slowapi + `mcp_server`\nfurther down in `app.py`, uvicorn by the server). So the import-time\npass **no-ops for those loggers** — it even logs the warning it was\nbuilt to emit:\n\n> `logger 'fastmcp' has no own handlers at rerouting time; rerouting was\na no-op (library may not be imported yet — call\n_route_third_party_to_root from an ASGI lifespan startup handler if this\nis a uvicorn-fronted service)`\n\nResult: those libraries' records never reach the JSON/GCP handler.\n**Most consequentially, FastMCP's `Error executing tool …` tool-error\nlines are invisible in prod** — an MCP tool that raises surfaces the\nerror to the client but leaves **no server-side log to debug from**.\n(Concretely: this is why a recently-surfaced MCP `memclaw_write` failure\nproduced a client-side `'memory'` error with nothing in Cloud Logging\nfrom FastMCP.)\n\n## What\n\nAdd an **idempotent** `_route_third_party_to_root()` call at the start\nof the ASGI **lifespan startup** — by then\n`uvicorn`/`fastmcp`/`mcp`/`slowapi` are imported, so the re-route\nactually takes. This is exactly what the no-op warning instructs. The\nimport-time call in `configure_logging()` is unchanged (still routes\neverything imported by then).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ruff check` ✓, `ruff format --check` ✓ (repo-pinned ruff 0.15.10),\n`mypy` ✓ on `core-api/src/core_api/app.py`.\n- The routing function is already covered by `tests/test_logging.py`\n(incl. an idempotency test and a \"re-call after a handlerless no-op\nreroute\" test), so the second call is safe.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:30:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f8f39ef85360e37c1aca510feab770de9b926fe/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0"}]},{"sha":"44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ0NzQzZTE5YjE5NzJhNDQzOWI5ZjQzYzhmNzkxOWRmMjgyMzYzZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-23T07:13:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:13:31Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): route evolve through storage + delete _mcp_session (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR2) (#472)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5b — PR2: route evolve through storage + **delete\n`_mcp_session`**\n\nSecond of the two Ph5b PRs (PR1 insights = #471, merged). Routes\n`evolve_service` + `memclaw_evolve` + `/evolve/report` off core-api's\ndirect DB, and as the final step **deletes `_mcp_session`** —\n`memclaw_evolve` was its last consumer once PR1 moved insights to\n`_no_db`. This completes the mcp_server DB migration.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints\n- `POST /evolve/filter-by-scope` — SELECT ids by tenant+scope (ORM\n`.in_()`).\n- `POST /evolve/apply-weights` — the weight-clamp CTE\n(`GREATEST`/`LEAST`, `RETURNING` old/new) **and** the rule→outcome\n`jsonb_set` backfill, folded into **one atomic transaction** so evolve's\ndocumented split-commit doesn't widen. `_apply_outcome_to_db` is\nre-sequenced so rule/outcome ids exist before this single call.\n\n### `_mcp_session` deleted\nRemoved the `_mcp_session` def + the `async_session` import + an\norphaned `sa_text` import. `grep -rn \"_mcp_session\" core-api/src/` →\nzero consumers.\n\n### ⚠️ Write-pipeline made db-free (broader than evolve — flagging for\nreview)\nEvolve's outcome/rule persist now calls `create_memory(db=None)` (the\nSTM path). Four `write_fast` steps — `load_tenant_config`,\n`detect_near_duplicate`, `check_semantic_duplicate`, and\n`write_memory_row`'s audit hook — used `ctx.require_db` (which\n**raises** on `db=None`) to call functions that are **already\nstorage-routed and ignore `db`** (`resolve_config`,\n`_find_semantic_duplicate`, `log_action`). Switched all four to the\nnullable `ctx.db`: transparent for db-present callers, and it unblocks\nthe db-free STM write path. The warm-cache full suite masked this\n(near-dup got skipped under the cached org config); a **clean-DB** run\nsurfaced it.\n\nAlso cast `metadata::jsonb` in the apply-weights backfill — CAURA-595\n`json`/`jsonb` column drift (mirrors the merged `memory_update` fix).\n\n### Deviation (documented in-code)\nThe persisted outcome memory's `metadata.weight_adjustments` is `[]` on\nthe apply path — the exact post-clamp deltas are in the `report_outcome`\nresponse and the audit log, but the outcome must be persisted *before*\napply-weights to fold the backfill atomically. Nothing reads the\npersisted field.\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, **full suite\n3604 passed on a clean DB** (the rigorous run — no warm-cache masking).\nNew `tests/test_ph5b_evolve_storage.py` (filter-by-scope agent/fleet/all\n+ tenant isolation; apply-weights clamp at floor/cap, RETURNING,\nbackfill / no-backfill, isolation; 422 guards); reworked\n`test_evolve_service.py` to seed/assert via the storage client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"0ebf645a3fc23ff138ae22dd5ea09c3c59b0c600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0ebf645a3fc23ff138ae22dd5ea09c3c59b0c600"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjIbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZekQAD8eJ4d9Bv0H5WTN5TCrd3dt\nBZavntRwzpTR6t+3iK+LgfDpyRd3fUdycnDI08DidiLirlif+FG6oglW2klz5o7h\nioCCl2O4EvmllAlqhk4EdDaO9dp9xbKEnl+qSEg1L1KixLOj6GweoHvP49grPh1w\nUnX962Cm+BZX/FLBeuuj0aYoERDASN1lCk7HbYCgLPbmldvVZNsOFL0GYFxeXxyd\nu12yP2pfI8JRtZhKpaAAodtyuZ3WjbBIzBtpI0UHM86GwGnqFbcXvWt3ij3hvqqT\nn557U0KQmYUP63vWj7LnZjwZ01R8wsmT+S5ZyfJYcfN63jyOZNMKfrzqUPf15o/f\nWvNQExznF4VargNKOMGMiQxaKsXjI4qplgVOsnIWdGZf1vYBOe5EMdNjLGpQYzfA\n4TbXljOM0GgA0AQQXCFHhm91/hlUfZDM5oPPqgpYyODkqv8yNbHcqWVHyqTnLwx7\nXr3xRFzXKCn6BMDm9bxZwx8ifUR6Mg9xflOB8FifUd3gELIjvsIkTzFqr/+4u0YM\n0GsKK3UlQA2j7Cb2LsrCqO7PLynUIafvp5UWfQxMjYLh481i3GP77sLcc9igHyzf\nlRlZU75Ny0gdb8rY+fxFqhyhLEg1uuC3ysAKVNLutdtpYbuOy1iRGZO/0rimIwii\n1IgiCcSoNCdCdCh4TVhG\n=tCFc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0ebf645a3fc23ff138ae22dd5ea09c3c59b0c600\nparent 2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782198811 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782198811 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): route evolve through storage + delete _mcp_session (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR2) (#472)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5b — PR2: route evolve through storage + **delete\n`_mcp_session`**\n\nSecond of the two Ph5b PRs (PR1 insights = #471, merged). Routes\n`evolve_service` + `memclaw_evolve` + `/evolve/report` off core-api's\ndirect DB, and as the final step **deletes `_mcp_session`** —\n`memclaw_evolve` was its last consumer once PR1 moved insights to\n`_no_db`. This completes the mcp_server DB migration.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints\n- `POST /evolve/filter-by-scope` — SELECT ids by tenant+scope (ORM\n`.in_()`).\n- `POST /evolve/apply-weights` — the weight-clamp CTE\n(`GREATEST`/`LEAST`, `RETURNING` old/new) **and** the rule→outcome\n`jsonb_set` backfill, folded into **one atomic transaction** so evolve's\ndocumented split-commit doesn't widen. `_apply_outcome_to_db` is\nre-sequenced so rule/outcome ids exist before this single call.\n\n### `_mcp_session` deleted\nRemoved the `_mcp_session` def + the `async_session` import + an\norphaned `sa_text` import. `grep -rn \"_mcp_session\" core-api/src/` →\nzero consumers.\n\n### ⚠️ Write-pipeline made db-free (broader than evolve — flagging for\nreview)\nEvolve's outcome/rule persist now calls `create_memory(db=None)` (the\nSTM path). Four `write_fast` steps — `load_tenant_config`,\n`detect_near_duplicate`, `check_semantic_duplicate`, and\n`write_memory_row`'s audit hook — used `ctx.require_db` (which\n**raises** on `db=None`) to call functions that are **already\nstorage-routed and ignore `db`** (`resolve_config`,\n`_find_semantic_duplicate`, `log_action`). Switched all four to the\nnullable `ctx.db`: transparent for db-present callers, and it unblocks\nthe db-free STM write path. The warm-cache full suite masked this\n(near-dup got skipped under the cached org config); a **clean-DB** run\nsurfaced it.\n\nAlso cast `metadata::jsonb` in the apply-weights backfill — CAURA-595\n`json`/`jsonb` column drift (mirrors the merged `memory_update` fix).\n\n### Deviation (documented in-code)\nThe persisted outcome memory's `metadata.weight_adjustments` is `[]` on\nthe apply path — the exact post-clamp deltas are in the `report_outcome`\nresponse and the audit log, but the outcome must be persisted *before*\napply-weights to fold the backfill atomically. Nothing reads the\npersisted field.\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, **full suite\n3604 passed on a clean DB** (the rigorous run — no warm-cache masking).\nNew `tests/test_ph5b_evolve_storage.py` (filter-by-scope agent/fleet/all\n+ tenant isolation; apply-weights clamp at floor/cap, RETURNING,\nbackfill / no-backfill, isolation; 422 guards); reworked\n`test_evolve_service.py` to seed/assert via the storage client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:13:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/44743e19b1972a4439b9f43c8f7919df282363e0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866"}]},{"sha":"2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDI2NTViODRhOTE2MjRiMGFjZjM4YmU1NjQxODFiM2M4ZGQwNmU4NjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T21:12:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:12:29Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): route insights_service through storage (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR1 — insights) (#471)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5b — PR1: route insights_service through core-storage-api\n\nFirst of two Ph5b PRs (**insights** here; **evolve + the `_mcp_session`\ndeletion** in PR2). Moves the insights pipeline off core-api's direct DB\npool. **`_mcp_session` intentionally remains** — `memclaw_evolve` still\nuses it; PR2 deletes it as its final step.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (router `insights.py` +\nPostgresService methods)\nAll explicit-tenant-scoped; analytic reads use SQLAlchemy ORM (sidesteps\nasyncpg array-cast pitfalls):\n- `POST /insights/{contradictions,failures,stale,divergence,patterns}` —\nthe 5 focus reads. `contradictions`/`divergence` keep the `GROUP BY …\nHAVING COUNT(DISTINCT …)` entity pre-query. Return the MEMORY_LIST shape\n(no embedding).\n- `POST /insights/discover-sample` — embedding-bearing sample; numpy\nk-means + cluster summarisation stay client-side.\n- `POST /insights/supersede-priors` + `POST /insights/restore-priors` —\n`_persist_findings`'s prior-outdate (JSONB\n`metadata->>'insight_focus'`/`scope` select + `UPDATE\nstatus='outdated'`, one atomic txn) and the all-failed restore.\n- `POST /insights/activity-gate` — `MAX(created_at)` by\ninsight/non-insight for the lifecycle discover gate.\n\n### core-api migration\n`insights_service` (`_query_*` + `_persist_findings`),\n`memclaw_insights` (both phases now `_no_db`), `/insights/generate`\n(drops `Depends(get_db)`), and `lifecycle_audit`'s discover pass call\nthe storage client. `resolve_caller_and_gate` + the db-ignoring storage\nhelpers widened to `db: AsyncSession | None` (pure type widening) so the\nroute's `None` threads cleanly.\n\n### Atomicity note\n`_persist_findings`'s `db.begin_nested()` savepoint becomes\nclient-orchestrated: each storage call is its own atomic txn, and the\nexisting \"all findings failed → restore priors\" branch now calls\n`/insights/restore-priors`. The only behavioural delta — priors are\ncommitted-outdated *before* the bulk-create (vs. held in a savepoint) —\nis documented in the docstring.\n\n### Out of scope (PR2)\n`evolve_service` + `memclaw_evolve` + `/evolve/report`, and the\n`_mcp_session` deletion.\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, full suite\n**3584 passed**. New `tests/test_ph5b_insights_storage.py` covers every\nendpoint incl. tenant isolation, scope filters, the COUNT(DISTINCT)\nreads, the JSONB supersede + fleet arm, restore, activity-gate, and 422\nguards.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"f0ae29b0b6a6d18200b675f429ec3c1def4eea6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f0ae29b0b6a6d18200b675f429ec3c1def4eea6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOaU9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp+EQABJuyGhrejXATZT8V6Qhx/rL\n/4EQFxeiaFKAe+GrIRjJR8A4FpkT1OjSCCOJl3uDSph0wbYp97yTeOoo1bSjeob+\n4JDDB7ei1WlO051ZRYuUD0tJ+2MJi0zGXFzwMLykFEHvdw6hG6HSNE8Tca8jjkTZ\nkVuSAqgc2FRESjzZSdHo5lqsrxEW3FF9tcfnTUHRlHILkf3agwzAVHYemGmQqxGa\n7cmUniKhQqUUZUD9fukfVZrePl85Y3uYG15t4iC79RUatRNGpjsK3C76ZTu807RC\nyiBbez6YSkjQGsPTLgBM5cIc+Y1Ath26mNnQR3nMAKtxI9qkoWVPsA/rCJliePAW\nDPX3vYhPyzrUIlZQ+NiwlVSt+5JPmhAolr+2HpY0w4HK0elcYIi5VQ5rOeBpl+Ag\ncU6M3pmNcg1UI/WmHbsNxxd+H+0A/pykyXRS0FbIDuH5lDtPRtuwzlFBuD+EmcFH\npTF6bk5Y17BoiistEHaeITpPdfxDzdcQLho0sPXaJ19wEmQQ5boYzyX91BMZqrCf\nAevsDBo3h4u73fnVE0IQWd7NLhNsQVDnsT5mnROxIs6FmB6ukMOY00oMtfEPofPs\nW7ccso71nFjvzRzvaDuVYj7TxlmXbMchQnkwTfAy4JyBDKTU+aRgjhFJpcg2mSVo\nN4KB4qGYHpmujKfiTtnP\n=HK3w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f0ae29b0b6a6d18200b675f429ec3c1def4eea6d\nparent 81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782162749 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782162749 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): route insights_service through storage (Fix 2 Ph5b, PR1 — insights) (#471)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5b — PR1: route insights_service through core-storage-api\n\nFirst of two Ph5b PRs (**insights** here; **evolve + the `_mcp_session`\ndeletion** in PR2). Moves the insights pipeline off core-api's direct DB\npool. **`_mcp_session` intentionally remains** — `memclaw_evolve` still\nuses it; PR2 deletes it as its final step.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (router `insights.py` +\nPostgresService methods)\nAll explicit-tenant-scoped; analytic reads use SQLAlchemy ORM (sidesteps\nasyncpg array-cast pitfalls):\n- `POST /insights/{contradictions,failures,stale,divergence,patterns}` —\nthe 5 focus reads. `contradictions`/`divergence` keep the `GROUP BY …\nHAVING COUNT(DISTINCT …)` entity pre-query. Return the MEMORY_LIST shape\n(no embedding).\n- `POST /insights/discover-sample` — embedding-bearing sample; numpy\nk-means + cluster summarisation stay client-side.\n- `POST /insights/supersede-priors` + `POST /insights/restore-priors` —\n`_persist_findings`'s prior-outdate (JSONB\n`metadata->>'insight_focus'`/`scope` select + `UPDATE\nstatus='outdated'`, one atomic txn) and the all-failed restore.\n- `POST /insights/activity-gate` — `MAX(created_at)` by\ninsight/non-insight for the lifecycle discover gate.\n\n### core-api migration\n`insights_service` (`_query_*` + `_persist_findings`),\n`memclaw_insights` (both phases now `_no_db`), `/insights/generate`\n(drops `Depends(get_db)`), and `lifecycle_audit`'s discover pass call\nthe storage client. `resolve_caller_and_gate` + the db-ignoring storage\nhelpers widened to `db: AsyncSession | None` (pure type widening) so the\nroute's `None` threads cleanly.\n\n### Atomicity note\n`_persist_findings`'s `db.begin_nested()` savepoint becomes\nclient-orchestrated: each storage call is its own atomic txn, and the\nexisting \"all findings failed → restore priors\" branch now calls\n`/insights/restore-priors`. The only behavioural delta — priors are\ncommitted-outdated *before* the bulk-create (vs. held in a savepoint) —\nis documented in the docstring.\n\n### Out of scope (PR2)\n`evolve_service` + `memclaw_evolve` + `/evolve/report`, and the\n`_mcp_session` deletion.\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, full suite\n**3584 passed**. New `tests/test_ph5b_insights_storage.py` covers every\nendpoint incl. tenant isolation, scope filters, the COUNT(DISTINCT)\nreads, the JSONB supersede + fleet arm, restore, activity-gate, and 422\nguards.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:12:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2655b84a91624b0acf38be564181b3c8dd06e866/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8"}]},{"sha":"81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDgxZTc5YmU1YmQ2NGUwNDdjMjI5Yjk1NWQ4NzE3ZThlN2RlMDRhZjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T15:21:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:21:33Z"},"message":"feat(core-storage-api): route the skill-factory pipeline through storage (Fix 2 Ph5a) (#470)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5a — route the skill-factory pipeline through\ncore-storage-api\n\nFirst of three Ph5 PRs (**5a** skill-factory / 5b\ninsights+evolve+`_mcp_session` deletion / 5c capability_usage). Moves\nthe skill-factory background pipeline's direct DB access onto the\nstorage HTTP client, removing `get_db`/`async_session`/`db.execute` from\n`skill_promoter`, `forge/poison`, `forge/cron_handler`, `session_trace`,\nand `outcome_inference/*`.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (+ PostgresService + storage_client\nmethods)\nAll explicit-tenant-scoped; PG SQL ported verbatim (DISTINCT ON,\nsupersedes self-join, `ON CONFLICT`, `jsonb_set`, `INTERVAL '1 day' *\ncooloff_days`, `ANY(CAST(:ids AS uuid[]))`):\n- **`POST /documents/update-status`** — conditional CAS status flip (the\ndeferred Ph3 endpoint). 404 on a no-op → client `None` → promoter raises\n`AlreadyTransitionedError`.\n- **forge rejected-fingerprints** — write + 3-arm-fleet cooloff-window\npoison check.\n- **session-traces** — batch upsert `ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, run_id,\nagent_id)`.\n- **bespoke memory reads** — session-window, entity-links-batch,\nmemory-content, + the 4 outcome signals (contradiction / supersession /\ncross-agent-reuse / terminal).\n- **`GET`/`DELETE /documents/{collection}/{doc_id:path}`** — now accept\nslashed doc_ids; forge-distilled skills use `forge/<slug>` (the doc_id\nis only ever a bound SQL param, never a filesystem path).\n\n### core-api migration\nCallers moved to the typed client; `lifecycle_audit.forge_distill` stops\nopening its own session and threads `tenant_id`. Adds ORM models\n`ForgeRejectedFingerprint`/`SessionTrace` mirroring migrations 020/021\nfor the test `create_all` path (prod schema stays alembic-owned).\n\n### Notable\nThe `contradictions` signal windows on `created_at`, not the source's\n`COALESCE(updated_at, created_at)` — OSS `memories` has **no**\n`updated_at` column, so the original reference was dead against the real\nschema.\n\n### Out of scope (later PRs)\ninsights/evolve + `_mcp_session` deletion (Ph5b); capability_usage\n(Ph5c).\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, full suite\n**3560 passed**. New `tests/test_ph5a_skill_factory_storage.py` (25\ntests) covers each endpoint incl. tenant isolation, CAS hit/miss, poison\ncooloff window, ON-CONFLICT refresh, and the slashed-doc_id round-trip.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"9f1ee9c50789ceaaf80391d77c221f4ddea72a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9f1ee9c50789ceaaf80391d77c221f4ddea72a9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOVL9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEAAQAFDO94KPghybuH07670yT72/\n0MI4XhlBrO65VffLMhdagbotV9XnZAVANRZ0z7OYmO9O+SuNv+h2/UooGmJiBR2Y\nb4cFg/xVw7ZiXvJTvg6UbWbiHgqg4IVOQt8N+zCXEXafSHr9NE/eFaQZQHq6pPP2\nbE0Fso6loeINzti3gb9A26ERdsbUlwvfijJQkh4F4FaBqNDVWVvSAeYns/HNfkvt\n82ZaHgosBUL/oQNhB4iBVoGFI+6vtpdeVvHliovDpl+AnrpzHAP8i49Q+NqsCanK\njJZdgoj2wPalCnex+5AgAF+PvjU6zYkvNVND4hNh7oqf2O8FOKEBsWFFicezrkl2\nj+Zzq5ZVWGHyv89THm7Fk5lDDr6kQ1KD97M5z+9knZbxRSZ1u7PMJCm3Aq/wHhQD\nL8DMpoxMcQMo3SqRfrTCgDh87honjyU355yFLchnFRBzAlWqalxaTchiiR6lgOIF\nB1sKPRwYaUf0Apsklztd6fn8elJa6EdWIi0vVuxqctsb0Yq+4D50m3xtIHM/LWvK\n4Zo9afAAv53wRrXRk8YJBM1u07Sc9uODayRHC7ohzDmVarCyF1oXTtmKvU32SM9/\no6PYAW0EkRiot0Xzom9itT1fRzco6qQtaIV4CDb0OZN+kyDoyD6ycEOHPLPreDvD\nJo9TnLU2PJC9rujue2bc\n=LsOl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f1ee9c50789ceaaf80391d77c221f4ddea72a9c\nparent 1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782141693 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782141693 +0300\n\nfeat(core-storage-api): route the skill-factory pipeline through storage (Fix 2 Ph5a) (#470)\n\n## Fix 2 Ph5a — route the skill-factory pipeline through\ncore-storage-api\n\nFirst of three Ph5 PRs (**5a** skill-factory / 5b\ninsights+evolve+`_mcp_session` deletion / 5c capability_usage). Moves\nthe skill-factory background pipeline's direct DB access onto the\nstorage HTTP client, removing `get_db`/`async_session`/`db.execute` from\n`skill_promoter`, `forge/poison`, `forge/cron_handler`, `session_trace`,\nand `outcome_inference/*`.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (+ PostgresService + storage_client\nmethods)\nAll explicit-tenant-scoped; PG SQL ported verbatim (DISTINCT ON,\nsupersedes self-join, `ON CONFLICT`, `jsonb_set`, `INTERVAL '1 day' *\ncooloff_days`, `ANY(CAST(:ids AS uuid[]))`):\n- **`POST /documents/update-status`** — conditional CAS status flip (the\ndeferred Ph3 endpoint). 404 on a no-op → client `None` → promoter raises\n`AlreadyTransitionedError`.\n- **forge rejected-fingerprints** — write + 3-arm-fleet cooloff-window\npoison check.\n- **session-traces** — batch upsert `ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, run_id,\nagent_id)`.\n- **bespoke memory reads** — session-window, entity-links-batch,\nmemory-content, + the 4 outcome signals (contradiction / supersession /\ncross-agent-reuse / terminal).\n- **`GET`/`DELETE /documents/{collection}/{doc_id:path}`** — now accept\nslashed doc_ids; forge-distilled skills use `forge/<slug>` (the doc_id\nis only ever a bound SQL param, never a filesystem path).\n\n### core-api migration\nCallers moved to the typed client; `lifecycle_audit.forge_distill` stops\nopening its own session and threads `tenant_id`. Adds ORM models\n`ForgeRejectedFingerprint`/`SessionTrace` mirroring migrations 020/021\nfor the test `create_all` path (prod schema stays alembic-owned).\n\n### Notable\nThe `contradictions` signal windows on `created_at`, not the source's\n`COALESCE(updated_at, created_at)` — OSS `memories` has **no**\n`updated_at` column, so the original reference was dead against the real\nschema.\n\n### Out of scope (later PRs)\ninsights/evolve + `_mcp_session` deletion (Ph5b); capability_usage\n(Ph5c).\n\n### Gates\nruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`, mypy both projects, full suite\n**3560 passed**. New `tests/test_ph5a_skill_factory_storage.py` (25\ntests) covers each endpoint incl. tenant isolation, CAS hit/miss, poison\ncooloff window, ON-CONFLICT refresh, and the slashed-doc_id round-trip.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T15:21:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/81e79be5bd64e047c229b955d8717e8e7de04af8/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172"}]},{"sha":"1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFmMDgyZDg3ODNhMGY0ZGUwM2NkNjI5Yjc5ZDY2ZTk3ODIwMjYxNzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T13:49:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T13:49:20Z"},"message":"perf(core-api): make document-ingest (kreuzberg) an opt-in extra to cut cold start (#469)\n\n## Why\ncore-api Cloud Run `startup_latencies` p99 is **36–58s** — the real\nsource of the load-test `single_write`/search latency tails (the handler\nis fast: p99 ~1.6s; pgvector 241ms; TEI 17ms). Profiling showed the\n**logged** app startup is only ~9s (and the `agent-backfill` lifespan\nstep is already a no-op in this mode), so the remaining 30s+ is\n**pre-process**: container image pull (**183MB** compressed) +\ncold-instance interpreter/imports.\n\n## What\nShrink the default image by making the **64MB `kreuzberg`**\ndocument-extraction lib an **opt-in `ingest` extra**:\n- `kreuzberg` → `[project.optional-dependencies] ingest`; the `dev`\nextra keeps it so CI/local still run the ingest tests.\n- `ingest_service` guards the import at **top level** (`try/except\nImportError → kreuzberg = None`, rule-compliant — no inline imports);\n`_extract_with_kreuzberg` raises a clear **501** when the extra is\nabsent. Every non-ingest path is unchanged.\n- Dockerfile builds the slim image by default; **`--build-arg\nWITH_INGEST=1`** re-adds the extra for deployments serving `/ingest/*`.\n\n## Honest scope\nThis is a **moderate** cold-start reduction (drops the kreuzberg tree +\nits import cost), **not** a full fix — a 150MB+ Python image has an\ninherent ~20s+ cold-start floor. The next-largest lever is\n**google-cloud-aiplatform (~99MB)**; making it conditional on the Vertex\nprovider is a follow-up.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src) ✓; `mypy\ncore-api/src` ✓ (192 files).\n- `uv.lock` regenerated: default export (`--extra pubsub`) **excludes**\nkreuzberg; `--extra ingest` **includes** it.\n- `pytest` ✓ — **54 ingest tests pass**, including a new test that\n`_extract_with_kreuzberg` returns 501 when kreuzberg is absent.\n\nCompanion to the harness cold-start-attribution finding\n([caura-test-automation\n#172](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-test-automation/pull/172)).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ecc7ee69edb73090b2963fb0939e82caa95d837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8ecc7ee69edb73090b2963fb0939e82caa95d837"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOT1gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcxcQAJjMCVuaDD/LIivb5J3SLsFL\nFs69Euo0x3IKyaSR7Lcn2P4nQjFS48/oWMLpdLSut2xNUWN6yteKC7QnOsMagnzr\nTaJA34HYMzsdE5sjSOp4O8PUAKcVnGd7SBJQCLAnB20Tk1IDDMbEIg6Bu3o0BAx/\nWQ/l0ZkeXR7A3IqXMyYHJndbWdhlcRiVUbGmkQncx94349mcjDD7npKUWbKn1kKv\nHta37IRaeyTlWDTatWG8uamYPl1uTM25v3LRrYAS45cF+c4tmWU/F+4HcFze00QZ\nFFfHMFtppe/fYhSRSRfbtB4h/i+hDVAjPTiTMY+QiBPoXyFDVWcBW8LSP492CCTb\nnOg6GG+/RUD46Aqt0tC8sO9G7fE4IgadSJs1GzlcPraMXVqoRdQJbHsOVg6tU1th\n/zK9JQSwrI8vxRF1gTlAnupsxHqdanbBNcqdC3PO0u7RpbERD1fqDykV5s3d2Tca\n5ozc+3yFI/vhajakp/MRHedylHiarpF9Vko1t/vUWrbTsG6K7K8KK7JoV32Ai0qq\nMJXnFUfPqiMRzoc0wBUO+jNrKNpoO87Ls4XngcawI+ad1j0DZVABDiXC/mfsrRzu\nIdSRjfjKg3eyqi56pNxC+FNwxN4yPvwwkgWpqTmpw6fqIimkh1/YycrrFkqGqlmA\nhVx+k7uiwnkWW41huEsa\n=uAIc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8ecc7ee69edb73090b2963fb0939e82caa95d837\nparent 56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782136160 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782136160 +0300\n\nperf(core-api): make document-ingest (kreuzberg) an opt-in extra to cut cold start (#469)\n\n## Why\ncore-api Cloud Run `startup_latencies` p99 is **36–58s** — the real\nsource of the load-test `single_write`/search latency tails (the handler\nis fast: p99 ~1.6s; pgvector 241ms; TEI 17ms). Profiling showed the\n**logged** app startup is only ~9s (and the `agent-backfill` lifespan\nstep is already a no-op in this mode), so the remaining 30s+ is\n**pre-process**: container image pull (**183MB** compressed) +\ncold-instance interpreter/imports.\n\n## What\nShrink the default image by making the **64MB `kreuzberg`**\ndocument-extraction lib an **opt-in `ingest` extra**:\n- `kreuzberg` → `[project.optional-dependencies] ingest`; the `dev`\nextra keeps it so CI/local still run the ingest tests.\n- `ingest_service` guards the import at **top level** (`try/except\nImportError → kreuzberg = None`, rule-compliant — no inline imports);\n`_extract_with_kreuzberg` raises a clear **501** when the extra is\nabsent. Every non-ingest path is unchanged.\n- Dockerfile builds the slim image by default; **`--build-arg\nWITH_INGEST=1`** re-adds the extra for deployments serving `/ingest/*`.\n\n## Honest scope\nThis is a **moderate** cold-start reduction (drops the kreuzberg tree +\nits import cost), **not** a full fix — a 150MB+ Python image has an\ninherent ~20s+ cold-start floor. The next-largest lever is\n**google-cloud-aiplatform (~99MB)**; making it conditional on the Vertex\nprovider is a follow-up.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` (core-api/src) ✓; `mypy\ncore-api/src` ✓ (192 files).\n- `uv.lock` regenerated: default export (`--extra pubsub`) **excludes**\nkreuzberg; `--extra ingest` **includes** it.\n- `pytest` ✓ — **54 ingest tests pass**, including a new test that\n`_extract_with_kreuzberg` returns 501 when kreuzberg is absent.\n\nCompanion to the harness cold-start-attribution finding\n([caura-test-automation\n#172](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-test-automation/pull/172)).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T13:49:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1f082d8783a0f4de03cd629b79d66e9782026172/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70"}]},{"sha":"56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU2ZGIxZjVmYWRiN2UzYWJjMjRjZjJlZjZhZWM3ZGYzZDM1YWJkNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T13:01:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T13:01:07Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): resolve home fleet on omitted fleet_id for MCP writes (#465)\n\n## Why\n\nValidated follow-up **B1** from the \"One Skill Company Brain\" review. An\nMCP write that **omits `fleet_id`** persists `fleet_id=NULL`, and a\nNULL-fleet row silently drops out of teammates' `scope_team` /\nfleet-filtered recall. REST already resolves the agent's **home fleet**\non omit (`routes/memories.py:937` single, `:1125` bulk) — MCP did not,\nso the *same* write scoped differently by transport. This also hit\n`memclaw_doc op=write collection=skills`, i.e. the \"publish a skill, the\nfleet inherits it\" flow could strand a skill at `fleet_id=NULL`.\n\nGrounded: `enforce_fleet_write` returns the home-fleet-bearing agent but\nthe MCP paths discarded it; the shared `create_memory` service uses\n`data.fleet_id` as-is (no backfill). No fleet ContextVar / `X-Fleet-ID`\nheader / `?fleet_id=` parse exists at the MCP layer, so the kwarg was\nthe only source.\n\n## Change\n\nTwo sites in `core_api/mcp_server.py` (`memclaw_write` and `memclaw_doc\nop=write`): capture the agent `enforce_fleet_write` already returns and\nbackfill before the write:\n\n```python\nagent = await enforce_fleet_write(db, tenant_id, agent_id, fleet_id)\nif not fleet_id and agent.get(\"fleet_id\"):\n    fleet_id = agent[\"fleet_id\"]\n```\n\n### Safety (no existing flow touched)\n- **Explicit writes untouched** — backfill fires only when `fleet_id` is\nfalsy; an explicit (incl. cross-fleet) value is unchanged.\n- **No new cross-fleet surface** — `enforce_fleet_write` runs *first*\nwith the original value; the backfill target is always the agent's\n**own** home fleet (always self-writable), so no re-enforcement needed\n(mirrors REST's order-independence here).\n- **Worst case unchanged** — agent with no home fleet → no-op → row\nstays NULL. Closing that residual (seed home fleet from the connection\n`?fleet_id=`) is a separate decision, not this PR.\n- **Batch** — `BulkMemoryItem` inherits fleet from the parent, so one\ntop-level backfill covers the whole batch.\n\n## Tests\n`memclaw_write`: omit→home · explicit-untouched · batch omit→home ·\n**no-home-fleet→NULL** (guards against over-claiming). `memclaw_doc\nop=write`: omit→home · explicit-untouched. The pre-existing\n`persists_null` test is clarified to the no-home-fleet case it actually\ncovers. All 6 pass; `ruff check core-api/src/` + mypy clean on the\ntouched file.\n\n## Out of scope (flagged)\n`memclaw_evolve` / `memclaw_insights` / `memclaw_keystones_set` also\ntake `fleet_id` (different default scope) — audit separately. Layer 2\n(connection-fleet seeding) is its own ticket. Static skill's `fleet_id`\nwarning text becomes partially stale post-merge — to be updated in the\nseparate skill-reconciliation work.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c97544be9004b0851cc29cf8d102ba3769e7ef5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3c97544be9004b0851cc29cf8d102ba3769e7ef5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOTITCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyFYQAD1H1hcPyieZhXkPSwQpPJDg\n0sM9AfdvfGCroOLL2Jujag0aD+eFVOm38idMB2zpYLkC0HW2g5aEw8oWMLXRwd6K\nk09dAkHczwE9iVS/BDG84y87sv2qM4l4txsrYegxooJedik1viFRBG8mpIHY1uBL\nGfsDKeEjuCtN7BqNGxyuxG0CHfRTYx+RGhadlmJfAKnw3Sz2yyBXx+Cx08ufLeSe\nxQi53zUnDiTyEVVX60GQwYBprNeMJ3xmZetAqIn8m1ikeShproqBosbqlBu4h1sS\nFcTgA225muZ0G6hon+o2K2zjsFGyteEnOEsHUtQQzy+OEftB5NTPvchNCd0X0JrS\nKf+VaBkTrAcYtYeybLRlAwl84KxctNgWZOXHNF+rVt74ze1JXyUi9vKIHNFoDfHc\ndwgBjhJlVU51uZG35wvJBXxJEwWg//eTMz8PkcVevTDVqz8UbBbqjYy1PuGQ2+91\nyNNA3ThfPDIta6NRP6Z1N6hAxkOJufGrXGSGv5dD8/JcsVrV9hlO6qTWMrrOR2tz\nTAMb78w6D/XpI0kPwWD1S+p5bfW5vixBd/5B1g+mKGTNcUHiiReZelVzfm+glntI\n7gPKRgdEVTa66vx2GhsCWTp9D3YczevZllF+5sBGHW7VxMk/+uQzN5Z5agKRS80f\n4BqeET4aVyOb06NptlFi\n=T7gN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c97544be9004b0851cc29cf8d102ba3769e7ef5\nparent bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1782133267 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782133267 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): resolve home fleet on omitted fleet_id for MCP writes (#465)\n\n## Why\n\nValidated follow-up **B1** from the \"One Skill Company Brain\" review. An\nMCP write that **omits `fleet_id`** persists `fleet_id=NULL`, and a\nNULL-fleet row silently drops out of teammates' `scope_team` /\nfleet-filtered recall. REST already resolves the agent's **home fleet**\non omit (`routes/memories.py:937` single, `:1125` bulk) — MCP did not,\nso the *same* write scoped differently by transport. This also hit\n`memclaw_doc op=write collection=skills`, i.e. the \"publish a skill, the\nfleet inherits it\" flow could strand a skill at `fleet_id=NULL`.\n\nGrounded: `enforce_fleet_write` returns the home-fleet-bearing agent but\nthe MCP paths discarded it; the shared `create_memory` service uses\n`data.fleet_id` as-is (no backfill). No fleet ContextVar / `X-Fleet-ID`\nheader / `?fleet_id=` parse exists at the MCP layer, so the kwarg was\nthe only source.\n\n## Change\n\nTwo sites in `core_api/mcp_server.py` (`memclaw_write` and `memclaw_doc\nop=write`): capture the agent `enforce_fleet_write` already returns and\nbackfill before the write:\n\n```python\nagent = await enforce_fleet_write(db, tenant_id, agent_id, fleet_id)\nif not fleet_id and agent.get(\"fleet_id\"):\n    fleet_id = agent[\"fleet_id\"]\n```\n\n### Safety (no existing flow touched)\n- **Explicit writes untouched** — backfill fires only when `fleet_id` is\nfalsy; an explicit (incl. cross-fleet) value is unchanged.\n- **No new cross-fleet surface** — `enforce_fleet_write` runs *first*\nwith the original value; the backfill target is always the agent's\n**own** home fleet (always self-writable), so no re-enforcement needed\n(mirrors REST's order-independence here).\n- **Worst case unchanged** — agent with no home fleet → no-op → row\nstays NULL. Closing that residual (seed home fleet from the connection\n`?fleet_id=`) is a separate decision, not this PR.\n- **Batch** — `BulkMemoryItem` inherits fleet from the parent, so one\ntop-level backfill covers the whole batch.\n\n## Tests\n`memclaw_write`: omit→home · explicit-untouched · batch omit→home ·\n**no-home-fleet→NULL** (guards against over-claiming). `memclaw_doc\nop=write`: omit→home · explicit-untouched. The pre-existing\n`persists_null` test is clarified to the no-home-fleet case it actually\ncovers. All 6 pass; `ruff check core-api/src/` + mypy clean on the\ntouched file.\n\n## Out of scope (flagged)\n`memclaw_evolve` / `memclaw_insights` / `memclaw_keystones_set` also\ntake `fleet_id` (different default scope) — audit separately. Layer 2\n(connection-fleet seeding) is its own ticket. Static skill's `fleet_id`\nwarning text becomes partially stale post-merge — to be updated in the\nseparate skill-reconciliation work.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T13:01:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/56db1f5fadb7e3abc24cf2ef6aec7df3d35abd70/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373"}]},{"sha":"bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJlYzgyMjk3ODU3NDFiOTU0MjQ3MThhNWZkMzhhMzg3YmJmOGMzNzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T12:20:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T12:20:45Z"},"message":"fix(core-storage-api): 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding write (#468)\n\n## 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding write\n\nFollow-up to the post-merge review on\n[#467](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/467#issuecomment-4767916672).\n\n#467 scoped `memory_update_embedding`'s UPDATE to `tenant_id`, but the\nmethod stayed `-> None` and the route always returned `{\"ok\": True}` —\nso a wrong-tenant call was a silent 200 no-op, and\n`crystallizer_service._remediate_missing_embeddings` counted it as a\nsuccessful patch (inflating the remediated tally in its log).\n\n### Change\n- `memory_update_embedding` → `-> bool`, returns `(result.rowcount or 0)\n> 0` (mirrors `memory_update_status`).\n- `PATCH /memories/{id}/embedding` raises **404** on a no-op instead of\n200 (consistent with `PATCH /memories/{id}`); the client then returns\n`None`.\n- crystallizer increments `patched` only when the write actually landed.\n\n### Reachability\nThe mismatch is **unreachable in practice today** —\n`_remediate_missing_embeddings` fetches candidates scoped to `tenant_id`\nand writes with that same tenant, so the counter was already accurate.\nThis is a consistency + defense-in-depth fix so the three by-id ops\nbehave uniformly. (`mark_dedup_checked` is intentionally left as a bulk\n200 — per-row 404 doesn't fit a bulk stamp, and it has no\nsuccess-counter caller.)\n\n### Tests\nExtended `test_update_embedding_wrong_tenant_is_noop` to assert the\nwrong-tenant call now returns `None` (404) and the same-tenant call\nreturns `{\"ok\": True}`. Gates: ruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`,\nmypy both projects, full suite **3530 passed**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"5860e5bd25f0ccebf3e9e2afcfb57add51869cf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5860e5bd25f0ccebf3e9e2afcfb57add51869cf9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOSidCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvtEQAD8zB9R0lPGdieGH7Y8abDCg\nj2xB9922ktLWlX7IkTyHYFQ1AY5lsRr2tqgYD6/fFbAz0/+ygnagrYMQyd2BowTr\nBX8TYfrBgbafmvW17zKqQSIGDS/zydyxfkdqbTqCgqjGe3V8z+vaILg1zcirzj8V\nTlR2GUmgwppFD5aXIp1arXqPTf3+BpZus65Ti0DU42FCSX1tcZP3Pvs6XH11XC8l\n7NUe9tcXMuKOq7SGi/cZhtckLnmHEbuv2RESaM/t74Di9xbNK3oBow6BHxtnTbpV\nZ/aeLHJXfLagJfZJ0qe1H/assev/vFz+F+3j5Jg23gW6OzBr1BPB2KNvei37hSJB\nZDCGPeg1T0M2N7xlx+IFm4VgYHr167SVin9799QsfpwEq9ET1UMiQvFiAVcWercT\nwneqgIHdUqpw1tZgP0gcEwFx8zx8hkSYnNvlyAlYF74brmtUNx5GLrkWXnJCaRWG\nVQOcIZY4fNZSZXnsW46DyogJ+nQjh4KL66fJGIFWG4AQtMOiCVbfgsX4tUDzbU3Q\nAOXxMsIge1dQ5cSTxiHulmPf0xWHKlWU7MvWnsE6k9Mf0vTyyJ6kYuQd3oJbOqsf\nWJlrhwu4cNJJv4pkUl2YKfiOXfZA1aDOLSe5BUyoGGf15QF5hFOfJkDZ9tJvQluo\nMtPHq0uF5IHBa9adCmYJ\n=QxRQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5860e5bd25f0ccebf3e9e2afcfb57add51869cf9\nparent 4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782130845 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782130845 +0300\n\nfix(core-storage-api): 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding write (#468)\n\n## 404 (not silent 200) on wrong-tenant embedding write\n\nFollow-up to the post-merge review on\n[#467](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/467#issuecomment-4767916672).\n\n#467 scoped `memory_update_embedding`'s UPDATE to `tenant_id`, but the\nmethod stayed `-> None` and the route always returned `{\"ok\": True}` —\nso a wrong-tenant call was a silent 200 no-op, and\n`crystallizer_service._remediate_missing_embeddings` counted it as a\nsuccessful patch (inflating the remediated tally in its log).\n\n### Change\n- `memory_update_embedding` → `-> bool`, returns `(result.rowcount or 0)\n> 0` (mirrors `memory_update_status`).\n- `PATCH /memories/{id}/embedding` raises **404** on a no-op instead of\n200 (consistent with `PATCH /memories/{id}`); the client then returns\n`None`.\n- crystallizer increments `patched` only when the write actually landed.\n\n### Reachability\nThe mismatch is **unreachable in practice today** —\n`_remediate_missing_embeddings` fetches candidates scoped to `tenant_id`\nand writes with that same tenant, so the counter was already accurate.\nThis is a consistency + defense-in-depth fix so the three by-id ops\nbehave uniformly. (`mark_dedup_checked` is intentionally left as a bulk\n200 — per-row 404 doesn't fit a bulk stamp, and it has no\nsuccess-counter caller.)\n\n### Tests\nExtended `test_update_embedding_wrong_tenant_is_noop` to assert the\nwrong-tenant call now returns `None` (404) and the same-tenant call\nreturns `{\"ok\": True}`. Gates: ruff@0.15.4 check + `format --check`,\nmypy both projects, full suite **3530 passed**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T12:20:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bec8229785741b95424718a5fd38a387bbf8c373/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e"}]},{"sha":"4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQyNDhiNGRiNTFmNWJlNDZkNDcyNjBmYjViNmNjMzRkYTA3NWZkMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T11:46:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:46:22Z"},"message":"fix(core-storage-api): tenant-guard by-id memory UPDATEs (#467)\n\n## Tenant-guard the by-id memory UPDATEs\n\nContinues the \"no DB outside core-storage-api\" migration's hardening:\nevery by-id memory **write** that core-api routes through\ncore-storage-api is now scoped to the row's **home tenant**, so a\nwrong-tenant `memory_id` can never mutate a foreign row.\n\n### Ops hardened (`PostgresService`)\n| Op | Route | Guard |\n|---|---|---|\n| `memory_update` | `PATCH /memories/{id}` (content PATCH —\nuser-reachable) | scope the `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` existence check **and\nboth** UPDATEs (column `values` + the raw JSONB metadata-merge) to\n`tenant_id` |\n| `memory_update_embedding` | `PATCH /memories/{id}/embedding`\n(worker/backfill) | scope the UPDATE |\n| `memory_mark_dedup_checked` | `POST /memories/mark-dedup-checked` |\nscope the bulk `last_dedup_checked_at` stamp to `Memory.id.in_(ids) AND\ntenant_id` |\n\n### Threading\n`tenant_id` is a **required** argument end-to-end: storage routes (422\nif missing) → typed storage client → every caller. Each caller passes\nthe row's **HOME** tenant — `routes/testing.py` uses the\nalready-verified `row[\"tenant_id\"]`; the governance / crystallizer /\nmemory_service callers pass their in-scope `tenant_id`. The two\n`memory_service` callers that previously reached into the private\n`sc._patch` now go through the guarded `sc.update_memory`.\n\n### Out of scope (by design)\n- `memory_update_status` — its cross-tenant write guard lands on the\nPhase 4 PR (#432); left untouched here to avoid a merge conflict.\n- `memory_increment_recall` — deferred (internal counter, repo-direct,\nalready tenant-scoped ids).\n- Entity by-id updates are already tenant-guarded.\n\n### Tests\n`tests/test_tenant_guard_byid_updates.py` (mirrors\n`tests/test_ph3_storage_documents_fleet.py`): wrong-tenant write = no-op\n(row untouched / 404 / silent skip), same-tenant write applies, and each\nroute 422s without `tenant_id`. Existing caller tests updated for the\nnew signature.\n\nGates: ruff check + `format --check` (0.15.4), mypy both projects, full\nsuite **3516 passed**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"ab03ee1d3748cf4c4e8d9db4e14ca6c602d1cb36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ab03ee1d3748cf4c4e8d9db4e14ca6c602d1cb36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOSCOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2tQQAG0/edjbMGK855Dl5lIPNAwY\ncZpFHaJUxGLEx6KbSn06zyy6CxoZ59w0EP/4TSoZkMVRFkJD09M6/C8zAD4ZQ4Qt\nfKDLUABE6CBymlZ2q8kbjjGQ01OjGT/0PRIbigQ4hQBxcMpcRSv4f5CEEWyscnuH\nJTT3kVqY/ia5N7Uyhl/S6ssDy1WXmkspKQLxBWoEmhwwEj7hJb71oLbGo6QsFIh0\nC8qzPJTXgd6LVDYBxddrrkOJk9j0WaB4ewPvUMOlo9KDyjWOYOMlCy/fnMKfgoFi\nLqbPeX4T33B0DJDCAqalQWz09KijR95k8dbYvNFSJoYyjO+0xasXG+lNDQ9+rUt6\n4G8Y7xnW5tRQ/JJDvVRieL5w4KXeCB2TaEBaQ+b+AhVAOUvciuBaf0MlD6Xu/Ffp\nkfgj4b2NI9GCShbaBR3bcL5Ou1TiLe2eQ2m8nr8q6FGQUA7XUGdzUlrSedsH2Slg\nLHk4zG8FoI8uSjWLU8FvvEoeo+YGbySbw48EryTpu9AOzsTSpyAALFKO4perWn/t\ndTLj7llTyFvvWN2FJBsft98k+crXciB+YT+lluMT6P7yl8qSu2i2eWX3RFDGUUZL\nK3SGDYdBDnft8hUcbzpx6GdVbbQFsOkIDDtqwQvlgUmUjupoFzdZIQCTDkWaIh+H\nKY/hnbvcDVFc88qpxQ7x\n=3H8c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ab03ee1d3748cf4c4e8d9db4e14ca6c602d1cb36\nparent cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782128782 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782128782 +0300\n\nfix(core-storage-api): tenant-guard by-id memory UPDATEs (#467)\n\n## Tenant-guard the by-id memory UPDATEs\n\nContinues the \"no DB outside core-storage-api\" migration's hardening:\nevery by-id memory **write** that core-api routes through\ncore-storage-api is now scoped to the row's **home tenant**, so a\nwrong-tenant `memory_id` can never mutate a foreign row.\n\n### Ops hardened (`PostgresService`)\n| Op | Route | Guard |\n|---|---|---|\n| `memory_update` | `PATCH /memories/{id}` (content PATCH —\nuser-reachable) | scope the `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` existence check **and\nboth** UPDATEs (column `values` + the raw JSONB metadata-merge) to\n`tenant_id` |\n| `memory_update_embedding` | `PATCH /memories/{id}/embedding`\n(worker/backfill) | scope the UPDATE |\n| `memory_mark_dedup_checked` | `POST /memories/mark-dedup-checked` |\nscope the bulk `last_dedup_checked_at` stamp to `Memory.id.in_(ids) AND\ntenant_id` |\n\n### Threading\n`tenant_id` is a **required** argument end-to-end: storage routes (422\nif missing) → typed storage client → every caller. Each caller passes\nthe row's **HOME** tenant — `routes/testing.py` uses the\nalready-verified `row[\"tenant_id\"]`; the governance / crystallizer /\nmemory_service callers pass their in-scope `tenant_id`. The two\n`memory_service` callers that previously reached into the private\n`sc._patch` now go through the guarded `sc.update_memory`.\n\n### Out of scope (by design)\n- `memory_update_status` — its cross-tenant write guard lands on the\nPhase 4 PR (#432); left untouched here to avoid a merge conflict.\n- `memory_increment_recall` — deferred (internal counter, repo-direct,\nalready tenant-scoped ids).\n- Entity by-id updates are already tenant-guarded.\n\n### Tests\n`tests/test_tenant_guard_byid_updates.py` (mirrors\n`tests/test_ph3_storage_documents_fleet.py`): wrong-tenant write = no-op\n(row untouched / 404 / silent skip), same-tenant write applies, and each\nroute 422s without `tenant_id`. Existing caller tests updated for the\nnew signature.\n\nGates: ruff check + `format --check` (0.15.4), mypy both projects, full\nsuite **3516 passed**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T11:46:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4248b4db51f5be46d47260fb5b6cc34da075fd2e/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0"}]},{"sha":"cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNjMWM0NmIyZWJhODliNzUzMDUzYmFkNTg0N2NhMjgyOGI4ODA1ZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T11:37:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:37:42Z"},"message":"chore(core-api): attribute single_write latency (dedup lookup + storage_total_ms) (#466)\n\n## Why\n`slo-p99-single_write`: ~**18.6s p99** with ~**575ms p50** on staging.\nInvestigation showed the report's \"move enrichment to a worker\" fix is\n**already live** (staging defers both enrichment and embedding off the\nhot path), so the tail is downstream — storage-DB contention (likely\n**CAURA-686** PG row-lock on the insert) or core-api-side overhead. To\nlocalise it before changing code, the write path needs to attribute time\nacross its storage roundtrips.\n\n## What\nToday only `WriteMemoryRow`'s insert is timed (`storage_ms`). The dedup\nlookup (`GET /memories/by-content-hash` in `CheckExactDuplicate`) was an\n**untimed** slice of `total_ms`, leaving `total_ms - storage_ms` an\nundifferentiated bucket. This PR:\n- Times the dedup lookup → `phase_timings[\"dedup_lookup_ms\"]` (mirrors\n`storage_ms`/`entity_links_ms`).\n- Surfaces `dedup_lookup_ms` + a derived `storage_total_ms` (dedup +\ninsert + entity-links) in the existing `memory_write_latency` log.\n\n`total_ms - storage_total_ms` is then **pure core-api-side time** — the\nsplit that tells us whether the 18.6s tail is storage-DB or core-api.\nAdditive only, no behaviour change.\n\n## How we'll use it\nQuery `memory_write_latency` p99 of `storage_total_ms` vs the residual,\nand pair with the existing `GET /api/v1/storage/_debug/pg_locks` toolkit\n(+ `scripts/capture_pg_locks_during_storm.py`) under a\nsame-(tenant,fleet) write burst to confirm/refute `Lock/transactionid`\non `INSERT INTO memories` (CAURA-686).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/pipeline/test_write_pipeline.py::test_check_exact_duplicate_records_dedup_lookup_ms`\n(pure unit). Local gate: `ruff check core-api/src/` ✓, `ruff format\n--check` ✓, `mypy core-api/src/` ✓ (192 files), unit tests ✓.\n\nCompanion to the noisy-neighbor fix in #464.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b2515eee3781a3c0174dc6ee466b8ecc5608bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0b2515eee3781a3c0174dc6ee466b8ecc5608bac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOR6GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgqkQAA5MRmLaNj44zZNIPrGgig11\nkOiwJhkEu3hF2xEKLPzp1l3HL2nJWSAqiUJIyGxXp8WV55R7qKmhTmn9xiYXu00U\nfCdtKj5AWl3LbaPHYl3TXLnp54h78a4qU+00sxaMt2WDpNYGOZCgM9VTEIPRpqe0\nrlmc1WDq1tScY/T7w6xRRl91zBBBd4gLUjgOZNKiXPikrAVvLPUdkvqqieDCdHm4\n/ZS4zmMvC1GwkewUFrojKv5eX7v8rlUDY/SFs9UW3YLZ1gdHLCEbW0EUqSP65JDm\njqFzLbEfnjflHL0cQv39bhfqQnrXh1cGuyeAzzZiv6/afM6hRuHmYVvX4AcTJ6DZ\nWs8vquFDdb3+ZVHE/UcJgm6sMXSgLiv8SVdKJfq1EnCeqY+nxR8rf5Nz5mAiB0MZ\nX3Uudy9a9B3G7Akn7rF4022sihq0gTB1oCoW/wh05VORIus+uNSq7ihTH0gRl+R2\nHC4SRyHB2Ig+LOTMn25c8HN6csGCsoRDHTLQC8CbGQdJs5yW4fMHT3+ClIr6GHMA\nu6GxKVfE1Wi/8Ax8v8OKAzXVi/CIJIyZP+IRl628G07BMhDd9KHQXpuLrWd5U3ps\nYOWMqrSGe2i9x5eCqK+PZtyz/fpedQXMTw/CN6v9rrZkseBfCLxgsVs9Htss9PPc\nv8XN2osjVS+reVPOkhbq\n=VBsk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0b2515eee3781a3c0174dc6ee466b8ecc5608bac\nparent 043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782128262 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782128262 +0300\n\nchore(core-api): attribute single_write latency (dedup lookup + storage_total_ms) (#466)\n\n## Why\n`slo-p99-single_write`: ~**18.6s p99** with ~**575ms p50** on staging.\nInvestigation showed the report's \"move enrichment to a worker\" fix is\n**already live** (staging defers both enrichment and embedding off the\nhot path), so the tail is downstream — storage-DB contention (likely\n**CAURA-686** PG row-lock on the insert) or core-api-side overhead. To\nlocalise it before changing code, the write path needs to attribute time\nacross its storage roundtrips.\n\n## What\nToday only `WriteMemoryRow`'s insert is timed (`storage_ms`). The dedup\nlookup (`GET /memories/by-content-hash` in `CheckExactDuplicate`) was an\n**untimed** slice of `total_ms`, leaving `total_ms - storage_ms` an\nundifferentiated bucket. This PR:\n- Times the dedup lookup → `phase_timings[\"dedup_lookup_ms\"]` (mirrors\n`storage_ms`/`entity_links_ms`).\n- Surfaces `dedup_lookup_ms` + a derived `storage_total_ms` (dedup +\ninsert + entity-links) in the existing `memory_write_latency` log.\n\n`total_ms - storage_total_ms` is then **pure core-api-side time** — the\nsplit that tells us whether the 18.6s tail is storage-DB or core-api.\nAdditive only, no behaviour change.\n\n## How we'll use it\nQuery `memory_write_latency` p99 of `storage_total_ms` vs the residual,\nand pair with the existing `GET /api/v1/storage/_debug/pg_locks` toolkit\n(+ `scripts/capture_pg_locks_during_storm.py`) under a\nsame-(tenant,fleet) write burst to confirm/refute `Lock/transactionid`\non `INSERT INTO memories` (CAURA-686).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/pipeline/test_write_pipeline.py::test_check_exact_duplicate_records_dedup_lookup_ms`\n(pure unit). Local gate: `ruff check core-api/src/` ✓, `ruff format\n--check` ✓, `mypy core-api/src/` ✓ (192 files), unit tests ✓.\n\nCompanion to the noisy-neighbor fix in #464.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T11:37:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cc1c46b2eba89b753053bad5847ca2828b8805f0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e"}]},{"sha":"043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA0M2MwMmU1ZGY0YTEwOTg4MWRhYmY5MDJjMTk2OTM3MWNmM2IwOGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T11:32:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:32:59Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): per-tenant embed concurrency cap (noisy-neighbor-search) (#464)\n\n## Problem\n`noisy-neighbor-search` from the latest loadtest: a single tenant's\n20-concurrency search storm degraded **another** tenant's search p95 by\n**6.43×** while Cloud Run CPU was idle. Root cause confirmed via live\ninfra pull — the embedding backend `staging-memclaw-tei` is pinned at\n`minScale=2, maxScale=2, containerConcurrency=10` (1 GPU each) → only\n**~20 concurrent embedding slots platform-wide, no autoscale**. A hot\ntenant's query embeddings fill all 20 slots; other tenants' query embeds\nqueue behind them. Route-level `per_tenant_slot(\"search\")=32` is\nper-tenant and too coarse — it doesn't protect *across* tenants at the\nshared embedding backend.\n\n## Fix\nCap concurrent embedding-backend calls **per tenant**, reusing the\nexisting `per_tenant_slot` bulkhead:\n- New `\"embed\"` scope in `middleware/per_tenant_concurrency.py` +\n`per_tenant_embed_concurrency` config knob (**default 6**).\n- The slot wraps **only the single-flight cold-miss leader** in\n`memory_service._get_or_cache_embedding` (the one call that actually\nhits TEI) — cache hits and in-flight joiners return earlier and take no\nslot.\n- A hot tenant fast-fails **429** on excess concurrent cold embeds\nrather than starving the shared pool. With cap `N` on `M` core-api\ninstances, one tenant holds at most `N*M` of the ~20 TEI slots, leaving\nheadroom for others.\n\nCap rationale: on 2 staging core-api instances a single tenant holds\n≤`6×2=12`/20 (60%), ≥8 free — enough that a cold tenant-B query never\nqueues (failure mode was 100% occupancy). Sits under the route-level\nsearch cap of 32 (many searches in flight, few concurrent cold embeds).\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_per_tenant_concurrency.py`: `embed`-scope 429-on-exhaustion,\nscope isolation vs `search`, tenant isolation, release-on-exception.\n`tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`:\n`test_embed_slot_only_held_by_leader` — N concurrent same-key cold\ncallers all succeed at cap=1, proving joiners/cache-hits take no slot.\n\nLocal gate (CI-exact): `ruff check core-api/src/` ✓, `ruff format\n--check core-api/src/` ✓, `mypy core-api/src/` ✓ (192 files), `pytest` ✓\n(20 passed, no DB needed for these).\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n- Ingest/worker batch embed (`ingest_service.py`) left ungated — storm\nis search-side; worker already bulkheaded by\n`per_tenant_storage_write_concurrency`.\n- Pairs with a staging infra bump to TEI capacity (raise maxScale) —\ntracked separately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2dbc47f25b67e9a1c049b4830c78bcba9916ef59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2dbc47f25b67e9a1c049b4830c78bcba9916ef59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOR1rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATuEQAGxYJfeD9fDACHry41+EdPRd\nGx852J1kKH5pF+met8oMMR+dGyLszbNvJoqc82E0axpiezqhFQWXb/P4TgAFRHjj\nRFD1pIF3NTzRovHgoyyCR7JyoEcgmpiE4qWiowHaLHkTVituOzIeiN87a7szrHLy\nOxah+u/t4vK5PHsJY7brncLgAgyr+tZwSB4+BPljxZnkdmByv//b9q3XqWoWpuBQ\nVkPlUKASv2n80JjDb4hIde1IGggFzI/w6kxvGdjeAbvEL6EmAPZObPNuTxdGF+5w\ntbgNjjsrFe3LViaMMv8yiZfdXXOQJRyRvAxZpT9EhuGK74VoSbdS6oz0/kn/3iPY\n98ShHs2CsEcdICUqQ6PVCJ4CjuWW5IMBB1j0eAOY55d3UoD34H++f/CFyBP799tK\nyYxB46gWhlYyKB5xjPaGsGhfBUl62YUR1/Qj6t5JXYoGHTyDCF+8aQRuec6MusZP\nzRK7YQC27BDUKod5rKvEWgO2S1K08svpOTOG+A5M4mAyuFhKNQxCs8AfbbOP++EI\nyvgjimwSsDrs4YL/SAv6ap/tyGcNLrCrlVuHkR/zFvGCLzUeULkNRXyb/RcGL16S\nfdqJBp9kAr7hPsA0G2HOfcTgCHf+Z1zlLQvfdvRwNnV7X8qqswKKu+O3ol2ECRv7\nXNCToYY6LcD6RlqfGid4\n=6Ezi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2dbc47f25b67e9a1c049b4830c78bcba9916ef59\nparent dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782127979 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782127979 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): per-tenant embed concurrency cap (noisy-neighbor-search) (#464)\n\n## Problem\n`noisy-neighbor-search` from the latest loadtest: a single tenant's\n20-concurrency search storm degraded **another** tenant's search p95 by\n**6.43×** while Cloud Run CPU was idle. Root cause confirmed via live\ninfra pull — the embedding backend `staging-memclaw-tei` is pinned at\n`minScale=2, maxScale=2, containerConcurrency=10` (1 GPU each) → only\n**~20 concurrent embedding slots platform-wide, no autoscale**. A hot\ntenant's query embeddings fill all 20 slots; other tenants' query embeds\nqueue behind them. Route-level `per_tenant_slot(\"search\")=32` is\nper-tenant and too coarse — it doesn't protect *across* tenants at the\nshared embedding backend.\n\n## Fix\nCap concurrent embedding-backend calls **per tenant**, reusing the\nexisting `per_tenant_slot` bulkhead:\n- New `\"embed\"` scope in `middleware/per_tenant_concurrency.py` +\n`per_tenant_embed_concurrency` config knob (**default 6**).\n- The slot wraps **only the single-flight cold-miss leader** in\n`memory_service._get_or_cache_embedding` (the one call that actually\nhits TEI) — cache hits and in-flight joiners return earlier and take no\nslot.\n- A hot tenant fast-fails **429** on excess concurrent cold embeds\nrather than starving the shared pool. With cap `N` on `M` core-api\ninstances, one tenant holds at most `N*M` of the ~20 TEI slots, leaving\nheadroom for others.\n\nCap rationale: on 2 staging core-api instances a single tenant holds\n≤`6×2=12`/20 (60%), ≥8 free — enough that a cold tenant-B query never\nqueues (failure mode was 100% occupancy). Sits under the route-level\nsearch cap of 32 (many searches in flight, few concurrent cold embeds).\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_per_tenant_concurrency.py`: `embed`-scope 429-on-exhaustion,\nscope isolation vs `search`, tenant isolation, release-on-exception.\n`tests/test_query_embedding_stampede_guard.py`:\n`test_embed_slot_only_held_by_leader` — N concurrent same-key cold\ncallers all succeed at cap=1, proving joiners/cache-hits take no slot.\n\nLocal gate (CI-exact): `ruff check core-api/src/` ✓, `ruff format\n--check core-api/src/` ✓, `mypy core-api/src/` ✓ (192 files), `pytest` ✓\n(20 passed, no DB needed for these).\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n- Ingest/worker batch embed (`ingest_service.py`) left ungated — storm\nis search-side; worker already bulkheaded by\n`per_tenant_storage_write_concurrency`.\n- Pairs with a staging infra bump to TEI capacity (raise maxScale) —\ntracked separately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T11:33:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/043c02e5df4a109881dabf902c1969371cf3b08e/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5"}]},{"sha":"dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRjMGI2NzQyODdiN2ZkNTIzYTU5OGIxMjc3ZTlhNGJiZjJkNDBlZDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-22T11:27:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:27:06Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): route mcp_server's 9 ready tools through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 4) (#432)\n\n## Fix 2 Phase 4 — route mcp_server's 9 ready tools through\ncore-storage-api\n\nContinues the \"no DB outside core-storage-api\" migration. Routes the DB\naccess of **9 MCP tools** off the local `_mcp_session()` (which set the\nRLS GUCs `app.tenant_id` / `app.readable_tenant_ids`) onto the storage\nHTTP client, carrying tenant scope **explicitly** as params. Builds on\nPh0–3 (#427/#428/#429/#431).\n\n**Tools migrated:** `memclaw_recall`, `memclaw_write`, `memclaw_manage`,\n`memclaw_entity_get`, `memclaw_tune`, `memclaw_doc`, `memclaw_list`,\n`memclaw_stats`, `memclaw_keystones_set`.\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (+ `PostgresService` methods, +\nstorage_client methods)\n| Endpoint | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /memories/list` → `memory_list_by_filters` |\n**Visibility-scoped** list + cursor pagination + `readable_tenant_ids`\nwidening. Verbatim port of `memory_repository.list_by_filters`. Distinct\nfrom the existing *unscoped* admin-list. |\n| `POST /memories/stats-breakdown` → `memory_stats_breakdown` | GROUPING\nSETS (`total`/`by_type`/`by_agent`/`by_status`/`by_tenant`) +\n`include_deleted` CTE. Verbatim port of `compute_memory_stats`. |\n| `GET /documents/collection-count` | Status-filtered active-only skills\ncount (was a raw `db.execute` in mcp_server). |\n| Widened `GET /documents/{collection}/{doc_id}`\n(+`readable_tenant_ids`), `DELETE` (+`require_status` atomic guard) |\nCross-tenant read widening + atomic status-guarded skills delete. |\n\nEverything else **reuses** existing Ph2/Ph3 client methods (memory\nCRUD/search/`soft_delete_by_ids`/`update_search_profile`, the\n`/documents/*` + `/fleet/*` surface, audit).\n\n### Tenant isolation (the correctness-critical part)\nRemoving `_mcp_session()` for these tools means isolation is carried\nexplicitly. Preserved exactly: **writes → home tenant only**; **reads →\nhome + `readable_tenant_ids` only on cross-tenant reads**;\n**`scope='agent'` stays home-only** (forces\n`caller_agent_id`/`written_by`); `_UNAUTH`/`_ADMIN`/`_NO_AUTH` → empty\nreadable ⇒ no widening. The new SQL ports keep the `tenant_id == X` vs\n`IN (readable)` split and the `scope_agent` visibility predicate\nverbatim.\n\n**Verification beyond the gates:** ran an adversarial tenant-isolation\nreview across the diff (writes, read-widening, the new SQL ports,\nsentinel handling, and whether any test assertion was weakened) — clean\non all axes (one list-scope test was *strengthened*). It also caught +\nfixed one real regression in the in-progress work: a soft-deleted\n`older` memory could have leaked into lineage's `superseded_by`;\nrestored the `older.deleted_at is None` filter client-side (matching\nREST `/contradictions`).\n\n### Deferred to Ph5 (unchanged roadmap)\n`memclaw_insights` + `memclaw_evolve` stay on `_mcp_session()`;\ncapability_usage; **`_mcp_session()` deletion is the last step of Ph5**.\nAfter this PR, `fleet_repo` is fully unused and `document_repo`'s last\ncallers are gone (both dropped at cleanup).\n\n### Quality (`/simplify`)\nExtracted `_storage_error_envelope()` (folded 6 duplicate `httpx`-error\ntails → 1 helper); dropped now-dead ORM-shape fallbacks in\n`memclaw_recall` (`sc.get_agent` returns `dict | None`).\n\n### Gates\n`ruff check` + `format --check` ✓ · `mypy` (core-api + core-storage-api)\n✓ · **3507 tests pass** (incl. all `tests/test_mcp_*.py` + the\ncross-tenant-audit / by-id-authz isolation guards). conftest\nASGI-bridges the client to in-process storage on the test engine, so the\nmigration is test-transparent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2eea2b44da8d3212f51ab2b7d526f1f368a048d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2eea2b44da8d3212f51ab2b7d526f1f368a048d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqORwKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW2kQAFpcZc1G9UgKazAI7cnJR0Xq\nX0KnIGk7JLO212pbHjddQb21C39WSrUhJnvpMF6xzuB+LNT31UAXSc7p6ZVpWLNo\nfriSq6056uracbUL+oplu8YBR6mR+fIq1Y55+Y4G/ykbolg+b6oa5eKe0MS6wQZU\n2wwtRgornINF2lPyNXXyLTtJa4oED9m38tD6mkLpesH9S1HpDHd8Df5j9hM6tK5B\n2v4ngwfyJZ6DPPENqMRuJ2Arl5S824IcyZ