ion-count` | Status-filtered active-only skills\ncount (was a raw `db.execute` in mcp_server). |\n| Widened `GET /documents/{collection}/{doc_id}`\n(+`readable_tenant_ids`), `DELETE` (+`require_status` atomic guard) |\nCross-tenant read widening + atomic status-guarded skills delete. |\n\nEverything else **reuses** existing Ph2/Ph3 client methods (memory\nCRUD/search/`soft_delete_by_ids`/`update_search_profile`, the\n`/documents/*` + `/fleet/*` surface, audit).\n\n### Tenant isolation (the correctness-critical part)\nRemoving `_mcp_session()` for these tools means isolation is carried\nexplicitly. Preserved exactly: **writes → home tenant only**; **reads →\nhome + `readable_tenant_ids` only on cross-tenant reads**;\n**`scope='agent'` stays home-only** (forces\n`caller_agent_id`/`written_by`); `_UNAUTH`/`_ADMIN`/`_NO_AUTH` → empty\nreadable ⇒ no widening. The new SQL ports keep the `tenant_id == X` vs\n`IN (readable)` split and the `scope_agent` visibility predicate\nverbatim.\n\n**Verification beyond the gates:** ran an adversarial tenant-isolation\nreview across the diff (writes, read-widening, the new SQL ports,\nsentinel handling, and whether any test assertion was weakened) — clean\non all axes (one list-scope test was *strengthened*). It also caught +\nfixed one real regression in the in-progress work: a soft-deleted\n`older` memory could have leaked into lineage's `superseded_by`;\nrestored the `older.deleted_at is None` filter client-side (matching\nREST `/contradictions`).\n\n### Deferred to Ph5 (unchanged roadmap)\n`memclaw_insights` + `memclaw_evolve` stay on `_mcp_session()`;\ncapability_usage; **`_mcp_session()` deletion is the last step of Ph5**.\nAfter this PR, `fleet_repo` is fully unused and `document_repo`'s last\ncallers are gone (both dropped at cleanup).\n\n### Quality (`/simplify`)\nExtracted `_storage_error_envelope()` (folded 6 duplicate `httpx`-error\ntails → 1 helper); dropped now-dead ORM-shape fallbacks in\n`memclaw_recall` (`sc.get_agent` returns `dict | None`).\n\n### Gates\n`ruff check` + `format --check` ✓ · `mypy` (core-api + core-storage-api)\n✓ · **3507 tests pass** (incl. all `tests/test_mcp_*.py` + the\ncross-tenant-audit / by-id-authz isolation guards). conftest\nASGI-bridges the client to in-process storage on the test engine, so the\nmigration is test-transparent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T11:27:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dc0b674287b7fd523a598b1277e9a4bbf2d40ed5/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331"}]},{"sha":"0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBiYTUxYjQzZDdiYmFhOGI1MmI5N2VlZTdlYzZkY2Y3ZjA1YzMzMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-21T23:00:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T23:00:29Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out (VPC-connector ConnectTimeout residual) (#434)\n\n## Keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out — stop the\nVPC-connector ConnectTimeout storms\n\nAddresses the **residual VPC-connector cold-handshake class** (Ran's\n`BUG-staging-vpc-connector-saturation`, re-confirmed in the 2026-06-21\npost-promote triage). The `e2-standard-4` connector upgrade raised the\nceiling, but **bursts of simultaneous cold TCP handshakes** still trip\nit. Triage data (staging core-api, 6h): **174 `ConnectTimeout`s**,\ndominated by the Path-C entity-context fan-out — `GET /memories/<id>`\n×124, `/entities/*` ×26 — plus `/audit-logs/bulk` ×16 (the audit \"events\nlost\"). Almost all `attempt 1/5` = brand-new connections.\n\n### Two app-side levers (no infra change)\n1. **`storage_client._make_pool`: `keepalive_expiry=90s`** (was httpx's\n5s default). The fan-out's bursts arrive seconds-to-tens-of-seconds\napart; at 5s the warm keep-alive pool drained *between* bursts, so the\nnext burst re-handshook. 90s keeps connections warm across the gap → the\nfan-out **reuses** them. (`max_keepalive_connections=150` was already\ngenerous — expiry was the missing piece.)\n2. **`contradiction_detector`: bound the Path-C entity-context fan-out**\nvia a `_bounded_gather` helper (limit 8), applied to both the\nper-candidate `_fetch_entity_context` fan-out (candidates up to **40**)\nand the per-link `_hydrate` fan-out — so one burst can't open dozens of\nsimultaneous handshakes. Order preserved (gather semantics); fresh\nper-call semaphore (loop-safe).\n\nTogether: warm reuse eliminates the cold handshakes; the cap keeps any\ncold burst within the connector's handshake headroom. **Benefits all\nstorage callers** (entity-context, audit-flush, etc.), so it also\nreduces the `/audit-logs/bulk` connect-timeout \"events lost\".\n\n### Verification\n- New unit test: `_bounded_gather` caps concurrency (peak ≤ limit) +\npreserves order.\n- The **41 existing Path-C tests** (`caura_131` entity-aware detection,\n`caura_130` safety, `a4_13` retraction, storage-client pool recovery)\nstill pass — behavior unchanged.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` ✓, `mypy` (core-api +\ncore-storage-api) ✓, full suite green.\n\nIndependent of the Fix 2 migration.\n\n### Related / not in this PR\n- **Embedding (TEI) timeouts** ride a *separate* httpx client (already\ntimeout-tuned per #332). Same `keepalive_expiry` idea may apply there —\nflagging as a follow-up rather than touching a second client here.\n- **Audit-flush durability** (don't silently drop events on connect\nfailure — retry/dead-letter) is the other lever from triage; this PR\nremoves most of the *triggering* timeouts, but durable audit is worth\nits own change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43ca95c78b5243ffc839a960a9146f6e3ddbc017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/43ca95c78b5243ffc839a960a9146f6e3ddbc017"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOG0NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgUQQABl8h97zOesdMmHJSlxgBJ5s\ncy8w3oyRBnZThcW9wsyaoJpXb6gmKChEgFyvyOVbOZ59V/UjMS9Z98Ho8i04BgLR\nN2g211gB2zpdilkG4/chcFxsScoROD3vtr7+c62LrfFpd4I6Ymup47BNRItmElPz\nh20/snycBgNvF0eVl9H1sc0SMg0n0zvWb66tgJyjpCVq+l+q2lSpE82lkz9eElaq\nDt23G2X41A7yxlNImn90yTMC3HDRqRcYMB9I9xs6IlOkvilHP7zlJNruzAPxETUq\n+1nAe1lrJ8MRin1pGMpW79iYhhO7pnrMC7gGQ3e9IDLqOVQTLDvojcAUMtpymLPj\njT230PlwMIceJcxwCd8DkujpCn4G8Zs45aV57wKEw0gDrzy4OzIW3ZAodTCbZg1J\nE751/AujuA1QhGmG8WboKkGgkimX6QbrhP7FKXEVFGgF/4Ll5qB/wsfdtZfNvJ/c\nxfhss3FT1SAg+uoGuPfo+fRWkm6BnPXOthVeSoQm5leR/q/BgB8kvwCTF8ZGVyhq\nLNDnSlOsKnEtmULBnfVdZvpHzhfbKM9FcDFMOIkIyboLbAE2GwI6qR2GEtqZc/kA\n+m+LzFFNclua2NV1QJRZTNA7AwYmZDgUUWKcyUnTN+O5lo814NBwdzIe2WrZSjI7\n43QSRWxcQqAit+s7cb/C\n=TdpA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 43ca95c78b5243ffc839a960a9146f6e3ddbc017\nparent 2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782082829 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782082829 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out (VPC-connector ConnectTimeout residual) (#434)\n\n## Keep-alive pool + bounded entity-context fan-out — stop the\nVPC-connector ConnectTimeout storms\n\nAddresses the **residual VPC-connector cold-handshake class** (Ran's\n`BUG-staging-vpc-connector-saturation`, re-confirmed in the 2026-06-21\npost-promote triage). The `e2-standard-4` connector upgrade raised the\nceiling, but **bursts of simultaneous cold TCP handshakes** still trip\nit. Triage data (staging core-api, 6h): **174 `ConnectTimeout`s**,\ndominated by the Path-C entity-context fan-out — `GET /memories/<id>`\n×124, `/entities/*` ×26 — plus `/audit-logs/bulk` ×16 (the audit \"events\nlost\"). Almost all `attempt 1/5` = brand-new connections.\n\n### Two app-side levers (no infra change)\n1. **`storage_client._make_pool`: `keepalive_expiry=90s`** (was httpx's\n5s default). The fan-out's bursts arrive seconds-to-tens-of-seconds\napart; at 5s the warm keep-alive pool drained *between* bursts, so the\nnext burst re-handshook. 90s keeps connections warm across the gap → the\nfan-out **reuses** them. (`max_keepalive_connections=150` was already\ngenerous — expiry was the missing piece.)\n2. **`contradiction_detector`: bound the Path-C entity-context fan-out**\nvia a `_bounded_gather` helper (limit 8), applied to both the\nper-candidate `_fetch_entity_context` fan-out (candidates up to **40**)\nand the per-link `_hydrate` fan-out — so one burst can't open dozens of\nsimultaneous handshakes. Order preserved (gather semantics); fresh\nper-call semaphore (loop-safe).\n\nTogether: warm reuse eliminates the cold handshakes; the cap keeps any\ncold burst within the connector's handshake headroom. **Benefits all\nstorage callers** (entity-context, audit-flush, etc.), so it also\nreduces the `/audit-logs/bulk` connect-timeout \"events lost\".\n\n### Verification\n- New unit test: `_bounded_gather` caps concurrency (peak ≤ limit) +\npreserves order.\n- The **41 existing Path-C tests** (`caura_131` entity-aware detection,\n`caura_130` safety, `a4_13` retraction, storage-client pool recovery)\nstill pass — behavior unchanged.\n- `ruff check` + `format --check` ✓, `mypy` (core-api +\ncore-storage-api) ✓, full suite green.\n\nIndependent of the Fix 2 migration.\n\n### Related / not in this PR\n- **Embedding (TEI) timeouts** ride a *separate* httpx client (already\ntimeout-tuned per #332). Same `keepalive_expiry` idea may apply there —\nflagging as a follow-up rather than touching a second client here.\n- **Audit-flush durability** (don't silently drop events on connect\nfailure — retry/dead-letter) is the other lever from triage; this PR\nremoves most of the *triggering* timeouts, but durable audit is worth\nits own change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-21T23:00:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ba51b43d7bbaa8b52b97eee7ec6dcf7f05c3331/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d"}]},{"sha":"2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJkYjE5YWE3M2YxOWRmYmUwMDZhNTk5ODE5YmQwYmI5ZDUwNWNhMmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-21T22:47:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T22:47:29Z"},"message":"test(security): de-flake test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok (#433)\n\n## De-flake\n`test_security_tenant_isolation::test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok`\n\n`test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok` wrote a memory to a **shared**\n`\"self-org\"` tenant and asserted the listing returned `len(items) >= 1`.\nIt intermittently failed under full-suite load (observed ~1/4 runs).\n\n### Root cause\nThe test DB keeps **storage-committed rows across pytest sessions** —\nthe storage write path commits on its own connection, so those rows are\n*not* rolled back like the `db` fixture's transaction. Under accumulated\ndata, a freshly-written row can fall outside the **default list page**,\nso the bare `len >= 1` presence check flakes. (Confirmed the same\nmechanism by reproducing a sibling failure:\n`test_api_keystones::test_set_then_list_round_trip` fails once the\nshared `\"default\"` tenant accumulates enough keystones to push the\njust-set one off the page — see \"Related\" below.)\n\nThe cross-tenant `all(m[\"tenant_id\"] == tenant_id)` assertion is **not**\nthe flaky part and is **kept unchanged** — a pinned `tenant_id` scopes\nthe list to a single tenant even for the admin key (verified in\n`routes/memories.py`: `tenant_id_explicit` forces\n`readable_tenant_ids=None`), so it's a genuine isolation invariant.\n\n### Fix (test-only)\n- Use a **unique per-run tenant** (`self-org-{uid()}`) → the listing\ncan't pick up ambient / cross-session rows.\n- Assert the **just-written memory is present by id**, not a bare count.\n- Keep the cross-tenant isolation assertion unchanged.\n- Drop a now-unused `get_admin_headers` import on the edited line.\n\n### Verification\n- Passes **3×** against a heavily-accumulated DB (strong stress) and on\na clean full-suite run (**3507 passed**).\n- `ruff check` ✓, `mypy` (core-api + core-storage-api) ✓.\n\nPre-existing flake; unrelated to the Fix 2 migration.\n\n### Related (not fixed here)\nThe same class — *present-after-create assertions against a\nshared-tenant list with a default page limit* — affects other tests\n(e.g. `test_api_keystones::test_set_then_list_round_trip`, which uses\nthe shared `\"default\"` tenant). Worth a broader pass (unique tenants /\npresent-by-id, or a session-level committed-data reset in conftest), but\nout of scope for this one-test fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9429b9a248a8b09cc86a0889df2bb5b3ba6d35ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9429b9a248a8b09cc86a0889df2bb5b3ba6d35ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOGoBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEmsQAG2vx0pKOS7byKznsgBNNtdb\n7SXOPutMV6+r3AZhlPyQJCuC8xF00DFunI9Cv6ayplvwKOA0uCI471I+RM8q4wF3\nhvg4TF68VQyPiQajcpn7vp8hHip9nib3D3lF5uDs+SueH3gNjdrnagclvBCoiDz7\nc6adsaSNiriEMv4rqjb2OvNJFERI/T/IpCh+WM4vQmnJOjXV7qdLLmdN3omgHuzU\n0EW0rIPl/RUt43mCB8Ie0Rck0+uSayVR93t4SLRHbG/4aiG4U8OzNEeRFn8Tyzhq\nTKULatai2yPgA1DSkSAehC2vyDs+pntJWR/R7/BtxeRa+NIUbl9zxBZept13quf5\n66JK62lGvEBUQKBUbD1OiaLzDYuSEwfA1kTaAlThpBsVaJC9Eezs0vc0Vai546cI\nU5leKrtkSRrLO2ee/QfBKkeHjVpmD4mojaBQVETB8HLx0+3QyEfD+mNZLBM4SkKi\n+/oJva5YW+y0IaadiJurNNxjFTKYGtBpYngkqL5Nhx0puglL/xjahr1+roC0nFom\nVKo6HWnqpyhKXs8QhYUqyfSpEV3MPwCQNrIjkyk6UUNyBpV2PShYgQ7Q2RUVSvTw\n6O72K763myDohrH37gSFEOnDhybltfPRqoCIDvZtBOCr2S6bAc20WVKtBd1scZ8O\nBOep1q+XsKp2q57JWzLw\n=/rYr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9429b9a248a8b09cc86a0889df2bb5b3ba6d35ac\nparent ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782082049 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782082049 +0300\n\ntest(security): de-flake test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok (#433)\n\n## De-flake\n`test_security_tenant_isolation::test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok`\n\n`test_own_tenant_memory_access_ok` wrote a memory to a **shared**\n`\"self-org\"` tenant and asserted the listing returned `len(items) >= 1`.\nIt intermittently failed under full-suite load (observed ~1/4 runs).\n\n### Root cause\nThe test DB keeps **storage-committed rows across pytest sessions** —\nthe storage write path commits on its own connection, so those rows are\n*not* rolled back like the `db` fixture's transaction. Under accumulated\ndata, a freshly-written row can fall outside the **default list page**,\nso the bare `len >= 1` presence check flakes. (Confirmed the same\nmechanism by reproducing a sibling failure:\n`test_api_keystones::test_set_then_list_round_trip` fails once the\nshared `\"default\"` tenant accumulates enough keystones to push the\njust-set one off the page — see \"Related\" below.)\n\nThe cross-tenant `all(m[\"tenant_id\"] == tenant_id)` assertion is **not**\nthe flaky part and is **kept unchanged** — a pinned `tenant_id` scopes\nthe list to a single tenant even for the admin key (verified in\n`routes/memories.py`: `tenant_id_explicit` forces\n`readable_tenant_ids=None`), so it's a genuine isolation invariant.\n\n### Fix (test-only)\n- Use a **unique per-run tenant** (`self-org-{uid()}`) → the listing\ncan't pick up ambient / cross-session rows.\n- Assert the **just-written memory is present by id**, not a bare count.\n- Keep the cross-tenant isolation assertion unchanged.\n- Drop a now-unused `get_admin_headers` import on the edited line.\n\n### Verification\n- Passes **3×** against a heavily-accumulated DB (strong stress) and on\na clean full-suite run (**3507 passed**).\n- `ruff check` ✓, `mypy` (core-api + core-storage-api) ✓.\n\nPre-existing flake; unrelated to the Fix 2 migration.\n\n### Related (not fixed here)\nThe same class — *present-after-create assertions against a\nshared-tenant list with a default page limit* — affects other tests\n(e.g. `test_api_keystones::test_set_then_list_round_trip`, which uses\nthe shared `\"default\"` tenant). Worth a broader pass (unique tenants /\npresent-by-id, or a session-level committed-data reset in conftest), but\nout of scope for this one-test fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-21T22:47:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2db19aa73f19dfbe006a599819bd0bb9d505ca2d/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346"}]},{"sha":"ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGFkMmEyZDlmOTFkNjgwMmE4YTY2ZDg5MzViZWZlZjM5Y2FmYTkzNDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-21T15:14:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T15:14:14Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): route documents + fleet residuals through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 3) (#431)\n\n## Fix 2 Phase 3 — documents + fleet residuals via core-storage-api\n\nContinues the \"no DB outside core-storage-api\" migration. Moves the last\ndirect-DB **document** and **fleet** usages out of core-api route\nhandlers and behind core-storage-api HTTP. Builds on Phase 2 (#429).\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (+ `PostgresService` methods)\n| Method / path | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /documents/upsert-xmax` | `INSERT … ON CONFLICT … RETURNING\nxmax` for insert-vs-update detection. Extends the existing service\nmethod to write the optional `embedding` column — passing `None` on a\nre-write clears a previously-indexed vector (intentional). |\n| `GET /documents/collections` | Per-collection document counts;\ncross-tenant (`readable_tenant_ids`) widening preserved. |\n| `POST /documents/search` | Vector (cosine) search, optional `status`\nfilter. core-api still owns the embedding step and passes the vector\nacross (storage stays a pure DB choke-point). |\n| `GET /fleet/commands/in-flight-deploy` | Auto-upgrade in-flight deploy\ngate. |\n| `GET /fleet/commands/deploy-attempt-count` | Auto-upgrade attempt\nbudget. |\n\nAll service methods are verbatim ports of the existing\n`DocumentRepository` / `FleetRepository` logic — same SQL, predicates,\nand semantics; only the execution moves to storage-api (reads →\n`get_read_session`, writes → `get_session`).\n\n### core-api migration\n- **`routes/documents.py`** — `upsert` / `list_collections` / `search`\nnow call the storage client. Dropped the intermediate `db.commit()`\n(storage commits its own session); audit `log_action` + final commit\npreserved. `get_embedding` hoisted to a top-level import; dead `db`\ndependency dropped from `list_collections`.\n- **`routes/fleet.py`** — the two auto-upgrade gates call the storage\nclient, preserving the fail-open `try/except`; removed the `fleet_repo`\nimport.\n- **`clients/storage_client.py`** — 5 new client methods\n(read/write-routed).\n\n### Deferred (by design)\n- `document_repo` / `fleet_repo` modules **stay** — `mcp_server.py`\nstill uses them (Phase 4).\n- `POST /documents/update-status` is **not** added here — its only\nconsumers are the skill-lifecycle paths (`skills_inbox` / forge\n`cron_handler`), which migrate in Phase 5.\n\n### No schema change\n`documents.embedding` is already mapped (migration 003); the fleet gates\nuse the partial index `ix_fleet_commands_node_created_deploy` from\nmigration 024.\n\n### Gates\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓\n- `mypy` core-api ✓ · `mypy` core-storage-api ✓\n- **3506 tests pass** (+14 new Phase 3 tests covering xmax INSERT/UPDATE\n+ embedding store/clear, collections counts/scoping/widening, search\nordering/NULL-exclusion/status/widening, and both fleet gates). conftest\nASGI-bridges the storage client to an in-process core-storage-api, so\nthe route swaps are test-transparent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ac77fb309997943cd1a27d4de010822432a57f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4ac77fb309997943cd1a27d4de010822432a57f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN//GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWsEQACo/aq2k7Vs40Njza0pCyESH\nRwM7QRI0jNwQvJcYmgZ9jQThX1kYZ+X41awH06pOTmokmqQAEcoQGFGEvpgl0UzI\ngfhzCjgGGRuuL+WwgXF86kXPANf0iIrs0P5gFF/vKZk8035wWI7OyXkU+HxLwEFY\n0DnyczhDkXjZ2jFznQdSCJEiVEJNl3HdfhSkqLF2EDmmLh1y+BsvmHjIy0Yb6hEo\nBwwQal/fWdaonzU8jeXIdcAOz4QqbDWp6aFHLRJH6fUm8cWEJsCT9kVQk2uKWy0b\nS5cr+XkQKiBN4sssISHaid3c1BOCWRTljyYhPKXWOKhVbr2LfBQKPTpVg6An1mlu\nNv+xYzZbW7+oMjkFYzTjvq6ZzppArySdfgbFeC5VGpDuMXZ7OoU9Jeuu/BNZV9nD\ndSLXdRtp2zsA2RwitDlRT5Xh7E4jsvOBi3eZ9QX/6XUqzF9/hpnGdT752WxbbGq/\nJcXxb1UOp2HqEY/UA1wfVsXWxzPXdvWj4jbsY2obSF27KUynXmLRTbIux80zFCgM\nz5VEVnFvJZmpXv5WuHxwgKxh8jeTOgUGCpqhJr3xfQgmLSfrxPCVmCjexet0dM9B\nDoc/aL9DeYbB0RkF8iHko6MfHmfQWYGLUpqdU0ukfnk/yQlOxC1b6Zd43eteU9yb\n/gFBP75QFLOGFT3rP0fm\n=qmG9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ac77fb309997943cd1a27d4de010822432a57f3\nparent 1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782054854 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782054854 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): route documents + fleet residuals through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 3) (#431)\n\n## Fix 2 Phase 3 — documents + fleet residuals via core-storage-api\n\nContinues the \"no DB outside core-storage-api\" migration. Moves the last\ndirect-DB **document** and **fleet** usages out of core-api route\nhandlers and behind core-storage-api HTTP. Builds on Phase 2 (#429).\n\n### New core-storage-api endpoints (+ `PostgresService` methods)\n| Method / path | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /documents/upsert-xmax` | `INSERT … ON CONFLICT … RETURNING\nxmax` for insert-vs-update detection. Extends the existing service\nmethod to write the optional `embedding` column — passing `None` on a\nre-write clears a previously-indexed vector (intentional). |\n| `GET /documents/collections` | Per-collection document counts;\ncross-tenant (`readable_tenant_ids`) widening preserved. |\n| `POST /documents/search` | Vector (cosine) search, optional `status`\nfilter. core-api still owns the embedding step and passes the vector\nacross (storage stays a pure DB choke-point). |\n| `GET /fleet/commands/in-flight-deploy` | Auto-upgrade in-flight deploy\ngate. |\n| `GET /fleet/commands/deploy-attempt-count` | Auto-upgrade attempt\nbudget. |\n\nAll service methods are verbatim ports of the existing\n`DocumentRepository` / `FleetRepository` logic — same SQL, predicates,\nand semantics; only the execution moves to storage-api (reads →\n`get_read_session`, writes → `get_session`).\n\n### core-api migration\n- **`routes/documents.py`** — `upsert` / `list_collections` / `search`\nnow call the storage client. Dropped the intermediate `db.commit()`\n(storage commits its own session); audit `log_action` + final commit\npreserved. `get_embedding` hoisted to a top-level import; dead `db`\ndependency dropped from `list_collections`.\n- **`routes/fleet.py`** — the two auto-upgrade gates call the storage\nclient, preserving the fail-open `try/except`; removed the `fleet_repo`\nimport.\n- **`clients/storage_client.py`** — 5 new client methods\n(read/write-routed).\n\n### Deferred (by design)\n- `document_repo` / `fleet_repo` modules **stay** — `mcp_server.py`\nstill uses them (Phase 4).\n- `POST /documents/update-status` is **not** added here — its only\nconsumers are the skill-lifecycle paths (`skills_inbox` / forge\n`cron_handler`), which migrate in Phase 5.\n\n### No schema change\n`documents.embedding` is already mapped (migration 003); the fleet gates\nuse the partial index `ix_fleet_commands_node_created_deploy` from\nmigration 024.\n\n### Gates\n- `ruff check` ✓ · `ruff format --check` ✓\n- `mypy` core-api ✓ · `mypy` core-storage-api ✓\n- **3506 tests pass** (+14 new Phase 3 tests covering xmax INSERT/UPDATE\n+ embedding store/clear, collections counts/scoping/widening, search\nordering/NULL-exclusion/status/widening, and both fleet gates). conftest\nASGI-bridges the storage client to an in-process core-storage-api, so\nthe route swaps are test-transparent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-21T15:14:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ad2a2d9f91d6802a8a66d8935befef39cafa9346/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247"}]},{"sha":"1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFlMzljNTlhMGQyMzY2MDIzZTQwNjVjNDY5MjZkZWI5NGIxM2MyNDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-21T11:29:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T11:29:47Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): route memory REST surface through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 2) (#429)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 2** — third slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (after Phase 0 settings #427, Phase 1\ntenant-discovery #428). Moves the remaining direct-DB handlers in\n`routes/memories.py` off core-api's pool and behind new core-storage-api\nendpoints. **No schema change.**\n\n**Key framing:** the feared \"mutation + audit in one transaction\"\nrequirement doesn't exist today — `log_action` is already a decoupled\nasync `POST /audit-logs`, `usage_service` is a no-op stub in OSS, and\n`soft_delete`/`update`/`agent_service` already route through the storage\nclient. So this migrates the inline `db.execute`/`db.get`/`db.commit`\nthat remained; the `db.commit()`s become no-ops and are removed; **audit\nstays the existing async POST** (not folded into storage transactions).\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access) — 9 `postgres_service`\nmethods + routes on the memories router\n- `memory_fleet_distribution` (reader) — serves `/fleets` +\n`/admin/fleets` via an `exclude_scope_agent` flag.\n- `memory_get_detail` (reader) — row + entity-link outerjoin in one\nround-trip; **embedding stats computed server-side**, raw vector +\n`search_vector` stripped.\n- `memory_contradiction_rows` (reader) — 3 reads bundled; cross-tenant\n`older` guard server-side.\n- `memory_soft_delete_by_filter` / `_by_ids` / `_by_run` (writer) —\nby-filter JSONB metadata predicate via **bound params** (no string\ninterpolation).\n- `memory_redistribute` (writer) — `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` + reassign +\nauto-promote `scope_agent`→`scope_team` + `not_found`, all in **one\ntransaction**.\n- `memory_admin_list` (reader) — cross-tenant, no visibility scoping,\ncursor.\n- `memory_admin_stats` (reader) — single **GROUPING SETS** scan →\n`{total,by_type,by_agent,by_status}` (bound-param `text()` with `CAST(:p\nAS text)` so asyncpg can type the optional NULL filters).\n\n### core-api\n- `storage_client` gains 9 methods; list/dict GETs raise on 404, by-id\nreads return `None` for the caller to 404-translate.\n- 12 handlers switched to the client. Trust gates / validation / cursor\nencode-decode / response shaping / audit stay in core-api. **`get_db` is\nretained** on the router (write/search/recall/ingest/list handlers still\nuse it — deferred to later phases); the `db` Depends is dropped only\nfrom handlers that no longer touch db at all.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff@0.15.4 + mypy clean on **both** projects.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3490 passed**.\n- `/simplify` ran (clean); I reviewed the correctness-critical methods\n(redistribute txn, JSONB binding, server-side embedding stats, GROUPING\nSETS) by hand.\n- New `tests/test_memory_storage_phase2.py` (21 tests) exercises the\nfull path.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"648382f6a015dc76319b9508d4011170fe4f7232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/648382f6a015dc76319b9508d4011170fe4f7232"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN8srCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuO8QAJ1qswyl4H2BEV7BN4Z7SXjS\nGxZEwhXaF+msaCLYTrimsrdXPJuVmNa3sMc0JoXagosWRs65PKugJZeqTBvPCmQq\nHYJpAPS5irs7FgmBcKQb42nxftPsvlt1BHkmxavIpQOF+gfOJgpN4/a/5ouzjFID\nthMUXDupiUrzqLcTL+Uavg9Kz1h2HFedARMCiNnLLy12p2yQyqqlGxok+A+QLNoR\ngx9zniLRhi5dQiJ6eLw4dQuKBWZ43oFImpJrNCXfazCrQFpiynUhqC19BZqhYIsm\nTDc29Ye/QGG7hr9WNh8FAlra/QWpK/mNbi0FLPQ1cYQgFDnwVQPMmE1KuCr7pPVf\n6kSVJrF0Pv+gTNqrrfzxKHqAwpJhI1+y25cogiZVLyghzxI7yW4Axdi8xQl2vUzH\nVR7H0mOMLtwytW1w4Ggfb0G+JA7JyL+TCXctDH4Ehglpzrs71y39sHItsLQme2+K\nS2lb3GRt46F22zD2wKOg8JIhKWEBbLGOQ5aHG+BBIyem/VU5jk9Eds4Q/QAG0iEp\n6ki3Mw7Sz3Ti+2x80L2OOywBJ95cnbQ/8s0U7r5Ze20vSC43eGL81l7Mtl3hO708\nmjEx617MNuNFyfm5VqvK/El7QXtQS7zFVfjRo7lAYfxX4d8P2SgHHf2ONNF8lbWp\n+X2EkP7nskAQLe0fAJ2c\n=ZzV5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 648382f6a015dc76319b9508d4011170fe4f7232\nparent f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782041387 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782041387 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): route memory REST surface through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 2) (#429)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 2** — third slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (after Phase 0 settings #427, Phase 1\ntenant-discovery #428). Moves the remaining direct-DB handlers in\n`routes/memories.py` off core-api's pool and behind new core-storage-api\nendpoints. **No schema change.**\n\n**Key framing:** the feared \"mutation + audit in one transaction\"\nrequirement doesn't exist today — `log_action` is already a decoupled\nasync `POST /audit-logs`, `usage_service` is a no-op stub in OSS, and\n`soft_delete`/`update`/`agent_service` already route through the storage\nclient. So this migrates the inline `db.execute`/`db.get`/`db.commit`\nthat remained; the `db.commit()`s become no-ops and are removed; **audit\nstays the existing async POST** (not folded into storage transactions).\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access) — 9 `postgres_service`\nmethods + routes on the memories router\n- `memory_fleet_distribution` (reader) — serves `/fleets` +\n`/admin/fleets` via an `exclude_scope_agent` flag.\n- `memory_get_detail` (reader) — row + entity-link outerjoin in one\nround-trip; **embedding stats computed server-side**, raw vector +\n`search_vector` stripped.\n- `memory_contradiction_rows` (reader) — 3 reads bundled; cross-tenant\n`older` guard server-side.\n- `memory_soft_delete_by_filter` / `_by_ids` / `_by_run` (writer) —\nby-filter JSONB metadata predicate via **bound params** (no string\ninterpolation).\n- `memory_redistribute` (writer) — `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` + reassign +\nauto-promote `scope_agent`→`scope_team` + `not_found`, all in **one\ntransaction**.\n- `memory_admin_list` (reader) — cross-tenant, no visibility scoping,\ncursor.\n- `memory_admin_stats` (reader) — single **GROUPING SETS** scan →\n`{total,by_type,by_agent,by_status}` (bound-param `text()` with `CAST(:p\nAS text)` so asyncpg can type the optional NULL filters).\n\n### core-api\n- `storage_client` gains 9 methods; list/dict GETs raise on 404, by-id\nreads return `None` for the caller to 404-translate.\n- 12 handlers switched to the client. Trust gates / validation / cursor\nencode-decode / response shaping / audit stay in core-api. **`get_db` is\nretained** on the router (write/search/recall/ingest/list handlers still\nuse it — deferred to later phases); the `db` Depends is dropped only\nfrom handlers that no longer touch db at all.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff@0.15.4 + mypy clean on **both** projects.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3490 passed**.\n- `/simplify` ran (clean); I reviewed the correctness-critical methods\n(redistribute txn, JSONB binding, server-side embedding stats, GROUPING\nSETS) by hand.\n- New `tests/test_memory_storage_phase2.py` (21 tests) exercises the\nfull path.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-21T11:29:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1e39c59a0d2366023e4065c46926deb94b13c247/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562"}]},{"sha":"f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGYwNWY0OTgyZDcwNDQ5ZGI1ZGU2ZTIxYzEyMzlmZjU3YzUzZTE1NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-20T20:48:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T20:48:49Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): route tenant-discovery through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 1) (#428)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 1** — second slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (after Phase 0 settings, #427). Moves the\nlifecycle-fanout's tenant-discovery queries off core-api's direct\nSQLAlchemy pool and behind new core-storage-api endpoints. **No schema\nchange.**\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access)\n- `postgres_service.tenants_list_active / _purgeable /\n_skills_factory_enabled` — the distinct-tenant and JSONB-flag SELECTs,\non the **reader replica** (`get_read_session`). Same SQL that lived in\n`core-api/services/tenants.py`.\n- `routers/tenants.py` — `GET /tenants/active`, `/tenants/purgeable`,\n`/tenants/skills-factory-enabled`. Envelope responses:\n`{tenant_ids:[...]}` for the memory-backed reads, `{org_ids:[...]}` for\nthe settings-backed one.\n\n### core-api (now a client)\n- `storage_client.list_active_tenants / list_purgeable_tenants /\nlist_skills_factory_enabled_orgs`.\n- `services/tenants.py` — the 3 helpers are now thin storage-client\nwrappers (domain \"why\" stays in docstrings; SQL moved to storage). The\n`db` param is retained (ignored) for call-site back-compat (e.g.\n`routes/memories.py` still passes it), matching the Phase 0 pattern.\n- `routes/lifecycle.py` — the cron fanout no longer opens its own\n`async_session` just to fetch the org list; it calls the now-sessionless\ndiscovery helpers directly, so the fan-out holds **no DB connection at\nall**. Drops the `core_api.db.session` import.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff + mypy clean on **both** core-api and core-storage-api.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3469 passed**.\n- `/simplify` ran (clean). New `test_tenant_discovery_storage` exercises\nthe full core-api → storage-api → DB path; forge-cron routing tests\nupdated for the dropped `db` arg.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"461bb6fe432de673db1ab5a718e30aa84339df10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/461bb6fe432de673db1ab5a718e30aa84339df10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNvyxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnEcQAErR0BXMBv4LX9xZmTHM/IDG\n/tjW+5o+RP6LoOAR+pvbYigagG3CFfIFdCYfS1nqX0amCZp+4FtdAzwizB/hz7qP\ne2//fm3uEcqSX3tIvtXyMbN87qd7M24B1Y7IBpyNhCpx3Rg2kKsuUthTA5kklGUe\nkKVA4IIvnnaS9F135Jvezq123lD5ilEv8RGMyR7AMjyAY7ZO6lNGjRmeK/2bdrc+\n/Z94XrUTdFm0wGzFu/3aKAbD6oSJMWsDZzxom6zORhcuqIT517NaE9HB189F97Yv\nCaz0jJfiYsnx45DvEjQRJj8FtMhBIgA6ioFp5j08OitrZCZ+LkF+BOaxPX90sc72\nVS0xO2/qBn6DwrI1GIhPfHwfzQbpBUo55ekq4RMPGrF+rPiAfu9xrKQFdynyGd0X\nbDjp8lJlOr2UtB4gCpEuVBcA/r5/tgUrYZO85aHb6/XYNzJYKp+Z8cyRmlc5nty8\nrl5VLyAOffa0AA1umuTBmc12Cc7kFHfCYkeEE7EPv1P91RM3fIRCcbScJQcpi2Oo\njYoojK3bdCeQIOfGghV0TxPTJ/uikX3eNxTJH9//6EOWa4nTmkhsTtPl74Koeqij\nt96BKELIfAqHOtQsApEHEVryoq0u2HZVHIFd0AUtdY8XVXiwlhadlk0EFuCN4Htv\npwyxbwfR6cEF9fr0NFWd\n=HQ5X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 461bb6fe432de673db1ab5a718e30aa84339df10\nparent 819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781988529 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781988529 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): route tenant-discovery through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 1) (#428)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 1** — second slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (after Phase 0 settings, #427). Moves the\nlifecycle-fanout's tenant-discovery queries off core-api's direct\nSQLAlchemy pool and behind new core-storage-api endpoints. **No schema\nchange.**\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access)\n- `postgres_service.tenants_list_active / _purgeable /\n_skills_factory_enabled` — the distinct-tenant and JSONB-flag SELECTs,\non the **reader replica** (`get_read_session`). Same SQL that lived in\n`core-api/services/tenants.py`.\n- `routers/tenants.py` — `GET /tenants/active`, `/tenants/purgeable`,\n`/tenants/skills-factory-enabled`. Envelope responses:\n`{tenant_ids:[...]}` for the memory-backed reads, `{org_ids:[...]}` for\nthe settings-backed one.\n\n### core-api (now a client)\n- `storage_client.list_active_tenants / list_purgeable_tenants /\nlist_skills_factory_enabled_orgs`.\n- `services/tenants.py` — the 3 helpers are now thin storage-client\nwrappers (domain \"why\" stays in docstrings; SQL moved to storage). The\n`db` param is retained (ignored) for call-site back-compat (e.g.\n`routes/memories.py` still passes it), matching the Phase 0 pattern.\n- `routes/lifecycle.py` — the cron fanout no longer opens its own\n`async_session` just to fetch the org list; it calls the now-sessionless\ndiscovery helpers directly, so the fan-out holds **no DB connection at\nall**. Drops the `core_api.db.session` import.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff + mypy clean on **both** core-api and core-storage-api.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3469 passed**.\n- `/simplify` ran (clean). New `test_tenant_discovery_storage` exercises\nthe full core-api → storage-api → DB path; forge-cron routing tests\nupdated for the dropped `db` arg.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-20T20:48:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f05f4982d70449db5de6e21c1239ff57c53e1562/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa"}]},{"sha":"819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDgxOWE3N2Y5MTEwMzUyYWQ1MDA4YzdkMTE2MGE2MGE0M2I1NDUxZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-20T16:18:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T16:18:22Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path (PR3b) (#425)\n\n## What\n\nFinal phase of the configurable-skill-targets track\n([#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/413) PR1 ·\n[#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/417) PR2 ·\n[#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/424) PR3a).\n\nAn `additive` target dir is reconciled to disk, but — unlike the\nplugin's own `owned` dir, which is published as a plugin skill — it is\n**not** on OpenClaw's skill load path, so its skills land yet stay\ninvisible to agents. This closes that gap behind an explicit **opt-in**.\n\n## Grounding (against `openclaw/openclaw`)\n\nThe documented, watched mechanism for extra skill dirs is\n**`skills.load.extraDirs: string[]` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`** —\n`docs/tools/skills-config.md`, consumed by\n`src/skills/runtime/refresh.ts`.\n\n- **NOT** `settings.skills.customDirectories` (the value the PR2 docs\nguessed) — that nested form is **deprecated**, auto-migrated by\n`settings-manager.ts` to a flat *per-agent* `settings.skills` array.\nThis PR also corrects that stale doc line.\n- `skills.load.watch` defaults `true` → a newly added dir is picked up\n**without a restart**. Caveat: a long-lived agent *session* keeps its\ncached `<available_skills>` snapshot until a fresh session\n(`--session-key`).\n- OpenClaw's own `plugins-install-command` uses the same\nread→merge→write pattern for `hooks.internal.load.extraDirs` — direct\nprecedent.\n\n## Change\n\n- `SkillTarget` gains **`register: boolean`** (default false; owned\ndefault dir always false). Parsed from `MEMCLAW_SKILL_TARGETS` entries\n(`{ dir, mode, register? }`).\n- `config.ts: ensureExtraSkillDirs(dirs)` — append-only, **idempotent**\n(canonical-path dedup, so a `~` entry matches an absolute dir), writes\n`openclaw.json` only when a dir is newly added (mirrors the\n`autoFixAllowlist` write idiom). **Fail-safe**: missing/unreadable\nconfig or a write error returns an `error`, never throws.\n- `reconcileSkills` registers `register: true` dirs after the reconcile\nloop and reports them in a new `summary.registeredDirs` (standing truth;\nrides the heartbeat → `/fleet/nodes`, **no backend change**). A\nregistration failure is logged, never aborts the heartbeat.\n- Docs corrected + `register`/watch/stale-session documented.\n\n## Tests\n\n+11: `ensureExtraSkillDirs`\n(create/append/preserve/idempotent/`~`-canonical-match/missing-config-fail-safe/empty-noop),\n`register` parsing (default false, per-entry, owned never registered),\n`reconcileSkills` integration (registers an additive dir, untouched\nwithout the flag, idempotent re-run). **344 plugin tests pass; tsc\nclean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0dfd85c9b0a9fc8966e265383dbb53816e6a5ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0dfd85c9b0a9fc8966e265383dbb53816e6a5ba9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNr1OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY3oQAFrMU3Aw5x4jTTflzeky0J9N\nvnG0nqzaYhlubsRHBwX20rBHMNW86DwDTV0ySEAMhnc0bi7hkuwhGQtuTeBelXk6\nlP5dclRCAWUgjvx5G8kSVS55SOpPpCOitqyDcT3R9xOXk1NeID/JxSp1UKDCFMFV\n/0Pibkp7wpqLHKnTtlUoBjsFcqCseUmipC7egesQXLHFm0OZz6IRz9s72OuY/YfE\nYSCNiHctjub6pk4Wg6ttdLYUJgfft5sEqBuPbqKhZejLRT/AGWad3SRUeytEN2Mn\nESDVSiwm+4efKnkd7UKNRqNZTKxi49apx6kCT4qEaKa2MrnphdJjTTuB2yk5ziYq\nzpHidqV75xUYKJhy9YIjJmQiQGyZiDxyX++a/STQ1ymV7FEbWS3D8VMMnQ/kAbpb\nKDwrZbuYDmmxUVGmNHpJE6+nqWo2W1d3A74Y4CNZSVtip6rRcMcdXMeh0S4NZ5Dg\nX2z8Anp33upjAJesQEogZQ21LRc2liTAtb85m1NWvOO5FtCq9spwOp15QGJUGIT/\nDfc6wK4nQQjwUlmi1HbXXBcnsvdm1l3KN3LKMRkYc6Gw5E+Vu0ncK6kyZ4MkkDb2\nnso+lrhaEMVTmIpJmncrsiK9QoerU6YnBUYLA1ipSjxivVn2XzJEBcWH/ILpEud1\nhtMhZ8W3nhN/jMw+iMP0\n=PCkq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0dfd85c9b0a9fc8966e265383dbb53816e6a5ba9\nparent 4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781972302 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781972302 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): auto-register additive skill dirs on OpenClaw's load path (PR3b) (#425)\n\n## What\n\nFinal phase of the configurable-skill-targets track\n([#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/413) PR1 ·\n[#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/417) PR2 ·\n[#424](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/424) PR3a).\n\nAn `additive` target dir is reconciled to disk, but — unlike the\nplugin's own `owned` dir, which is published as a plugin skill — it is\n**not** on OpenClaw's skill load path, so its skills land yet stay\ninvisible to agents. This closes that gap behind an explicit **opt-in**.\n\n## Grounding (against `openclaw/openclaw`)\n\nThe documented, watched mechanism for extra skill dirs is\n**`skills.load.extraDirs: string[]` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`** —\n`docs/tools/skills-config.md`, consumed by\n`src/skills/runtime/refresh.ts`.\n\n- **NOT** `settings.skills.customDirectories` (the value the PR2 docs\nguessed) — that nested form is **deprecated**, auto-migrated by\n`settings-manager.ts` to a flat *per-agent* `settings.skills` array.\nThis PR also corrects that stale doc line.\n- `skills.load.watch` defaults `true` → a newly added dir is picked up\n**without a restart**. Caveat: a long-lived agent *session* keeps its\ncached `<available_skills>` snapshot until a fresh session\n(`--session-key`).\n- OpenClaw's own `plugins-install-command` uses the same\nread→merge→write pattern for `hooks.internal.load.extraDirs` — direct\nprecedent.\n\n## Change\n\n- `SkillTarget` gains **`register: boolean`** (default false; owned\ndefault dir always false). Parsed from `MEMCLAW_SKILL_TARGETS` entries\n(`{ dir, mode, register? }`).\n- `config.ts: ensureExtraSkillDirs(dirs)` — append-only, **idempotent**\n(canonical-path dedup, so a `~` entry matches an absolute dir), writes\n`openclaw.json` only when a dir is newly added (mirrors the\n`autoFixAllowlist` write idiom). **Fail-safe**: missing/unreadable\nconfig or a write error returns an `error`, never throws.\n- `reconcileSkills` registers `register: true` dirs after the reconcile\nloop and reports them in a new `summary.registeredDirs` (standing truth;\nrides the heartbeat → `/fleet/nodes`, **no backend change**). A\nregistration failure is logged, never aborts the heartbeat.\n- Docs corrected + `register`/watch/stale-session documented.\n\n## Tests\n\n+11: `ensureExtraSkillDirs`\n(create/append/preserve/idempotent/`~`-canonical-match/missing-config-fail-safe/empty-noop),\n`register` parsing (default false, per-entry, owned never registered),\n`reconcileSkills` integration (registers an additive dir, untouched\nwithout the flag, idempotent re-run). **344 plugin tests pass; tsc\nclean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-20T16:18:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/819a77f9110352ad5008c7d1160a60a43b5451fa/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583"}]},{"sha":"4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ0NTBlYzBjYmNkZDNlMjk3YmRjMzUwZDVlYzc0ZjA1YjljYzE1ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-20T14:10:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T14:10:55Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): route organization_settings through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 0) (#427)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 0** — first slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (ticket task_eda5ab48). Moves the per-org\nsettings read/write off core-api's direct SQLAlchemy pool and behind new\ncore-storage-api endpoints.\n\nSettings are the highest-traffic pool acquisition and were the root of\nthe 06-19 prod `ConnectTimeout` — the fire-and-forget\n`get_raw_settings(db=None)` cold-cache path opened its own DB session.\nThis removes that DB dependency entirely. **No schema change**\n(`organization_settings`/`_audit` already live in core-storage-api's\nmigrations).\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access)\n- `postgres_service.organization_settings_get` — read overrides (reader\nreplica).\n- `postgres_service.organization_settings_update` — the transactional\nupsert (`FOR UPDATE` read → flat diff → JSONB `||` merge → audit row)\nkept in **one** server-side transaction so the lost-update guard still\nholds (it can't span an HTTP read+write). Returns `{settings, changed}`;\na no-op payload writes neither row.\n- `routers/organization_settings.py` — `GET` + `POST\n/organization-settings/{org_id}`. POST (not PUT) so the storage_client's\nnon-idempotent `_post` path applies (connection-phase retry only);\nre-applying an identical payload is a no-op anyway.\n\n### core-api (now a client)\n- `storage_client.get_org_settings` / `update_org_settings`.\n- `services/organization_settings.py` now calls the storage client. The\n**TTL cache** (cache hits still short-circuit before any HTTP call), the\n`SETTINGS_CHANGED` publish, the schema validators, and\n`DEFAULT_SETTINGS` resolution all stay client-side. The old `db=None`\nself-session fallback is gone — every caller takes the same\nstorage-client path. The `db` params are retained (ignored) for\ncall-site back-compat; removing them across ~49 sites is a later phase.\n\n### common\n- `common/organization_settings_merge.py` — `deep_merge` /\n`diff_settings` lifted here (dependency-free) so both services share one\nimplementation.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff + mypy clean on **both** core-api and core-storage-api.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3464 passed**.\n- `/simplify` applied.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ebf8d9e547a77f8133c9b8d641992932c9d54d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3ebf8d9e547a77f8133c9b8d641992932c9d54d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNp9vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQLIQAGihuZya5Fh8RDVtKiblb60E\nbPmnz8BcGTcXb/NL/oNbAwwO4JW3CalBIIkTglRsn2lnKB3XgfnKdMqQO4x6V5q8\nA90/ZJ0suJjPwCMOLAn9rb5FZTzgR4IU8GYr01p65MzFvj1El2BLkCGrJzTUFzT1\nAy4UhHrn7cR5JI1Mk13a5G4yDUpYz5ElbqGp97IHzEFJhddPpVSxFZjXH9euRpic\n6g76pf2FYbynwnzeGm8YhfU3hE5FrPdrQtFf9f86EiggZToNQKL9mQnYgB60lE9t\n9nayrykbC9ovTSZobbvPvNcy17bV6xoRsiT/hReFZPN/6hpwxckz/aA7rIMmyOoj\nW2FfvRlxP8GXYumZLpXkqpnEAh8DZcjIkyig+1Ne5Pwu06FUjKSyqRurhwAe/mRs\nvFAlyYhYKNgO8uGeI15Exgsk04cQx0fxOJRWlO/Qiwgcasq65J1hwgXSWZngah3Q\nEmk3ZiINPJHrnR+NJ7iQ4nm4+GtE/pC+YNB9crqU46IATP/6d8aKFTFiFIUCR0iE\nFeeCcfONCazUTAsjER4VwJbL/NJ7V7oMmj7LdhZp5DilyVm39jfjewUsGgdEXxOS\nSZE1qBNMUpCDLWbsOm77Fqfhw8WZFi6mzG71vcnHKLSGf9jayidQvZpTQYmsX7m8\niruse2Ddf3MXFmv8igRV\n=L9WS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3ebf8d9e547a77f8133c9b8d641992932c9d54d3\nparent a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781964655 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781964655 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): route organization_settings through core-storage-api (Fix 2 Phase 0) (#427)\n\n**Fix 2 Phase 0** — first slice of the Tier-2 *\"no DB outside\ncore-storage-api\"* migration (ticket task_eda5ab48). Moves the per-org\nsettings read/write off core-api's direct SQLAlchemy pool and behind new\ncore-storage-api endpoints.\n\nSettings are the highest-traffic pool acquisition and were the root of\nthe 06-19 prod `ConnectTimeout` — the fire-and-forget\n`get_raw_settings(db=None)` cold-cache path opened its own DB session.\nThis removes that DB dependency entirely. **No schema change**\n(`organization_settings`/`_audit` already live in core-storage-api's\nmigrations).\n\n### core-storage-api (now owns the DB access)\n- `postgres_service.organization_settings_get` — read overrides (reader\nreplica).\n- `postgres_service.organization_settings_update` — the transactional\nupsert (`FOR UPDATE` read → flat diff → JSONB `||` merge → audit row)\nkept in **one** server-side transaction so the lost-update guard still\nholds (it can't span an HTTP read+write). Returns `{settings, changed}`;\na no-op payload writes neither row.\n- `routers/organization_settings.py` — `GET` + `POST\n/organization-settings/{org_id}`. POST (not PUT) so the storage_client's\nnon-idempotent `_post` path applies (connection-phase retry only);\nre-applying an identical payload is a no-op anyway.\n\n### core-api (now a client)\n- `storage_client.get_org_settings` / `update_org_settings`.\n- `services/organization_settings.py` now calls the storage client. The\n**TTL cache** (cache hits still short-circuit before any HTTP call), the\n`SETTINGS_CHANGED` publish, the schema validators, and\n`DEFAULT_SETTINGS` resolution all stay client-side. The old `db=None`\nself-session fallback is gone — every caller takes the same\nstorage-client path. The `db` params are retained (ignored) for\ncall-site back-compat; removing them across ~49 sites is a later phase.\n\n### common\n- `common/organization_settings_merge.py` — `deep_merge` /\n`diff_settings` lifted here (dependency-free) so both services share one\nimplementation.\n\n### Validation\n- ruff + mypy clean on **both** core-api and core-storage-api.\n- Full core-api suite green: **3464 passed**.\n- `/simplify` applied.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-20T14:10:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4450ec0cbcdd3e297bdc350d5ec74f05b9cc1583/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180"}]},{"sha":"a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGEwODJmM2ZhNDcwZWI3NTAzZjdmN2MzOTk2MWFmNjU3YTc2MTAxODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-19T19:52:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T19:52:29Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): cut prod connect-timeout + rate-limit-Redis log noise (#426)\n\n## Why\nFollow-up from the 2026-06-19 prod error review. Two transient\nsignatures dominate the (low) prod error volume — both already\nretry-handled / fail-open, so this **reduces noise**, not a correctness\nfix:\n- `pubsub handler raised; nacking for redelivery` —\n`httpx.ConnectTimeout` from the `memory.embedded`/`enriched` consumers'\n`get_memory` reads to core-storage during cold starts/recycles.\n- `Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error` — Redis `ConnectionReset`\n(single-zone Memorystore maintenance / idle eviction) → slowapi fails\nopen.\n\n## What\n**1. Idempotent storage reads ride out a storage cold start**\n(`common/http_retry.py` + `storage_client.py`)\n`with_retry` gains `connect_phase_max_attempts`: connection-phase\nexceptions (`ConnectTimeout`/`ConnectError`/`PoolTimeout` — provably\nnever sent) get a higher retry budget, while `ReadTimeout`/5xx stay\ncapped at `max_attempts` (no 5xx-storm amplification; backoff still\ncapped at `RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_S`). `_get`/`_get_list` opt in via a small\n`_read_retry` wrapper using `CONNECT_PHASE_MAX_ATTEMPTS` — **the same\nbudget POSTs already use** (`with_connect_phase_retry`). So a\nmulti-second storage blip no longer exhausts the 3 GET attempts and\nsurfaces as a handler failure → nack → redelivery on the Pub/Sub path.\n\n**2. Rate-limiter Redis resilience** (`rate_limit.py`)\nThe slowapi `Limiter`'s Redis client now gets `socket_keepalive` +\n`health_check_interval=30s` + bounded connect/op timeouts via\n`storage_options` (Redis-only — `memory://` takes none). A connection\nthe server already closed is PING-detected and reconnected **before**\nuse rather than reset mid-command. `swallow_errors` fail-open stays the\nsafety net.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- GET-only (the connect-timeout noise is on the read path);\n`_patch`/`_delete` unchanged (no documented noise there).\n- No behavior change when healthy; backoff bounded; 5xx not\nover-retried.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `mypy` clean on core-api +\ncore-storage-api; `/simplify` applied.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68078279f2d31ccb71fbb486fe906bb8bb410a76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/68078279f2d31ccb71fbb486fe906bb8bb410a76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNZ39CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAccQQAEgXvkLxx61+KQbrowNXe9qX\n7Z74kVW8ORYZ/WTmnx64Amz3QexY13HiNYRJh1RHpjtzhfDk7KYzXTMAjzewzDVR\nqDBSUyN5gTUYXORP+M6iKSM5Y93/uM2/4ZVtyL+rA8ZDA67I6N+4TX9XC9uOGB+T\nms/ULaReqVqRIa5rDOe9hQ6X9KFzHKg49/8hCbTW1W488Z5G3L9VjN1S+kMbZTul\nYTV3R9HkNhaURps9mBXdUlwcW4hyuUg3jZ6p282GUfOMPzIDiZpqCOmb9XPBbHmI\niwPf/aFBIP4V5biRypZg+xaWayGIcOgScrJc3Jm0roMW1YydgPkPO5SS1SwX1Mm3\nBIwGBSYBkgbWIeZJxBcSuVKKENoYWG5ztWaNsYQw9pgly63BDRDIUbxrcpttCsIN\nuCI94EPlqQI+ENnHNXMYUxIx+KME7Wx6EvoAxk5yMR0m8VKu0QAXbDzldmpjOttJ\nUsi6T/57cdBjn5GPF2T+N/R6+BdzbdXmGHNVDrDstqS4LTnbX9iRbZt7nDY2I72k\nw6cppeNPlBMu+eN349nVVUbRWJZeDicMhJCbL9RhH7VV6cm54pofYXN2Jv8gvAAm\nC+IajuXHIcg+gHyDDOdzRF2qkdQnpWdsWvw6vVH3qtx4V9OMJe75Nzd5zEPHPdJn\nnEEqa0kYPLv8ZyMlsmlO\n=x/eE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 68078279f2d31ccb71fbb486fe906bb8bb410a76\nparent 04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781898749 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781898749 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): cut prod connect-timeout + rate-limit-Redis log noise (#426)\n\n## Why\nFollow-up from the 2026-06-19 prod error review. Two transient\nsignatures dominate the (low) prod error volume — both already\nretry-handled / fail-open, so this **reduces noise**, not a correctness\nfix:\n- `pubsub handler raised; nacking for redelivery` —\n`httpx.ConnectTimeout` from the `memory.embedded`/`enriched` consumers'\n`get_memory` reads to core-storage during cold starts/recycles.\n- `Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error` — Redis `ConnectionReset`\n(single-zone Memorystore maintenance / idle eviction) → slowapi fails\nopen.\n\n## What\n**1. Idempotent storage reads ride out a storage cold start**\n(`common/http_retry.py` + `storage_client.py`)\n`with_retry` gains `connect_phase_max_attempts`: connection-phase\nexceptions (`ConnectTimeout`/`ConnectError`/`PoolTimeout` — provably\nnever sent) get a higher retry budget, while `ReadTimeout`/5xx stay\ncapped at `max_attempts` (no 5xx-storm amplification; backoff still\ncapped at `RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_S`). `_get`/`_get_list` opt in via a small\n`_read_retry` wrapper using `CONNECT_PHASE_MAX_ATTEMPTS` — **the same\nbudget POSTs already use** (`with_connect_phase_retry`). So a\nmulti-second storage blip no longer exhausts the 3 GET attempts and\nsurfaces as a handler failure → nack → redelivery on the Pub/Sub path.\n\n**2. Rate-limiter Redis resilience** (`rate_limit.py`)\nThe slowapi `Limiter`'s Redis client now gets `socket_keepalive` +\n`health_check_interval=30s` + bounded connect/op timeouts via\n`storage_options` (Redis-only — `memory://` takes none). A connection\nthe server already closed is PING-detected and reconnected **before**\nuse rather than reset mid-command. `swallow_errors` fail-open stays the\nsafety net.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- GET-only (the connect-timeout noise is on the read path);\n`_patch`/`_delete` unchanged (no documented noise there).\n- No behavior change when healthy; backoff bounded; 5xx not\nover-retried.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `mypy` clean on core-api +\ncore-storage-api; `/simplify` applied.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-19T19:52:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a082f3fa470eb7503f7f7c39961af657a7610180/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334"}]},{"sha":"04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA0MTIwZjI0MWY2MDgzNjE1ZGNhYjJkZTQ5ZmNhNjYxZDY5MmMzMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-18T07:17:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T07:17:57Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): per-target reconcile observability (PR3a) (#424)\n\n## What\n\nThird phase of the configurable-skill-targets track (after\n[#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/413) PR1 and\n[#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/417) PR2). This is\n**PR3a** — the observability half. The auto-register-into-OpenClaw half\n(**PR3b**) is deferred until the OpenClaw `customDirectories` key path +\nreload behavior are confirmed against OpenClaw source.\n\nThe reconcile summary aggregates `installed` / `added` / `removed` /\n`collisions` / `protected` across **all** configured targets (deduped +\nsorted). With more than one target — an extra `owned` dir, or an\n`additive` shared dir — an operator can't tell **which** dir a skill\nlanded in, or collided in.\n\n## Change\n\n`ReconcileSummary` gains a `targets[]` field — one\n`TargetReconcileResult` per dir reconciled this tick:\n\n```ts\n{ dir, mode, installed, added, removed, collisions, protected }\n```\n\nin `resolveSkillTargets()` order (owned dir first), each array sorted.\nThe existing top-level arrays are **unchanged** (still the cross-target\ndedup), so this is purely additive.\n\nThe whole summary already rides the heartbeat, and the backend stores\n`nodes.metadata.reconcile` as an opaque blob — so `targets[]` surfaces\non `GET /api/v1/fleet/nodes` with **no backend change**.\n\nAlso fixes a stale doc comment on `SkillTargetMode` that still claimed\n`additive` was \"parsed but NOT yet acted on … skipped with a warning\" —\nPR2 implemented it.\n\n## Tests\n\n+2: default single target → one entry mirroring the aggregate; owned +\nadditive each report their own slice while the aggregate dedups (install\nfrom owned, collision from additive). Docs updated. **333 plugin tests\npass; tsc clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad2cab7e81d76c7e47745589ea58da55ff5809ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ad2cab7e81d76c7e47745589ea58da55ff5809ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqM5ulCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqxYQAJ3ms1byqH9KUwBdtiCwzmxZ\nlixzOTRQ5spqBDkqNx44MjZI/Rw4+W7XNXIvXv559W5fsC+Qh9rEFM4ltQADSS6q\nLDBGQz5gCZTCL/mtcPAAEtfy4TD3sDGhSP1At1D7OZVcEazXmDOU9XUI99Aop9GQ\nCshNq33VXovcyBfRs47HSakMgNTye8TeuNmENt27IMUKihxzaOOhi0AxoDEI/JDi\nioOAnIF5kOJjH8a5yjEtgiXhCzp7hE9vFZznJPiV3jARe6ACD/c8i0o/nsBeIAgh\npVOVmEFGhLs+W91bIouwW34Xlloq5aHJmoXqA1bLJTQ0zdf8aJfOiC5nkEEdgCtx\nhuYk4R38VQ+Z4+MLkeL6Q87I/BwB9mISNmjlaFqe+GdJIuB8199+q3Hx2tI6h99d\ncHZGeguRWZb0e5zaoklFVXMGhyp1/WhFGFfl21JJ3bDR1VXL98n77RVjbzYmDb0+\nsdDOHZeTZuAXkxzVOpJqVHrGeRPkkBIjOuU+McWGX+EevIsrPfazYrWbYFtfdq47\nSabJfMbxlMrvQlnHXuXJOY62S0uBjZc8EYowQapW74o0yRwDGhGKztLp6lFgX8km\naNnZErlDBV0XzyVvDh7Ho5nzz0eT/dc4DGJeBhtOqY2ZvGeSaZVTkwPh6nS6GKrI\nAQJNRKMqyViKKqcTDut2\n=hMDh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ad2cab7e81d76c7e47745589ea58da55ff5809ec\nparent eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781767077 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781767077 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): per-target reconcile observability (PR3a) (#424)\n\n## What\n\nThird phase of the configurable-skill-targets track (after\n[#413](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/413) PR1 and\n[#417](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/417) PR2). This is\n**PR3a** — the observability half. The auto-register-into-OpenClaw half\n(**PR3b**) is deferred until the OpenClaw `customDirectories` key path +\nreload behavior are confirmed against OpenClaw source.\n\nThe reconcile summary aggregates `installed` / `added` / `removed` /\n`collisions` / `protected` across **all** configured targets (deduped +\nsorted). With more than one target — an extra `owned` dir, or an\n`additive` shared dir — an operator can't tell **which** dir a skill\nlanded in, or collided in.\n\n## Change\n\n`ReconcileSummary` gains a `targets[]` field — one\n`TargetReconcileResult` per dir reconciled this tick:\n\n```ts\n{ dir, mode, installed, added, removed, collisions, protected }\n```\n\nin `resolveSkillTargets()` order (owned dir first), each array sorted.\nThe existing top-level arrays are **unchanged** (still the cross-target\ndedup), so this is purely additive.\n\nThe whole summary already rides the heartbeat, and the backend stores\n`nodes.metadata.reconcile` as an opaque blob — so `targets[]` surfaces\non `GET /api/v1/fleet/nodes` with **no backend change**.\n\nAlso fixes a stale doc comment on `SkillTargetMode` that still claimed\n`additive` was \"parsed but NOT yet acted on … skipped with a warning\" —\nPR2 implemented it.\n\n## Tests\n\n+2: default single target → one entry mirroring the aggregate; owned +\nadditive each report their own slice while the aggregate dedups (install\nfrom owned, collision from additive). Docs updated. **333 plugin tests\npass; tsc clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T07:17:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/04120f241f6083615dcab2de49fca661d692c334/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c"}]},{"sha":"eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVhZTQwYzg5MGVlZjk1OWU1Zjc5MTQ1MjNjMTc3YmJkNGVlYjIzNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T22:17:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T22:17:52Z"},"message":"test(authz): de-flake search scope_agent test (query exact content, not bare marker) (#423)\n\nHardens\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py::test_rest_search_scope_agent_uses_authenticated_identity`,\nwhich flaked in CI on its positive assertion (\"author cannot see own\nscope_agent row in search\") — e.g. the failure on #416's run.\n\n## Root cause\n`/search` ranks by a composite vector+relevance score over the **shared\ntest corpus**. The test queried the **bare random marker**, which under\nthe word-set fake embedder (`text.lower().split()`) is only a *partial*\nmatch to the row's full content — so the author's row ranked **out of\n`top_k` / below the relevance cutoff** (observed: `top_k=20` returned\nonly ~5 rows). The scope_agent *visibility* logic was always correct;\nonly the ranking-dependent retrieval was non-deterministic.\n`write_mode=\"strong\"` already removed the embed-timing race, but not the\nranking one.\n\n## Fix (robust, kept on /search)\nQuery the row's **exact content** instead of the bare marker. The fake\nembedder is symmetric and deterministic, so an exact-content query is a\n**similarity-1.0** hit — the author's freshly-written row clears any\ncutoff and is returned **regardless of corpus noise**. The assertions\nnow hinge only on the scope_agent **filter** (bob excluded; author\nincluded), not on stochastic rank ordering. Bob is filtered out\npre-ranking regardless, so the security assertion stays deterministic\ntoo.\n\nKept on `/search` (the test's purpose) rather than moving the positive\nto `/list` — the adjacent\n`test_rest_list_uses_authenticated_identity_not_param` already covers\nlist-side scope_agent visibility deterministically, so a `/list`\nassertion here would just duplicate it.\n\n`ruff check` clean for the file; the change is test-only. (Note: this PR\ndoes **not** touch the pre-existing ruff-version-skew formatting drift\nelsewhere in the file — `tests/` isn't part of CI's ruff paths.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae595638c1643f866994dde74dfd2dcad18094cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ae595638c1643f866994dde74dfd2dcad18094cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMx0QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqjsQAEchDjlM+ASqAdaRMIWDXtLq\nh3513/E6wDxKIxq8HlEzVSzQFvgIO+1MazsHSIs3i9JxaXMc5js2GX2eRiTzaFMm\ndaoiYCPDWTPdoFssD+cIb1rgT+YA/0dzxDfogPUO27J3Rwycj+gKx3pRFcoFsa2r\nBOLbIYPLuqkV7xS4zUTofzk53wrJQ9BCVIyQ/4mDXktD4s4TOOVD4smYSATUuCnc\nQaemZqR212hgg9+KaGgz6ny+PLEheWtxWnPvV+QAc040UUXvGAgAiThD/dE3oAxF\nM2unbemVfXyTX/isyoQbaywqgvKv2i5/l+T05ADvMlFV3q86NZEDrZDOMDMdvHmU\nVmUXYCGMxdsSsvLvK1Sbf675U+SnFabA2MvrdZK1PFaFe/5WRph59PMx/+QXa9Cu\ndeRaqNJY27UIwIZ48z9oQ9ranwrTsOFmZh+nTQk4lmaftXOjiBYBbaVPTRl8PzVn\nXT0MvjmvD357FXl82wGwKgx1/GAw6l1ewQiz76wYAjOWLgHyf+Irzi6FEk4ddLaS\nfCPaJ218se9y9hzHDODSLRjPyFTQczAl9lkYHHZMJYI372sEAON0kcmFcacJyJF5\n5IOQSryW0r+j250WH3ricvXjNVieDg+xh3hNHeneB3A+yqDW/wFy1IsEkvnfq0X2\n52nagUQi6ZHsRLRThMJk\n=otbs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ae595638c1643f866994dde74dfd2dcad18094cb\nparent 414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781734672 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781734672 +0300\n\ntest(authz): de-flake search scope_agent test (query exact content, not bare marker) (#423)\n\nHardens\n`tests/test_memory_byid_authz.py::test_rest_search_scope_agent_uses_authenticated_identity`,\nwhich flaked in CI on its positive assertion (\"author cannot see own\nscope_agent row in search\") — e.g. the failure on #416's run.\n\n## Root cause\n`/search` ranks by a composite vector+relevance score over the **shared\ntest corpus**. The test queried the **bare random marker**, which under\nthe word-set fake embedder (`text.lower().split()`) is only a *partial*\nmatch to the row's full content — so the author's row ranked **out of\n`top_k` / below the relevance cutoff** (observed: `top_k=20` returned\nonly ~5 rows). The scope_agent *visibility* logic was always correct;\nonly the ranking-dependent retrieval was non-deterministic.\n`write_mode=\"strong\"` already removed the embed-timing race, but not the\nranking one.\n\n## Fix (robust, kept on /search)\nQuery the row's **exact content** instead of the bare marker. The fake\nembedder is symmetric and deterministic, so an exact-content query is a\n**similarity-1.0** hit — the author's freshly-written row clears any\ncutoff and is returned **regardless of corpus noise**. The assertions\nnow hinge only on the scope_agent **filter** (bob excluded; author\nincluded), not on stochastic rank ordering. Bob is filtered out\npre-ranking regardless, so the security assertion stays deterministic\ntoo.\n\nKept on `/search` (the test's purpose) rather than moving the positive\nto `/list` — the adjacent\n`test_rest_list_uses_authenticated_identity_not_param` already covers\nlist-side scope_agent visibility deterministically, so a `/list`\nassertion here would just duplicate it.\n\n`ruff check` clean for the file; the change is test-only. (Note: this PR\ndoes **not** touch the pre-existing ruff-version-skew formatting drift\nelsewhere in the file — `tests/` isn't part of CI's ruff paths.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T22:17:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/eae40c890eef959e5f7914523c177bbd4eeb235c/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283"}]},{"sha":"414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQxNGFjNzM0ZGEwYzZjOGQ4ZGE2Njk4ODJlZTA3ZTExMjdkMzAyODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T22:08:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T22:08:00Z"},"message":"ci: add CodeQL SAST workflow (python + js/ts) (#422)\n\n## What\nAdds GitHub **CodeQL** SAST (`.github/workflows/codeql.yml`) over the\nPython (`core-api`, `core-storage-api`) + JS/TS (`plugin`,\n`clients/typescript`) sources.\n\n## Why\n**Free on this public repo** (no GitHub Advanced Security needed) — the\ndeeper, dataflow-based SAST layer that complements `ci.yml`\n(ruff/mypy/pytest), `claude_code_review.yml`, and the new\n`security-scan.yml` (bandit + pip-audit, #420). Results land in\n**Security → Code scanning** + inline PR annotations.\n\n## Triggers\nPRs (diff-scoped alerts), push to `main` (the default-branch baseline\nthe PR diffs compare against), and weekly. Actions are SHA-pinned\n(`codeql-action` v4.36.2) per the repo convention.\n\n## Notes\n- Python + JS/TS are interpreted → no build step (CodeQL extracts\ndirectly).\n- Default query suite; `queries: security-extended` can be added later\nfor broader coverage once the initial baseline is triaged.\n- On the **private** `caura-memclaw-enterprise` repo CodeQL needs GitHub\nAdvanced Security enabled — out of scope here (that repo gets bandit +\npip-audit via #568).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c808e233d3334006fb5991a81283cbdaa9b1f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9c808e233d3334006fb5991a81283cbdaa9b1f43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMxrACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoMYQAF/NpB2Navx54FMX/KqNMIZ4\nYUpm4Ghfu7+NpH+7WowETZO3EONVULSMBI3iVVNJXiCNX+ssQTsnQZ6Nvig5m6HO\nHFa//jowJjeP/WKYQrN0tte5GanVMQ3UwWwTWLXbdXnQ6dZdQrcOxI9A4Fz03iz5\nccYUnlTg0AlXYL8uK+DEU1UbkWsNOGKSTNnCL98JWZggzA35p8h0Z3UucL6Fu8CX\nuQALNevODTrfYXgEFis0GWjxI/GdCGkd/HHY9Ja2u4bRTXrpQu9rzsWQYfiML1o7\nk7L7WMBgXG4KOu6ZvoEeLUwjzPgB213d+PDuMmyume/kZgEUAjWf0fK7Y/ag+wXd\nHR9g1Ws2oUcQBMH4DCNPHn0qu6W72EfX8F7IGFFr5KeExVXLuQVvqA/8pl3GGr4f\nIvFuHB/gT1qn4r+QPNwGvO7cnr8irAmbgW2YeUU06MLL8zbNdp191PLD7hSNK2uJ\nxeP7lR7hWRd+KKwrgmCccG/HBT9ZS72AYBJ97YGH1KS/bpIZbaJfpPGeYS55+v/P\nFAAuGdss/juTFbD4SVbFSNU/m6qL5LTv/1THSRuL0glR+0ovVWNnIQnT0qs38dS2\ne6IQPVab2NxLKbxmRRGFwUU/Zm4gEeahx92H7ssQ8RSVvbUW3Ry/oRdfXVsAE8mE\nFhc/LFwXomV/UPbnEF8k\n=mb7y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9c808e233d3334006fb5991a81283cbdaa9b1f43\nparent 7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781734080 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781734080 +0300\n\nci: add CodeQL SAST workflow (python + js/ts) (#422)\n\n## What\nAdds GitHub **CodeQL** SAST (`.github/workflows/codeql.yml`) over the\nPython (`core-api`, `core-storage-api`) + JS/TS (`plugin`,\n`clients/typescript`) sources.\n\n## Why\n**Free on this public repo** (no GitHub Advanced Security needed) — the\ndeeper, dataflow-based SAST layer that complements `ci.yml`\n(ruff/mypy/pytest), `claude_code_review.yml`, and the new\n`security-scan.yml` (bandit + pip-audit, #420). Results land in\n**Security → Code scanning** + inline PR annotations.\n\n## Triggers\nPRs (diff-scoped alerts), push to `main` (the default-branch baseline\nthe PR diffs compare against), and weekly. Actions are SHA-pinned\n(`codeql-action` v4.36.2) per the repo convention.\n\n## Notes\n- Python + JS/TS are interpreted → no build step (CodeQL extracts\ndirectly).\n- Default query suite; `queries: security-extended` can be added later\nfor broader coverage once the initial baseline is triaged.\n- On the **private** `caura-memclaw-enterprise` repo CodeQL needs GitHub\nAdvanced Security enabled — out of scope here (that repo gets bandit +\npip-audit via #568).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T22:08:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/414ac734da0c6c8d8da669882ee07e1127d30283/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e"}]},{"sha":"7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc4MjlkMjQzOTNmZWMxZGJiZTMxZWNhOGYwY2RiZjMzYzVjODY2NmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T22:01:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T22:01:09Z"},"message":"test: de-flake scope_agent search test (synchronous write_mode) (#421)\n\n## What\nDe-flakes `test_rest_search_scope_agent_uses_authenticated_identity`.\n\n## Root cause\nThe test writes a `scope_agent` memory then immediately `POST\n/api/v1/search` for it. The write→search index (embedding) is\n**eventually consistent**, so the search could transiently return `[]`\nand the \"author sees own row\" assertion failed intermittently — this is\nthe flake that reddened CI on the security-scan PR #420 (which touched\nno source).\n\n## Fix\nWrite with **`write_mode=\"strong\"`** so embedding/indexing is\nsynchronous and the row is searchable immediately — the same\ndeterministic pattern\n`test_a13_fleet_less_visible_to_fleet_scoped_search` documents and uses.\n`_write` gains an optional `write_mode` (default unset), so the\nby-id/list tests (which read from the DB directly, not search) are\nunaffected.\n\nAs a bonus, the negative check (bob can't see it) is now meaningful —\nthe row is guaranteed indexed when bob searches, rather than passing\nvacuously on an empty index.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"070fbde105db363835828a51f8e0d0cf5c26f2d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/070fbde105db363835828a51f8e0d0cf5c26f2d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMxklCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/LcQAKVbovZoSJ0K3zTstLj04w92\nQ4YP8K3qJ5khRgXRYMgsmvc2UwNn3UqvNMGDX2o7FMzDtDM9d3m3ra8hiBGMbO99\nX7LYKfrOFzguJ7Z7/9KOsAKcCR5nx0TQBlR2QTjhj30MWOtI62MqESReBnrPS30r\n6fX5tKhdok8Haamy84I3reecWgG9SXM8hVC/dvC8ogEB9lXkr9EjE6vTevC0WGdB\nPqbiJ6TdYmBq4LwVZidiKAW6wD9Ujm5ArHP+4DtFEkB48aHqdvLKYb4Dkg6pTbVp\nLz1GMeZfmFIB/ZDz1htZlrUSj2MevxIZtOoemT/ZE9HcQh6YV4FK3tTOV8SnBgGH\nETlLaFwh2qioQjNmebeuibwSH/yES56S7nLZuCtxoYi8F/A4CZn2zgIAXdT6O+Rt\np7u/xe5L0hmPFivt5hSSLVC8i7UAvZSjzs6JI8dxBH1tsGn6wGFhsZsOEAoraNZ+\nhpnrshgwZxoMZKLcHfZJbMKLX43Ndu1FUrEIZF10a2IrKR/YoLZPVZr/fboO0rNv\n1BHx3/eG7WB8BG3DdReVlj1rhexglU5DHufvbbxvM+aft8SpiqO+BDVfF96oYUDv\nrcTdiH9nPtD0iIWNnogmMKy6J3+UC9dGazRAz/MFHINEXYdtTLhOsR5magGp8fXX\n9idAjykzFwqJkdAB0LWn\n=Tmju\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 070fbde105db363835828a51f8e0d0cf5c26f2d1\nparent aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781733669 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781733669 +0300\n\ntest: de-flake scope_agent search test (synchronous write_mode) (#421)\n\n## What\nDe-flakes `test_rest_search_scope_agent_uses_authenticated_identity`.\n\n## Root cause\nThe test writes a `scope_agent` memory then immediately `POST\n/api/v1/search` for it. The write→search index (embedding) is\n**eventually consistent**, so the search could transiently return `[]`\nand the \"author sees own row\" assertion failed intermittently — this is\nthe flake that reddened CI on the security-scan PR #420 (which touched\nno source).\n\n## Fix\nWrite with **`write_mode=\"strong\"`** so embedding/indexing is\nsynchronous and the row is searchable immediately — the same\ndeterministic pattern\n`test_a13_fleet_less_visible_to_fleet_scoped_search` documents and uses.\n`_write` gains an optional `write_mode` (default unset), so the\nby-id/list tests (which read from the DB directly, not search) are\nunaffected.\n\nAs a bonus, the negative check (bob can't see it) is now meaningful —\nthe row is guaranteed indexed when bob searches, rather than passing\nvacuously on an empty index.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T22:01:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7829d24393fec1dbbe31eca8f0cdbf33c5c8666e/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931"}]},{"sha":"aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGFhNGJlOGU5MTNkYTVmOGQ2NDNjYTFmOThkNmQ5YWFhMGY4MjE5MzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T21:45:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T21:45:33Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): harden business/personal pre-gate (timeout, audit truth, fail-closed, audit durability) (#416)\n\nHardens the opt-in business/personal pre-gate\n([#403](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/403)) against\nfive findings. **Opt-in throughout — no behavior change for tenants that\nhaven't enabled it; `fail_closed` defaults to false (current fail-open\npreserved).**\n\n## Findings addressed\n\n| # | Finding | Fix |\n|---|---------|-----|\n| **1** | Classifier ran inline on the write path with **no whole-chain\ntimeout** — a slow/unreachable provider could stall a write ~100s\n(retries × fallback). | Hard ceiling\n`PREGATE_CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (env-tunable, default **5s**) via\n`asyncio.wait_for`; on timeout fail-open + alertable warning.\n`call_with_fallback`'s `timeout=` is per-attempt, so it can't bound the\nchain — hence the outer wrap. |\n| **2** | `min_confidence` does **not** reduce false rejects as\ndocumented — the post-enrichment backstop drops any `\"personal\"` verdict\nunconditionally (no enrichment confidence exists to gate on). |\nDoc-only: corrected the settings comment + `_GovNBPregate` docstring to\ndescribe the real behavior (gates the *early* drop only; defers\nborderline content to the accurate backstop). |\n| **3** | Under provider fallback the audit recorded the **intended**\nprovider/model, not the one that actually classified. | Capture the live\n`provider`/`model` on `BusinessClassification` (from the `LLMProvider`\ninstance) and audit those. |\n| **4** | A `drop` tenant whose classifier is unavailable **silently\nstored** unclassified content. | Detect it (`result.provider is None`) +\nalertable warning; add opt-in `pregate.fail_closed` (default false) that\nrejects the write (**503** + `nonbusiness_pregate_unavailable` audit)\ninstead of storing unclassified content. |\n| **5** | Governance enforcement audits could be **dropped under\naudit-queue overflow** while the write was still refused — contradicting\n`emit_governance_audit`'s \"can't be silently disabled\" promise. |\n`log_action(critical=True)`: on overflow, critical events fall back to a\nsynchronous storage write instead of dropping; `enqueue()` now reports\nwhether it queued. Applied to **every** reject/destructive-enforcement\naudit (pregate drop + unavailable, deterministic + LLM PII drop,\nnon-business drop, fast-mode remediation soft-deletes, bulk drop).\nFlag/mask/keep-private stay best-effort. |\n\n## Decisions\n- **Finding 2** is doc-only because the enrichment signal carries no\nconfidence (`business_relevance: str` in `common/enrichment/schema.py`),\nso wiring a confidence floor into the backstop would need a broad\nenrichment-schema change affecting all tenants.\n- **Finding 4** `fail_closed` setting lives in OSS\n`organization_settings` `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` (no split). Enterprise\n\"Content Policy\" UI toggle is a follow-up in the enterprise repo.\n- **Finding 5** `critical` is scoped to reject/destructive paths (audit\nis the only record); high-volume flag/keep-private paths keep the\nfire-and-forget queue, so the hot path is unaffected.\n\n## Verification\n- New/updated tests: `tests/test_business_personal_pregate.py`\n(timeout→fail-open, fallback audit attribution, fail-open observability\ndefault, `fail_closed` 503) and `tests/test_audit_queue.py` (`enqueue`\nbool contract, critical sync-fallback on overflow). All green.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src); `mypy` clean on **both** core-api and\ncore-storage-api.\n- The DB-backed `test_governance_e2e.py` / `test_audit_chain.py`\nintegration suites fail identically on clean `main` in this sandbox (no\ndatabase) — they'll exercise these changes under CI's DB.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"107a992fff5d6a44daf294b8ecc1f1893d51ad73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/107a992fff5d6a44daf294b8ecc1f1893d51ad73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMxV9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiH8QACbrNzw2DQ3Q6fB8geeSFmPD\nFCPzeoE+7gMwwIKOVlQocjRokVT5soB49hi8ofqpzNP/xx7VFoRm10oDS945fiHl\nYoOktEyg7uHekn/hHjp/xUSJ9La0S7WPN4mSS2CDLdMLGkmFfnF142Su/zUBXQ6v\n8nycfZMgP5L6IR2uJUakOAz/pyukyyEMAkhmEKs/E8FBZvATaNIwFRqlSvpvP+GS\nno/itijGxYYxzeKZSzBZZwLq2y1jARirulPQfzmMzvLbYCDPBQ2pxHw7j0uWqTht\nkV6OvoQQQdIlqVaymBylNOuTsGeE1VEorVsoel4LFfjmT5CaiYdVLGj2iB9ZYz7O\nXqSp611wo9Is/iYgRmY6/eD9ZwVAlSNAQ4U2zmKXP/4R6P6Y085YoHBlXq5TjaoW\nEMRltKt834S8R2w/3iO+6iv9VXM5iFWbvVxw8moF8obk4qlTdjdFOCUTUNc9N//j\nKa5lyCI1lMCLaQ0qn4fQ1YWNQhjH1BL007qzGGd4ZgeunVFfAFpNKVIDjsZ3gElX\npA1DUyGEg0toEgv4iUGrqCLK+xY8s3M8wvMBLQ5MJVHRpNwwmKa7qYh3RMppOUbF\naPbtwTUXnEKClfaTZ9oaiRUwbH3UbJHw9rb4PYmjEUpj1VpA3Sl/ZMbmggdmj5Qc\n1z966D92TtEGPGJ6xKeL\n=KUKY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 107a992fff5d6a44daf294b8ecc1f1893d51ad73\nparent dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781732733 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781732733 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): harden business/personal pre-gate (timeout, audit truth, fail-closed, audit durability) (#416)\n\nHardens the opt-in business/personal pre-gate\n([#403](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/403)) against\nfive findings. **Opt-in throughout — no behavior change for tenants that\nhaven't enabled it; `fail_closed` defaults to false (current fail-open\npreserved).**\n\n## Findings addressed\n\n| # | Finding | Fix |\n|---|---------|-----|\n| **1** | Classifier ran inline on the write path with **no whole-chain\ntimeout** — a slow/unreachable provider could stall a write ~100s\n(retries × fallback). | Hard ceiling\n`PREGATE_CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (env-tunable, default **5s**) via\n`asyncio.wait_for`; on timeout fail-open + alertable warning.\n`call_with_fallback`'s `timeout=` is per-attempt, so it can't bound the\nchain — hence the outer wrap. |\n| **2** | `min_confidence` does **not** reduce false rejects as\ndocumented — the post-enrichment backstop drops any `\"personal\"` verdict\nunconditionally (no enrichment confidence exists to gate on). |\nDoc-only: corrected the settings comment + `_GovNBPregate` docstring to\ndescribe the real behavior (gates the *early* drop only; defers\nborderline content to the accurate backstop). |\n| **3** | Under provider fallback the audit recorded the **intended**\nprovider/model, not the one that actually classified. | Capture the live\n`provider`/`model` on `BusinessClassification` (from the `LLMProvider`\ninstance) and audit those. |\n| **4** | A `drop` tenant whose classifier is unavailable **silently\nstored** unclassified content. | Detect it (`result.provider is None`) +\nalertable warning; add opt-in `pregate.fail_closed` (default false) that\nrejects the write (**503** + `nonbusiness_pregate_unavailable` audit)\ninstead of storing unclassified content. |\n| **5** | Governance enforcement audits could be **dropped under\naudit-queue overflow** while the write was still refused — contradicting\n`emit_governance_audit`'s \"can't be silently disabled\" promise. |\n`log_action(critical=True)`: on overflow, critical events fall back to a\nsynchronous storage write instead of dropping; `enqueue()` now reports\nwhether it queued. Applied to **every** reject/destructive-enforcement\naudit (pregate drop + unavailable, deterministic + LLM PII drop,\nnon-business drop, fast-mode remediation soft-deletes, bulk drop).\nFlag/mask/keep-private stay best-effort. |\n\n## Decisions\n- **Finding 2** is doc-only because the enrichment signal carries no\nconfidence (`business_relevance: str` in `common/enrichment/schema.py`),\nso wiring a confidence floor into the backstop would need a broad\nenrichment-schema change affecting all tenants.\n- **Finding 4** `fail_closed` setting lives in OSS\n`organization_settings` `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` (no split). Enterprise\n\"Content Policy\" UI toggle is a follow-up in the enterprise repo.\n- **Finding 5** `critical` is scoped to reject/destructive paths (audit\nis the only record); high-volume flag/keep-private paths keep the\nfire-and-forget queue, so the hot path is unaffected.\n\n## Verification\n- New/updated tests: `tests/test_business_personal_pregate.py`\n(timeout→fail-open, fallback audit attribution, fail-open observability\ndefault, `fail_closed` 503) and `tests/test_audit_queue.py` (`enqueue`\nbool contract, critical sync-fallback on overflow). All green.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean (core-api/src,\ncore-storage-api/src); `mypy` clean on **both** core-api and\ncore-storage-api.\n- The DB-backed `test_governance_e2e.py` / `test_audit_chain.py`\nintegration suites fail identically on clean `main` in this sandbox (no\ndatabase) — they'll exercise these changes under CI's DB.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T21:45:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/aa4be8e913da5f8d643ca1f98d6d9aaa0f821931/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9"}]},{"sha":"dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRkOGNkNjIzOWVjZmY5YTQxMTk0MGJkMjQ2YmRlOTBjZDA0ZmRkZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T21:35:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T21:35:44Z"},"message":"ci: add static security scanning (bandit SAST + pip-audit) (#420)\n\n## What\nAdds a **Security Scan** workflow — **bandit** (Python SAST) +\n**pip-audit** (dependency CVEs) over `core-api` / `core-storage-api`\nsource — running per-PR + weekly.\n\n## Why\n`ci.yml` already gates **ruff (lint) + mypy (types) + pytest** every PR,\nand `claude_code_review.yml` adds an LLM correctness review. The one\nlayer nothing scanned is **security/SAST + known-vulnerable\ndependencies** — this closes that gap.\n\n## Notes\n- **Report-only for now** (`continue-on-error`) so the existing backlog\ndoesn't block merges — findings surface in the job log. Drop\n`continue-on-error` to make it a hard gate once triaged. `bandit` is\nfiltered to medium+ severity/confidence to keep noise down.\n- Reuses the pinned `actions/checkout` + `astral-sh/setup-uv` SHAs and\nthe `uv` setup from `ci.yml`. No new GHAS/Advanced-Security requirement.\n- **Optional follow-up:** this repo is public, so **GitHub CodeQL**\n(deeper SAST, covers TypeScript too) is free — I can add\n`.github/workflows/codeql.yml` next if you want it.\n\n_Draft — proposal for review; tune the scope / severity thresholds /\nblocking-vs-reporting before merge._\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9724691891e0785aab99703f79576202092f9c31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9724691891e0785aab99703f79576202092f9c31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMxMwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp1IQAEMUySOIqjrpkc0GJJ/d112C\nWADAZS5Upo4Kixmn0jHhlalRosqTTXiXt9h0LWeZhUT/DAIocoi5Ez7yptvooepy\nfHRFsp4RiUjaqmqFPq7uv732saqXu4riJlzz/y3mRy1fcAcFRWVxOrTf4Fetz1BC\nxgM1mDNwAuqTjl6ZNLc+oAenioYc5aJoZ1ymPAQc6TPX6tKmmaJCYgp3rw7hgR8R\nrAfN0actnJYyj02rBAfIHmVIKu9K5PZYUqYr5CwZZwnJNF+yMfkpt4gxcDLb7UNo\nJRtL/KjPz1CI8TP1VPaI82KFb2RC16RvXvxkNYDgsddviLflKwBVsi1jYFFPpUNs\nNEVT44O0BsVA5/egJYNLggM96G35usIS6/AzbRstpez2kgiADYB4YiVYmp6j5LZ7\npvJWLf7W/oyvUKLD7ZFbGsFkg7dn9HzBZOUzyMkfU4I+8ecVDumjOGH3bIKmGeXE\nNDlFwt/aEUa5lyRqCSDtQ3TSRAsPL9jR9bnqehGTpnyFZzqccxZc+bwJa9m/9YqM\nY8w21uHpBs5qgyTjCkXzpUMJ1ZXzPafngLhSl506oBWeFMXsXPDf5/4SFxk7+luE\nIFX5FcF653HxGwUvthnkhcXbY9JF4sHWN4mjn5FQTLusC1RAUwWRhaF+XgkOe4q4\n8SnYp8XB3JAGu8cdhDva\n=qWGT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9724691891e0785aab99703f79576202092f9c31\nparent 86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781732144 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781732144 +0300\n\nci: add static security scanning (bandit SAST + pip-audit) (#420)\n\n## What\nAdds a **Security Scan** workflow — **bandit** (Python SAST) +\n**pip-audit** (dependency CVEs) over `core-api` / `core-storage-api`\nsource — running per-PR + weekly.\n\n## Why\n`ci.yml` already gates **ruff (lint) + mypy (types) + pytest** every PR,\nand `claude_code_review.yml` adds an LLM correctness review. The one\nlayer nothing scanned is **security/SAST + known-vulnerable\ndependencies** — this closes that gap.\n\n## Notes\n- **Report-only for now** (`continue-on-error`) so the existing backlog\ndoesn't block merges — findings surface in the job log. Drop\n`continue-on-error` to make it a hard gate once triaged. `bandit` is\nfiltered to medium+ severity/confidence to keep noise down.\n- Reuses the pinned `actions/checkout` + `astral-sh/setup-uv` SHAs and\nthe `uv` setup from `ci.yml`. No new GHAS/Advanced-Security requirement.\n- **Optional follow-up:** this repo is public, so **GitHub CodeQL**\n(deeper SAST, covers TypeScript too) is free — I can add\n`.github/workflows/codeql.yml` next if you want it.\n\n_Draft — proposal for review; tune the scope / severity thresholds /\nblocking-vs-reporting before merge._\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T21:35:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dd8cd6239ecff9a411940bd246bde90cd04fdde9/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654"}]},{"sha":"86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDg2YmJlOWVjMGFhMDYxNzQxZGYwNDIyYmRjNWI4ZGVjMjg2ZmE2NTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T21:29:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T21:29:33Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): cross-worker settings-cache invalidation (CAURA-571) (#418)\n\nCloses the cross-worker settings-cache staleness gap (the PII findings'\n\"5-min cross-worker settings staleness\" — confirmed live).\n\n## Problem\nThe per-process org-settings cache (`TTLCache`, 5-min TTL in\n`organization_settings.py`) only invalidates **locally** on a write —\n`invalidate_cache` evicts the serving worker only. Sibling uvicorn\nworkers and other Cloud Run instances keep serving the **stale** value\nfor up to the TTL. For a governance control that's a correctness gap:\nflipping a policy to a **stricter** action (e.g. PII `flag → drop/mask`)\nhas an up-to-5-minute window where some workers still apply the looser\none.\n\n## Fix — fan out invalidation over the event bus\n- New **broadcast** topic `Topics.Org.SETTINGS_CHANGED` +\n`OrgSettingsChangedEvent` payload (carries only `org_id` — nothing to\nkeep in sync, no secret on the wire).\n- `update_settings` publishes it after `commit()` (**best-effort**: a\npublish failure can't fail an already-committed write — siblings then\nfall back to the TTL, exactly as today).\n- `core-api` consumer `handle_org_settings_changed` →\n`invalidate_cache(org_id)`.\n\n### Broadcast vs work-queue (the crux)\nThe existing bus names subscriptions `{prefix}--{topic}` per\n**service**, so every core-api process shares one subscription →\n**competing consumers**: each message reaches exactly **one** worker.\nThat's correct for the existing enrich/embed/suppression consumers, but\nwrong for cache invalidation, which needs **every** process to act.\n\nSo this adds `EventBus.subscribe(broadcast=True)`:\n- **InProcessEventBus**: no-op (a single process already dispatches to\nall local handlers).\n- **PubSubEventBus**: gives a broadcast topic a **per-process ephemeral\nsubscription** (`{prefix}--{topic}--{instance_id}`), created at\n`start()` with an `expiration_policy` backstop (a crashed process's sub\nself-reaps after 1 day) and deleted at `stop()`. Create-failure (e.g.\nmissing IAM) **degrades to TTL-only invalidation** rather than crashing\nstartup; the consumer is idempotent + TTL-backstopped.\n\nHonors the standing rules: no new direct DB pool (reuses the event bus),\nno ad-hoc migration.\n\n## ⚠️ Deploy dependency — IAM grant required (infra)\nDurable subscriptions are Terraform-provisioned, but per-process\nephemeral subscriptions embed a runtime `instance_id`, so they're\ncreated at runtime. The **core-api service account** needs subscription\ncreate/delete. Until this lands, core-api boots fine and invalidation\nfalls back to the cache TTL (no regression).\n\n```hcl\n# Grant the core-api runtime SA permission to create/delete its own\n# ephemeral broadcast subscriptions (CAURA-571).\nresource \"google_pubsub_topic_iam_member\" \"core_api_settings_changed_subscriber\" {\n  topic  = google_pubsub_topic.memclaw_org_settings_changed.name  # new topic\n  role   = \"roles/pubsub.editor\"   # or a custom role with\n                                   # pubsub.subscriptions.{create,delete,consume}\n  member = \"serviceAccount:${var.core_api_service_account_email}\"\n}\n```\nAlso provision the topic `memclaw.org.settings-changed` (mirroring the\nother `memclaw.*` topics; the per-env `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` applies\nas usual). I can adjust to a tighter custom role if you prefer\nleast-privilege over `pubsub.editor`.\n\n## Verification\n- New tests: `test_pubsub_bus.py` (per-process sub create /\nalready-exists / degrade-on-failure / stop-delete),\n`test_inprocess_bus.py` (broadcast no-op dispatch),\n`test_cross_worker_settings_invalidation.py` (handler + payload +\nbroadcast wiring); `test_consumer_enriched.py` register assertion\nupdated. All green.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` and `mypy` clean on core-api +\ncore-storage-api.\n- (Pre-existing DB-backed settings/e2e suites need a database — not\nrunnable in this sandbox; they exercise the publish path under CI's DB.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6e402edf4709ac7801882a3c16797d2a5ef6cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b6e402edf4709ac7801882a3c16797d2a5ef6cd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMxG9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5mMQAB5uwe/Lon6OjYm5cQ53A1Wn\naTA13wbfWx6ZNqNVsqUpdgQ8bdq6A0LWaQCSdotkJIqw7OYw69CkFtR7WYNzISU5\nhdqoNFxI0Pwr1Ioj47NEilsW6D7moeGH+FR9LUQw4cmQrWsVk93MT3KDbrSheWlL\n2sqWV5rN4Fs8H7emh56ZHwQzOycGJqUFWOIp/Me5clfySdNNetbRJ/Um6YPQNoC2\ntwcZYKh+0QO3evGFz691I5TxukbZeZzJ4ZDoUzIAf4n/GQ0fszl38dFCVcHA4kMT\nUM17qcsr70+0OQ1UE4JawTz8FxJSxVKK/JxvSoc7Z01Uj3/y7ZOcTOBuof2cGN/H\n/ts9rmnUckHqn7mi8/48Bs/1jqxk0GBXFNyFwQl1pYtd0D0hbcsdQMaq8FFZsC1G\nEnAUyBaYNd8ZwdOk+TUvkvOMl8s+2CvY77O1w2Qc3v814Hd37Hki8qPgNtFjZ19m\ngoE1nt5C5smkbYk7Vq/CbIWNhMUjZQ/rIVkH+EWrdeuwW8fats/vO+mBmbfqG75q\nG8pU+KCIGeoVEmpLFVw2Z4zmFfmzJ27vVHPH1s+oNyOInozCqdGuz2FWvZyUulTv\nffEFj/TWUneX0xc96IUf+vRaVe/QHkItsudkDzh40eq9/k2BwOGBP+YeW92JK4iJ\nw/O+HTPPj7nxlMp2P0rD\n=ZEKp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b6e402edf4709ac7801882a3c16797d2a5ef6cd2\nparent 3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781731773 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781731773 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): cross-worker settings-cache invalidation (CAURA-571) (#418)\n\nCloses the cross-worker settings-cache staleness gap (the PII findings'\n\"5-min cross-worker settings staleness\" — confirmed live).\n\n## Problem\nThe per-process org-settings cache (`TTLCache`, 5-min TTL in\n`organization_settings.py`) only invalidates **locally** on a write —\n`invalidate_cache` evicts the serving worker only. Sibling uvicorn\nworkers and other Cloud Run instances keep serving the **stale** value\nfor up to the TTL. For a governance control that's a correctness gap:\nflipping a policy to a **stricter** action (e.g. PII `flag → drop/mask`)\nhas an up-to-5-minute window where some workers still apply the looser\none.\n\n## Fix — fan out invalidation over the event bus\n- New **broadcast** topic `Topics.Org.SETTINGS_CHANGED` +\n`OrgSettingsChangedEvent` payload (carries only `org_id` — nothing to\nkeep in sync, no secret on the wire).\n- `update_settings` publishes it after `commit()` (**best-effort**: a\npublish failure can't fail an already-committed write — siblings then\nfall back to the TTL, exactly as today).\n- `core-api` consumer `handle_org_settings_changed` →\n`invalidate_cache(org_id)`.\n\n### Broadcast vs work-queue (the crux)\nThe existing bus names subscriptions `{prefix}--{topic}` per\n**service**, so every core-api process shares one subscription →\n**competing consumers**: each message reaches exactly **one** worker.\nThat's correct for the existing enrich/embed/suppression consumers, but\nwrong for cache invalidation, which needs **every** process to act.\n\nSo this adds `EventBus.subscribe(broadcast=True)`:\n- **InProcessEventBus**: no-op (a single process already dispatches to\nall local handlers).\n- **PubSubEventBus**: gives a broadcast topic a **per-process ephemeral\nsubscription** (`{prefix}--{topic}--{instance_id}`), created at\n`start()` with an `expiration_policy` backstop (a crashed process's sub\nself-reaps after 1 day) and deleted at `stop()`. Create-failure (e.g.\nmissing IAM) **degrades to TTL-only invalidation** rather than crashing\nstartup; the consumer is idempotent + TTL-backstopped.\n\nHonors the standing rules: no new direct DB pool (reuses the event bus),\nno ad-hoc migration.\n\n## ⚠️ Deploy dependency — IAM grant required (infra)\nDurable subscriptions are Terraform-provisioned, but per-process\nephemeral subscriptions embed a runtime `instance_id`, so they're\ncreated at runtime. The **core-api service account** needs subscription\ncreate/delete. Until this lands, core-api boots fine and invalidation\nfalls back to the cache TTL (no regression).\n\n```hcl\n# Grant the core-api runtime SA permission to create/delete its own\n# ephemeral broadcast subscriptions (CAURA-571).\nresource \"google_pubsub_topic_iam_member\" \"core_api_settings_changed_subscriber\" {\n  topic  = google_pubsub_topic.memclaw_org_settings_changed.name  # new topic\n  role   = \"roles/pubsub.editor\"   # or a custom role with\n                                   # pubsub.subscriptions.{create,delete,consume}\n  member = \"serviceAccount:${var.core_api_service_account_email}\"\n}\n```\nAlso provision the topic `memclaw.org.settings-changed` (mirroring the\nother `memclaw.*` topics; the per-env `EVENT_BUS_TOPIC_PREFIX` applies\nas usual). I can adjust to a tighter custom role if you prefer\nleast-privilege over `pubsub.editor`.\n\n## Verification\n- New tests: `test_pubsub_bus.py` (per-process sub create /\nalready-exists / degrade-on-failure / stop-delete),\n`test_inprocess_bus.py` (broadcast no-op dispatch),\n`test_cross_worker_settings_invalidation.py` (handler + payload +\nbroadcast wiring); `test_consumer_enriched.py` register assertion\nupdated. All green.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` and `mypy` clean on core-api +\ncore-storage-api.\n- (Pre-existing DB-backed settings/e2e suites need a database — not\nrunnable in this sandbox; they exercise the publish path under CI's DB.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T21:29:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/86bbe9ec0aa061741df0422bdc5b8dec286fa654/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd"}]},{"sha":"3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNkOTcwZWYyY2JkMjZjNGFiMzgzMDEwMWJiNGFlMzEzNDA5NTQ1YmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T21:05:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T21:05:26Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2) (#417)\n\n## What\n\nPR1 (#413) made reconcile targets configurable but left **`additive`**\nmode a warn-skip no-op. This PR implements it: MemClaw can now reconcile\nits active skills into **shared/foreign** target dirs **without ever\ndeleting or overwriting an entry it does not own**.\n\n## Mechanism — per-skill ownership marker\n\nA sentinel file `<dir>/<slug>/.memclaw-owned` stamps every skill MemClaw\nwrites into an `additive` dir. `reconcileAdditiveDir`:\n\n- **write** — a desired slug is written only when its dir is **absent**\n(new → stamp marker) or **already MemClaw-owned** (update in place). A\nslug occupied by an **unowned** dir is a **collision** → skipped, never\noverwritten (reported in `summary.skipped`).\n- **remove** — an on-disk slug not in the catalog is removed **only if\nit carries the marker**. Unowned (foreign) entries are left untouched.\n\nThis is **fail-safe**: a missing marker means *\"leave it alone\"*, never\n*\"delete it\"*. So an empty catalog — or a misconfigured tenant returning\nan empty installable set — prunes only MemClaw's own entries in additive\ndirs. The destructive \"wipe the dir\" hazard stays confined to\n**`owned`** dirs.\n\nThe marker lives **inside** the skill dir; OpenClaw's loader reads only\n`SKILL.md` and halts recursion at a skill root, so the marker is\ninvisible to the agent (verified against agent-core `skills.ts` /\n`session.ts`).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `OWNED_MARKER` + `isMemclawOwned` helpers.\n- `DirReconcileResult.skipped` (additive collisions); `owned` dirs\nalways return it empty.\n- `reconcileAdditiveDir` — mirrors `reconcileOwnedDir`'s shape with\nmarker-gated removal + collision-skip writes.\n- `reconcileSkills` loop dispatches `additive` → the new path;\n`summary.skipped` now merges bad-shape catalog rows + collisions\n(deduped + sorted, consistent with the other arrays).\n- `reconcileOwnedDir` and the default single-target behavior are\n**unchanged**.\n- Docs (`mcp-skill-delivery.md`) section describing `owned` vs\n`additive` (collision/never-remove/marker semantics).\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new `additive` tests: write + marker stamp; foreign skill never\nremoved (incl. empty catalog); collision → skipped + foreign bytes\nuntouched; owned orphan removed (foreign neighbour survives); owned\nskill updated in place. Replaces the PR1 \"additive not implemented\"\nplaceholder. **328 plugin tests pass; tsc clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79de1c553d9c07196a2520d5b9581d343b8a04fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/79de1c553d9c07196a2520d5b9581d343b8a04fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMwwWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhpsQAAAfj6Ga917SKmlUczpEr4rk\nGf1DTUpZoNrhNCjXqrsCIgd/qywxH9icKxNpRYPsmEUGhb9yRaWhEoShAdc9euuJ\niNV42pwe4fYTeejY0MK8MveRhbw9nopTdwAg0XSzB/IzzvMwTMpatPNcd88X+cxr\nId9nvE4uK1iRu8HcOUlkmiTP/DI6Phh1p1uaMRKmoS9GcwNYM/XBQehtO8sVmFS2\ny46Az6MygFd8Vi6uvxDXfGS9bwhq1ogIqbvptPW3qzjqOHTHAc3uUEs6H2D0D70l\neZ2dJUY5gHM+mEqzEjiIZ/DUArc1cMU6AhoYa+rBDT7rlkqr5UJdsPwbiV1PULTi\nW6GMwC5bSdmNzKwxVNfWZfvwzAP8jSjowzTEejKoyynvp2ndpdaKfgdNZcTjPYZt\nzzK3hgO+oDaA5dlJnDrHyEq3cqBX2rdfHVcVsEqSepdV1ZLUWOKOO6xw1DHN1uph\nHC+XPX/71vUiiOCXWUct67n2je/tazmWbbjU5NPfue2Q+1VvW1SUraEdQkL+HFLv\nsJp/gZU53RZw1CHQM0JWY3/x2p39TUWqfC+LDDqneRJTOkN++V2Awt2H09sGb/90\nn6VkoNZC1V/BfPmdToE6o26nCtG2kjYBZiOnzsH/WsncV6L94gkQ8yd7VtfuiCjp\nrWcmQV8yEugvUaJVsSrL\n=SbSb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 79de1c553d9c07196a2520d5b9581d343b8a04fe\nparent 36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781730326 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781730326 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): additive-mode skill reconcile with ownership marker (PR2) (#417)\n\n## What\n\nPR1 (#413) made reconcile targets configurable but left **`additive`**\nmode a warn-skip no-op. This PR implements it: MemClaw can now reconcile\nits active skills into **shared/foreign** target dirs **without ever\ndeleting or overwriting an entry it does not own**.\n\n## Mechanism — per-skill ownership marker\n\nA sentinel file `<dir>/<slug>/.memclaw-owned` stamps every skill MemClaw\nwrites into an `additive` dir. `reconcileAdditiveDir`:\n\n- **write** — a desired slug is written only when its dir is **absent**\n(new → stamp marker) or **already MemClaw-owned** (update in place). A\nslug occupied by an **unowned** dir is a **collision** → skipped, never\noverwritten (reported in `summary.skipped`).\n- **remove** — an on-disk slug not in the catalog is removed **only if\nit carries the marker**. Unowned (foreign) entries are left untouched.\n\nThis is **fail-safe**: a missing marker means *\"leave it alone\"*, never\n*\"delete it\"*. So an empty catalog — or a misconfigured tenant returning\nan empty installable set — prunes only MemClaw's own entries in additive\ndirs. The destructive \"wipe the dir\" hazard stays confined to\n**`owned`** dirs.\n\nThe marker lives **inside** the skill dir; OpenClaw's loader reads only\n`SKILL.md` and halts recursion at a skill root, so the marker is\ninvisible to the agent (verified against agent-core `skills.ts` /\n`session.ts`).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `OWNED_MARKER` + `isMemclawOwned` helpers.\n- `DirReconcileResult.skipped` (additive collisions); `owned` dirs\nalways return it empty.\n- `reconcileAdditiveDir` — mirrors `reconcileOwnedDir`'s shape with\nmarker-gated removal + collision-skip writes.\n- `reconcileSkills` loop dispatches `additive` → the new path;\n`summary.skipped` now merges bad-shape catalog rows + collisions\n(deduped + sorted, consistent with the other arrays).\n- `reconcileOwnedDir` and the default single-target behavior are\n**unchanged**.\n- Docs (`mcp-skill-delivery.md`) section describing `owned` vs\n`additive` (collision/never-remove/marker semantics).\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new `additive` tests: write + marker stamp; foreign skill never\nremoved (incl. empty catalog); collision → skipped + foreign bytes\nuntouched; owned orphan removed (foreign neighbour survives); owned\nskill updated in place. Replaces the PR1 \"additive not implemented\"\nplaceholder. **328 plugin tests pass; tsc clean.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T21:05:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3d970ef2cbd26c4ab3830101bb4ae313409545bd/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7"}]},{"sha":"36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM2YjFiMzBhZDkyZGViOTg3YWFjMDQyN2IwNjhjMDI1MGQ0ZjY2Zjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T20:43:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T20:43:26Z"},"message":"docs(core-api): document LLM free-form PII recall limit (recommend a capable enrichment model) (#419)\n\nCloses the second PII caveat from the findings (\"nano under-detects\nsubtly-phrased free-form PII\"). **Doc/comment only — no behavior\nchange.**\n\n## Why\nThe PII `action` (mask/drop/flag) is backed by two detection paths with\nvery different recall, and the difference is load-bearing for a tenant\nrelying on `drop`/`mask` for compliance:\n\n1. **Deterministic span-aware validators** (`GovernanceScanContent`) —\nregex/Luhn/IBAN/entropy. Precise, fail-closed, and the only path that\ncan honestly `mask` (it has span offsets). Precision confirmed live.\n2. **The enrichment LLM's free-form `contains_pii` signal**\n(`GovernanceDecision`) — catches unstructured/contextual PII the\npatterns can't (e.g. *\"X is in addiction recovery\"*), but its **recall\nis bounded by the enrichment model**. Live testing confirmed a\nsmall/cheap model (e.g. `*-nano`) under-detects subtly-phrased free-form\nPII.\n\n## What\nA note in the `governance.pii` `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` block (right where\n`action` is chosen) spelling out the two paths and recommending a\n**capable `enrichment.model`** for tenants relying on free-form\n`drop`/`mask` — the deterministic path stays the precise backstop, but\nfree-form coverage is only as strong as the model's recall. It also\nrecords that the LLM path has no offsets, so a `mask` policy can only\nflag a free-form match (`llm_pii_audit_detail` / `configured_action`).\n\nThis is a model-recall limitation, not a code bug — so the fix is to\nmake the trade-off explicit at the configuration site rather than change\nenforcement.\n\nruff check + format clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7687fdc11e3b786c1077b1d7f1085f4fa6416bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7687fdc11e3b786c1077b1d7f1085f4fa6416bb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMwbuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXcQQAKoF+BBkEpZ53ReO7BqdIo0s\nVXu+Cp5FsiJ8CntL4/eTpqF3h2iWD5Uiz080XV/1ZLYLbSAKpTrxfBo/5lTNreZn\nsUD3Qg6o8P2X2zWZ+RCAsjRAJiQjU2SElcBQt/Ha6Tnm0BMNT4EJAolGJ3YOfKHd\nHzpRtZ/ULk63RJjn1gV3tokS/+bkpp4OvtA1TKVodLogsiyqajws38YQf2VacgeM\nPuL1On8DlOIxV603IQYQaa0ju8Qw41Xy5hYnOWQbkU/NSf1xV3HJ96Eol/I8t0E3\nOxeu3+sYkBDbFdYnymAPV1QijJdp05+N2SKe7qGRfOhjnqMvjkjgXMKI2kFx+z2M\nWJ8K+Ag+HuqyNqYR1yCfZt/QQ9bN/AMkZmlsqq+g6Fnh5g2FdQRclRJ1Y3Q06N6k\n2hSbQ5xHEbeMPbR/no0l5eFnr09rNHpCiL2xp318MmpY19H7RUP1G2Mt1dyjr2ZL\ntKpiEsoZntMRw0+kNw5nCelo6BPQqdzLrhzi3aLB5gRjTMKOgZvQY5QinsuzwgeO\nHy+OvJaRicH3ZO5lf7t/h34uJS/Vi5jEVsG6Vn9TqEje8Khcoq6HtXK5RjgCGOTb\nVhaFLIbFBxTRst0b/YpSIFn4Zh8/NJDYXfIKtxLaDXf1CAViDag/0A6C7WrRz5YL\n4lMEi6Pz2kSNVqfSI8Gp\n=Qkbb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7687fdc11e3b786c1077b1d7f1085f4fa6416bb9\nparent 5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781729006 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781729006 +0300\n\ndocs(core-api): document LLM free-form PII recall limit (recommend a capable enrichment model) (#419)\n\nCloses the second PII caveat from the findings (\"nano under-detects\nsubtly-phrased free-form PII\"). **Doc/comment only — no behavior\nchange.**\n\n## Why\nThe PII `action` (mask/drop/flag) is backed by two detection paths with\nvery different recall, and the difference is load-bearing for a tenant\nrelying on `drop`/`mask` for compliance:\n\n1. **Deterministic span-aware validators** (`GovernanceScanContent`) —\nregex/Luhn/IBAN/entropy. Precise, fail-closed, and the only path that\ncan honestly `mask` (it has span offsets). Precision confirmed live.\n2. **The enrichment LLM's free-form `contains_pii` signal**\n(`GovernanceDecision`) — catches unstructured/contextual PII the\npatterns can't (e.g. *\"X is in addiction recovery\"*), but its **recall\nis bounded by the enrichment model**. Live testing confirmed a\nsmall/cheap model (e.g. `*-nano`) under-detects subtly-phrased free-form\nPII.\n\n## What\nA note in the `governance.pii` `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` block (right where\n`action` is chosen) spelling out the two paths and recommending a\n**capable `enrichment.model`** for tenants relying on free-form\n`drop`/`mask` — the deterministic path stays the precise backstop, but\nfree-form coverage is only as strong as the model's recall. It also\nrecords that the LLM path has no offsets, so a `mask` policy can only\nflag a free-form match (`llm_pii_audit_detail` / `configured_action`).\n\nThis is a model-recall limitation, not a code bug — so the fix is to\nmake the trade-off explicit at the configuration site rather than change\nenforcement.\n\nruff check + format clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T20:43:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36b1b30ad92deb987aac0427b068c0250d4f66f7/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9"}]},{"sha":"5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU4ODllM2ZhY2JiYTNmNjZiNTE3NjQ0ZmYzZDAxMWVhMjI2OTYwZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T17:47:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T17:47:47Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): self-heal storage pool + cancellation-safe requests (CAURA-000) (#415)\n\n## Why\n\nRoot cause of the **2026-06-16 core-api pool-starvation SEV-2** on eToro\non-prem (~2h recall/write stall). `CoreStorageClient` holds a\nprocess-wide httpx pool to core-storage (`max_connections=200`,\n`pool=5s`). When an in-flight call was cancelled mid-request — the 35s\nenrichment `wait_for` or the 45s request timeout — httpcore (1.0.9,\ncurrent) did **not** return the connection to the pool. Leaked slots\naccumulated over ~4.5 days of uninterrupted uptime until every acquire\nhit `PoolTimeout`; the singleton never self-healed → **restart-only\nrecovery**.\n\nForensics (incident addendum): there was **no acute trigger** that\nmorning — the prior day had *more* slow upstream calls and *more*\ntimeouts yet survived; the leak simply crossed the 200-slot ceiling at\n07:37. So this recurs on a cadence set by the cancellation rate until\nthe pool defect is fixed — which is what this PR does.\n\n## What\n\nTwo layered fixes in `CoreStorageClient`, both routed through a single\n`_execute()` funnel that all six request helpers\n(`_get`/`_get_list`/`_post`/`_post_optional`/`_patch`/`_delete`) **and**\nthe two direct call sites (`list_keystones`, `claim_idempotency`) now\nuse:\n\n- **Fix B — prevention (`_cancel_safe`)**: shields the in-flight request\nvia `asyncio.shield` so a cancelled caller still lets the request finish\nand release its slot. The caller observes `CancelledError` immediately;\nthe orphaned result is consumed so it isn't logged as never-retrieved.\nBounded by the existing 120s read timeout, so worst case it\nself-releases instead of leaking forever.\n- **Fix A — recovery (`_recycle_pools`)**: on a `PoolTimeout` that\nsurvives the retry policy (i.e. genuine exhaustion), rebuild the pool\n**once** under a lock with a generation guard (concurrent `PoolTimeout`s\ncollapse to one rebuild), background-close the old pool, and retry on\nthe fresh one. Converts a restart-only outage into a **seconds-long\nself-heal** and emits an `ERROR` log (also closes the observability gap\nfrom the incident).\n\nHelpers read `self._http`/`self._read_http` **lazily** so a recycle is\npicked up on retry. No behavioural change on the happy path or to\nexisting retry semantics.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `tests/test_storage_client_pool_recovery.py`:\n- cancellation mid-request lets the shielded call complete (no leak)\n- POST + GET recycle the pool on exhaustion, then succeed on the fresh\npool\n- a transient `PoolTimeout` ridden out by retries does **not** recycle\n(no churn)\n\nThe existing F5 / 2026-06-11 retry suite\n(`test_storage_client_retry.py`, 19 tests) passes unchanged — the\n`_execute` refactor preserves all retry behaviour. `ruff check`, `ruff\nformat --check`, and `mypy` are clean.\n\n## Tradeoff\n\nA write cancelled by the 45s budget now completes in the background\nrather than being abandoned — benign, because writes are\nidempotency-keyed (`client_request_id`) and reads are side-effect-free.\n\n## Rollout\n\n- Targets `caura-memclaw`; rides the next on-prem release. **Do not\nmerge without staging on erni-onprem first** per the 5-phase upgrade\nprotocol, then eToro.\n- Rename `CAURA-000` to the real ticket before merge.\n- Out of scope (separate, fill-rate-only PRs): the `cluster_id`\nValidationError fix and 429-aware backoff — they reduce how fast the\npool fills, not the leak itself.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3bcafc57a19d0b67ec419fff553dc8f70854e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a3bcafc57a19d0b67ec419fff553dc8f70854e68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMt3DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOk4QABDsvZ702Y1FDkvUzsCQwIAt\nOccXO1tFpRsXWInsheQ33u4CA1QcVar0cYtX/GxjHyqvlTt4Pq1Bi39m4x18qKrK\n/fDKjnCwlzTX1k0sScRLuOB33IibmaGFhoUqQiN8VE1WYJPpE6HMP9zBIEFuO2GX\nR+Nj75xPJ0nwy5eOUjMTCCUVB6/mcqhyYPw55LW5zoMbdPk9OasNgaCJ0mduEiXd\nQCn/pd0Omkm31HqitZWC59Ws6X9qgx0OunnizwhR9akcwg46Gg281H2gMIiTF9Ea\nlPF7cTz8Mr8aFzrevTWoYmnc25f9uVB3VnMyWBkssZkdCAlYvFtJNZB/7PMfWCID\nz1CcrfYqhryp6hVE86zMIwAodLjocQKUg9McSIVqpPS0vit8gpQBybEmpUbjIcxR\nyHRz11AqwQvJoFDpoIbN2hwU1TV21w/Vu8ITs1xWpWGBk0EQB97fjtuNFmukxJun\nJedIrfgTgmLHEvTLW5T5YweT+lpl3nC4EPx5ZS7TeF6yPzIYYUhXrqSdlnkHn45K\nn7ff0NTCkYR47akLzZwX3SsnhuNUuvzhgCD2rRWKqS1WJ2hsc5FtywEBtjfp72PW\nZ6/ZKW1s4pREt2QNvQUtA9g8cNaa0n3I8nitoD51nJ13onZBMIBcv9VO37Olxp1h\nb9z7Gnv9BNv7b2PH4PW9\n=/jPC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3bcafc57a19d0b67ec419fff553dc8f70854e68\nparent 57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781718467 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781718467 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): self-heal storage pool + cancellation-safe requests (CAURA-000) (#415)\n\n## Why\n\nRoot cause of the **2026-06-16 core-api pool-starvation SEV-2** on eToro\non-prem (~2h recall/write stall). `CoreStorageClient` holds a\nprocess-wide httpx pool to core-storage (`max_connections=200`,\n`pool=5s`). When an in-flight call was cancelled mid-request — the 35s\nenrichment `wait_for` or the 45s request timeout — httpcore (1.0.9,\ncurrent) did **not** return the connection to the pool. Leaked slots\naccumulated over ~4.5 days of uninterrupted uptime until every acquire\nhit `PoolTimeout`; the singleton never self-healed → **restart-only\nrecovery**.\n\nForensics (incident addendum): there was **no acute trigger** that\nmorning — the prior day had *more* slow upstream calls and *more*\ntimeouts yet survived; the leak simply crossed the 200-slot ceiling at\n07:37. So this recurs on a cadence set by the cancellation rate until\nthe pool defect is fixed — which is what this PR does.\n\n## What\n\nTwo layered fixes in `CoreStorageClient`, both routed through a single\n`_execute()` funnel that all six request helpers\n(`_get`/`_get_list`/`_post`/`_post_optional`/`_patch`/`_delete`) **and**\nthe two direct call sites (`list_keystones`, `claim_idempotency`) now\nuse:\n\n- **Fix B — prevention (`_cancel_safe`)**: shields the in-flight request\nvia `asyncio.shield` so a cancelled caller still lets the request finish\nand release its slot. The caller observes `CancelledError` immediately;\nthe orphaned result is consumed so it isn't logged as never-retrieved.\nBounded by the existing 120s read timeout, so worst case it\nself-releases instead of leaking forever.\n- **Fix A — recovery (`_recycle_pools`)**: on a `PoolTimeout` that\nsurvives the retry policy (i.e. genuine exhaustion), rebuild the pool\n**once** under a lock with a generation guard (concurrent `PoolTimeout`s\ncollapse to one rebuild), background-close the old pool, and retry on\nthe fresh one. Converts a restart-only outage into a **seconds-long\nself-heal** and emits an `ERROR` log (also closes the observability gap\nfrom the incident).\n\nHelpers read `self._http`/`self._read_http` **lazily** so a recycle is\npicked up on retry. No behavioural change on the happy path or to\nexisting retry semantics.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `tests/test_storage_client_pool_recovery.py`:\n- cancellation mid-request lets the shielded call complete (no leak)\n- POST + GET recycle the pool on exhaustion, then succeed on the fresh\npool\n- a transient `PoolTimeout` ridden out by retries does **not** recycle\n(no churn)\n\nThe existing F5 / 2026-06-11 retry suite\n(`test_storage_client_retry.py`, 19 tests) passes unchanged — the\n`_execute` refactor preserves all retry behaviour. `ruff check`, `ruff\nformat --check`, and `mypy` are clean.\n\n## Tradeoff\n\nA write cancelled by the 45s budget now completes in the background\nrather than being abandoned — benign, because writes are\nidempotency-keyed (`client_request_id`) and reads are side-effect-free.\n\n## Rollout\n\n- Targets `caura-memclaw`; rides the next on-prem release. **Do not\nmerge without staging on erni-onprem first** per the 5-phase upgrade\nprotocol, then eToro.\n- Rename `CAURA-000` to the real ticket before merge.\n- Out of scope (separate, fill-rate-only PRs): the `cluster_id`\nValidationError fix and 429-aware backoff — they reduce how fast the\npool fills, not the leak itself.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T17:47:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5889e3facbba3f66b517644ff3d011ea226960f9/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49"}]},{"sha":"57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU3ZTVlOTYyY2JjNWEwZjk1NTU1ZTBiZmU3NjJlNWEzYWUzMDliNDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T12:52:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T12:52:53Z"},"message":"refactor(plugin): configurable skill-reconcile targets (PR1 — refactor + config plumbing) (#413)\n\nFirst slice of \"reconcile MemClaw skills into additional folders.\"\n**No-behavior-change refactor + config scaffolding only** — `owned` mode\nis implemented; `additive` mode is a follow-up (PR2).\n\n## What changes\n- Extract per-dir converge logic into **`reconcileOwnedDir(dir,\ndesired)`** (read on-disk → prune orphans except `PROTECTED_SKILLS` →\nwrite/update → report installed). Owned-mode behaviour moved\n**verbatim**.\n- `reconcileSkills()` fetches the catalog + builds `desired` **once**,\nthen reconciles each configured target and aggregates into the unchanged\nflat `ReconcileSummary` (`installed` deduped+sorted across targets).\n- New **`SkillTarget { dir, mode }` + `resolveSkillTargets()`**:\n- Always includes the plugin's own dir (`getPluginDir()/skills`,\n`owned`).\n- Extra targets via **`MEMCLAW_SKILL_TARGETS`** (JSON array, read at\ncall time).\n- Parse **fails safe**: invalid JSON / non-array / malformed entry / bad\nmode / owned-dir duplicate → logged + ignored. A bad config can't crash\nthe heartbeat or alter the owned dir.\n- **`additive` targets are parsed but skipped with a warning** (not\nimplemented yet) → a misconfigured additive dir is a no-op, never a\ndestructive prune.\n\n## Why a refactor-only PR\nThe reconciler's prune is destructive (`onDisk ∉ catalog → rmSync`,\nexcept `memclaw`). Before we point it at *shared* folders, the plumbing\n+ the owned/additive split need to land cleanly so the additive\n(ownership-tracked, non-destructive) mode can slot in without touching\nthe proven owned path.\n\n## Invariants preserved (verified)\n- **Default (env unset) = byte-identical** to before: one `owned` target\n= the plugin skills dir. All pre-existing reconcile tests pass\nunchanged.\n- Empty-catalog / `memclaw`-protected / convergence / idempotency /\nbad-slug-skip / fail-open are unchanged (now inside\n`reconcileOwnedDir`).\n\n## Tests (+10)\n- `resolveSkillTargets`: default → single owned; valid JSON appends\nowned+additive; invalid/non-array JSON → owned-only; malformed entries\nskipped; owned-dir dup dropped.\n- configured targets: an `additive` target is parsed but skipped and its\nforeign dir is left **completely untouched**; an extra `owned` target IS\nreconciled alongside the default.\n- 323 plugin tests pass; tsc clean.\n\n## Follow-ups (per plan)\n- **PR2:** `additive` mode + per-skill ownership marker + same-slug\ncollision policy.\n- **PR3:** per-target heartbeat observability; optional auto-register\ntargets into OpenClaw `settings.skills.customDirectories`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"89642ec73acb128bf92cac600266242b91bc946f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/89642ec73acb128bf92cac600266242b91bc946f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMpilCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATY0QAA3ejOvh4nEwuALD+8mXtCRO\nkrfSRRmk+VfGu9QCAf3NB7Cqb/gx+W/yWD91oDgOzCLkR/iPkE/V9BsLYRf15EYZ\njgCbKzxXrE7c2uf6DQ1bcygFrl1l6xjZDAi6+WcFwtebvKGfRo/PBaEsWXIpj3Gc\nqzcn3SYh7610BxV4DNqMTG0nAmXxKLGVwVBJb54y4D6OfplmOGT82TdRTAvAdNkz\nOp3A+5dVZLlLBo+efifWQYXsehZeNQOum40/C736kDn7PQ6E47IU7ECTLQt2JD8R\n/Qm7ZDSLVtJEAm+aFRd+GxQGHZFuGnzXH1fG+DKKHhmdI+O3aTr1X1NDiuzeviRJ\nVBTUQCgoxAV+72jPhmJCgcZ6t9SO9Jm3Pc0N+CYZynNrpxLv9/87Fa8/g9xF4IsR\nCFl/7ACKYMbA2bsZalHqZVRW9fy4SAqkeNoCtnCNto/ArTSLVMw54jDXylHoqJwL\nV77V8T3oZItYffabL9HfatLjdm0o4rpXnxVX2ZCAQSFm0hq+kMEJd/3LEnNPAFc8\nt2xqku2OYchgGPflQuiLTH9LSO+BaLB35VU04LXkDYfh3X/R9DqKo4ArrvRXHxeI\nDImAqAPUhAS1/CsckhvvnG9Vu0sCUySG6pQhogQjUwlZQ8wyjsar5ctNbUK9OGqU\nqS+zSwIVNU2oFdCaUmbp\n=5xJY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 89642ec73acb128bf92cac600266242b91bc946f\nparent 4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781700773 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781700773 +0300\n\nrefactor(plugin): configurable skill-reconcile targets (PR1 — refactor + config plumbing) (#413)\n\nFirst slice of \"reconcile MemClaw skills into additional folders.\"\n**No-behavior-change refactor + config scaffolding only** — `owned` mode\nis implemented; `additive` mode is a follow-up (PR2).\n\n## What changes\n- Extract per-dir converge logic into **`reconcileOwnedDir(dir,\ndesired)`** (read on-disk → prune orphans except `PROTECTED_SKILLS` →\nwrite/update → report installed). Owned-mode behaviour moved\n**verbatim**.\n- `reconcileSkills()` fetches the catalog + builds `desired` **once**,\nthen reconciles each configured target and aggregates into the unchanged\nflat `ReconcileSummary` (`installed` deduped+sorted across targets).\n- New **`SkillTarget { dir, mode }` + `resolveSkillTargets()`**:\n- Always includes the plugin's own dir (`getPluginDir()/skills`,\n`owned`).\n- Extra targets via **`MEMCLAW_SKILL_TARGETS`** (JSON array, read at\ncall time).\n- Parse **fails safe**: invalid JSON / non-array / malformed entry / bad\nmode / owned-dir duplicate → logged + ignored. A bad config can't crash\nthe heartbeat or alter the owned dir.\n- **`additive` targets are parsed but skipped with a warning** (not\nimplemented yet) → a misconfigured additive dir is a no-op, never a\ndestructive prune.\n\n## Why a refactor-only PR\nThe reconciler's prune is destructive (`onDisk ∉ catalog → rmSync`,\nexcept `memclaw`). Before we point it at *shared* folders, the plumbing\n+ the owned/additive split need to land cleanly so the additive\n(ownership-tracked, non-destructive) mode can slot in without touching\nthe proven owned path.\n\n## Invariants preserved (verified)\n- **Default (env unset) = byte-identical** to before: one `owned` target\n= the plugin skills dir. All pre-existing reconcile tests pass\nunchanged.\n- Empty-catalog / `memclaw`-protected / convergence / idempotency /\nbad-slug-skip / fail-open are unchanged (now inside\n`reconcileOwnedDir`).\n\n## Tests (+10)\n- `resolveSkillTargets`: default → single owned; valid JSON appends\nowned+additive; invalid/non-array JSON → owned-only; malformed entries\nskipped; owned-dir dup dropped.\n- configured targets: an `additive` target is parsed but skipped and its\nforeign dir is left **completely untouched**; an extra `owned` target IS\nreconciled alongside the default.\n- 323 plugin tests pass; tsc clean.\n\n## Follow-ups (per plan)\n- **PR2:** `additive` mode + per-skill ownership marker + same-slug\ncollision policy.\n- **PR3:** per-target heartbeat observability; optional auto-register\ntargets into OpenClaw `settings.skills.customDirectories`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T12:52:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57e5e962cbc5a0f95555e0bfe762e5a3ae309b49/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a"}]},{"sha":"4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDRkMWM0ODZiZjdjMjhmZGRjYzBjYWQyZDkzY2Q1MzU4OTQ2MDgzMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T11:20:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T11:20:37Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): stamp version into image so /api/v1/version stops serving \"dev\" (CAURA-000) (#414)\n\n## Summary\n\n`/api/v1/version` (and the `version` field of `/api/v1/status`) returns\n`\"dev\"` instead of the real release version.\n\n**Root cause:** the Dockerfile installs dependencies with `uv export\n--frozen --no-emit-project`, which deliberately excludes the project\nitself — so **core-api is never installed as a package** in the image.\n`core_api.constants.VERSION` resolves via\n`importlib.metadata.version(\"core-api\")`, which raises\n`PackageNotFoundError`, and the silent `except` fallback returns\n`\"dev\"`. Confirmed by inspecting the built image: `pip show core-api` →\nnot found, and the module loads from source via `PYTHONPATH`.\n\nThis is invisible in CI (which installs core-api editable, so metadata\nresolves) — the bug only exists inside the built image.\n\n## Fix\n\nBake the version into the image at build time and read it\ndeterministically:\n\n- **Dockerfile** — stamp `/app/VERSION` from `pyproject.toml` (the\nsource of truth) in the builder, with an optional `MEMCLAW_VERSION`\nbuild-arg override (e.g. a release tag).\n- **constants.py** — `_resolve_version()` precedence: `MEMCLAW_VERSION`\nenv → `/app/VERSION` file → installed-package metadata → `\"dev\"`.\nIndependent of install method / `PYTHONPATH` ordering.\n- **.dockerignore** — add recursive `**/*.egg-info` (a bare `*.egg-info`\nonly matches the context root) so a stray nested `core_api.egg-info`\nfrom a local editable install can't bake into the image and shadow the\nstamp.\n- **ci.yml** — new `image-version` job that builds the image and asserts\nthe baked version is a real semver matching `pyproject.toml` (not\n`\"dev\"`). A pytest assertion can't catch this; the job builds the actual\nimage.\n- **tests** — version-resolution precedence guards in\n`test_api_status.py`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `docker build` of the image → `VERSION = <pyproject version>` (was\n`\"dev\"`)\n- [x] Verified `pip show core-api` is absent in the image — the stamp is\nthe sole source\n- [x] `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean; `mypy` clean\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_api_status.py -k version` — 3 passed\n- [x] New `image-version` CI job fails loudly if the baked version is\n`\"dev\"` or drifts from `pyproject.toml`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02b9e5954f63089dfe6b3f9a6b743dc3723286ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/02b9e5954f63089dfe6b3f9a6b743dc3723286ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMoMFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3yMQACDDeF3bCht93RILMiKhjXZl\nptLVx7nPf63saSh4++tNGILfv/aWQ7uNxrP553GQORwuuD4meCnwf+GFz8JQ/kDH\nmiM53r6DkLs1HLsMhYbax7OCoWU5d8lBpIzF2BnWUEKjC3eqBD9qQ+bkpNwSamTO\nwRGHTI3ihCQF3aQKiB5dQl3tUn12ucvVxNXcGLnUqb51i82bArJQdFIMuwd3h6U8\nPbUAUaSAyMKSb8IDNqK/kMVA56BeDnD8V6L2phda0zWxaelrV3ooIuzPxEYLa9bG\nAk5Iv4QSfl0PSN+7jt7vfWzZ/AUPDUa8+ZsW6t2RoGI0CXI3hxbhlqreP5Vr5HW/\npe46XWNbKuRxyLT7LTTolNAqKZluBNxlJ1ne6NCKsxTRzAv3mx0TixsjI70nZb6L\n5DwzLsJqDU8he+FwJh3dwqvCEj/pAhr2ToCusVleho8v6F3Hq3u3F0+GtB4VHvxi\n4BMCwVKbfEBO1Jgg7JCyrtJg85JtxlKGvuAoYC6J17SmAn+PyoXAI/Ei4rgD0bqe\nmkXoOdvu5WhpxMVrXK4fwEicmA2Tkhg5VhlpUs0Gf+kdtSKAHk5+HKIbpy9KMcoj\nho1KzEDugbGmc1THcGYnUGX39s5iXCJ6UHIOx2C18m9Bl1nUFxHOnVrDzjOBMCQH\nln8MDXfPAz/sAW8xOCUf\n=3IMG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 02b9e5954f63089dfe6b3f9a6b743dc3723286ca\nparent 53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781695237 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781695237 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): stamp version into image so /api/v1/version stops serving \"dev\" (CAURA-000) (#414)\n\n## Summary\n\n`/api/v1/version` (and the `version` field of `/api/v1/status`) returns\n`\"dev\"` instead of the real release version.\n\n**Root cause:** the Dockerfile installs dependencies with `uv export\n--frozen --no-emit-project`, which deliberately excludes the project\nitself — so **core-api is never installed as a package** in the image.\n`core_api.constants.VERSION` resolves via\n`importlib.metadata.version(\"core-api\")`, which raises\n`PackageNotFoundError`, and the silent `except` fallback returns\n`\"dev\"`. Confirmed by inspecting the built image: `pip show core-api` →\nnot found, and the module loads from source via `PYTHONPATH`.\n\nThis is invisible in CI (which installs core-api editable, so metadata\nresolves) — the bug only exists inside the built image.\n\n## Fix\n\nBake the version into the image at build time and read it\ndeterministically:\n\n- **Dockerfile** — stamp `/app/VERSION` from `pyproject.toml` (the\nsource of truth) in the builder, with an optional `MEMCLAW_VERSION`\nbuild-arg override (e.g. a release tag).\n- **constants.py** — `_resolve_version()` precedence: `MEMCLAW_VERSION`\nenv → `/app/VERSION` file → installed-package metadata → `\"dev\"`.\nIndependent of install method / `PYTHONPATH` ordering.\n- **.dockerignore** — add recursive `**/*.egg-info` (a bare `*.egg-info`\nonly matches the context root) so a stray nested `core_api.egg-info`\nfrom a local editable install can't bake into the image and shadow the\nstamp.\n- **ci.yml** — new `image-version` job that builds the image and asserts\nthe baked version is a real semver matching `pyproject.toml` (not\n`\"dev\"`). A pytest assertion can't catch this; the job builds the actual\nimage.\n- **tests** — version-resolution precedence guards in\n`test_api_status.py`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `docker build` of the image → `VERSION = <pyproject version>` (was\n`\"dev\"`)\n- [x] Verified `pip show core-api` is absent in the image — the stamp is\nthe sole source\n- [x] `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean; `mypy` clean\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_api_status.py -k version` — 3 passed\n- [x] New `image-version` CI job fails loudly if the baked version is\n`\"dev\"` or drifts from `pyproject.toml`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T11:20:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4d1c486bf7c28fddcc0cad2d93cd53589460831a/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427"}]},{"sha":"53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDUzYjQ2N2QyYzYyMmRhN2QzMzlkN2MzOTA2MjRmMzdhYWNmOWM0Mjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T10:55:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T10:55:14Z"},"message":"fix(rate-limit): fail open on Redis outage instead of 500 (view_rate_limit AttributeError) (#410)\n\n## Prod incident (2026-06-17)\n\nA Redis connection reset turned into **500s on `POST /api/v1/search`**\n(found while reviewing today's prod alerts):\n```\nslowapi: Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error → redis.ConnectionError: Connection reset by peer\nUnhandled exception on POST /api/v1/search → AttributeError: 'State' object has no attribute 'view_rate_limit'\n```\nThe limiter is configured `swallow_errors=True` — the *intent* is to\nfail open when the rate-limit backend is down. But it doesn't fully\nwork.\n\n## Root cause (slowapi 0.1.10)\n\nslowapi sets `request.state.view_rate_limit` only **after** it hits the\nstorage backend:\n```\nextension.py:514   if not self.limiter.hit(lim.limit, *args, cost=cost): ...\nextension.py:530   request.state.view_rate_limit = limit_for_header\n```\nWhen `hit()` raises (Redis down) and `swallow_errors=True` catches it\n(extension.py:647, the `\"Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error\"` log),\nline 530 is **skipped**. But the limit decorator then reads\n`request.state.view_rate_limit` **unconditionally** on the way out to\ninject headers (extension.py `async_wrapper`), so the swallow path\n`AttributeError`s → 500 instead of failing open. (`_inject_headers`\nitself tolerates `None`, and headers are off — the crash is purely the\neager attribute read.)\n\n## Fix\n\nSeed `request.state.view_rate_limit = None` in **`_key_func`**, which\nruns first in every limit check (to compute the bucket key) and never\ntouches the backend:\n- a successful check overwrites it with the real limit;\n- a swallowed one leaves it `None`, which `_inject_headers` tolerates —\nso `swallow_errors` now genuinely fails open.\n\nAlso harden the 429 handler (`app.py`) to read it via\n`getattr(request.state, \"view_rate_limit\", None)` for defense in depth.\n\n**Why `_key_func` and not a new middleware:** it runs in the route's own\nexecution context (no BaseHTTPMiddleware scope-propagation caveat — see\nthe existing `SlowAPIMiddleware` note in `app.py`) and adds **zero**\nrequest-path overhead.\n\n## Test\n\n`test_search_fails_open_when_rate_limit_storage_errors` monkeypatches\nthe limiter backend (`limiter.limiter.hit`) to raise and asserts\n`/api/v1/search` returns **200, not 500** — reproduces the prod crash\nwithout the seed. Full `tests/test_rate_limit.py` → 8 passed;\n`ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\nFound during the 2026-06-17 alert review; the only new category not\nalready covered by #405–#408.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8af60ef136612aa5b420c7abcbfe8be1ff804c39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8af60ef136612aa5b420c7abcbfe8be1ff804c39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMn0TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+U8QAAHlrJJnnsJ7Bt2mTNwCJeaf\n3x+WcnS6wmNMmyu/dHDnyMAhK2PfRnEBeTVdUSh1jKpvUa/Pl+tZ9P6cMvuy1+kv\n6bTjJCCmPAiPNnqRR6Yamk6HuQjOQ4ljWqsnhUsWLiyc/XuYpNKYQv1IQCxuar4F\nivBul/MnKnA8hr2sDnXPHLCsg1DNOGl0WZ+OOnyDK6f56SNoxnnng5d7L4uSgu8a\n3oQ68iixO3UH7Fg2cov0K3bm7nXP2MMVUpMhUkZZQeyjNmRPfj7zAQ0rMwH3Qx4p\nMAtHQ9o56njxlCsIHvimvH2b/9AyPCPXevpO977WQikP74fdCBBqNVMv1xCk7yz2\ng3/dtwhNrqFlVqWUSr1oQRDe5GvBLjF0CXDP8p4iSeei9a3AkfvYUcl4KXSyIwOX\n7d0QA5X/WJBwFzK0JPJxUKHC7K2EMfGLIRaU2+RaSspRqU3Ghr80FeKgIRfuFZWF\nfr2kDln8yPcV3Dbp14giuArhOpRhUcFlNZ42tDyYYsLRodZZhgp8+Cy/Fn/YSTaX\nBjgjLRag+BIDCspKpwuhKtTZyUCHJFDqHfKSU76UpNt1KEIs843ZoiUXbCuoak4v\nZDr54nyLMq+pd0VKhcBn7qgDA/i+01XFBHAHsNtOBc2e/+0MTXDpuLSpBwgM3x6X\ncliUIzisYkJCwEbpvLRG\n=GFla\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8af60ef136612aa5b420c7abcbfe8be1ff804c39\nparent ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781693714 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781693714 +0300\n\nfix(rate-limit): fail open on Redis outage instead of 500 (view_rate_limit AttributeError) (#410)\n\n## Prod incident (2026-06-17)\n\nA Redis connection reset turned into **500s on `POST /api/v1/search`**\n(found while reviewing today's prod alerts):\n```\nslowapi: Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error → redis.ConnectionError: Connection reset by peer\nUnhandled exception on POST /api/v1/search → AttributeError: 'State' object has no attribute 'view_rate_limit'\n```\nThe limiter is configured `swallow_errors=True` — the *intent* is to\nfail open when the rate-limit backend is down. But it doesn't fully\nwork.\n\n## Root cause (slowapi 0.1.10)\n\nslowapi sets `request.state.view_rate_limit` only **after** it hits the\nstorage backend:\n```\nextension.py:514   if not self.limiter.hit(lim.limit, *args, cost=cost): ...\nextension.py:530   request.state.view_rate_limit = limit_for_header\n```\nWhen `hit()` raises (Redis down) and `swallow_errors=True` catches it\n(extension.py:647, the `\"Failed to rate limit. Swallowing error\"` log),\nline 530 is **skipped**. But the limit decorator then reads\n`request.state.view_rate_limit` **unconditionally** on the way out to\ninject headers (extension.py `async_wrapper`), so the swallow path\n`AttributeError`s → 500 instead of failing open. (`_inject_headers`\nitself tolerates `None`, and headers are off — the crash is purely the\neager attribute read.)\n\n## Fix\n\nSeed `request.state.view_rate_limit = None` in **`_key_func`**, which\nruns first in every limit check (to compute the bucket key) and never\ntouches the backend:\n- a successful check overwrites it with the real limit;\n- a swallowed one leaves it `None`, which `_inject_headers` tolerates —\nso `swallow_errors` now genuinely fails open.\n\nAlso harden the 429 handler (`app.py`) to read it via\n`getattr(request.state, \"view_rate_limit\", None)` for defense in depth.\n\n**Why `_key_func` and not a new middleware:** it runs in the route's own\nexecution context (no BaseHTTPMiddleware scope-propagation caveat — see\nthe existing `SlowAPIMiddleware` note in `app.py`) and adds **zero**\nrequest-path overhead.\n\n## Test\n\n`test_search_fails_open_when_rate_limit_storage_errors` monkeypatches\nthe limiter backend (`limiter.limiter.hit`) to raise and asserts\n`/api/v1/search` returns **200, not 500** — reproduces the prod crash\nwithout the seed. Full `tests/test_rate_limit.py` → 8 passed;\n`ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\nFound during the 2026-06-17 alert review; the only new category not\nalready covered by #405–#408.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T10:55:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/53b467d2c622da7d339d7c390624f37aacf9c427/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c"}]},{"sha":"ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGFiMGQyZDZiMTI2ODQxZjgyYWYzOTdkNWI2NGQ4NGQ5Zjk4Yzk2MGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-17T10:31:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T10:31:43Z"},"message":"fix(extraction): re-fold split-off subject discriminators (A33) (#412)\n\n## What\n\nEntity extraction inconsistently **splits a trailing disambiguator off\nits subject**: `\"Acme Corp #0033's …\"` becomes a bare subject `acme\ncorp` **+** a separate identifier `#0033` (`role=mentioned`). So every\n`Acme Corp #NNNN` collapses onto one shared `acme corp` subject entity.\nWith `same_subject = (entity_id == entity_id)` (CAURA-133), that shared\nid is a **guaranteed false contradiction**, and the bare hub also\n**dilutes `entity_lookup`** (the A30 person-hub class). This is the\ndominant mechanism behind the V2 ~6.3% false-`conflicted` rate.\n\nThe #304 B-guard can't help here — the name being resolved is literally\n`acme corp` (no digits), which correctly matches the existing bare\nentity. The discriminator already left the subject upstream, in\nextraction.\n\n## Fix\n\n`_reattach_subject_discriminators` — a deterministic normalization on\nthe `ExtractedGraph` **before any resolution**: re-fold a trailing\ndisambiguator (a `#tag` or a `(qualifier)`) back into its subject when\nthe content shows the two adjacent, remapping relation endpoints +\nmention links.\n\nGuards: only `#`/parenthetical shapes qualify, and only when\n**content-adjacent** to the subject — so real named identifiers\n(`pr-2025-a`, `build-734`) and non-adjacent tags are left untouched.\n\n**Scope**: forward-only (corrects new extractions, not already-baked\ncorpora). Covers mechanism ① (the split). The cosine-merge of\n*already-distinct* qualified names (two `John Smith`s, `Acme (Delaware)`\nvs `(Ohio)`) is a separate mechanism, tracked as a follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **7 unit** (`test_a33_subject_discriminator.py`): fold,\nsibling-distinctness, relation/mention remap, parenthetical, + 3\nnegatives (non-adjacent, real named identifier, no-subject).\n- **Wet-tested on the local stack** (real OpenAI extraction): two\nsibling writes resolve to **distinct** subject entities — `acme corp\n#0028` (active) vs `acme corp #0033` (confirmed), **neither marked\n`conflicted`**. Pre-fix these collapsed to one bare `acme corp` + a\nfalse conflict (V2 trace).\n- Entity-extraction/resolution suite: 49 passed, no regression.\nruff/format/mypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e273b88d89dd126f277dd2b88e2f1722f1d40ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9e273b88d89dd126f277dd2b88e2f1722f1d40ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMnePCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeycQAEoiObT4xb84TH0BWpZqvatn\n9wU1li3oMOmRpgqPOXlWTaF6k9bUn96jtTZ4LLJksD2EpAvGTquBTnMu41Wzzo4y\nZK/Oh7zowYpJioPyceGP1AurH0gmRGFJKnMgir2PMSK35NKMmuoq7oKKB9HL6ygm\n+JBVsUsFDKMreoRjBxlv+6sR9scfd8dooNQBfEI+RVvDuxqQkZjVPO6qfoBheWdj\nMB3CNxmpQruA9GUmcDZj++3oXllBET+HFSmL2ZkPZYZdoSRI3E8sAm66pBf7KfMq\nK0+1tZpP9s0xBdd5JC/RxaH5focrqLBW3/gZUyeikAUAzmA8H0tY6JbHVCpjWIjA\nvnu9IEGRQQEGu/OgXElHITlaBbtVPVRpQt+GygttG2NNyOW0+2C/bFIIFCbSHIZ2\nEcEUbUAEKi03GND49Co8tAg+x6muk+dlft/gxXgK+cFNkwwhFK3Pt+VlUH7QLci7\nwiAktXaUCFyWXyP8DjL3XoYoecjrmTH4/BJwGzN12r6CV1ekOn5wD/KJiNKMNXY2\nFLUE7FY//hlpXeUw7opTf2KSnOaEzNsE5rmi5jF0vMoKRSrpfb84ktJdzkkQ+fG3\nselEdc/HkBaaZ+3H++f2fzyqG0mBZX3vIRWrmUb1yz0KzIUSWrTVuldXS+jadzFy\nLpJSRE+gVzlHDEckr+zL\n=ZYMB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9e273b88d89dd126f277dd2b88e2f1722f1d40ce\nparent 1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781692303 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781692303 +0300\n\nfix(extraction): re-fold split-off subject discriminators (A33) (#412)\n\n## What\n\nEntity extraction inconsistently **splits a trailing disambiguator off\nits subject**: `\"Acme Corp #0033's …\"` becomes a bare subject `acme\ncorp` **+** a separate identifier `#0033` (`role=mentioned`). So every\n`Acme Corp #NNNN` collapses onto one shared `acme corp` subject entity.\nWith `same_subject = (entity_id == entity_id)` (CAURA-133), that shared\nid is a **guaranteed false contradiction**, and the bare hub also\n**dilutes `entity_lookup`** (the A30 person-hub class). This is the\ndominant mechanism behind the V2 ~6.3% false-`conflicted` rate.\n\nThe #304 B-guard can't help here — the name being resolved is literally\n`acme corp` (no digits), which correctly matches the existing bare\nentity. The discriminator already left the subject upstream, in\nextraction.\n\n## Fix\n\n`_reattach_subject_discriminators` — a deterministic normalization on\nthe `ExtractedGraph` **before any resolution**: re-fold a trailing\ndisambiguator (a `#tag` or a `(qualifier)`) back into its subject when\nthe content shows the two adjacent, remapping relation endpoints +\nmention links.\n\nGuards: only `#`/parenthetical shapes qualify, and only when\n**content-adjacent** to the subject — so real named identifiers\n(`pr-2025-a`, `build-734`) and non-adjacent tags are left untouched.\n\n**Scope**: forward-only (corrects new extractions, not already-baked\ncorpora). Covers mechanism ① (the split). The cosine-merge of\n*already-distinct* qualified names (two `John Smith`s, `Acme (Delaware)`\nvs `(Ohio)`) is a separate mechanism, tracked as a follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **7 unit** (`test_a33_subject_discriminator.py`): fold,\nsibling-distinctness, relation/mention remap, parenthetical, + 3\nnegatives (non-adjacent, real named identifier, no-subject).\n- **Wet-tested on the local stack** (real OpenAI extraction): two\nsibling writes resolve to **distinct** subject entities — `acme corp\n#0028` (active) vs `acme corp #0033` (confirmed), **neither marked\n`conflicted`**. Pre-fix these collapsed to one bare `acme corp` + a\nfalse conflict (V2 trace).\n- Entity-extraction/resolution suite: 49 passed, no regression.\nruff/format/mypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T10:31:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ab0d2d6b126841f82af397d5b64d84d9f98c960c/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0"}]},{"sha":"1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFkZTIxOWM4YTQwNzhmOTcxMTAyZGNiNmM4MmZjMTAwMjhlMDI1ZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-17T08:40:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T08:40:22Z"},"message":"fix(search): dampen recall_boost so it can't hijack rankings (A26) (#411)\n\n## What\n\n`recall_count` is bumped for **every returned row, used or not**\n(`TrackRecalls` → `memory_increment_recall`) and feeds `recall_boost`\nback into the rank score (`memory_scored_search` / `memory_repository`)\n— a self-reinforcing **returned → boosted → returned** loop with no\nusefulness signal. Popular-but-unused memories asymptote toward the\nboost cap and entrench at the top; the S1 bench has to pin\n`recall_boost=false` to avoid run-over-run drift, which is the same bug\nin miniature.\n\n## Why this PR is the interim, not the full fix\n\nTruly breaking the loop requires a **usefulness signal**\n(confirmation-gated bump — only count a recall when the memory was\nactually used/cited). That needs new signal plumbing that overlaps the\nevals + write-time-signal work (D5/D1), so it's filed as a separate\nfollow-up. This PR is the low-risk damage-reducer: dial the boost down\nso it can no longer overcome a base-score gap.\n\n## Change\n\n- `RECALL_BOOST_CAP` **1.5 → 1.1** — shrinks the \"hijack zone\" (how much\nmore relevant a row must be to be safe from a saturated popular one)\nfrom **~50% → ~10%**.\n- `RECALL_DECAY_WINDOW_DAYS` **90 → 14** — stale popularity fades in ~2\nweeks instead of a quarter.\n\nSingle source of truth: `resolve_search_profile` propagates both to\nstorage via `search_params` (verified). The boost stays enabled —\nbounded, not removed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New guard `test_a26_boost_cannot_hijack_a_more_relevant_memory` —\nencodes the guarantee (a saturated popular row can't out-rank a\n>12%-more-relevant fresh one). **Verified to fail at cap=1.5 and pass at\n1.1.**\n- Updated two existing assertions that hard-coded the old 1.5-cap\nmagnitude to assert *shape relative to the constant* (survives future\ntuning).\n- Full recall/scoring unit suite: 29 passing; ruff/format/mypy clean.\n\nLive S1 replay intentionally skipped: the bench runs with\n`recall_boost=false`, so a cap/window constant cannot change its result.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"425ab15166e9284ce3c2f50ce7f1dd312b4ad75e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/425ab15166e9284ce3c2f50ce7f1dd312b4ad75e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMl12CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2TwQAHaaX1e+poCgOPeV8N1ApsDC\nCbGPCqvm/fmEkUo8v/sJ7rkexi2P4NHsFQhHwD3GpPE9k5ljduAX861l7p4cKq1n\ny1p3/JK6Mhv2Fds5mkU6tq+YJBnvdGKCtI3Z8nBDV352tSPyiJv7XaLs/2DgbHId\nogsqlNqhIwkf8xjKB1GBz/a1P+L7lXf/5/qK+5XLs2KM3qn2S5qJkefRu8/Q6qR0\nvNMfN12Psgho7zmv92Ayrw/Z6H/Ui6GWNtWMxrAjoEh6cyW/Cly5QY/GvwJaXATS\nCY+TzYUNR6yBgi0Qdg5RSJONFEF4wz0tHONdxh3cX/kPQLLYuqJeTRcIlFAxXB1D\nZflM00mUYEeyp/7LL1FUIUKriasBxc+ZbfM2gi9WHlt6nuUZKjDsgcNincrNfb7T\n1wAFPqVLFVdYq7UhxrVfgWZO+Fm9a+oQFtVsudvCWrNZ5E7WORUNyd8GgQ6YoW1M\nL/g2to9q5agYj3cyKVSLiUZq/5j2/LmQqhuw3sPaWLiOwv5IJuYFL4xSBoAH26o7\nLnt6hEEXdy2Bh1foKGzGWxnIQogz5aJLpBhYq5Q8qHPO6AcHmu/S+JFQV7cYhfZ7\nwtHg7GjYuk+auZ9uiQrK9OtP8tENZQcGt+o2bve4MvIGxEgcreDauoOh/QXL6DVJ\n3quhTTXdaiMuX3+/G4mF\n=JkdQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 425ab15166e9284ce3c2f50ce7f1dd312b4ad75e\nparent 8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781685622 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781685622 +0300\n\nfix(search): dampen recall_boost so it can't hijack rankings (A26) (#411)\n\n## What\n\n`recall_count` is bumped for **every returned row, used or not**\n(`TrackRecalls` → `memory_increment_recall`) and feeds `recall_boost`\nback into the rank score (`memory_scored_search` / `memory_repository`)\n— a self-reinforcing **returned → boosted → returned** loop with no\nusefulness signal. Popular-but-unused memories asymptote toward the\nboost cap and entrench at the top; the S1 bench has to pin\n`recall_boost=false` to avoid run-over-run drift, which is the same bug\nin miniature.\n\n## Why this PR is the interim, not the full fix\n\nTruly breaking the loop requires a **usefulness signal**\n(confirmation-gated bump — only count a recall when the memory was\nactually used/cited). That needs new signal plumbing that overlaps the\nevals + write-time-signal work (D5/D1), so it's filed as a separate\nfollow-up. This PR is the low-risk damage-reducer: dial the boost down\nso it can no longer overcome a base-score gap.\n\n## Change\n\n- `RECALL_BOOST_CAP` **1.5 → 1.1** — shrinks the \"hijack zone\" (how much\nmore relevant a row must be to be safe from a saturated popular one)\nfrom **~50% → ~10%**.\n- `RECALL_DECAY_WINDOW_DAYS` **90 → 14** — stale popularity fades in ~2\nweeks instead of a quarter.\n\nSingle source of truth: `resolve_search_profile` propagates both to\nstorage via `search_params` (verified). The boost stays enabled —\nbounded, not removed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New guard `test_a26_boost_cannot_hijack_a_more_relevant_memory` —\nencodes the guarantee (a saturated popular row can't out-rank a\n>12%-more-relevant fresh one). **Verified to fail at cap=1.5 and pass at\n1.1.**\n- Updated two existing assertions that hard-coded the old 1.5-cap\nmagnitude to assert *shape relative to the constant* (survives future\ntuning).\n- Full recall/scoring unit suite: 29 passing; ruff/format/mypy clean.\n\nLive S1 replay intentionally skipped: the bench runs with\n`recall_boost=false`, so a cap/window constant cannot change its result.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T08:40:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1de219c8a4078f971102dcb6c82fc10028e025f0/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b"}]},{"sha":"8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhmODA5YzA5MTRlODMyNzFhMTA4YzVjZmViYTUzZDc5NGE2NjRjNmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-17T07:56:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T07:56:56Z"},"message":"fix(search): rank entity-lookup fan-out cap by query-match count (A30) (#409)\n\n## What\n\n`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories` caps the entity-lookup candidate pool\nto `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES` (50) **before** loading content, sorting\nonly by **near-uniform hop-boost**. When a query hits a hub entity (e.g.\na bare `john smith` linking 100+ memories), the gold is one of N\nnear-equal-boost candidates and gets cut by the arbitrary cap — *before*\nthe discriminator-aware `_query_overlap` rerank ever runs. This is the\nperson-hub dilution behind the S1 K=10000 residual misses (**A30**).\n\n## Fix\n\nRank the cap by **how many of the query's directly-matched (hop-0)\nentities each memory links to** first, with hop-boost as the tiebreak. A\n`\"What is X's manager?\"` gold links to **both** the person hub *and* the\nmatched `manager` role (match-count 2), whereas sibling facts about\nother attributes link to only the hub (count 1) — so the gold survives\nthe cut regardless of hub size (robust even for the 1000+-member hubs\nseen at K=10000). The `#NNNN` discriminator is then resolved by the\nexisting `_query_overlap` rerank after load.\n\n- No new constants, no routing change (strategy split unchanged).\n- 21-line change, isolated to `_collect_memories`.\n\n## Validation\n\nS1 retrieval bench (replay-only against already-seeded tenants,\n`text-embedding-3-small@1024`):\n\n| Tenant | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| k1k | 23/25 | **25/25** |\n| k10k | 25/25 | **25/25** (no regression) |\n\nDistractors 25/25 on both; strategy split unchanged (k1k 34/16, k10k\n42/8).\n\nNew regression test\n`test_collect_memories_cap_prefers_multi_matched_entity_gold_over_hub_siblings`\n— constructed so the gold is enqueued **last** (a boost-only stable-sort\ncap drops it); **verified to fail on pre-A30 code** and pass with the\nfix.\n\n`ruff check` / `ruff format` / `mypy` clean; related search-pipeline\ntests (45 + 8) pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b7da4f08e9103390ab590aaf4ebeef7848407d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2b7da4f08e9103390ab590aaf4ebeef7848407d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMlNJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA37YQABJqVQ5Pi+hEbmRe9JzSOnu9\nMBGZ77IyCQB7GuKvpgYFlhPPqLHFcGu0SF95Lj98acyH6ErZs7LiO5MCIQqQunx9\n6hPxpEaAcRVEiQRUWe1Mkv7wCC6dHZ7tCxg3SPBCTUdVpCrlJS6mjn2Neax+QbAJ\n1X8UJCLta+ReceOuTrUWzZNv3OSVMbqDSUwYzdZkPsqKs0Pcx/1OAl68uAQBYzeJ\niSrqWZnEEAi7zeuG2pRwiZV/kmXJgG3dpslGfttS9/ZDUgN+T094iFW0JgL6vgFJ\nTmUqESYCr7zE5jkl4ucVS1hxAqCJPD06lPzfy+cQk4tUfjro9OJF7qgO9UZyJ589\nucoZDmalzlHmBhNG7qJF0+UGJnDd3kMws36vt2cNHhfuRHoZNxdy24dxn8ly+kKE\n2fjBYvWLyV6GpcokNBzAoxXXSXUxCdpP126vORxIZdgLoUEzXTmraRH30MmPxcqZ\nGpVPOWpJ0HA5A3ssgzPtWQl9OXquZvgMqvS5dTGtV7k+FcPW/gcJh22CpOOKLKDd\ni3C6j3uXCPXzn9qxX5UE4qncMtgJt6nKlQ5i70qxTShQSl88r2HIHTWcJ5STeovB\nMoRaEQ/uyWCQDtIJKrfeqgUTlWYZc6xGG2zJvwxmOHJ/ZzlTmjN7FVN0Q2VXvrW3\nNl6JX2XgdIU5ZYI6HZta\n=xazY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b7da4f08e9103390ab590aaf4ebeef7848407d2\nparent 54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781683016 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781683016 +0300\n\nfix(search): rank entity-lookup fan-out cap by query-match count (A30) (#409)\n\n## What\n\n`ClassifyQuery._collect_memories` caps the entity-lookup candidate pool\nto `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES` (50) **before** loading content, sorting\nonly by **near-uniform hop-boost**. When a query hits a hub entity (e.g.\na bare `john smith` linking 100+ memories), the gold is one of N\nnear-equal-boost candidates and gets cut by the arbitrary cap — *before*\nthe discriminator-aware `_query_overlap` rerank ever runs. This is the\nperson-hub dilution behind the S1 K=10000 residual misses (**A30**).\n\n## Fix\n\nRank the cap by **how many of the query's directly-matched (hop-0)\nentities each memory links to** first, with hop-boost as the tiebreak. A\n`\"What is X's manager?\"` gold links to **both** the person hub *and* the\nmatched `manager` role (match-count 2), whereas sibling facts about\nother attributes link to only the hub (count 1) — so the gold survives\nthe cut regardless of hub size (robust even for the 1000+-member hubs\nseen at K=10000). The `#NNNN` discriminator is then resolved by the\nexisting `_query_overlap` rerank after load.\n\n- No new constants, no routing change (strategy split unchanged).\n- 21-line change, isolated to `_collect_memories`.\n\n## Validation\n\nS1 retrieval bench (replay-only against already-seeded tenants,\n`text-embedding-3-small@1024`):\n\n| Tenant | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| k1k | 23/25 | **25/25** |\n| k10k | 25/25 | **25/25** (no regression) |\n\nDistractors 25/25 on both; strategy split unchanged (k1k 34/16, k10k\n42/8).\n\nNew regression test\n`test_collect_memories_cap_prefers_multi_matched_entity_gold_over_hub_siblings`\n— constructed so the gold is enqueued **last** (a boost-only stable-sort\ncap drops it); **verified to fail on pre-A30 code** and pass with the\nfix.\n\n`ruff check` / `ruff format` / `mypy` clean; related search-pipeline\ntests (45 + 8) pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T07:56:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8f809c0914e83271a108c5cfeba53d794a664c6b/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1"}]},{"sha":"54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU0Y2JlMWFjZDFlNDg0MzFiMzk3NGM4MjhhNDdkMGE4NmNlNTk3ZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T07:33:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T07:33:04Z"},"message":"fix(storage): harden migration advisory-lock so a slow migration can't crash booting writers (#408)\n\n## Background — the 2026-06-16 incident\n\nOn a `core-storage-writer` deploy, all N replicas race for a Postgres\nadvisory lock (`8675309`); one wins and runs `alembic upgrade head`\n**while holding the lock**, the rest poll for it and only serve once\nit's released. The wait was a **hardcoded 300s**. But the lock is held\nfor the *entire* migration — including minutes-long `CREATE INDEX\nCONCURRENTLY` builds — so a slow-but-healthy migration crashes the N-1\nwaiting replicas.\n\nOn 2026-06-16, migration **025** (a plain, non-`CONCURRENTLY` `CREATE\nINDEX` on the large `audit_log` table) ran past 300s and failed **6**\n`prod-memclaw-core-storage-writer` boots:\n```\nTimeoutError: Migration advisory lock 8675309 not acquired within 300s → Application startup failed. Exiting.\n```\nIt self-healed (Cloud Run restarted them once the winner finished), but\nthe next slow migration repeats it.\n\n## Approach (A + B + D, chosen with the team)\n\nKeeps migrations in the lifespan startup — the deliberate **CAURA-621**\natomic-deploy property stays intact (no pre-deploy migration job /\ndeploy-ordering orchestration).\n\n1. **Configurable + generous wait (A):** `MIGRATION_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS`\n(`settings.migration_lock_wait_seconds`), default raised **300s →\n1800s**. The wait is now a *stuck-migration backstop*, not a routine cap\n— it must exceed the slowest real migration so a progressing one never\ncrashes a booting replica.\n2. **Wait-don't-crash, observably (B):** keeps the **safe**\n`pg_try_advisory_lock`-in-`AUTOCOMMIT` poll (a blocking\n`pg_advisory_lock` would hold an idle-in-transaction that stalls the\nwinner's `CONCURRENTLY` build — the existing comment documents this),\nand **logs progress every 30s** while waiting, so a long-but-healthy\nmigration reads as progress in the logs instead of a silently hung boot.\nThe deadline still raises a clear *stuck-migration* error (better than\nletting the Cloud Run probe kill the instance silently).\n3. **CI guard (D):** `test_no_plain_create_index_on_large_tables` fails\nif a migration from **005 onward** does a plain `CREATE INDEX` on a\nlarge pre-existing table (`audit_log` / `memories` / `entities` /\n`documents` / `memory_entity_links` / `relations`) — it must be `CREATE\nINDEX CONCURRENTLY` in an `autocommit_block` (see 007 / 026). `025` is\nallow-listed as documented, already-applied debt; `001–004` build the\ninitial schema (indexes on empty tables) and are exempt.\n\n**Caveat:** the effective wait is `min(MIGRATION_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS,\nCloud Run startup-probe deadline)`. The 300s error fired first in the\nincident, so the probe grace was ≥300s — but the storage-writer's Cloud\nRun startup timeout should be confirmed ≥ 1800s (Terraform, out of this\nrepo) or raised alongside, else the probe kills the instance before the\nlonger wait helps.\n\nThis is the root-cause follow-up to #407's migration 026 (which already\nfollows the `CONCURRENTLY` pattern). It does **not** retroactively\nchange 025 (already applied in prod) — it stops the *next* slow\nmigration from repeating the crash.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_no_plain_create_index_on_large_tables` (the new guard) + the\nexisting migration-chain tests pass; full `test_skill_schema_v1.py` → 79\npassed.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on `config.py` +\n`init.py`. The acquire→upgrade happy path is exercised by CI's \"Run\nmigrations\" step.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1c417f4f4196b822face243b87f0c491a92a55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e1c417f4f4196b822face243b87f0c491a92a55f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMk2wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdlAQAGAYztvgDpZ60adx3mnnLNlH\n0POkd7tMKTGtN7gY+68Wdai6RLtgUFKPh76Tp4spEX3zHKyiTFzhxqeyQd92yOJ3\niawRs0T5AgbyFkaYPudpMsdX88FUr5MMK1Ut48U4qRU6PPsoK6cgT6RsT9U6YH8M\nsIDck7fvYGABu88ajdwv8hyPguwlLUVvj+EiXWme6YC7JAAT99yilfReBldldZyb\nM8cvbuunfIkO2TyEBDJLSIn1QU9OcyDXznimkEKN7G6dkEir0uHsg5fyPHql2JCZ\nmVlq7FBjvJgYSUXVxOVuFYk4Xf8oB8ZrJUETM7x8qwzFACotNYTCiEbMEHULCxQg\nlGfD0FHbu30uR3VJ+RX6sTUJPz3TDDQ5MxSxBWrGwggVLIjK6h7KhtjIUMKSZdDc\n3W/AOP2SegeRjOEitF903OzuBG5IaM6hC7IWgUjanCWgTrPhyP3yu2VPEJxXQ0a0\nt0fnuvJIvICWdxhMQ8QiqLWVtTZOw4bMvGKfuW+tqqBFtX3uwO+5vxSEK8xXfwxO\n/MkhX0EsskQO+qNGGqvuThAtX6WRU6qSd0b2wy8zmwkgLPL8mf4mOYOPjFJ602rR\nCQpsRpCOpWtNm662OoGs7rTpyuV6Li3j9e1XMOUqNRnpF/cvIfm5GWkBJoqum65V\nxJyPxljACPoVKW7yCl7v\n=7NQi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e1c417f4f4196b822face243b87f0c491a92a55f\nparent bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781681584 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781681584 +0300\n\nfix(storage): harden migration advisory-lock so a slow migration can't crash booting writers (#408)\n\n## Background — the 2026-06-16 incident\n\nOn a `core-storage-writer` deploy, all N replicas race for a Postgres\nadvisory lock (`8675309`); one wins and runs `alembic upgrade head`\n**while holding the lock**, the rest poll for it and only serve once\nit's released. The wait was a **hardcoded 300s**. But the lock is held\nfor the *entire* migration — including minutes-long `CREATE INDEX\nCONCURRENTLY` builds — so a slow-but-healthy migration crashes the N-1\nwaiting replicas.\n\nOn 2026-06-16, migration **025** (a plain, non-`CONCURRENTLY` `CREATE\nINDEX` on the large `audit_log` table) ran past 300s and failed **6**\n`prod-memclaw-core-storage-writer` boots:\n```\nTimeoutError: Migration advisory lock 8675309 not acquired within 300s → Application startup failed. Exiting.\n```\nIt self-healed (Cloud Run restarted them once the winner finished), but\nthe next slow migration repeats it.\n\n## Approach (A + B + D, chosen with the team)\n\nKeeps migrations in the lifespan startup — the deliberate **CAURA-621**\natomic-deploy property stays intact (no pre-deploy migration job /\ndeploy-ordering orchestration).\n\n1. **Configurable + generous wait (A):** `MIGRATION_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS`\n(`settings.migration_lock_wait_seconds`), default raised **300s →\n1800s**. The wait is now a *stuck-migration backstop*, not a routine cap\n— it must exceed the slowest real migration so a progressing one never\ncrashes a booting replica.\n2. **Wait-don't-crash, observably (B):** keeps the **safe**\n`pg_try_advisory_lock`-in-`AUTOCOMMIT` poll (a blocking\n`pg_advisory_lock` would hold an idle-in-transaction that stalls the\nwinner's `CONCURRENTLY` build — the existing comment documents this),\nand **logs progress every 30s** while waiting, so a long-but-healthy\nmigration reads as progress in the logs instead of a silently hung boot.\nThe deadline still raises a clear *stuck-migration* error (better than\nletting the Cloud Run probe kill the instance silently).\n3. **CI guard (D):** `test_no_plain_create_index_on_large_tables` fails\nif a migration from **005 onward** does a plain `CREATE INDEX` on a\nlarge pre-existing table (`audit_log` / `memories` / `entities` /\n`documents` / `memory_entity_links` / `relations`) — it must be `CREATE\nINDEX CONCURRENTLY` in an `autocommit_block` (see 007 / 026). `025` is\nallow-listed as documented, already-applied debt; `001–004` build the\ninitial schema (indexes on empty tables) and are exempt.\n\n**Caveat:** the effective wait is `min(MIGRATION_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS,\nCloud Run startup-probe deadline)`. The 300s error fired first in the\nincident, so the probe grace was ≥300s — but the storage-writer's Cloud\nRun startup timeout should be confirmed ≥ 1800s (Terraform, out of this\nrepo) or raised alongside, else the probe kills the instance before the\nlonger wait helps.\n\nThis is the root-cause follow-up to #407's migration 026 (which already\nfollows the `CONCURRENTLY` pattern). It does **not** retroactively\nchange 025 (already applied in prod) — it stops the *next* slow\nmigration from repeating the crash.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_no_plain_create_index_on_large_tables` (the new guard) + the\nexisting migration-chain tests pass; full `test_skill_schema_v1.py` → 79\npassed.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on `config.py` +\n`init.py`. The acquire→upgrade happy path is exercised by CI's \"Run\nmigrations\" step.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T07:33:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/54cbe1acd1e48431b3974c828a47d0a86ce597d1/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb"}]},{"sha":"bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJmODdlNjQxNDYzMDM4NjVjNzVjZGJiNjVjMDhhN2M5NWNiZDRhZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-17T07:04:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T07:04:28Z"},"message":"fix(audit): idempotent bulk flush via client_event_id — stop dropping audit rows (#407)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe async audit flush (`POST /audit-logs/bulk`) used\n**connect-phase-only retry**, so a `ReadTimeout`/5xx dropped a whole\ntenant's slice (logged `audit batch flush failed … events lost`, never\nrequeued) — **silent audit-log data loss**. This was the known gap\nbehind the `audit chunk flush failed` / `audit batch flush failed`\nsignatures (the connect-timeout occurrences are separately addressed by\nwidening connect-phase retry).\n\nNaively switching to full retry was **unsafe**: `audit_log` is a\ntamper-evident **per-tenant hash chain** with **no per-event identity**,\nso re-sending an already-committed batch would re-append every event\nwith fresh `seq`s and silently **double the chain** — and it would still\npass `verify_chain`, so the corruption is invisible.\n\n## Fix — make the flush idempotent, then retry is safe\n\n1. **core-api `log_action`** mints a UUID `client_event_id` per event\n(stable across a retry of the same enqueued event).\n2. **Migration 026**: `audit_log` gains a nullable `client_event_id`\ncolumn + a partial unique index `(tenant_id, client_event_id) WHERE\nclient_event_id IS NOT NULL`, built with `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX\nCONCURRENTLY` inside an `autocommit_block`. This follows the **007**\nonline pattern and deliberately **not** the **025** plain in-transaction\n`CREATE INDEX` that stalled storage-writer startup past the 300s\nmigration-lock timeout.\n3. **`_audit_chain_one_tenant`** dedups already-chained\n`client_event_id`s **under the per-tenant head `FOR UPDATE` lock, BEFORE\nassigning `seq`** (plus intra-batch duplicates). Survivors get\n**contiguous** seqs, so the chain stays gap-free and the head consistent\n— avoiding the seq-gap trap a bare `ON CONFLICT` would create. Events\nwith no `client_event_id` (legacy single-event path) are never deduped.\n4. **`create_audit_logs_bulk`** switches to full `with_retry`\n(`ReadTimeout` + 5xx), now safe: a replayed batch dedups instead of\ndouble-appending. Recovers the lost-ack case that previously dropped the\nslice.\n\n## Why it's safe\n\n`_audit_chain_one_tenant` already commits one atomic transaction per\ntenant. With the dedup, the three retry cases are all correct:\n- **pre-commit failure** → rolled back, nothing chained → retry\nre-inserts.\n- **committed but lost ack** (`ReadTimeout`) → retry's dedup SELECT\n(under the head lock) sees the committed rows → skips them, no\ndouble-append.\n- **partial** → impossible (single transaction).\n\n## Deploy ordering\n\nStorage-first (storage owns the schema; the migration runs in the\nlifespan startup before serving). New core-api + old storage is safe\n(extra field ignored); new storage + old core-api is safe (column\nnullable).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_audit_chain.py` *(integration, runs against Postgres in CI)*: a\nreplayed batch dedups — no duplicate rows, contiguous seqs,\n`verify_chain` stays valid; intra-batch duplicate chained once.\n- `test_storage_client_retry.py`: `create_audit_logs_bulk` retries\n`ReadTimeout` and 5xx (unlike a bare POST).\n- `test_audit_queue.py`: `log_action` mints a unique `client_event_id`\nper event.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on the\n`core-api/src` + `core-storage-api/src` files (28 mock tests pass\nlocally; the chain-integration tests run in CI).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93d206eaf5d2e36fd1f2df0403077572c261b1a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/93d206eaf5d2e36fd1f2df0403077572c261b1a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMkb8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADBkQAIPfVbVy45xxdL9VnXb6BA27\n5nrDLiHQu3Zg6tpS70fK5rx5u8A/PZCzxWN0dr8/iYIaLVQxxNGasmk9P31FiBGk\nWaqU4kOfgTOIXU98v0djRZtZwp0lsr8t6MUNuI0epIYKjS/wEe7QZneOYI3YJ3cX\nefpIuEPDDGBKzpNDrX1eYBIX5c7S+YLq6EkJMgIfed/0KyHfbT2DZlee01mngQop\nPtESdQvyoPEAQnaOIJkb0fPbQ2cI+uo91o3vypxnbjngR+Q/ve1TQTp4I8nD0K/3\nb1+flCP52mtVAeYeBOhMYU9yhfgnCKOH/bcfrj4YZeoNdNvb26c4YZJD/EIwebLz\nny9FdacKOMk26/ZR0F/wJQIKE/1Z6GZdbzSbfH32VRtcWS4AlNZmRdT9AeTEyhqN\nPXlsgVHHrpVeWg/QTUNg5UDDCkkInzSUSLNWLQ7EgOYg3MQGNPdi2KzuR8Ni9lFp\n1c52AOaGtmWcWDU0VBpeUnJE5X3rdb3vlIubWmCuFjm4uHhuRdGnToLbIbByDj5T\n3MY2S4PSeTpWFl2v4SimN0G7hAdmbbAx7kAGNrWUzhpfIb+KTAmiZHTwl3X9K5lq\ngAbWSeBy0+2LBILpJQ6ppjGdGS7v3lo3HuYJtD+e5clzaVoACoju9jWB/T/GKhqI\nh3DqRJJ3zboaeX6CVbTL\n=eUfh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 93d206eaf5d2e36fd1f2df0403077572c261b1a8\nparent 5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781679868 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781679868 +0300\n\nfix(audit): idempotent bulk flush via client_event_id — stop dropping audit rows (#407)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe async audit flush (`POST /audit-logs/bulk`) used\n**connect-phase-only retry**, so a `ReadTimeout`/5xx dropped a whole\ntenant's slice (logged `audit batch flush failed … events lost`, never\nrequeued) — **silent audit-log data loss**. This was the known gap\nbehind the `audit chunk flush failed` / `audit batch flush failed`\nsignatures (the connect-timeout occurrences are separately addressed by\nwidening connect-phase retry).\n\nNaively switching to full retry was **unsafe**: `audit_log` is a\ntamper-evident **per-tenant hash chain** with **no per-event identity**,\nso re-sending an already-committed batch would re-append every event\nwith fresh `seq`s and silently **double the chain** — and it would still\npass `verify_chain`, so the corruption is invisible.\n\n## Fix — make the flush idempotent, then retry is safe\n\n1. **core-api `log_action`** mints a UUID `client_event_id` per event\n(stable across a retry of the same enqueued event).\n2. **Migration 026**: `audit_log` gains a nullable `client_event_id`\ncolumn + a partial unique index `(tenant_id, client_event_id) WHERE\nclient_event_id IS NOT NULL`, built with `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX\nCONCURRENTLY` inside an `autocommit_block`. This follows the **007**\nonline pattern and deliberately **not** the **025** plain in-transaction\n`CREATE INDEX` that stalled storage-writer startup past the 300s\nmigration-lock timeout.\n3. **`_audit_chain_one_tenant`** dedups already-chained\n`client_event_id`s **under the per-tenant head `FOR UPDATE` lock, BEFORE\nassigning `seq`** (plus intra-batch duplicates). Survivors get\n**contiguous** seqs, so the chain stays gap-free and the head consistent\n— avoiding the seq-gap trap a bare `ON CONFLICT` would create. Events\nwith no `client_event_id` (legacy single-event path) are never deduped.\n4. **`create_audit_logs_bulk`** switches to full `with_retry`\n(`ReadTimeout` + 5xx), now safe: a replayed batch dedups instead of\ndouble-appending. Recovers the lost-ack case that previously dropped the\nslice.\n\n## Why it's safe\n\n`_audit_chain_one_tenant` already commits one atomic transaction per\ntenant. With the dedup, the three retry cases are all correct:\n- **pre-commit failure** → rolled back, nothing chained → retry\nre-inserts.\n- **committed but lost ack** (`ReadTimeout`) → retry's dedup SELECT\n(under the head lock) sees the committed rows → skips them, no\ndouble-append.\n- **partial** → impossible (single transaction).\n\n## Deploy ordering\n\nStorage-first (storage owns the schema; the migration runs in the\nlifespan startup before serving). New core-api + old storage is safe\n(extra field ignored); new storage + old core-api is safe (column\nnullable).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_audit_chain.py` *(integration, runs against Postgres in CI)*: a\nreplayed batch dedups — no duplicate rows, contiguous seqs,\n`verify_chain` stays valid; intra-batch duplicate chained once.\n- `test_storage_client_retry.py`: `create_audit_logs_bulk` retries\n`ReadTimeout` and 5xx (unlike a bare POST).\n- `test_audit_queue.py`: `log_action` mints a unique `client_event_id`\nper event.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` / `mypy` clean on the\n`core-api/src` + `core-storage-api/src` files (28 mock tests pass\nlocally; the chain-integration tests run in CI).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T07:04:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bf87e64146303865c75cdbb65c08a7c95cbd4afb/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a"}]},{"sha":"5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDViYmVkZTc0ODEwMzIzOTdlYzUwNDAwZjE2NmYxMmYxMzJiNWZjNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-16T18:23:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T18:23:40Z"},"message":"fix(http-retry): widen connection-phase retry to ride out storage cold starts (#406)\n\n## Prod signal (2026-06-16)\n\nA steady trickle of `httpx.ConnectTimeout` reached\n`prod-memclaw-core-api` across **every** core-api → core-storage-api\npath — Pub/Sub enrichment (`pubsub handler raised; nacking for\nredelivery`), entity extraction, contradiction detection, and audit\nflush. All are storage-api connect timeouts during cold starts /\ninstance recycles.\n\nThe current policy is 3 attempts (~0.6s of backoff). That is too short\nto ride out a Cloud Run cold start, so a transient connect blip surfaces\nas a handler failure — and on the Pub/Sub path it triggers a nack →\nimmediate-redelivery storm (`common/events/pubsub.py` nacks with\n`ack_deadline=0`).\n\n## Change\n\nWiden **only** the connection-phase path (`with_connect_phase_retry`) to\n`CONNECT_PHASE_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5`.\n\nWhy only that path: `ConnectTimeout` / `ConnectError` / `PoolTimeout`\nare raised *before* the request is sent, and against an instance that\nisn't accepting connections yet — so retrying them:\n- cannot double-insert (request provably never sent), and\n- adds **zero load to a healthy server** (the connection never lands),\nso extra attempts just wait out the cold start.\n\nThe idempotent path (`with_retry`, which also retries `ReadTimeout`/5xx)\n**stays at 3 attempts** so a genuine 5xx storm isn't amplified by extra\nload against a struggling server.\n\nAlso:\n- `RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_S = 2.0` caps a single backoff sleep so the higher\nattempt count stays bounded.\n- Factored the capped + jittered delay into a small `_backoff_delay()`\nhelper (dedups the two call sites).\n\nThis **complements, not replaces**, keeping storage-api warm (Cloud Run\nmin-instances) — the durable fix for the cold starts themselves.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_post_gives_up_after_max_attempts_on_connect_timeout` now asserts\n5 attempts for the connect-phase path;\n`test_get_retries_then_gives_up_after_max_attempts` still asserts 3 for\nthe idempotent path — the contrast is the regression guard.\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` → 16 passed. `ruff check`\n/ `ruff format --check` / `mypy common/http_retry.py` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"299b9b66116282030919a321b81a6e90d9cc7c5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/299b9b66116282030919a321b81a6e90d9cc7c5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMZSsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd6AQAE+1r1R5sZ7sNR8TssiVMjCM\nUI2i/EmxVlAHXlJ+s4AyxztXBQjaAJ/FMnlYEGfk2IelSxaLcU688w8GFleTPHsH\nS5qAITXOeATmFIRwVSqS4CmUnqxEyAmY3pmvCypn+NaCLx2AVGws9iTtyFIyS2iu\nNXDM14wzq2fn4zofje3rfs82GPSECozUheKObfnYXgkMcuu6zf/ocnpcg5VIrc2w\nosK/HXF44Rob/lomSN5o8KosIhYxd8ermvqbU2NMu5LA2KJukBThRWIncZqrn1Dk\nikCnik9CYPuUc69JhbhtpzeVQjLwznfPdqWVdLbneF2Keo+584O1WLqm+dNxwQbD\nM5fVX8DI4LrQA275SXgM1s55nbnwOaKuQxFltSXuYZmphOg/AShruS4dxgHh+Jt0\nnhCAXXq8+6LBejPR7H8KJIw1Ut4o4IGPzStOWMvEv1qu3mewCdgptbLXKjYgN3KG\nAPlGB8jqZBtzARJ1wR39Gxa5hqyf5qsmFdHZ7G0I74nVU5bx3NOeYpXo9Q6Qz4M2\nD2BpujmFlM2+GL2CXH3QStaeLr9PK9HDv6e0ujPZHaTYFIF9T6vDoF1TwTrEBiM9\nEgDm58dta2VTtgaBqoyWOIks5yIf0r1kG51LspJbULTBaboN1xxKb+As5KShfwxN\nQYZX6QXm1O9qiv6paCym\n=I5eL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 299b9b66116282030919a321b81a6e90d9cc7c5c\nparent 2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781634220 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781634220 +0300\n\nfix(http-retry): widen connection-phase retry to ride out storage cold starts (#406)\n\n## Prod signal (2026-06-16)\n\nA steady trickle of `httpx.ConnectTimeout` reached\n`prod-memclaw-core-api` across **every** core-api → core-storage-api\npath — Pub/Sub enrichment (`pubsub handler raised; nacking for\nredelivery`), entity extraction, contradiction detection, and audit\nflush. All are storage-api connect timeouts during cold starts /\ninstance recycles.\n\nThe current policy is 3 attempts (~0.6s of backoff). That is too short\nto ride out a Cloud Run cold start, so a transient connect blip surfaces\nas a handler failure — and on the Pub/Sub path it triggers a nack →\nimmediate-redelivery storm (`common/events/pubsub.py` nacks with\n`ack_deadline=0`).\n\n## Change\n\nWiden **only** the connection-phase path (`with_connect_phase_retry`) to\n`CONNECT_PHASE_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5`.\n\nWhy only that path: `ConnectTimeout` / `ConnectError` / `PoolTimeout`\nare raised *before* the request is sent, and against an instance that\nisn't accepting connections yet — so retrying them:\n- cannot double-insert (request provably never sent), and\n- adds **zero load to a healthy server** (the connection never lands),\nso extra attempts just wait out the cold start.\n\nThe idempotent path (`with_retry`, which also retries `ReadTimeout`/5xx)\n**stays at 3 attempts** so a genuine 5xx storm isn't amplified by extra\nload against a struggling server.\n\nAlso:\n- `RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_S = 2.0` caps a single backoff sleep so the higher\nattempt count stays bounded.\n- Factored the capped + jittered delay into a small `_backoff_delay()`\nhelper (dedups the two call sites).\n\nThis **complements, not replaces**, keeping storage-api warm (Cloud Run\nmin-instances) — the durable fix for the cold starts themselves.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_post_gives_up_after_max_attempts_on_connect_timeout` now asserts\n5 attempts for the connect-phase path;\n`test_get_retries_then_gives_up_after_max_attempts` still asserts 3 for\nthe idempotent path — the contrast is the regression guard.\n- `pytest tests/test_storage_client_retry.py` → 16 passed. `ruff check`\n/ `ruff format --check` / `mypy common/http_retry.py` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T18:23:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5bbede7481032397ec50400f166f12f132b5fc4a/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4"}]},{"sha":"2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJhMjJmODhhZTFkNzQzMTM2MjJjODNmMjhkZDlhYzY4NDlkMmFmZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-16T16:09:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:09:14Z"},"message":"fix(entity-linking): backfill embeddings via Core table, not ORM bulk-by-PK (#405)\n\n## Prod incident\n\nThe nightly `entity_linking_full` pipeline's\n**`backfill_entity_embeddings`** step has been failing in prod (observed\n2026-06-16, ~6 occurrences/night, all in the 02:00–02:11 UTC cron\nwindow) with:\n\n```\nentity_linking_full.backfill_entity_embeddings: FAILED — No primary key value supplied\nfor column(s) entities.id; per-row ORM Bulk UPDATE by Primary Key requires that records\ncontain primary key values\n```\n\nEffect: entity `name_embedding`s are silently **not** backfilled for\naffected tenants, and the runner `break`s the rest of that org's linking\nrun for the night.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`session.execute(update(Entity), [param dicts])` (an **ORM-mapped**\nclass + an executemany param list) routes to SQLAlchemy's *\"ORM Bulk\nUPDATE by Primary Key\"*, which requires every param dict to carry the PK\ncolumn `id`. Our dicts key the PK off a custom `eid` bindparam in the\n`WHERE` clause, so the bulk-by-PK machinery finds no `id` and raises.\n\nThe earlier `synchronize_session=False` change (prod 2026-06-13) only\nsilenced a *different* error on the same ORM path — it masked this\nsecond failure mode rather than removing the ORM bulk-update path.\n\nThis is the same `entity_linking_full` family as the prior\n`discover_cross_links` (#337) and `infer_relations` (#341) fixes.\n\n## Fix\n\nTarget the **Core table** `update(Entity.__table__)` instead of the\nORM-mapped `Entity`. That is a plain Core executemany `UPDATE` which\nhonours the custom `eid`/`emb` bindparams and has **no** ORM bulk-by-PK\nor session-synchronisation behaviour at all. The\n`.execution_options(synchronize_session=False)` is removed (irrelevant\non a Core statement).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced against **SQLAlchemy 2.0.49**: the ORM form\n(`update(Entity)` + executemany) raises the exact prod\n`InvalidRequestError`; the Core form (`update(Entity.__table__)`)\nsucceeds.\n- The regression test now asserts the statement is a Core `UPDATE` (no\nORM compile plugin) — the precise property that prevents the bulk-by-PK\npath — instead of the now-removed `synchronize_session` option.\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/` → 88 passed. `ruff check` / `ruff format\n--check` / `mypy` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a23c2c0bab0073206e3a34c04e3de22e99923e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1a23c2c0bab0073206e3a34c04e3de22e99923e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXUqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKCkQAHh1NOKh+qbn9WCLutMUUcDY\nqdbmy292PirmQHoQt/HUrqyZLFrsW/mED5ss16u9r2VI727gT2Gy04p2IcxuLu+t\nF0IsygC4AzBbOXPF7WWN2bSoi2PgkKMFP2OY6YM1sSGEGFNSRyFySaBAb090NXqc\ne07rg0xChKnnlo3GWdYtmJVOvK1hgm9nZQAHpLEBTvQxhzvt1G66mgLpNS3ZII9l\nkxNlEJMMNUOiubSNbkSe9q4hFzsArsN06S05LV6rBGos2JbDBDqa5JCCZeZHcgGN\nZ+TUilcIYr/aeNtWYz7H0G3YGU7NpIiecJ5bnsiFuJ41U1Rhn68rNadYPvpNUe+9\nA/Ss10xzQAS87lq+Agzt4i5bNuVX/l640BIGXSHt2uqXIKgmCncVf96w9HWxs4Dw\nv50GrjgNj7HZ5FRXqqXuVyh3saV3SmOlb92gT3zgQ3JQiAwoxx21gnCNTIhLUkvW\nRggvtpC99G/fRLNs+i4dqczLspLkKhFfo3i2VcZ4ZaHB0OTjH3RGRZH20gikX4A3\nC+GqZQ6C6IIGf3kwZ9nBgx3ZL9BI9pbo4PVw8oLysHI1R+98Jj6h9sDOk5xkDIi6\n7YgUr2lbPNEZyhjMAQJ2LuxLAEauUfSie4AMtP/PrgKJ/f4nkMrIvVZdN4fxE2bz\nQfQTjC1KDMCgjacPAUnm\n=/zHj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1a23c2c0bab0073206e3a34c04e3de22e99923e6\nparent ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781626154 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781626154 +0300\n\nfix(entity-linking): backfill embeddings via Core table, not ORM bulk-by-PK (#405)\n\n## Prod incident\n\nThe nightly `entity_linking_full` pipeline's\n**`backfill_entity_embeddings`** step has been failing in prod (observed\n2026-06-16, ~6 occurrences/night, all in the 02:00–02:11 UTC cron\nwindow) with:\n\n```\nentity_linking_full.backfill_entity_embeddings: FAILED — No primary key value supplied\nfor column(s) entities.id; per-row ORM Bulk UPDATE by Primary Key requires that records\ncontain primary key values\n```\n\nEffect: entity `name_embedding`s are silently **not** backfilled for\naffected tenants, and the runner `break`s the rest of that org's linking\nrun for the night.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`session.execute(update(Entity), [param dicts])` (an **ORM-mapped**\nclass + an executemany param list) routes to SQLAlchemy's *\"ORM Bulk\nUPDATE by Primary Key\"*, which requires every param dict to carry the PK\ncolumn `id`. Our dicts key the PK off a custom `eid` bindparam in the\n`WHERE` clause, so the bulk-by-PK machinery finds no `id` and raises.\n\nThe earlier `synchronize_session=False` change (prod 2026-06-13) only\nsilenced a *different* error on the same ORM path — it masked this\nsecond failure mode rather than removing the ORM bulk-update path.\n\nThis is the same `entity_linking_full` family as the prior\n`discover_cross_links` (#337) and `infer_relations` (#341) fixes.\n\n## Fix\n\nTarget the **Core table** `update(Entity.__table__)` instead of the\nORM-mapped `Entity`. That is a plain Core executemany `UPDATE` which\nhonours the custom `eid`/`emb` bindparams and has **no** ORM bulk-by-PK\nor session-synchronisation behaviour at all. The\n`.execution_options(synchronize_session=False)` is removed (irrelevant\non a Core statement).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced against **SQLAlchemy 2.0.49**: the ORM form\n(`update(Entity)` + executemany) raises the exact prod\n`InvalidRequestError`; the Core form (`update(Entity.__table__)`)\nsucceeds.\n- The regression test now asserts the statement is a Core `UPDATE` (no\nORM compile plugin) — the precise property that prevents the bulk-by-PK\npath — instead of the now-removed `synchronize_session` option.\n- `pytest tests/pipeline/` → 88 passed. `ruff check` / `ruff format\n--check` / `mypy` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T16:09:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2a22f88ae1d74313622c83f28dd9ac6849d2aff4/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604"}]},{"sha":"ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJhOTRhNTRiMmFkZTg2NDFmYTU4Y2JmNDQ3ZGIyNzU5Y2M1NTA2MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-16T14:00:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T14:00:04Z"},"message":"fix(prompts): stop brace-escaping content before str.format (#404)\n\n## The bug\n`enrich_memory` (`common/enrichment/service.py`), `_generate_rule`\n(`evolve_service.py`), and `synthesize_insights` (`insights_service.py`)\nall pre-escaped content (`{` → `{{`) before passing it as a\n**substitution value** to `str.format()`, with comments claiming an\nun-escaped value would raise `KeyError`.\n\nThat's incorrect. `str.format()` parses only the **template** for\nreplacement fields — a substituted value is inserted **literally** and\nnever re-scanned, so it never raises `KeyError` and never needs\nescaping. The escaping instead **corrupts** any brace-containing content\nbefore the LLM sees it:\n\n```python\n>>> \"{c}\".format(c='{\"a\": 1}')      # substituted value, literal — no error\n'{\"a\": 1}'\n>>> \"{c}\".format(c='{{\"a\": 1}}')    # escaped form is inserted as-is → corrupted\n'{{\"a\": 1}}'\n```\n\nSo JSON, code, regex, templates, and dict reprs (insights cluster mode)\nreached the enrichment/rule/insight LLM with doubled braces — degrading\nexactly the technical/business content these paths handle.\n\n## The fix\nPass `content` / `outcome` / `memories` directly to `.format()` at all\nthree sites and correct the misleading comments. The evolve\n`_sanitize_content(outcome, max_len=2000)` size cap is preserved — only\nthe escaping is removed.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_enrich_memory_prompt_preserves_braces` — exercises\n`enrich_memory` with a mocked provider and asserts brace-containing\ncontent reaches the prompt **verbatim** (fails on the old escaping).\n- Brace-preservation invariants for the evolve\n(`_RULE_GENERATION_PROMPT`) and insights (`_PROMPT_DISPATCH`) templates.\n- Verified empirically; `ruff check` + `format --check` + `mypy` clean;\nenrichment suites green (no regression).\n\n## Context\nSame class of bug was just fixed in\n`core_api/services/business_classifier.py` in #403 (the new pre-gate\nclassifier was modeled on `enrich_memory`); this PR fixes the\npre-existing occurrences in the enrichment / evolve / insights paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da912437a624096ed8458a2a2df7ebade4071646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/da912437a624096ed8458a2a2df7ebade4071646"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMVbkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP58QAFe5b7eN52dlfVNePdVE8RXU\ntCplXSOVWjT7Kq2kRtaddUB9EjBWtR4ifVKbTc5KStlndilmBd6LIfQT4XXUse4m\nCPKaIsRav0Hn8ONx6yOHaEQjaoIETR6Gkz7Uq0Rb5fRED0k4SS0+knl5/06lvwSQ\nsmoW/VlCB0isuZtRGMKalm+Ryj04UpwQRnlewTgi0OEkX8mTxdTjqXsZ3UyW3IkF\nDLFLuhK+3iS5mNCjUCtwlfdJ3fgrBSHTzlbguk0pvxzy/uP5C85OBeGHZc/T8FR7\nQZ2TcC6HtA7Kzrbr+mJjkFrJC0oxVoigInhnsEdGcopO6WhlKJogJ2EFcZxgTPX6\naUOLAH7VgNAI+Mh+AkxA8jAk/toXwevqZeQoUUPzHjLr+nozRsISSyZ5GximHJCT\ntai7mEp6DUTMorWlADae0Rg55FDQpah84qdP4ElI6FJQzSY+GVspb9rVwCR2IYvR\nDcWk4O6ZCvuRV47HCAJDjParrhmpIe2B3TbUDwnbDeiFcUuZumbXRP5dcYRLYgFw\nAv2zL5PoUqE3d0ZEY5Hvibvy8N+ZVioGJUrnf1+IagkzckeisQ59iCjLY0OjdufQ\nHDnCi0ZYHATEhkMUtmKIko5zKHjqTSX+sYkkz+N4QrzeWjIKK+LfypNpcIViEN5J\nZHN7JqReaP8iD3LPdul0\n=YQ01\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da912437a624096ed8458a2a2df7ebade4071646\nparent 095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781618404 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781618404 +0300\n\nfix(prompts): stop brace-escaping content before str.format (#404)\n\n## The bug\n`enrich_memory` (`common/enrichment/service.py`), `_generate_rule`\n(`evolve_service.py`), and `synthesize_insights` (`insights_service.py`)\nall pre-escaped content (`{` → `{{`) before passing it as a\n**substitution value** to `str.format()`, with comments claiming an\nun-escaped value would raise `KeyError`.\n\nThat's incorrect. `str.format()` parses only the **template** for\nreplacement fields — a substituted value is inserted **literally** and\nnever re-scanned, so it never raises `KeyError` and never needs\nescaping. The escaping instead **corrupts** any brace-containing content\nbefore the LLM sees it:\n\n```python\n>>> \"{c}\".format(c='{\"a\": 1}')      # substituted value, literal — no error\n'{\"a\": 1}'\n>>> \"{c}\".format(c='{{\"a\": 1}}')    # escaped form is inserted as-is → corrupted\n'{{\"a\": 1}}'\n```\n\nSo JSON, code, regex, templates, and dict reprs (insights cluster mode)\nreached the enrichment/rule/insight LLM with doubled braces — degrading\nexactly the technical/business content these paths handle.\n\n## The fix\nPass `content` / `outcome` / `memories` directly to `.format()` at all\nthree sites and correct the misleading comments. The evolve\n`_sanitize_content(outcome, max_len=2000)` size cap is preserved — only\nthe escaping is removed.\n\n## Tests\n- `test_enrich_memory_prompt_preserves_braces` — exercises\n`enrich_memory` with a mocked provider and asserts brace-containing\ncontent reaches the prompt **verbatim** (fails on the old escaping).\n- Brace-preservation invariants for the evolve\n(`_RULE_GENERATION_PROMPT`) and insights (`_PROMPT_DISPATCH`) templates.\n- Verified empirically; `ruff check` + `format --check` + `mypy` clean;\nenrichment suites green (no regression).\n\n## Context\nSame class of bug was just fixed in\n`core_api/services/business_classifier.py` in #403 (the new pre-gate\nclassifier was modeled on `enrich_memory`); this PR fixes the\npre-existing occurrences in the enrichment / evolve / insights paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T14:00:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba94a54b2ade8641fa58cbf447db2759cc550604/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6"}]},{"sha":"095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA5NWMzNjA0M2ViZWViMWMxM2U3Y2RlNzk4OTViZmRhNmFhMzI0ZjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-16T13:37:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T13:37:53Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): fast business/personal pre-gate before enrichment (opt-in) (#403)\n\nImplements the approved design (`DESIGN-business-personal-pregate.md`) —\n**Design A (additive), disabled by default.**\n\n## What it does\nAdds an optional **fast business-vs-personal go/no-go** at the front of\nthe write pipeline — after the deterministic PII scan, **before**\nenrichment, embedding, and the (already-deferred) entity extraction. On\na confident **`personal`** verdict when the tenant's disposition is\n**`drop`**, the write is rejected with `422` *before* any of that work\nruns and before a row is written.\n\n## Highlights\n- **New step `BusinessPersonalPregate`**, wired into the **strong +\nfast** write pipelines (after `GovernanceScanContent`, before\n`ParallelEmbedEnrich`); correctly absent from STM / enrichment-only.\n- **Its own provider/model** (via `common.llm` `call_with_fallback`), so\nthe signal is **independent of the enrichment provider** — it survives\n`ENTITY_EXTRACTION_PROVIDER=none` (the green-local/red-CI blind spot).\n- **Disabled by default.** New `governance.non_business.pregate`\nsettings (`enabled` / `provider` / `model` / `min_confidence`), all\nopt-in, validated + resolved alongside the existing governance settings.\n**Prod behavior is unchanged until a tenant enables it.**\n- **Truthful audit verb** `nonbusiness_pregate_drop` (nothing persisted\n— distinct from `nonbusiness_drop` which soft-deletes a stored row),\nemitted **before** the raise.\n- **Additive (Design A):** the post-enrichment `GovernanceDecision`\nremains the accurate backstop; `keep_private`/`store` stay there (they\npersist the row, so an early exit saves nothing).\n- **Fail-open:** a `none` provider or any classifier failure never\nblocks a write.\n\n## Open design decisions (per the doc, as approved)\nD1 additive-first · D2 model configurable (defaults to the cheap tier) ·\nD3 drop-only · D4 fail-open default with a `min_confidence` knob · D5\ndefault-off. Graduating to full separation (B) remains a documented\nfollow-up.\n\n## Verification\n- 43 tests green (new `tests/test_business_personal_pregate.py` +\nexisting governance suites — no regression): enablement gating,\ndrop/flow-through, `min_confidence`, **provider-independence + fail-open\nreproduced under `provider=none`**, settings default-off + validation,\nand pipeline wiring.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean; `mypy` clean on touched\nfiles.\n- `/simplify` run before commit (one cleanup applied: removed dead\n`isinstance` guards + a redundant cast in the settings validator).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4e0ad4b32a41de8e0680367f244facc6e647e8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e4e0ad4b32a41de8e0680367f244facc6e647e8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMVGxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyakQACeSZfQwN3quc6Or3eDFmZib\nGg3OBSjtuE9wBhuZ/vAx04/25Kz3k9wCQNYHVieLxtf/uIFDoXXcSgbnUfs8psB1\nKlwuiJ086ydRa4OMlE6Rgs0g4QUcqLpCNFFhYOVTDCb2LckJ3cocsh0ke51fyMLb\nGnLNMkQcKCHsgbi3gwyA5okwYQa4J3pB/EZ/nyYEAb2sdapYwWILiNaUe3AC1T69\njvDfxWIPBvpeP9A+E02xUqnbstNmTs4xcJAvL9vCBA2s9KL0QrU+44Tg8cDDX7rX\nuJ/OE6u+u99HrawBDbkftpEgND6WlL9IxUtGKfbhVD245AVd/631meYyUikp7uKw\ndn2Uf79okG9lNehbCxhMTLa5oi9XX4EyQq9KIGrF64ATwQOWJQhQubkkHJS8OUaT\nUf/Kw59XeK9k8N6GUTTR5hrebYHLpxaA8oul3jW1ZP8DJ+SxSR7vh6KMt8IjS/OQ\nKKPAKU+eHz8HfoqejxHfUkFCtVX8FluLCfQMyjMp1xGduokuPpYTXDfwAUZaBozs\nzxrUE8suIqCVb2u8oLHDasVKmPVi7e746HnTn/mcneZuKV7ViFus/oLAyU9Ke51M\njmyQFP++r66DYZgYZxCUXtSyd3pKsg49d+6KgPZptWYOsOnMziXPDvKQhCgB3fpc\nsOI1CjX55lwNWGdbq/RA\n=Oqiq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e4e0ad4b32a41de8e0680367f244facc6e647e8c\nparent e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781617073 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781617073 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): fast business/personal pre-gate before enrichment (opt-in) (#403)\n\nImplements the approved design (`DESIGN-business-personal-pregate.md`) —\n**Design A (additive), disabled by default.**\n\n## What it does\nAdds an optional **fast business-vs-personal go/no-go** at the front of\nthe write pipeline — after the deterministic PII scan, **before**\nenrichment, embedding, and the (already-deferred) entity extraction. On\na confident **`personal`** verdict when the tenant's disposition is\n**`drop`**, the write is rejected with `422` *before* any of that work\nruns and before a row is written.\n\n## Highlights\n- **New step `BusinessPersonalPregate`**, wired into the **strong +\nfast** write pipelines (after `GovernanceScanContent`, before\n`ParallelEmbedEnrich`); correctly absent from STM / enrichment-only.\n- **Its own provider/model** (via `common.llm` `call_with_fallback`), so\nthe signal is **independent of the enrichment provider** — it survives\n`ENTITY_EXTRACTION_PROVIDER=none` (the green-local/red-CI blind spot).\n- **Disabled by default.** New `governance.non_business.pregate`\nsettings (`enabled` / `provider` / `model` / `min_confidence`), all\nopt-in, validated + resolved alongside the existing governance settings.\n**Prod behavior is unchanged until a tenant enables it.**\n- **Truthful audit verb** `nonbusiness_pregate_drop` (nothing persisted\n— distinct from `nonbusiness_drop` which soft-deletes a stored row),\nemitted **before** the raise.\n- **Additive (Design A):** the post-enrichment `GovernanceDecision`\nremains the accurate backstop; `keep_private`/`store` stay there (they\npersist the row, so an early exit saves nothing).\n- **Fail-open:** a `none` provider or any classifier failure never\nblocks a write.\n\n## Open design decisions (per the doc, as approved)\nD1 additive-first · D2 model configurable (defaults to the cheap tier) ·\nD3 drop-only · D4 fail-open default with a `min_confidence` knob · D5\ndefault-off. Graduating to full separation (B) remains a documented\nfollow-up.\n\n## Verification\n- 43 tests green (new `tests/test_business_personal_pregate.py` +\nexisting governance suites — no regression): enablement gating,\ndrop/flow-through, `min_confidence`, **provider-independence + fail-open\nreproduced under `provider=none`**, settings default-off + validation,\nand pipeline wiring.\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean; `mypy` clean on touched\nfiles.\n- `/simplify` run before commit (one cleanup applied: removed dead\n`isinstance` guards + a redundant cast in the settings validator).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T13:37:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/095c36043ebeeb1c13e7cde79895bfda6aa324f6/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af"}]},{"sha":"e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU3ZjZmMWM2ZDMyYjIxOGRmYWM3MTg0M2VmZTkwNmVlOGQwMzE2YWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T21:10:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T21:10:00Z"},"message":"test(governance): comprehensive end-to-end use-case tests for the two gates (#402)\n\n## What\n\nComprehensive **end-to-end use-case tests** for the two\ningestion-boundary governance gates (PII/PCI/secret +\nbusiness-vs-personal) shipped in #397/#398.\n\n## Why\n\nThe gates shipped with solid **step-level**, config, pattern, and\nremediation **unit** tests — but *nothing drove a real memory write\nthrough the pipeline and inspected the stored row + audit log*. The\noriginal HTTP end-to-end test was deliberately dropped as flaky (it\ndepended on settings-cache propagation across the test/app process\nboundary). That left three places where real behavior diverges from the\nunit tests **untested end-to-end**: the fast-mode consumer path (the\n*default* write mode), the mask-vs-content-hash ordering, and the bulk\ngate (a separate inline implementation).\n\nThis restores that layer **without the flakiness** by driving the\npipeline **in-process** (`create_memory` / `create_memories_bulk`) —\nsingle process, single module identity, so the governance config the\ntest seeds is exactly what the pipeline reads. Config is seeded via\n`update_settings` + an autouse `_settings_cache.clear()`; the\nstrong-mode LLM signal is supplied by injecting a fixed\n`EnrichmentResult` (the `fake` providers give `llm_ms=0` → fail-closed\notherwise).\n\nThese tests also codify the staging acceptance criteria (AC1–AC4) as\nrepeatable automated checks.\n\n## Coverage added (29 tests)\n\n**`tests/test_governance_e2e.py`** — real writes:\n- **Deterministic PII gate**: `mask` stores the *redacted* content\n(proves mask-before-hash), `drop` rejects (422) + persists nothing,\n`flag` annotates metadata; category toggle; disabled no-op; mask across\n**fast + strong** modes — each asserting the stored outcome, the\n`audit_log` action + `write_mode`, PII-safe detail, and\n`audit_verify_chain` validity.\n- **LLM-signal + business/personal gate** (strong): personal →\n`keep_private` / `drop` / `store`, business flows through,\n`contains_pii` → drop (`source=llm`), **both gates on one memory**.\n- **Bulk gate** (`create_memories_bulk`): per-item `drop` / `mask` /\n`flag`, asserting the stored row + `write_mode=\"bulk\"` audit.\n\n**`tests/test_governance_consumer.py`** — fast-mode (default)\nenforcement wiring: `handle_memory_enriched` →\n`remediate_after_enrichment`, pinning the **drop →\nack-and-skip-detection** branch and the `keep_private` visibility\nupdate.\n\n**`tests/test_governance_patterns.py`** — detection-breadth gaps: UK\nNINO / US ITIN / Spain DNI, SSN invalid-range exclusions,\nAnthropic/OpenAI key prefixes, generic-secret **group-1 masking** (field\nname preserved), empty input.\n\n## Testing\n\n`tests/test_governance_*` — **81 passed** on the migrated osstest DB;\nruff check + format clean. Per-test isolation uses a unique\n`test-tenant-gov-<uuid>` (conftest auto-cleans `test-tenant-%`), so no\ncross-test bleed via committed rows, the audit chain, or the settings\ncache.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b7443d488573e6b41474413356fc40fb6af1b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4b7443d488573e6b41474413356fc40fb6af1b01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e7f6f1c6d32b218dfac71843efe906ee8d0316af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMGooCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKkEQACp87CLaiLoEA/PzUGWmhugb\nfbceBV9yFmDaa9zByNMcdj//wraKPDBX/XeJ72t7X9+dMteL4v/WzmCe/ktX4pwE\nhGBzKmUB0PcPBIK2Y1+yr1NCSmx1VRqYYY1MhEUB678zNQ1Sa6jeKysPA2g7GQHK\n5pISYBHfxGYmxltpbdRPOGMB950+7P4epgZKd66zXzbGrUafVjfq8enxZ3GKv/rc\nfEB5GQPBZTayT+ggr/YC+s2UT/45Gx+BD8HAPkcOF/midC4I6JJi3thPbUf1fGNc\n9LFdd6Kkswg+ZnI5dbTrVubBbDnWmnRf2jW2UhfND+XLVxbaIImTp7YbQrCDJz7n\nnFwmHW3sL+rRHUDmtEoPZarlIWD4Li+Vn55U26Vzk8KuM7thfWHSwXIaaUTRrlQ/\nvBO7XXSrAtV7vDRfxWMnXbmkr9nc9LP/WACbl5ZgE/12YjoX1zdRwMqkeA7rAsPq\nKh30LkC4LlPzvp76rRzKoyVYrXzj/ijc+VoRwZYW6aWwuw0xWjyR+jzTrSBtzdP9\npZRYgZgCcn1DwSV0oOi5Mx1k349uRvJdkzWEHr9kP7jVC4duArNGSJkq77GFEuD2\njgfmOdouKCL19/ghkNf961OC+tGrMrnDbwNwAJYU5E1i4XOpWhdpBWf0cDtgngz4\nrCClQP82YXY20+BLTZws\n=q6T8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4b7443d488573e6b41474413356fc40fb6af1b01\nparent baaa493cdc8a2bf71d031b0f457844d389c8f6c4\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781557800 +0300\ncommitter