7630324222956eb9d83fc4b9))\n* **core-api:** document the redis&lt;9 cap rationale (review follow-up)\n([#395](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/395))\n([cd5420c](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d))\n* lead Quick Start with a no-key, no-signup local quickstart\n([#348](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/348))\n([91ee613](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a))\n* README write-response field names match payload\n([#361](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/361))\n([2ecc098](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f))\n\n\n### Code Refactoring\n\n* **api:** unify evolve/insights caller-identity resolution; close F-7\ntail (§2) ([#400](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/400))\n([f4af240](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.10.1</summary>\n\n##\n[2.10.1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.10.0...plugin-v2.10.1)\n(2026-06-15)\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **plugin:** send X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header on bulk memory writes\n([#355](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/355))\n([a4515ed](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T14:35:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c8dccbe0e0c7d0cf26195825a24389e537537b7c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c8dccbe0e0c7d0cf26195825a24389e537537b7c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c8dccbe0e0c7d0cf26195825a24389e537537b7c/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4"}]},{"sha":"f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY0YWYyNDA5MTcwNjFiYzU2OGM4MTc3ZWE5ZmNiOGRiMDA0MDM2YTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T14:30:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T14:30:40Z"},"message":"refactor(api): unify evolve/insights caller-identity resolution; close F-7 tail (§2) (#400)\n\n## Summary (addendum §2)\n\n`routes/evolve.py` and `routes/insights.py` carried a **byte-identical,\ncopy-pasted** caller-identity + trust-gate block, each **hardcoding the\n`\"mcp-agent\"` literal** instead of the shared `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID`. The\nduplication had already drifted: the standalone-operator bypass (F-7,\n#354) was added to **keystones only**, so a bare standalone operator\nstill **403'd on evolve/insights**.\n\n## Change\nExtract the logic into\n**`services/caller_identity.resolve_caller_and_gate`**, used by both\nroutes:\n- precedence: verified `auth.agent_id` > `body.agent_id` >\n`DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` (kills the two hardcoded literals);\n- warn-on-mismatch, then the trust gate (`not_found → 403`);\n- skip the gate for **admins** and the **unidentified standalone\noperator** (`IS_STANDALONE` + no asserted identity), mirroring\n`keystones._is_standalone_admin` and `routes/memories`.\n\n## Behavior change (standalone only)\n`POST /evolve/report` and `POST /insights/generate` with **no\n`agent_id`** no longer 403 on a fresh standalone install — they proceed,\nattributing the outcome/insight to the reserved `mcp-agent` identity,\nmatching `memories` (#339) and `keystones` (#354).\n\n**Everything else is byte-for-byte unchanged:** non-standalone / gateway\n/ admin / identity-asserted paths still gate exactly as before\n(unregistered callers still 403, with the identical message). Verified\nearlier with a full case-analysis.\n\n## Deliberately scoped\n- **keystones is NOT folded in** (added a note in its docstring):\ngovernance writes must not fall back to a *registerable* identity (the\nnever-registered `rest-admin` sentinel forces explicit identity on the\ngateway), and keystones needs stricter anti-spoof handling (X-Agent-ID\nmismatch rejection + verified-floor bump).\n- **MCP is already consistent** — every tool shares the\n`agent_id=\"mcp-agent\"` param default; the divergence was REST-only.\n- No single all-routes resolver (the report's headline) — it would\nweaken governance or bloat the helper with reject/warn + sentinel flags.\n\n## Tests / validation\n- New `tests/test_caller_identity.py`: standalone bypass, admin bypass,\nasserted-unregistered → 403, verified-registered → pass (4 pass\nlocally).\n- `ruff check` (incl. F401) + `ruff format` + `py_compile` clean; no\ncircular import; no stray `require_trust`/`logger` left in the routes.\n- No test asserts `\"rest-admin\"` or the evolve/insights 403 message; the\nmessage is preserved verbatim.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"137e86f936c4bf9d302d35cd81d1d891b8bf0186","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/137e86f936c4bf9d302d35cd81d1d891b8bf0186"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMAyQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMgAQADU0UtvZkH5z6xdt/UZxvJuj\nY6rOphqKX2qiuJIhhdvj3jOtH3jx1lyFE20NAslbTT6FFAzTUA+y03l+aGZ0k+w9\nr9wcHQRaj14JCYcdzvCkwI0V02thUtJfqA+CORNQ2Ad692oOcNBIJL3DBSfyHj3E\n6+BQ5S98C3nRofI/4gmkydDfoU8XMxmv0cS0c+UdwMMO9waVFPTFIz8veFaCd5WU\nZ4VBN53CqZaXcDYUAcfWNqoWuDCF2bgjlXkj+hNxwDgUcAhfB2RGz9hCjv2IQsoQ\nI6yFnxq/pAU3CTpvb/ptbArj8aT6Omfv2xQTl3lYoaopfXvAjnct7ktsR17Cgt4c\nMTba1yLaW+OOwt0eqtDEchZjibrtdpAnsx7wjpLtK2Jma19MmRGreS3XrMiOmyuc\nFRBkAoMnberUs9v6O5uP7SXckd0FGJqpVKENDOiFnf48vUPlRhEApl/EbALOXZBP\njm6DjMEQYvg3Rrg82KkQ+DrX9H2GUDqGeKhdNIOwre3HzpujajJOtZfvgT4shKMy\nQ4+pSPG4kXKIkop3DNr7xVtTh46eMYcVTUphFcRegxVpHfR119FFLuYYKRx6v8Aj\nfqZaQyCqoqwYz3yTa7k9KhHVcHUNJpBe0XENI3BjoTrI//s/SvWFk/uI5llizelv\nNcDiym/nujV47i+tNyYi\n=l+cO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 137e86f936c4bf9d302d35cd81d1d891b8bf0186\nparent b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781533840 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781533840 +0300\n\nrefactor(api): unify evolve/insights caller-identity resolution; close F-7 tail (§2) (#400)\n\n## Summary (addendum §2)\n\n`routes/evolve.py` and `routes/insights.py` carried a **byte-identical,\ncopy-pasted** caller-identity + trust-gate block, each **hardcoding the\n`\"mcp-agent\"` literal** instead of the shared `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID`. The\nduplication had already drifted: the standalone-operator bypass (F-7,\n#354) was added to **keystones only**, so a bare standalone operator\nstill **403'd on evolve/insights**.\n\n## Change\nExtract the logic into\n**`services/caller_identity.resolve_caller_and_gate`**, used by both\nroutes:\n- precedence: verified `auth.agent_id` > `body.agent_id` >\n`DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` (kills the two hardcoded literals);\n- warn-on-mismatch, then the trust gate (`not_found → 403`);\n- skip the gate for **admins** and the **unidentified standalone\noperator** (`IS_STANDALONE` + no asserted identity), mirroring\n`keystones._is_standalone_admin` and `routes/memories`.\n\n## Behavior change (standalone only)\n`POST /evolve/report` and `POST /insights/generate` with **no\n`agent_id`** no longer 403 on a fresh standalone install — they proceed,\nattributing the outcome/insight to the reserved `mcp-agent` identity,\nmatching `memories` (#339) and `keystones` (#354).\n\n**Everything else is byte-for-byte unchanged:** non-standalone / gateway\n/ admin / identity-asserted paths still gate exactly as before\n(unregistered callers still 403, with the identical message). Verified\nearlier with a full case-analysis.\n\n## Deliberately scoped\n- **keystones is NOT folded in** (added a note in its docstring):\ngovernance writes must not fall back to a *registerable* identity (the\nnever-registered `rest-admin` sentinel forces explicit identity on the\ngateway), and keystones needs stricter anti-spoof handling (X-Agent-ID\nmismatch rejection + verified-floor bump).\n- **MCP is already consistent** — every tool shares the\n`agent_id=\"mcp-agent\"` param default; the divergence was REST-only.\n- No single all-routes resolver (the report's headline) — it would\nweaken governance or bloat the helper with reject/warn + sentinel flags.\n\n## Tests / validation\n- New `tests/test_caller_identity.py`: standalone bypass, admin bypass,\nasserted-unregistered → 403, verified-registered → pass (4 pass\nlocally).\n- `ruff check` (incl. F401) + `ruff format` + `py_compile` clean; no\ncircular import; no stray `require_trust`/`logger` left in the routes.\n- No test asserts `\"rest-admin\"` or the evolve/insights 403 message; the\nmessage is preserved verbatim.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T14:30:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f4af240917061bc568c8177ea9fcb8db004036a4/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b"}]},{"sha":"b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI2OTZhMjBhMTczZDI1ZGEyNDk1MzgwOGM0OTM0ZjVlNWE5NDEwOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T13:54:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T13:54:25Z"},"message":"test(core-worker): fix invalid memory_type fixture in enrich consumer test (#399)\n\n## What & why\n\n\n`core-worker/tests/test_consumer_enrich.py::test_enrichment_pending_cleared_even_with_heuristic_fallback`\nconstructs `EnrichmentResult(memory_type=\"generic\", ...)`, but\n**`\"generic\"` is not a valid `MemoryType`** (valid: fact, episode,\ndecision, preference, task, semantic, intention, plan, commitment,\naction, outcome, cancellation, rule, insight). Pydantic raises a\n`ValidationError`, so the test has been **failing since v1.0.0**.\n\nIt went unnoticed because **no GitHub Actions workflow runs\n`core-worker/tests/`** — main CI only runs the top-level `tests/`.\n\n## Fix\n\nChange `memory_type=\"generic\"` → `\"fact\"` so the test exercises its\nintended path (heuristic fallback: `llm_ms=0` → the always-write\nmetadata fields skip, and `enrichment_pending` is still cleared). The\nwhole file now passes **20/20**.\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n\nWorth gating `core-worker/tests/` in a CI workflow so this suite can't\nsilently rot again. Left out here to keep this a focused one-line fix —\nwiring the job up may surface other latent failures in that suite that\ndeserve their own triage.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ad2101589ecbfc11e1095031b1d6915f351c808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9ad2101589ecbfc11e1095031b1d6915f351c808"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMAQRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl9UQAA9aAK9zxOF1W9Jc7HWYMjIB\nZ8HfL9S+1Bs60FZtBGhXSrUAXE1kFqw0VJcTKuaHjk6E0xbjk62ZjIv0vDp0yHjT\nXY90n+ApdaqAtFtTRLhjMVj29nsF/u4VjHLSQYmKJ04rD4LlaVsmLmsGD/0pUB+i\n9QJ9Wp8h22giDSoq7vIg3xv7PegpT8cSRiiciXkY7ypFm14xuWkIB94Al7Q5vL29\nVRjZKKdMQnLOc+igC1RkTMxdM0VYjae2cblSBSUQZZA1wCgAJLZiHemHagEhevXF\nAxHcGKmszAzOFOdEiRLrtTH7zfoBQvXqd1nLrUKlhWhR2ohEaQpImfV7gY50W3Dc\ndB/JzW6QX3RG9dpmfgAViuMN1ZCqJnM5xTmX57M1lL0S82LFlCMEUqnDFmALt3Tn\naGeMjsIUaD0m8AqFsC/lqC97jya2kYojkigt6vIFPMkIOwuaXJRxogty4cLC+Nnf\nrhEFj6TVQpC1fgD62+wyWq9Xlq7JMi1HXpAL0fhH+uBr6Wc8/Vk2Xts6vx/JqzfN\nJNFTdarZVswc66ERoJwM3DnlSBZCB9ds2n5nm1enNAHo9xdj4ZQCGaRd82/GSZy/\nEzNflVNLoaxlDYmYYyY8toLzV8byb8RK7d30K79tpeC5PPQJnoxH7OlaGkgMmJvr\n1NXZMpTKWX5xrT5nr/pH\n=OoAI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ad2101589ecbfc11e1095031b1d6915f351c808\nparent 0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781531665 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781531665 +0300\n\ntest(core-worker): fix invalid memory_type fixture in enrich consumer test (#399)\n\n## What & why\n\n\n`core-worker/tests/test_consumer_enrich.py::test_enrichment_pending_cleared_even_with_heuristic_fallback`\nconstructs `EnrichmentResult(memory_type=\"generic\", ...)`, but\n**`\"generic\"` is not a valid `MemoryType`** (valid: fact, episode,\ndecision, preference, task, semantic, intention, plan, commitment,\naction, outcome, cancellation, rule, insight). Pydantic raises a\n`ValidationError`, so the test has been **failing since v1.0.0**.\n\nIt went unnoticed because **no GitHub Actions workflow runs\n`core-worker/tests/`** — main CI only runs the top-level `tests/`.\n\n## Fix\n\nChange `memory_type=\"generic\"` → `\"fact\"` so the test exercises its\nintended path (heuristic fallback: `llm_ms=0` → the always-write\nmetadata fields skip, and `enrichment_pending` is still cleared). The\nwhole file now passes **20/20**.\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n\nWorth gating `core-worker/tests/` in a CI workflow so this suite can't\nsilently rot again. Left out here to keep this a focused one-line fix —\nwiring the job up may surface other latent failures in that suite that\ndeserve their own triage.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T13:54:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b696a20a173d25da24953808c4934f5e5a94108b/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d"}]},{"sha":"0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBkNzVjNTk0ZDdlOWNlNWVmZDQ0MGJlMTIzZTIyMDM4YjNiMDM5NmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T12:43:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T12:43:40Z"},"message":"fix(api): add GET /memories/count (F-16) + document keystone doc_id (F-12) (#396)\n\nTwo Low-severity audit cleanups, bundled.\n\n## F-16 — `GET /memories/count` → confusing 422\nThere was no count route, so `count` was captured by `GET\n/memories/{memory_id}` (`memory_id: UUID`) → `422 \"Input should be a\nvalid UUID, invalid character 'o' at 2\"`.\n\n**Fix:** add a real `GET /memories/count`, declared **before**\n`/memories/{memory_id}` (exactly how `/memories/stats` already is, so\nthe literal segment matches first). Returns `{\"count\": N}` of active\nmemories via the existing `storage_client.count_active(tenant_id,\nfleet_id)`; optional `fleet_id`; same tenant/auth handling as\n`/memories/stats`. Resolves the confusing error **and** adds a useful\noperational primitive (for breakdowns, `/memories/stats` remains).\n\n## F-12 — keystone `doc_id` required but undocumented for REST\n`KeystoneSetRequest.doc_id` is required (kebab-case pattern), documented\nonly in the `memclaw_keystones_set` MCP tool description — so a\nREST-first integrator 422s blind.\n\n**Fix (no contract change — `doc_id` stays required):**\n- Added a REST keystone `POST` example to\n`docs/integration-without-plugin.md` showing `doc_id`, its slug format,\nand the upsert-on-reuse semantics.\n- Made the storage validation error suggest the format. **Kept the\nleading `\"doc_id is required\"` substring** so `test_mcp_keystones.py:94`\nstill matches.\n\n*(Not auto-slugifying `doc_id` from the title — that's a separate\ncontract change.)*\n\n## Tests / validation\n- `test_memory_count` — writes 2 memories to a unique fleet, asserts\n`{\"count\": 2}` (deterministic; also proves `count` resolves as a route,\nnot a UUID).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `py_compile` clean on both\n`core-api` and `core-storage-api`.\n- Confirmed `/memories/count` is declared before\n`/memories/{memory_id}`, and the `\"doc_id is required\"` substring is\npreserved.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e98ea2e2b99d5496c3360d483b54f33bc18b9c1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e98ea2e2b99d5496c3360d483b54f33bc18b9c1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL/N8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATXgQAB+rZ15bX8PdsWxAGg6UPOIB\n+iThvcxVvYWXvAQiDhnsy3e/AdECgtoByLWuGAvyoBEEw/OX/BrOSMggns6WZray\nemAsUtefvSGU8xFTLh+zZaTjLaGMgs6roJBRQU33I4ETMeYC9jJ/q9YkvmhvERA5\nKjic/bctWNxRdVj2KTYW3UPnOi6WMKy7/ZHLCFaU5fYVG92V+fWd6xlN/Jl/AJJK\n6ZCQXVFKAkUSlfsaYrKGAXTrC3DPg9Cyte9fLn1ZHu4qy659B7EFUAFS2t6Xk/u3\n4aUw/Z56oVwYcs57n+kRRJ+b8LlUqTOmJm1+9afBHF6ytdHtxnLqIsEdZ0jkMY8/\nLiM3GLnLoRbH6lRlRTZ06gWhyowEkOfBBPiQSe1MjQ+rjrIPT3WLIHc8XqBn7UoL\nNgRaBMbk8KjGpXKn/zyayI0YZxvpjE2hNemvmaytUSH8JqPAITSWrtUPnHcEutZo\nBDWY9sBZi6s2s84JcNlYQDC4bwxooohQ2ZSc6HmGxWq6bmgpu8cOsgxDHKYxyamB\nhjmUkL53vJ8uZpseoHphOupplSA7TF84ziRNs1GI+zzeQOStSQDVQgU/SDVeXLuc\nz24QwdeMlNCv+AO3MYBdX5i99S+UXp2GbkoWq3YpHGmCsdDMlwMdWxMZI59fC0J8\nhIYpWqnJ+ls+Ee9L0+6U\n=nksn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e98ea2e2b99d5496c3360d483b54f33bc18b9c1d\nparent cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781527420 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781527420 +0300\n\nfix(api): add GET /memories/count (F-16) + document keystone doc_id (F-12) (#396)\n\nTwo Low-severity audit cleanups, bundled.\n\n## F-16 — `GET /memories/count` → confusing 422\nThere was no count route, so `count` was captured by `GET\n/memories/{memory_id}` (`memory_id: UUID`) → `422 \"Input should be a\nvalid UUID, invalid character 'o' at 2\"`.\n\n**Fix:** add a real `GET /memories/count`, declared **before**\n`/memories/{memory_id}` (exactly how `/memories/stats` already is, so\nthe literal segment matches first). Returns `{\"count\": N}` of active\nmemories via the existing `storage_client.count_active(tenant_id,\nfleet_id)`; optional `fleet_id`; same tenant/auth handling as\n`/memories/stats`. Resolves the confusing error **and** adds a useful\noperational primitive (for breakdowns, `/memories/stats` remains).\n\n## F-12 — keystone `doc_id` required but undocumented for REST\n`KeystoneSetRequest.doc_id` is required (kebab-case pattern), documented\nonly in the `memclaw_keystones_set` MCP tool description — so a\nREST-first integrator 422s blind.\n\n**Fix (no contract change — `doc_id` stays required):**\n- Added a REST keystone `POST` example to\n`docs/integration-without-plugin.md` showing `doc_id`, its slug format,\nand the upsert-on-reuse semantics.\n- Made the storage validation error suggest the format. **Kept the\nleading `\"doc_id is required\"` substring** so `test_mcp_keystones.py:94`\nstill matches.\n\n*(Not auto-slugifying `doc_id` from the title — that's a separate\ncontract change.)*\n\n## Tests / validation\n- `test_memory_count` — writes 2 memories to a unique fleet, asserts\n`{\"count\": 2}` (deterministic; also proves `count` resolves as a route,\nnot a UUID).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `py_compile` clean on both\n`core-api` and `core-storage-api`.\n- Confirmed `/memories/count` is declared before\n`/memories/{memory_id}`, and the `\"doc_id is required\"` substring is\npreserved.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T12:43:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0d75c594d7e9ce5efd440be123e22038b3b0396d/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d"}]},{"sha":"cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNkNTQyMGMyNTU1OTRkM2YwZTgwNzk4YjY1ODQ3ZDExZDUxZGIxN2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T08:37:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T08:37:13Z"},"message":"docs(core-api): document the redis<9 cap rationale (review follow-up) (#395)\n\nFollow-up to the [#394 review\nnit](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/394): the redis cap\nwas lifted `<6`→`<9` (lock resolves 8.0.0) as the most significant\nruntime change, with no rationale comment.\n\n**Verified + documented:** core-api's only redis-py surface is\n`redis.asyncio.from_url` (`cache.py`) and\n`r.pipeline(transaction=False)` (`providers/redis_stm.py`) — both stable\nacross the 5→8 jump (not the deprecated/removed entry-points), and\nexercised by the full 3312-test suite under 8.0.0. Comment-only;\nconstraint unchanged. `<9` keeps the next major out as a guardrail.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5822c645faed5c900045711141d2e902dae096c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5822c645faed5c900045711141d2e902dae096c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL7m5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc7QQAJxP266+hgiGB/USoDNFNgvG\nSKye9tjQV4JpmIQ/3ZRPhPVLHfgifeY+807u9skHjoIxbGDbjczJgQFtf+6HPGur\nlvjIq3l+SQWvRLBIRJpvaU27YKnnAXUYClwHU8NbfRXKItEP0cOy1YnY2p3nVJBd\nVm6xBzcc6WMm4XSFP8yRBF9LE+XSYLdrlfWiTEAHbKy3gsycXCDoF0lWI69/wZDL\nvRZ1mQCtN+RN9ez9HWUyWfxQD7dzhnfyENDDYQYu7rMPthnpuOuN2PnLxCFZW6GO\nz75MBMzp0S0UWdWvZzJOnf6JSZWTKzSK7cu66tldhNn3183prm5ggnMTj2Pavz8l\n+9RN2qb71d0Hs1/NTlVULaL+WuBIw68S06MypzN5coaT7l23tm3TqCzNYwhxMnXS\nVQsdN6XdrE3poTUX0eWSPum7wjK2KjJmjCymMnI5eKXQ+qU9A8LzB7ZIff9sNG6S\nzsUl2nr5ptfXbW71xz7+iGWml6F4exwHGe2Z7yjfmICkJo/l1uYfoZhnxGsEZf8E\n/Q2yv54ELt1dNohLCfb9vTyzd1epEDx1bti2Oi9xNJRViafbuuo53HdNVmN/s8f/\nORUQosnQAScnU+7wS0SgbH8GD748j25O95iT1XzBJqfPCbtgUXu+fc9OKNQZ7FX2\nexH2ruNhLOBZVl4JniQO\n=6tzq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5822c645faed5c900045711141d2e902dae096c2\nparent 3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781512633 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781512633 +0300\n\ndocs(core-api): document the redis<9 cap rationale (review follow-up) (#395)\n\nFollow-up to the [#394 review\nnit](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/394): the redis cap\nwas lifted `<6`→`<9` (lock resolves 8.0.0) as the most significant\nruntime change, with no rationale comment.\n\n**Verified + documented:** core-api's only redis-py surface is\n`redis.asyncio.from_url` (`cache.py`) and\n`r.pipeline(transaction=False)` (`providers/redis_stm.py`) — both stable\nacross the 5→8 jump (not the deprecated/removed entry-points), and\nexercised by the full 3312-test suite under 8.0.0. Comment-only;\nconstraint unchanged. `<9` keeps the next major out as a guardrail.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T08:37:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cd5420c255594d3f0e80798b65847d11d51db17d/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422"}]},{"sha":"3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM4NjU2MDBjZTczYTkyNzNlNGZkNWRiNGYwYjIxOGY0NTRiOTk0MjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T08:02:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T08:02:26Z"},"message":"fix(search): return raw cosine in similarity, not the ranking composite (F-14) (#392)\n\n## Summary (audit finding F-14)\n\n`POST /api/v1/search` (and MCP `memclaw_recall` — same pipeline)\nreturned each item's `similarity` as the **multiplicative ranking\ncomposite** (`row.score`), not the raw vector cosine. The composite is\n`base_similarity * freshness * entity/recall/temporal boosts`, which\nroutinely **exceeds 1.0** — an in-window hit saturates\n`temporal_boost≈1.3`, which is exactly the \"every hit is `1.300`\" the\nreport observed. Rank order is fine, but the field is useless for\nclient-side threshold gating.\n\n## Root cause\n`pipeline/steps/search/load_and_serialize.py` filled\n`MemoryOut.similarity` from `row.score` (the composite) instead of\n`row.vec_sim` (the raw 0..1 cosine), even though `vec_sim` is computed\nand carried on the row — and is what the server's own `min_similarity`\ngate (`PostFilterResults`) uses.\n\n## Fix\nSource `similarity` from `row.vec_sim`:\n- 0..1 range → client gating now matches the server's `min_similarity`\nsemantics.\n- **Rank order unchanged** — rows are still ordered by `score` upstream;\nonly the surfaced number changes.\n- FTS-only hits (no vector match) → `similarity: null`, honest and\nalready allowed by the schema.\n\nCovers REST **and** MCP recall (shared `build_search_pipeline` →\n`LoadAndSerialize`).\n\n## Tests\nExtended `test_load_and_serialize_uses_preloaded_entity_links` (its row\nalready has distinct `score=0.85 / blend-similarity=0.8 / vec_sim=0.9`)\nto assert the serialized `similarity == 0.9` — locking it to `vec_sim`,\nnot `score` or the blend. Passes locally.\n\n## Validation\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `py_compile` clean.\n- Confirmed no other test asserts the serialized `similarity` value; the\n`PostFilterResults` test gates on `vec_sim` (unaffected); core-storage\n`test_integration` asserts the *storage-layer* `similarity` blend (a\ndifferent field, unaffected).\n- \"Exactly constant 1.3\" and the v2.5→v2.15 \"regression\" framing are\nruntime/history claims (squashed git history) — not relied on; the\nmis-sourcing is the demonstrable defect.\n\nIntentionally does **not** add a separate `score` field for the\ncomposite (additive schema change across many endpoints) — possible\nfollow-up if ranking-score transparency is wanted.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6388d5a4218981672a701031c01701b9a8bdd90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c6388d5a4218981672a701031c01701b9a8bdd90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL7GSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVG0QAC1l/vaLM51/FJMg0FQJoOhm\njbengWqXaSPbqYgCLtC3ga3L58IdejoOLHJYgVxl/OKY8396BOIhrR+1k/ny2lIX\nQGm8EM4wqN9kW0YXrE4CMrIuW5pd1E0PCCAcIORcLDCkeHGjVUneJzW7G5n7RvC5\nRpLiaoes5xs8R4aMwoArtteMa441TNrpJsuwJF6cuTz3OQ/pHylvAwaRAcKwYv4f\nGGKKjzo72LEqX3QGYBYkAKGoj3PHVaGSPA8srFoSJav3aPn82YsolmtXJccCPLlC\ns4NUiqslEXUadwp0W4svTrjFKZTgpG+i1BJTD0yb/BAG6DyRyiHb8TbllRa0ZVLD\nxH0IHjCUuvW2ezbd5iNk+eHvqBjQ/4kYvkCYdrIJ4vAr25OxgKo41HunYoJ4cthI\n8Zzm4KK3pL7kD7EwNY2498Wu2X0+GoIjV10+0Rv4VtkvQdk67TSWuuwkcAb8WwpN\nMFBYPp553d3/QXWSJzsCdoNCw4qZce8ngJ4jWovFVZasp8hjYcZeGisg8QOr4fcM\nE+61ybHxmDiIMcuEG6zkzk99+7E4yhjBW4UxVPVUzgfOy9BFh+TW8WKK5wllg05j\njJWWtjrtzjI39BDamNxgoqT8OetcLpUoJkFDzyE3OzeGwW0XAFJ+RtFXNMpZP7CB\nKigrF1BCT9VulfXYA2iJ\n=1rrk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c6388d5a4218981672a701031c01701b9a8bdd90\nparent 5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781510546 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781510546 +0300\n\nfix(search): return raw cosine in similarity, not the ranking composite (F-14) (#392)\n\n## Summary (audit finding F-14)\n\n`POST /api/v1/search` (and MCP `memclaw_recall` — same pipeline)\nreturned each item's `similarity` as the **multiplicative ranking\ncomposite** (`row.score`), not the raw vector cosine. The composite is\n`base_similarity * freshness * entity/recall/temporal boosts`, which\nroutinely **exceeds 1.0** — an in-window hit saturates\n`temporal_boost≈1.3`, which is exactly the \"every hit is `1.300`\" the\nreport observed. Rank order is fine, but the field is useless for\nclient-side threshold gating.\n\n## Root cause\n`pipeline/steps/search/load_and_serialize.py` filled\n`MemoryOut.similarity` from `row.score` (the composite) instead of\n`row.vec_sim` (the raw 0..1 cosine), even though `vec_sim` is computed\nand carried on the row — and is what the server's own `min_similarity`\ngate (`PostFilterResults`) uses.\n\n## Fix\nSource `similarity` from `row.vec_sim`:\n- 0..1 range → client gating now matches the server's `min_similarity`\nsemantics.\n- **Rank order unchanged** — rows are still ordered by `score` upstream;\nonly the surfaced number changes.\n- FTS-only hits (no vector match) → `similarity: null`, honest and\nalready allowed by the schema.\n\nCovers REST **and** MCP recall (shared `build_search_pipeline` →\n`LoadAndSerialize`).\n\n## Tests\nExtended `test_load_and_serialize_uses_preloaded_entity_links` (its row\nalready has distinct `score=0.85 / blend-similarity=0.8 / vec_sim=0.9`)\nto assert the serialized `similarity == 0.9` — locking it to `vec_sim`,\nnot `score` or the blend. Passes locally.\n\n## Validation\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` + `py_compile` clean.\n- Confirmed no other test asserts the serialized `similarity` value; the\n`PostFilterResults` test gates on `vec_sim` (unaffected); core-storage\n`test_integration` asserts the *storage-layer* `similarity` blend (a\ndifferent field, unaffected).\n- \"Exactly constant 1.3\" and the v2.5→v2.15 \"regression\" framing are\nruntime/history claims (squashed git history) — not relied on; the\nmis-sourcing is the demonstrable defect.\n\nIntentionally does **not** add a separate `score` field for the\ncomposite (additive schema change across many endpoints) — possible\nfollow-up if ranking-score transparency is wanted.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T08:02:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3865600ce73a9273e4fd5db4f0b218f454b99422/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc"}]},{"sha":"5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVjOTM5Njg0ZjgwMGQxZTViZTYwNTFlMjdkZmFjNDE2ODJjMzgzZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T07:46:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T07:46:48Z"},"message":"build(deps): consolidate all Dependabot bumps — modernize deps across core-* services (#394)\n\n## What\n**One coordinated dependency upgrade that replaces the ~38 open\nDependabot PRs.** Relaxes the blocking upper-bound caps and `uv lock\n--upgrade`s all four `core-*` services to a mutually-consistent modern\nset:\n\n| Package | From → To |\n|---------|-----------|\n| pytest | 8 → **9.1** |\n| pytest-asyncio | 0.26 → **1.4** |\n| pytest-cov | 6 → **7.1** |\n| mypy | 1.x → **2.1** |\n| structlog | 25 → **26** |\n| cachetools | 5 → **7.1** |\n| redis | 5 → **8** |\n| greenlet | 3.4 → **3.5.1** |\n| google-genai | 0.x → **2.8** |\n\n(FastAPI already at 0.137 from #391.)\n\n## Why consolidate instead of merging the individual PRs\nThe individual Dependabot PRs **fail CI** because each moves *one* dep\ninto an **incompatible partial combination** (e.g. pytest-asyncio 1.x\nagainst pytest 8). A single `uv lock --upgrade` resolves a\n**consistent** set — so the same bumps that fail one-by-one all pass\ntogether. It also dedups the overlapping/competing PRs (multiple\ngreenlet/pytest-asyncio/redis PRs) into one resolution.\n\n## Verification (CI-equivalent local run)\nNo code changes were needed — the modern stack is green:\n- **core-api + core-storage-api:** ruff clean · mypy 2.1 **0 errors** ·\n**3312 passed**\n- **core-operations:** ruff/mypy clean · **34 passed**\n- **core-worker:** ruff/mypy clean · 66 passed · **1 failure that is\nPRE-EXISTING and unrelated** — a stale test passing a removed\n`memory_type` enum value (`\"generic\"`); it fails on `main` too\n(verified) and core-worker's suite isn't CI-gated. Tracked separately.\n\ngreenlet cap lifted `<3.5.0`→`<3.6.0` (3.5.1 restored the Linux x86_64\nwheels). Locks stay **frozen + hash-verified** in the Dockerfiles.\n\n## Closes\nSupersedes the open Dependabot PRs (#366–#390 + the stale #5–#157\nbacklog). They'll be closed with a reference here once this merges\n(Dependabot auto-closes the satisfied ones).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc4e9826d0616a20596457cf021065a6d6edacf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/fc4e9826d0616a20596457cf021065a6d6edacf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL63oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1OUQAHHzxaWaP/5oZrOXc61LVbA4\nBiumCv/RxGo32tWET61DgwDKIiL/ay/+vepuThoFB5dQIzRnq10vRwG486C0AFlq\nEbQReTSDRiU5Vxc4pys/878lBn2StIvP/eOswWSAFx7GycxRNehwA1FlV3vNHZ9o\nzcyLOvIOLbD+G1SwwN/9KxGS6qGf5ZCFuXQcuoDRUnwOSz7ndngw0ZuhzUHaC+H5\n6ufVPLbDR/sDQijEVzQnaJ26qTg24lxaSUdGIPw5T0/pKoiaM2Gb9SqWuLyBwLFT\nWriAdT4P1srDKXbija02t5ojqmT9CptH+6Pd5YYJZrHqGrWnKA2z7Rm3e6+0D9BV\ngdH8M9mhwxZ+ULT/Xvxx+aRGv8FdT4asL1bGmc+0dRkWz9loK/79WpuwAHDW+XdO\n35a2YDWoUPpY+Gw3AaepHfAQMAO4GMO4vmG+dXkp3AzLsbICrlWkKRkcB32zdByJ\nbqoF0/ZJKQ587zuM1r3+fhjVa/no0A9bl21SyZrdPR33EMf/N7VBTciS+oNS3R9L\n2bFIEzPj0mDsOsRytBiYYGTokV6h8iDaUi/RsAyAn7oKQ7OGviIsa2F1zilvis3o\nZQ1Inbr/1T9A/VCrjYVBGBzBxUTV3081rBtUnyQ/D8mUINuBVF9vv1icqLZeO2Bj\n8Zw9W21K51Rc44On1nXU\n=H00L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fc4e9826d0616a20596457cf021065a6d6edacf4\nparent c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781509608 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781509608 +0300\n\nbuild(deps): consolidate all Dependabot bumps — modernize deps across core-* services (#394)\n\n## What\n**One coordinated dependency upgrade that replaces the ~38 open\nDependabot PRs.** Relaxes the blocking upper-bound caps and `uv lock\n--upgrade`s all four `core-*` services to a mutually-consistent modern\nset:\n\n| Package | From → To |\n|---------|-----------|\n| pytest | 8 → **9.1** |\n| pytest-asyncio | 0.26 → **1.4** |\n| pytest-cov | 6 → **7.1** |\n| mypy | 1.x → **2.1** |\n| structlog | 25 → **26** |\n| cachetools | 5 → **7.1** |\n| redis | 5 → **8** |\n| greenlet | 3.4 → **3.5.1** |\n| google-genai | 0.x → **2.8** |\n\n(FastAPI already at 0.137 from #391.)\n\n## Why consolidate instead of merging the individual PRs\nThe individual Dependabot PRs **fail CI** because each moves *one* dep\ninto an **incompatible partial combination** (e.g. pytest-asyncio 1.x\nagainst pytest 8). A single `uv lock --upgrade` resolves a\n**consistent** set — so the same bumps that fail one-by-one all pass\ntogether. It also dedups the overlapping/competing PRs (multiple\ngreenlet/pytest-asyncio/redis PRs) into one resolution.\n\n## Verification (CI-equivalent local run)\nNo code changes were needed — the modern stack is green:\n- **core-api + core-storage-api:** ruff clean · mypy 2.1 **0 errors** ·\n**3312 passed**\n- **core-operations:** ruff/mypy clean · **34 passed**\n- **core-worker:** ruff/mypy clean · 66 passed · **1 failure that is\nPRE-EXISTING and unrelated** — a stale test passing a removed\n`memory_type` enum value (`\"generic\"`); it fails on `main` too\n(verified) and core-worker's suite isn't CI-gated. Tracked separately.\n\ngreenlet cap lifted `<3.5.0`→`<3.6.0` (3.5.1 restored the Linux x86_64\nwheels). Locks stay **frozen + hash-verified** in the Dockerfiles.\n\n## Closes\nSupersedes the open Dependabot PRs (#366–#390 + the stale #5–#157\nbacklog). They'll be closed with a reference here once this merges\n(Dependabot auto-closes the satisfied ones).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T07:46:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5c939684f800d1e5be6051e27dfac41682c383fc/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a"}]},{"sha":"c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGM0Njk0OTA1MjMyNmY3ZWYzNzJjZjFhMTBmNGM1YmEyYjQxNzQwMmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-15T06:36:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T06:36:06Z"},"message":"chore(labels): add area/core-operations + use it in Dependabot (#393)\n\nSmall follow-up to #365: `core-operations` had no `area/*` label, so its\nDependabot PRs were routed through `area/infra`.\n\n- Add **`area/core-operations`** to `.github/labels.yml` (mirrors the\nother `core-*` area labels; `labels-sync` will create it).\n- Point the `core-operations` `uv` block in `.github/dependabot.yml` at\nthe new label (was `area/infra`).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9aed120ad38c1ab689037e6ce44542134622749e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9aed120ad38c1ab689037e6ce44542134622749e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL51WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArZMQAFWjk5WsQJGl9vcv2Ji4Rrbw\n8ZRIWiwRnLoS87E9MD5qJL0DA2ttttaFpyGb1Ru8MVS5EFY3e1IQdwG+nfRFYf/m\niQ92j1gEQUED6ULulY8gRIqC//JKeBKj2bTbx9KDdeDc2By/he95yy5dNjfRHNBj\n8SDlMbM4P1rFyD0xCMkxBIRb/Z7efHED+Y7gwqXQVNyo3SauhHnvlN22yn6kwFhA\n0A6+oCR+BSEw6upq+o/yMZGA5X+48SZf7MyJ3AfolXDq6I+udPutqFF9UI2yqS79\nJnVzyO820QBCI41C3fWiWfe11jmQOTMr2Adp8tPcee1CPwbS0vNAH9kOkIoFd6mH\nhQXAxQmtrYARN1ebhoBfvponXb7+If1Eo1121LhhJm8kXN0yOgSJut9MAQehleBF\nJloyKwQNSkDwn9u25bSHR3LrxkI4QWuKogCzIM1juV/g0oIsstVMxLXTkVLKBxWH\nSX0hpOmMbBUKSx36FRUtQUqXzGS4AOGcBzTly2R/e0HhwSNeKPuIUEQ9FAOroJdv\nr1FxGBNH2aTFdCSoQfDrmb8FXmifyWyNf+Va833JVeVA5TTlbVRg4xq+8WlZbD6s\n98ZBXiZEOOCVI/i/aNCtFIWBl7yCYDwae5Dewt0G8k4H7taFXoSFNJ9qzRC2cKqj\n/0gOo1PVbQCDpJ1lUV0y\n=Guyy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9aed120ad38c1ab689037e6ce44542134622749e\nparent fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781505366 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781505366 +0300\n\nchore(labels): add area/core-operations + use it in Dependabot (#393)\n\nSmall follow-up to #365: `core-operations` had no `area/*` label, so its\nDependabot PRs were routed through `area/infra`.\n\n- Add **`area/core-operations`** to `.github/labels.yml` (mirrors the\nother `core-*` area labels; `labels-sync` will create it).\n- Point the `core-operations` `uv` block in `.github/dependabot.yml` at\nthe new label (was `area/infra`).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T06:36:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c46949052326f7ef372cf1a10f4c5ba2b417402a/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d"}]},{"sha":"fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZkY2VjNTM1NDRjMTk5MWU4YTUxMzk3ZGUzYzlkMzlkYTY1MTUxM2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T21:59:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:59:28Z"},"message":"build(core-*): adopt FastAPI 0.137 — drop the <0.137 caps, relock (#391)\n\n## What\nNow that **#364** made core-api's CAURA-602 startup guard read\n`app.openapi()` (robust to FastAPI 0.137's `include_router` sub-app\nmounting), the temporary `fastapi<0.137` caps added during the\n2026-06-14 incident are no longer needed. This drops them and adopts\n0.137 fleet-wide.\n\n- All four `core-*` services: `fastapi>=0.115,<0.137` → **`<1`**.\n- Relocked (`uv lock --upgrade-package fastapi`) → **fastapi 0.137.0 +\nstarlette 1.3.1** across all four. The committed locks pin the exact\nversions; the Dockerfiles install frozen from them.\n- `greenlet<3.5.0` kept (platform-wheel guardrail, unrelated).\n\n## Verification\n- **CI runs the test suites under 0.137** here — CI installs lock-less\n(`uv pip install -e …`), so with the caps gone it resolves 0.137 and\nruns lint/mypy/pytest against it. **This PR's green CI is the gate**\n(the \"verify beyond import\" step).\n- Earlier proof that the guard holds under 0.137: a linux/amd64 build\nimported `core_api.app` green on fastapi 0.137.0 (#364).\n- If CI surfaces any 0.137 runtime/route-behavior issue beyond the\nguard, it shows here before merge.\n\n## Rollback\nTrivial — revert this PR; the locks return to 0.136.x and the caps come\nback.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c021264f347d397071337f7ad4c8c59da6daa1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6c021264f347d397071337f7ad4c8c59da6daa1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLyRACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUAYQAHVsw+WECjCXqGEciAfGca6C\nJ5stq3In7+rZK4O9Snto8HfnFY964lloPGyMCFGJXVT/Akh6yDx5wZkTNZtqmjba\nHvB/AOBr/D7d1rh5BQUqvwpvOcz8HwCA0vcoTrK7Lr2JuT2fAhBWsB8ZbKsLs6LI\n9zESPpdLmMpF6QMnnbGyF/q75MQuKj0WJO1Q7AJVDfNhZz0fBHj9ttwK1bP7K4zX\nmMqXeuHVu0jFVjXEF4yl28z96lX60V+RMm7RE5z3dBJ1VyMfIDPY8d062Mh3eXpA\nMWMs9dm7SyMIdt2il6snL+OrtbIcQIf55gKO/1Y7lfun7f1NMN+2e7qgJehH7i26\nhrwX0Q1cTjE+dHWqQIZ0RbcOugt+c54NB3XTALMehKu9S6q4mCJG9F3K11XckOmb\nf9OWHFWYHcFQE6jACC/iVQcK9fYloBFJRb7pQ04t8BsABh/cl7DOBC0/lzBJI1z5\ni/GVOu7a/hFW5tp5NlDnFN92Djhzvs/PDUFihz6GFAX1OHv0hYoYNA8znN8glUh4\njDPaLJKkK9gceDmby7egMqzkylFtpZ2U88k0ynB3PJcWKmYZTCLmEfz4wZr0fuba\nlQcZdmKFzCVoVE2qTHYFEuELSKgSsMTT4nWgToaSljNc6pvbYTE+pkvi/AjPCviJ\nAcO4OHkpyPey79iRUgo7\n=HiqC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c021264f347d397071337f7ad4c8c59da6daa1a\nparent 65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781474368 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781474368 +0300\n\nbuild(core-*): adopt FastAPI 0.137 — drop the <0.137 caps, relock (#391)\n\n## What\nNow that **#364** made core-api's CAURA-602 startup guard read\n`app.openapi()` (robust to FastAPI 0.137's `include_router` sub-app\nmounting), the temporary `fastapi<0.137` caps added during the\n2026-06-14 incident are no longer needed. This drops them and adopts\n0.137 fleet-wide.\n\n- All four `core-*` services: `fastapi>=0.115,<0.137` → **`<1`**.\n- Relocked (`uv lock --upgrade-package fastapi`) → **fastapi 0.137.0 +\nstarlette 1.3.1** across all four. The committed locks pin the exact\nversions; the Dockerfiles install frozen from them.\n- `greenlet<3.5.0` kept (platform-wheel guardrail, unrelated).\n\n## Verification\n- **CI runs the test suites under 0.137** here — CI installs lock-less\n(`uv pip install -e …`), so with the caps gone it resolves 0.137 and\nruns lint/mypy/pytest against it. **This PR's green CI is the gate**\n(the \"verify beyond import\" step).\n- Earlier proof that the guard holds under 0.137: a linux/amd64 build\nimported `core_api.app` green on fastapi 0.137.0 (#364).\n- If CI surfaces any 0.137 runtime/route-behavior issue beyond the\nguard, it shows here before merge.\n\n## Rollback\nTrivial — revert this PR; the locks return to 0.136.x and the caps come\nback.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:59:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fdcec53544c1991e8a51397de3c9d39da651513d/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112"}]},{"sha":"65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY1ZGUxMTBhYzk5NmZlN2JkNzljNTgyM2I5MmUzODUyOTM0Y2MxMTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T21:39:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:39:57Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): make the CAURA-602 startup guard FastAPI-0.137-proof (#364)\n\n## Why\nThe CAURA-602 startup guard asserts every `RequestTimeoutMiddleware`\nopt-out path (`/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `/api/v1/admin/org/purge-data`)\nis a registered route. It walked `app.routes` and string-matched\ntop-level `.path` entries.\n\n**FastAPI 0.137 broke that:** `include_router(prefix=...)` now mounts\nthe router as an opaque `_IncludedRouter` (`path=None`, no public\n`.routes`), so the prefixed opt-out paths are no longer top-level\n`APIRoute.path` entries → the guard raised at import → core-api crashed\non boot. That was the **2026-06-14 outage** (currently mitigated by the\nreactive `fastapi<0.137` caps).\n\n## Fix\nRead the registered paths from **`app.openapi()`** — the stable, public\nsurface — instead of walking the internal route objects. The OpenAPI\nschema lists the prefixed paths under **both** old (flatten) and new\n(mount) FastAPI. All core-api routes are `include_in_schema=True`, so\nnone is hidden from the check.\n\n```python\n_registered_paths = set(app.openapi().get(\"paths\", {}))\n```\n\n## Verification (linux/amd64)\nBuilt core-api and imported `core_api.app` under both versions:\n\n| FastAPI | `import core_api.app` | guard |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.136.3 (committed lock) | ✅ green, 106 routes | passes (no\nregression) |\n| 0.137.0 | ✅ green | **passes** — finds the opt-out paths via openapi\ndespite `_IncludedRouter` |\n\n## Impact\nThis makes the guard robust to FastAPI's routing-internals changes and\n**unblocks dropping the `fastapi<0.137` caps** (core-api +\ncore-storage-api + core-worker + core-operations) once the team chooses\nto adopt 0.137+. Recommend dropping the caps + a deliberate `uv lock\n--upgrade` to 0.137 in a follow-up, after this lands.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9fee6602a9d9cafc673d5dc1a2366569c06ecab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b9fee6602a9d9cafc673d5dc1a2366569c06ecab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLx+tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADfsQAAM0z7kj+GrccVWZarxq11WV\nBog7e5TyipZl+8mFEpoQue4MGbCiYQgYxJCf+aauvc9h0QLH6rvldD7CjDh8ZNwH\nes9iDw7zkw1h3HS1Uh7K0Fbutk8MRsD87BeR67FH6bn5N5Rmc0b2jcgzbLjWKSb1\nVUekpb0OmPHlXqWksedM6CMRwJ5pMwnrcrXR7tskgxwiUWryg/U4GjIHChuZYUj6\nMyJSsy1rs7KeSG9zRDp++BYF7hBHJLnq2VyWyp0nK+5KWkhrMyA5mTG2ayWUTl7U\nZTEhIICT2ilxGbXFk/M+MuYq2BR3bAbbwHIG4Ju770HucaXxNPfs/Dwwxwp8Xd+U\nXNB326T9Src+sp0kC2o4yWZTNexUz4EzejExGpC11G4LSvfPhFRopjfGGxSO292J\nRHVTrszld1W47f2MZsBkgwzvMbm4fgkFFTae8INY/mPuWpfJeuf1E/+xpsdNTUt4\npccSvOipqP0w3sazlFJxicuE8KYfd/9lqvykkunrzov4ZfnKEjH42FIqkcNGLwK9\nk9wUz6Wq7V1cMaFGv1B+s+iYGzJNXbpbmYTfE4fmtGFUK2p0HjqODezBFIAybFvv\n0dHSFKZFEhrP4NNbmM5NcLsMwT0p8qsPw2YdTQ+ygedeKjSuYlBXzzh3MADxJnVN\nagEiOO6YSK/QO8TxxyWd\n=MEc0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9fee6602a9d9cafc673d5dc1a2366569c06ecab\nparent 112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781473197 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781473197 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): make the CAURA-602 startup guard FastAPI-0.137-proof (#364)\n\n## Why\nThe CAURA-602 startup guard asserts every `RequestTimeoutMiddleware`\nopt-out path (`/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `/api/v1/admin/org/purge-data`)\nis a registered route. It walked `app.routes` and string-matched\ntop-level `.path` entries.\n\n**FastAPI 0.137 broke that:** `include_router(prefix=...)` now mounts\nthe router as an opaque `_IncludedRouter` (`path=None`, no public\n`.routes`), so the prefixed opt-out paths are no longer top-level\n`APIRoute.path` entries → the guard raised at import → core-api crashed\non boot. That was the **2026-06-14 outage** (currently mitigated by the\nreactive `fastapi<0.137` caps).\n\n## Fix\nRead the registered paths from **`app.openapi()`** — the stable, public\nsurface — instead of walking the internal route objects. The OpenAPI\nschema lists the prefixed paths under **both** old (flatten) and new\n(mount) FastAPI. All core-api routes are `include_in_schema=True`, so\nnone is hidden from the check.\n\n```python\n_registered_paths = set(app.openapi().get(\"paths\", {}))\n```\n\n## Verification (linux/amd64)\nBuilt core-api and imported `core_api.app` under both versions:\n\n| FastAPI | `import core_api.app` | guard |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.136.3 (committed lock) | ✅ green, 106 routes | passes (no\nregression) |\n| 0.137.0 | ✅ green | **passes** — finds the opt-out paths via openapi\ndespite `_IncludedRouter` |\n\n## Impact\nThis makes the guard robust to FastAPI's routing-internals changes and\n**unblocks dropping the `fastapi<0.137` caps** (core-api +\ncore-storage-api + core-worker + core-operations) once the team chooses\nto adopt 0.137+. Recommend dropping the caps + a deliberate `uv lock\n--upgrade` to 0.137 in a follow-up, after this lands.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:39:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/65de110ac996fe7bd79c5823b92e3852934cc112/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade"}]},{"sha":"112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDExMmYyYjVhOWVmNTcyZTUyYjM1OWNiNmIxOWYzMmUxNTI1MmJhZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T21:36:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:36:40Z"},"message":"build(deps): manage core-* uv.lock via Dependabot's uv ecosystem (#365)\n\n## Why\nThe `core-*` services now commit `uv.lock` and install **frozen** from\nit (#362, #363), so a dependency only changes when the lock changes. The\nexisting Dependabot config pointed those services at the **`pip`**\necosystem — which only bumps `pyproject.toml` and **never touches\n`uv.lock`**, so it would leave the frozen lock (the thing the image\nactually installs) stale and divergent. This points Dependabot at the\nlocks so bumps land as reviewed PRs — the last piece closing the loop on\nthe 2026-06-14 FastAPI 0.137 drift.\n\n## Changes (to the existing `.github/dependabot.yml`)\n- **`core-api` + `core-storage-api`:** `package-ecosystem: pip` →\n**`uv`** (updates pyproject **and** uv.lock together).\n- **Add `uv` blocks for `core-worker` + `core-operations`** — they had\n**no** Dependabot coverage at all.\n- Everything else unchanged: root `pip` (real `requirements.txt`), root\n+ plugin `npm`, `github-actions`, `docker`.\n\nResulting ecosystem map:\n```\npip            /                  (unchanged — root requirements.txt)\nuv             /core-api          (was pip)\nuv             /core-storage-api  (was pip)\nuv             /core-worker       (new)\nuv             /core-operations   (new)\nnpm            / , /plugin        (unchanged)\ngithub-actions /                  (unchanged)\ndocker         /                  (unchanged)\n```\n\n## Notes\n- `core-operations` uses `area/infra` — there's no\n`area/core-operations` label in `labels.yml` (adding one is a trivial\noptional follow-up).\n- Kept the repo's existing ungrouped, weekly, labelled style; no\nbehavior change beyond the ecosystem switch + the two new services.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f087e40336748696480e56e575232f819f0051ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f087e40336748696480e56e575232f819f0051ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLx7oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmAQAAMCtTjG/gxpHdJOaIVH3LwN\nuWe10EnMvzFOl2Xrjw5xQt1EBtW0+auhnEgZsvObMchZbOxA5vXlyCBFcApBQdX8\nQYHl1Hc6IN1J1haIH61w7gWnxM8fkQUMunNUHWXdZvT2vH1KT90DsV7EDGPOmZhf\nfLofp1n3U7RUQmZ9jrZjQUKpgpHwo0G+h2QpuKoS5OSr4U+eo6L7xO4L6yUtDadC\nov3k+AePaS96Iqq/mVzex/ImT0NNUJZx0gg54uLa14ebI+O/XPuJsm+3St4w+OJy\ngffo1B+KA816jwhCADvz9LPbKD58gHllQBOCPnn1ui2butifrVnhZPu1IJjGuSYO\nwThC2C8AF7tqNiQAuWXt0CBAnV9BzqnLFbzOB0aESL+OhWqYpvJNn3teBfZEfN2z\nWW8+5fas3HtRso7OZjeSf1L2iaWcdrY7ek4qmocADk8sXE/x2LJYsSIHZy8T9cFI\nK0/PWPLvDSXizkUy4PlMBppkRCNDWt3tvuUgi8kLhYaoxlz9rVXYlIgm68RwRQxi\nuviLhljHEIPRNKfgHowrU8baA8RXmUwMyeftKldUCgOffmffMUxtkih7QF0LVdKH\ntdBLiL95ZzhUJHXAOVG3amE+GZmI9rAdo1L3EssmC243cDB/bxDRe/4oqAZDeSqj\nirrH1Z/EaKAsOvvkQL15\n=+FOW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f087e40336748696480e56e575232f819f0051ee\nparent ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781473000 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781473000 +0300\n\nbuild(deps): manage core-* uv.lock via Dependabot's uv ecosystem (#365)\n\n## Why\nThe `core-*` services now commit `uv.lock` and install **frozen** from\nit (#362, #363), so a dependency only changes when the lock changes. The\nexisting Dependabot config pointed those services at the **`pip`**\necosystem — which only bumps `pyproject.toml` and **never touches\n`uv.lock`**, so it would leave the frozen lock (the thing the image\nactually installs) stale and divergent. This points Dependabot at the\nlocks so bumps land as reviewed PRs — the last piece closing the loop on\nthe 2026-06-14 FastAPI 0.137 drift.\n\n## Changes (to the existing `.github/dependabot.yml`)\n- **`core-api` + `core-storage-api`:** `package-ecosystem: pip` →\n**`uv`** (updates pyproject **and** uv.lock together).\n- **Add `uv` blocks for `core-worker` + `core-operations`** — they had\n**no** Dependabot coverage at all.\n- Everything else unchanged: root `pip` (real `requirements.txt`), root\n+ plugin `npm`, `github-actions`, `docker`.\n\nResulting ecosystem map:\n```\npip            /                  (unchanged — root requirements.txt)\nuv             /core-api          (was pip)\nuv             /core-storage-api  (was pip)\nuv             /core-worker       (new)\nuv             /core-operations   (new)\nnpm            / , /plugin        (unchanged)\ngithub-actions /                  (unchanged)\ndocker         /                  (unchanged)\n```\n\n## Notes\n- `core-operations` uses `area/infra` — there's no\n`area/core-operations` label in `labels.yml` (adding one is a trivial\noptional follow-up).\n- Kept the repo's existing ungrouped, weekly, labelled style; no\nbehavior change beyond the ecosystem switch + the two new services.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:36:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/112f2b5a9ef572e52b359cb6b19f32e15252bade/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd"}]},{"sha":"ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNlNmYyMWMzOTAwMGYwYjYyMTYzM2QwNGRjNmE5MjliNGFmNmZiZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T21:24:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:24:02Z"},"message":"build(core-*): commit uv.lock + frozen hash-verified Docker installs (expand pilot) (#363)\n\n## What\nRolls the **#362 core-api lock pilot** (validated green in staging) out\nto the remaining deployable services, so the whole `core-*` fleet builds\nreproducibly and can't silently float dependencies — the FastAPI 0.137\ndrift that crashed prod 2026-06-14.\n\n- **`core-storage-api` / `core-worker` / `core-operations`:** commit\n`uv.lock` (universal, multi-platform) + un-ignore them; Dockerfiles\ninstall **frozen + hash-verified** from the lock (`uv export --frozen …\n| uv pip install`, require-hashes mode) instead of lock-less `pip\ninstall`.\n- **Cap `fastapi<0.137`** on `core-worker` + `core-operations` (core-api\n+ core-storage-api already capped) so all four pin a uniform FastAPI\n`0.136.x` until the durable CAURA-602 guard fix lands; the caps drop\nrepo-wide then.\n\nPer-service install extras preserved: **storage** none, **worker**\n`pubsub`+`vertex`, **operations** `pubsub`.\n\n## Verification (linux/amd64 — the historical cross-platform failure\nmode)\nBuilt each modified Dockerfile and imported the app:\n\n| Service | Build | FastAPI | Hash lines | `import <svc>.app` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| core-storage-api | ✅ | 0.136.1 | 584 | ✅ |\n| core-worker | ✅ | 0.136.1 | 631 | ✅ |\n| core-operations | ✅ | 0.136.3 | 538 | ✅ |\n\n(As with #362, OSS PR CI doesn't build the images; the real-pipeline\nconfirmation is the post-merge enterprise staging deploy.)\n\n## After this\nAll four `core-*` services are now lock-pinned + frozen + hash-verified.\nRemaining follow-ups: wire **Renovate/Dependabot** for bump PRs, and\nship the **durable CAURA-602 guard fix** (recurse `Mount` sub-apps) →\nthen drop the `fastapi<0.137` caps to adopt 0.137+. Keep\n`greenlet<3.5.0`.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"efe08bec0f6c20808a7001958721cb118fc48539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/efe08bec0f6c20808a7001958721cb118fc48539"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLxvyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8mMQAAbj0Zou2P16Hob54WQml9Vn\nKYvmwXvEzb4Sf3jBwCdMmCgin4yAcM73FzHZHxljKKviailpsD9fPeX8hl+RMI1O\nKaazDLY1lIq+7op6zm+XWdIny8vfkz2/EniKqhxRSoOw5FkM0MXpl2oRO+eHZ9Za\nMwn8eMnTJu3rkgmsBwlCKWBPpA1jxewZTrCk6fNpifTKwL2J299iZZuC+2hlZ5Ka\nAuDUojvzmH5WmgWuqurEKsrBTRN5GA3JVj7Ii8TvUkscr0wtl/o/GeOIQMz1a/nB\nKTVRjePYA/2rEq82e3AHoMdJ6hwUQAfrRNbrVQuYGLVSWsmUbCP0kPe8YmWXXMQD\nD9dmS3Ky4Dj2ME2SA0CYBswSqSMwuK2pHc0xjAKQkA5FnV9MKp9QelTXjSvhJHNT\nPDAZUztGZHUPSL0CMuTgWIWZBxNxB/ys5ASNnstRU9W1VaQksnrZP2O/oayWFKcl\noZZbP1LzEVtDPtJMn9MFHDhBDT2u+LByTGrPmQEm6UJCZZT46hTHubJSnBo8lJ4d\n5n2dq/0F/EeDVzBYk6ejKgrZf/Bht0g/X7qNeedv+NGPHRAqE+9m5B5y+iD/GD98\nEzst0l/N6sf4NGbRg2Uynr2HNB7SEZTjWyC4trK9W8smYGnF0gHaExX7ZabeXl6R\n4Ij0My9MPiKj6spn7WvS\n=ZJ4M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree efe08bec0f6c20808a7001958721cb118fc48539\nparent 21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781472242 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781472242 +0300\n\nbuild(core-*): commit uv.lock + frozen hash-verified Docker installs (expand pilot) (#363)\n\n## What\nRolls the **#362 core-api lock pilot** (validated green in staging) out\nto the remaining deployable services, so the whole `core-*` fleet builds\nreproducibly and can't silently float dependencies — the FastAPI 0.137\ndrift that crashed prod 2026-06-14.\n\n- **`core-storage-api` / `core-worker` / `core-operations`:** commit\n`uv.lock` (universal, multi-platform) + un-ignore them; Dockerfiles\ninstall **frozen + hash-verified** from the lock (`uv export --frozen …\n| uv pip install`, require-hashes mode) instead of lock-less `pip\ninstall`.\n- **Cap `fastapi<0.137`** on `core-worker` + `core-operations` (core-api\n+ core-storage-api already capped) so all four pin a uniform FastAPI\n`0.136.x` until the durable CAURA-602 guard fix lands; the caps drop\nrepo-wide then.\n\nPer-service install extras preserved: **storage** none, **worker**\n`pubsub`+`vertex`, **operations** `pubsub`.\n\n## Verification (linux/amd64 — the historical cross-platform failure\nmode)\nBuilt each modified Dockerfile and imported the app:\n\n| Service | Build | FastAPI | Hash lines | `import <svc>.app` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| core-storage-api | ✅ | 0.136.1 | 584 | ✅ |\n| core-worker | ✅ | 0.136.1 | 631 | ✅ |\n| core-operations | ✅ | 0.136.3 | 538 | ✅ |\n\n(As with #362, OSS PR CI doesn't build the images; the real-pipeline\nconfirmation is the post-merge enterprise staging deploy.)\n\n## After this\nAll four `core-*` services are now lock-pinned + frozen + hash-verified.\nRemaining follow-ups: wire **Renovate/Dependabot** for bump PRs, and\nship the **durable CAURA-602 guard fix** (recurse `Mount` sub-apps) →\nthen drop the `fastapi<0.137` caps to adopt 0.137+. Keep\n`greenlet<3.5.0`.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:24:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce6f21c39000f0b621633d04dc6a929b4af6fbdd/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13"}]},{"sha":"21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDIxZTljZGZlNmVlYmNjMTkxNWEwZjk1OTE0MzNmYmU2NWFjMTVlMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T19:51:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T19:51:48Z"},"message":"build(core-api): commit uv.lock + install frozen in Docker (pin against dep drift) (#362)\n\n## Why\nThe 2026-06-14 prod outage was dependency drift: `core-api`'s Docker\nbuild ran a **lock-less** `pip install './core-api[pubsub]'`,\nre-resolving on every build. The moment **FastAPI 0.137.0** released, it\nfloated in — its `include_router` change drops prefixed paths from\n`app.routes`, tripping the CAURA-602 startup guard → core-api `exit(1)`\n→ every staging deploy failed. `#359`'s `fastapi<0.137` cap is a\nreactive stopgap; this fixes the **root cause**.\n\n## What (pilot — core-api only)\n- **Commit `core-api/uv.lock`** (universal, multi-platform) and\nun-ignore just this one in `.gitignore`.\n- **Dockerfile installs frozen** from the lock — `uv export --frozen … |\nuv pip install` instead of re-resolving the pyproject ranges. The\ndeployed image is now reproducible and **cannot float** between builds;\ndependency bumps become deliberate, reviewable `uv lock` changes\n(Renovate/Dependabot-friendly).\n\n## Verification (the historical objection, retired with evidence)\n`uv.lock` was gitignored originally because mac-pinned locks broke Linux\nCI (the `greenlet<3.5.0` saga). Modern `uv` does **universal** locking,\nso that no longer holds — proven by building this exact Dockerfile on\n**`linux/amd64`**:\n- frozen install resolved **101 packages, all wheels present** (no\nmissing-Linux-wheel failure), `fastapi==0.136.3`\n- `import core_api.app` inside the image → **green, 106 routes** (the\nguard passes; under the broken float this import is what crashed)\n\nNote: OSS PR CI doesn't build the Docker image (only `publish-docker` on\nrelease does, and the deployed image is built by the enterprise\npipeline), so this was verified by a local `linux/amd64` build of the\n**real** Dockerfile rather than in PR CI.\n\n## Scope / not in this PR\n- CI test-install and the `fastapi<0.137` cap are **unchanged** — the\ncap still guards CI's lock-less install; both can be revisited once the\ndurable CAURA-602 guard fix lands and locks roll out.\n- `core-worker` / `core-operations` / `core-storage-api` stay lock-less\nuntil this pilot is expanded to them.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a511f7493d1ed477628c4ae73d75c29304657062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a511f7493d1ed477628c4ae73d75c29304657062"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLwZUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGlYQAD2yZIk1HlirlxJYanl69Ocg\nSU62nVJGsvJ36uUG268nGfIF8fcLEqYI0tixHgHHMNmNqGk1AWiX2B94JROLwmZQ\nerIf5sRweq0O+Wg1xAb7ac66cnO6umRb2XK4hXYbaX9GvwpBJIwsQBzC2S4KhojD\nuwqFM6/6VIg2IVmKK+aAZsePT9lmthmolv77yHlKrR2RDEotYu++Zwsf6ZDofajb\nxvGGpfZYT9WvqKmplCkXMx1YZBzwNPHzz5ymf4we6Kezglgb0Rp8Efb2hjOxqW7Z\nIGCks1AEImZ1q8WHPU0QODGwm4WXqtcXLfXBjX1Sw0NeYOy9dSo466zGczPV4i9l\n6QbCcFQMjth2JYlaPxMBTXujHOCJJaRHct78hzQQ8/sQ1ZUJbbUYEuM+RqfkCd3O\nZkEBAaLylNkHnElE2ULG+wUdeLv0JuyXdRLL1KEImvNxAtYghdIz2jjUwwGu9/RH\n/Z51TWHcIPIyh87YkQ748lESr3vRWOi1Vsf7XogD5WMcaFybww2of9qg2+fM33G3\nVJYrqSb3Sh5U2hnZlg+mTxYqIqwNrL0lLgZ4OpJQ5UzBgWbAypGA+g+jUphYKiOq\nEXt+AMRzLuKTs7o094h0TiINE3skcYtA3USl8y/VlQHmU5/8Ouxt+9DEmsyKA1l2\nqRQ+or/ebtGgHnZkvlqg\n=Z+B6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a511f7493d1ed477628c4ae73d75c29304657062\nparent 2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1781466708 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781466708 +0300\n\nbuild(core-api): commit uv.lock + install frozen in Docker (pin against dep drift) (#362)\n\n## Why\nThe 2026-06-14 prod outage was dependency drift: `core-api`'s Docker\nbuild ran a **lock-less** `pip install './core-api[pubsub]'`,\nre-resolving on every build. The moment **FastAPI 0.137.0** released, it\nfloated in — its `include_router` change drops prefixed paths from\n`app.routes`, tripping the CAURA-602 startup guard → core-api `exit(1)`\n→ every staging deploy failed. `#359`'s `fastapi<0.137` cap is a\nreactive stopgap; this fixes the **root cause**.\n\n## What (pilot — core-api only)\n- **Commit `core-api/uv.lock`** (universal, multi-platform) and\nun-ignore just this one in `.gitignore`.\n- **Dockerfile installs frozen** from the lock — `uv export --frozen … |\nuv pip install` instead of re-resolving the pyproject ranges. The\ndeployed image is now reproducible and **cannot float** between builds;\ndependency bumps become deliberate, reviewable `uv lock` changes\n(Renovate/Dependabot-friendly).\n\n## Verification (the historical objection, retired with evidence)\n`uv.lock` was gitignored originally because mac-pinned locks broke Linux\nCI (the `greenlet<3.5.0` saga). Modern `uv` does **universal** locking,\nso that no longer holds — proven by building this exact Dockerfile on\n**`linux/amd64`**:\n- frozen install resolved **101 packages, all wheels present** (no\nmissing-Linux-wheel failure), `fastapi==0.136.3`\n- `import core_api.app` inside the image → **green, 106 routes** (the\nguard passes; under the broken float this import is what crashed)\n\nNote: OSS PR CI doesn't build the Docker image (only `publish-docker` on\nrelease does, and the deployed image is built by the enterprise\npipeline), so this was verified by a local `linux/amd64` build of the\n**real** Dockerfile rather than in PR CI.\n\n## Scope / not in this PR\n- CI test-install and the `fastapi<0.137` cap are **unchanged** — the\ncap still guards CI's lock-less install; both can be revisited once the\ndurable CAURA-602 guard fix lands and locks roll out.\n- `core-worker` / `core-operations` / `core-storage-api` stay lock-less\nuntil this pilot is expanded to them.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T19:51:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/21e9cdfe6eebcc1915a0f9591433fbe65ac15e13/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f"}]},{"sha":"2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJlY2MwOThmMDk5YzMzMzY1NWQ5MjJiMDhlYTdiYzAzY2E2OTljNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"yanki-m","email":"yanki@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T18:30:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T18:30:45Z"},"message":"docs: README write-response field names match payload (#361)\n\n## Summary\n- README Quick Start prose said the write response includes `type` and\n`importance_score`, but the actual `POST /memories` payload exposes\n`memory_type` and `weight`.\n- Aligns the prose at `README.md:75` with the real field names so a\nreader following the Quick Start sees what they expect.\n\nThis closes finding **F-5** from the OSS engineering report\n(`memclaw-tutorials/ENGINEERING-REPORT-caura-memclaw.md`). The fix was\nclaimed shipped in #344 but this one occurrence was missed.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `POST /api/v1/memories` against a fresh standalone stack and\nconfirm the returned JSON has `memory_type` and `weight` fields (no\n`type`, no `importance_score`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Yanki Margalit <yanki@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8f35b44eb8389d0127ddfa2f82860a789c751e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f8f35b44eb8389d0127ddfa2f82860a789c751e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLvNVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyN4QAAIey5nseXESzTDIRwzday/N\nGEmIAsm4ENP4goIryPf4qIQbmW0SXS70+HId/Xewhzen94Mqr4O3cF+EbANygNCg\nvowdnJV5RzF1lnzqexoKVVsCGcHXe48u/JLbB4VU50MQHQzT0jn0ttP7Rswqgcci\nlsplYt1D9+cIMVdYWuWlixYI08j+eqngdWXrJz+KagXJyN0pHWDa0bNsGKdM/k1n\nIzuYqMZ310PzDTMScrQeEjiGiSQp5Cs/hIP/WeusBpMmJgMS2hb6jTO1jlFLQTO7\n8dDs126fu5gGAqCD9TTTmffoUK0raF3+MjsCIizePeQrXU8J8wWjmMTJa7fif2iS\nfPkEEGCegeYs8VOLf8FO3nIiaoDLYK1ji5XCFX7YBT9QfQxNqkNhgiq1tXjY8AWV\n4YRczehnid0epIZNYsgtFnXfj0/06bZRM4DG4mz9iquqR9VGjbW9NV1WFT9yHZy7\n6nxfaGVs9tvOx3+kIy2WJAsmoo0MrLzMlGJz8iUW1k9EeaVgsfIp37LgdiqAbjpD\nWtGNJdUrBRKSah8FdC8TrchlG2PCfAcwhJ7wN/yazYf9QqIk/bqb8Xg1AENg1V8D\nYoM+OK528L+c5Tgrkd4G/mj2b1pz648SGK6TC+m7yrRrhWaT38KyfaNI2LNZ8gxC\nrPAz5q+nG5na3IB2MxfJ\n=EtR3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f8f35b44eb8389d0127ddfa2f82860a789c751e2\nparent c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9\nauthor yanki-m <yanki@caura.ai> 1781461845 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781461845 +0300\n\ndocs: README write-response field names match payload (#361)\n\n## Summary\n- README Quick Start prose said the write response includes `type` and\n`importance_score`, but the actual `POST /memories` payload exposes\n`memory_type` and `weight`.\n- Aligns the prose at `README.md:75` with the real field names so a\nreader following the Quick Start sees what they expect.\n\nThis closes finding **F-5** from the OSS engineering report\n(`memclaw-tutorials/ENGINEERING-REPORT-caura-memclaw.md`). The fix was\nclaimed shipped in #344 but this one occurrence was missed.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `POST /api/v1/memories` against a fresh standalone stack and\nconfirm the returned JSON has `memory_type` and `weight` fields (no\n`type`, no `importance_score`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Yanki Margalit <yanki@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T18:30:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2ecc098f099c333655d922b08ea7bc03ca699c4f/comments","author":{"login":"yanki-m","id":232570632,"node_id":"U_kgDODdy_CA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232570632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m","html_url":"https://github.com/yanki-m","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9"}]},{"sha":"c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGMwMGEzZjc2ZjZmMzkwMDI0NTY3ZjZkMjNhY2VmMDYyZjMwNGRjYTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T17:15:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T17:15:44Z"},"message":"fix(search): surface conflicted memories that exactly match the query (#357)\n\n## Problem\n\nS1 retrieval@10 collapses at corpus scale even after #304/#327: **22/25\n@ K=1000 → 18/25 @ K=10000**, and per-failure anatomy showed **every\nresidual miss was a gold memory with `status='conflicted'`** — flipping\njust those statuses to `confirmed` recovered **25/25**.\n\nTwo retrieval paths hard-excluded `conflicted`/`outdated` rows from\ndefault results:\n- `memory_scored_search` (semantic/keyword path): `WHERE status NOT IN\n('outdated','conflicted')`\n- `memory_load_by_ids` (entity_lookup short-circuit): same exclusion\n\nThe semantic contradiction detector marks the older of two\nembedding-near rows `conflicted`, and routinely mismarks **distinct\nentities that merely share a name prefix** (e.g. `Wayne Enterprises\n#0000` was marked conflicted against `Wayne Enterprises #0704`). The\nblanket exclusion then silently dropped the exact row the caller asked\nfor, leaving only confirmed near-duplicate siblings about *other*\nentities. ~10% of a 10k-fact corpus was marked conflicted this way.\n\n## Fix (retrieval-only — write/contradiction path untouched)\n\n- **`memory_scored_search`**: keep a `conflicted` row when it is an\nexact lexical (FTS) match for the query, and exempt that row from the\n`0.5` `status_penalty` so it isn't re-buried beneath confirmed siblings.\n`outdated` (a definitive retraction) stays fully excluded.\n- **`memory_load_by_ids`** (entity_lookup): rows here are already scoped\nto the resolved entity — the entity-graph analogue of an exact match —\nso keep `conflicted` and exclude only `outdated`.\n\n`load_and_serialize` still injects the supersedes successor for any\nreturned superseded row, so genuine knowledge-updates continue to show\nboth sides.\n\n## Results (S1 replay, local stack, retrieval@10)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| **k10k** | 18/25 | **25/25** |\n| k1k | 22/25 | 23/25 |\n\nThe 2 residual k1k misses are person-hub graph dilution in entity_lookup\n(gold's link dropped at the `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES` cap) — a\nseparate, deeper issue (tracked toward the exact-first cascade, A30).\n\n## Regression safety\n\n- New integration tests\n(`tests/test_integration_search.py::TestConflictedExactMatchSurfaces`)\npin all three semantics: conflicted exact-match surfaces; conflicted\nnon-match stays excluded; outdated exact-match stays excluded. They use\n`fake_embedding` (no external dependency).\n- `knowledge-update` regression category (the relevant risk — surfacing\nconflicted rows): **acc 91.7%, recall 1.0** vs baseline 92.9% / 1.0 —\nwithin noise, no regression. (The full 5-category local run was blocked\nby unrelated write-path LLM timeouts in the local env; the categories\nthat completed writes matched baseline exactly.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2d2ad86cea988f30e77cdfba6d4ef477e970df0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f2d2ad86cea988f30e77cdfba6d4ef477e970df0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLuHACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAohQQAKUgY7fBX6Gh5rptuzjcy2Wu\nqtp/WEkRbCurJ4dfJ/njgEDhfDPBecjIT9GdGz9xRDKRV3jDScPwHK2yndRDzKrc\nrT+N70NC0TNySjWOYxLS9fsSWRQE4zSqh7SBoZeYME77+hz7JSRt3s1S6hGMU2PC\nTaztcpAbaPTFZF8PSr8TeuqpCAFxi+kEYfjSt3BnLITqv07DNMt681m1PbZtJMfc\nwnef85BTof+AfYW+76IHAqsbBbsyRzcAB0q+1csjhx229r2EQ9qumnxrrHVrjKZC\nw2daKpLjVmkRTMstL8HF+eNJo5O4/z5CCXxjcoKIqKnuMrZNd98lP6YQKPbVN66J\nFNLuaAVHOTk6hSiQiuD/YIXNOZkBZjYm39oQ0+ei/Vzsl9TDFsJHHDs/JhN3hjVU\nG47OHYsWObDhC2ZBlrYrwybFczXjOaEpZatpR3AqjrGbFqOB4bnZIi1gI88oUXn6\n/jEfMtTxzKyBJTGyXaJRivqus7CRxFODR2Mtna8Wr3tVMotVIMJ9dYFlyqP785WL\nRq2At8iQHn2GnL85NhDWZFJRRAL9GFs6OoiTN4v26GAeJ+2AO5f/aja3ff+h6cHg\nhFyh0YmomLaBivC7ctpdeLhqVX7C6nr1vPCPaDDVHEfh1PD1R/5kisgpvOTGoxbT\nHeLa7asaSkGysiDJchPb\n=UwWy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f2d2ad86cea988f30e77cdfba6d4ef477e970df0\nparent 561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781457344 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781457344 +0300\n\nfix(search): surface conflicted memories that exactly match the query (#357)\n\n## Problem\n\nS1 retrieval@10 collapses at corpus scale even after #304/#327: **22/25\n@ K=1000 → 18/25 @ K=10000**, and per-failure anatomy showed **every\nresidual miss was a gold memory with `status='conflicted'`** — flipping\njust those statuses to `confirmed` recovered **25/25**.\n\nTwo retrieval paths hard-excluded `conflicted`/`outdated` rows from\ndefault results:\n- `memory_scored_search` (semantic/keyword path): `WHERE status NOT IN\n('outdated','conflicted')`\n- `memory_load_by_ids` (entity_lookup short-circuit): same exclusion\n\nThe semantic contradiction detector marks the older of two\nembedding-near rows `conflicted`, and routinely mismarks **distinct\nentities that merely share a name prefix** (e.g. `Wayne Enterprises\n#0000` was marked conflicted against `Wayne Enterprises #0704`). The\nblanket exclusion then silently dropped the exact row the caller asked\nfor, leaving only confirmed near-duplicate siblings about *other*\nentities. ~10% of a 10k-fact corpus was marked conflicted this way.\n\n## Fix (retrieval-only — write/contradiction path untouched)\n\n- **`memory_scored_search`**: keep a `conflicted` row when it is an\nexact lexical (FTS) match for the query, and exempt that row from the\n`0.5` `status_penalty` so it isn't re-buried beneath confirmed siblings.\n`outdated` (a definitive retraction) stays fully excluded.\n- **`memory_load_by_ids`** (entity_lookup): rows here are already scoped\nto the resolved entity — the entity-graph analogue of an exact match —\nso keep `conflicted` and exclude only `outdated`.\n\n`load_and_serialize` still injects the supersedes successor for any\nreturned superseded row, so genuine knowledge-updates continue to show\nboth sides.\n\n## Results (S1 replay, local stack, retrieval@10)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| **k10k** | 18/25 | **25/25** |\n| k1k | 22/25 | 23/25 |\n\nThe 2 residual k1k misses are person-hub graph dilution in entity_lookup\n(gold's link dropped at the `GRAPH_MAX_BOOSTED_MEMORIES` cap) — a\nseparate, deeper issue (tracked toward the exact-first cascade, A30).\n\n## Regression safety\n\n- New integration tests\n(`tests/test_integration_search.py::TestConflictedExactMatchSurfaces`)\npin all three semantics: conflicted exact-match surfaces; conflicted\nnon-match stays excluded; outdated exact-match stays excluded. They use\n`fake_embedding` (no external dependency).\n- `knowledge-update` regression category (the relevant risk — surfacing\nconflicted rows): **acc 91.7%, recall 1.0** vs baseline 92.9% / 1.0 —\nwithin noise, no regression. (The full 5-category local run was blocked\nby unrelated write-path LLM timeouts in the local env; the categories\nthat completed writes matched baseline exactly.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T17:15:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c00a3f76f6f390024567f6d23acef062f304dca9/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c"}]},{"sha":"561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU2MWQ1Yzk2ZmVlNmJlNjk4Y2MwZDIwNzdhN2U4MGYwYWFkYmJiMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T17:11:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T17:11:28Z"},"message":"fix(deps): cap fastapi <0.137 to unbreak CI (#359)\n\n## Why main's CI is red (no code change caused it)\n\nFastAPI **0.137.0** was released **2026-06-14 12:51 UTC** and changed\n`include_router(prefix=...)` to **mount a sub-app** instead of\nflattening the router's routes into `app.routes`. `app.py`'s import-time\nassertion — that every `RequestTimeoutMiddleware` opt-out path\n(`/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `/api/v1/admin/org/purge-data`) is registered\n— scans `app.routes` for those prefixed paths, no longer finds them, and\nraises at import. That errors every app-building test: **5 failed + 270\nerrors**.\n\nCI re-resolves dependencies with `uv pip install -e …[dev]` (lockfiles\nare gitignored), so the loose `fastapi>=0.115,<1` pin floated up to\n0.137.0 the instant it shipped — turning `main` red mid-day with **zero\ncommits**.\n\n### Proof it's the dependency, not any commit\n- All of `main`'s commits that day landed ≤12:06 UTC, before the 12:51\nrelease.\n- A throwaway PR on pristine `main` (empty commit) failed identically.\n- **Bisect:** commit `4d2d6ef` (2026-06-13, green CI the prior day)\nre-run today resolves 0.137.0 and throws the same `RuntimeError`. Same\nold code, new dep, fails.\n- Reproduced the mechanism directly: under 0.137.0\n`include_router(prefix=…)` adds **1 route** (a Mount) instead of the\nrouter's **20**; under 0.136.x it adds all 20.\n\n## Fix\n\nCap `fastapi>=0.115,<0.137` in both `core-api` and `core-storage-api`\npyprojects (same float-up rationale as the existing greenlet cap).\n\n**Verified:** the combined lock-less install (CI's exact failure mode)\nnow resolves fastapi 0.136.x and `import core_api.app` passes. Drop the\ncap once 0.137+'s mount-based routing is vetted against the\nroute-introspection assertion.\n\nUnblocks all PRs (incl. #357).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7dcb37c7dc4574403845f094075c012c6540986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b7dcb37c7dc4574403845f094075c012c6540986"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLuDACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA16YQACRHKHOIbIBehPTRukYThBTd\nxdyf5dzad0iZwD7FThAJFFy4iErXMwA9ZTr1bKjoW0Ur5SFrahREYECgltSEkKBA\nbCxPQMJ/IvHsas6RkXiWyyc/qBwBo9oiHX2k0USoM4zmlohwwKXOYxBSHfHNsSmb\nCt8V8eGzpnAhLrNfirC4GN4nCas4Dre28uT6r0bQwf4VcMX+UdqVD4m0qiQsy+Nu\neBzqa0NFOFq/vrCSecebTr/iDH/fA7RyDVvmcvhyKaCTkxcfmW3T5Zkrnj2SJIF+\ngjDWy2qD5HBfbzHiN+Lwnl04iutj0oft6I0Jdeqtcep6fQ6oU0Im+Q+thAFCUjJf\nbMXwLlrkzRcPn+MiYUiQ+t7fZPh5Khp0JLN9Fft2l9yqIP36opBOSXWGjt69m8Kc\n9EjeddTSp3/l+mrEVnIH+Ab3G2HETEojXlrdrcFUSTy9IOM4Jxj95ZJR3r7lCB7G\nnVFCyurWvRTMzcqSBNFhEBP9K9a10wB0mG9mmBdX6PKhz6wJhETdGfHEmhIMj9Ag\neSJ/R4iijpbIecUXrapbOs2tiBXTOvNiqNwSZQWGqoOOl1Tp13yvwRU0ShtkX3X8\nfiinU1OXdnnMfFBAsEjlv6DRQ+dCYS/xTC11yfHh8d+EbZ+UKBk73+/n1mrMN85X\nTSnKyopTEbMGAbT6J6wz\n=gPVX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b7dcb37c7dc4574403845f094075c012c6540986\nparent 22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781457088 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781457088 +0300\n\nfix(deps): cap fastapi <0.137 to unbreak CI (#359)\n\n## Why main's CI is red (no code change caused it)\n\nFastAPI **0.137.0** was released **2026-06-14 12:51 UTC** and changed\n`include_router(prefix=...)` to **mount a sub-app** instead of\nflattening the router's routes into `app.routes`. `app.py`'s import-time\nassertion — that every `RequestTimeoutMiddleware` opt-out path\n(`/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `/api/v1/admin/org/purge-data`) is registered\n— scans `app.routes` for those prefixed paths, no longer finds them, and\nraises at import. That errors every app-building test: **5 failed + 270\nerrors**.\n\nCI re-resolves dependencies with `uv pip install -e …[dev]` (lockfiles\nare gitignored), so the loose `fastapi>=0.115,<1` pin floated up to\n0.137.0 the instant it shipped — turning `main` red mid-day with **zero\ncommits**.\n\n### Proof it's the dependency, not any commit\n- All of `main`'s commits that day landed ≤12:06 UTC, before the 12:51\nrelease.\n- A throwaway PR on pristine `main` (empty commit) failed identically.\n- **Bisect:** commit `4d2d6ef` (2026-06-13, green CI the prior day)\nre-run today resolves 0.137.0 and throws the same `RuntimeError`. Same\nold code, new dep, fails.\n- Reproduced the mechanism directly: under 0.137.0\n`include_router(prefix=…)` adds **1 route** (a Mount) instead of the\nrouter's **20**; under 0.136.x it adds all 20.\n\n## Fix\n\nCap `fastapi>=0.115,<0.137` in both `core-api` and `core-storage-api`\npyprojects (same float-up rationale as the existing greenlet cap).\n\n**Verified:** the combined lock-less install (CI's exact failure mode)\nnow resolves fastapi 0.136.x and `import core_api.app` passes. Drop the\ncap once 0.137+'s mount-based routing is vetted against the\nroute-introspection assertion.\n\nUnblocks all PRs (incl. #357).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T17:11:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/561d5c96fee6be698cc0d2077a7e80f0aadbbb0c/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531"}]},{"sha":"22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDIyYTNhYzA2NGVjYWZjOTEyMTgwNzY3ODkwMzk5YTJjZTkzYWM1MzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T12:06:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T12:06:16Z"},"message":"fix(fleet): cap auto-upgrade re-queue with a per-(node,target) attempt budget (CAURA-000) (#351)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements **L1** from the auto-upgrade re-queue bug investigation: a\nbackend-side attempt budget that stops the gate from re-queuing deploys\nindefinitely against a node that never converges to the target version.\n\nToday `_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` has no attempt budget. Its only brakes\nare the 10-min in-flight window (stops *concurrent* storms only), the\nplugin-signalled `deploy_blocked_until` cooldown, and the hardcoded\n`KNOWN_BROKEN` set. A node that never converges is re-queued **every\nheartbeat (~60s ≈ 1,440/day)** with no brake and no operator-visible\nsignal — for any failure mode the plugin can't self-detect.\n\n## Validated failure modes (all un-braked today)\n\n| Mode | Plugin writes cooldown? |\n|---|---|\n| Persistent `/plugin-source` fetch error (`fetchOk=false`) | **No** —\n`status=failed`, no cooldown |\n| Unsafe-filename manifest abort | **No** |\n| **\"Succeeds but never advances\"** — served manifest version < gate's\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED` | **No** — every deploy builds, restarts,\npost-restart-verifies OK (clears cooldown), yet backend still sees\n`plugin_version < target` → re-queues forever, each attempt reporting\n*success* |\n\nThe plugin's 24h cooldown only covers its *own* self-detected failures\n(`build-failed`, `post-restart-version-mismatch`). `command_result`\nrecords failed deploys but feeds nothing back into the gate. Confirmed:\nno per-(node,target) counter anywhere.\n\n## Fix (backend-only)\n\nAfter `AUTO_UPGRADE_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (5) deploys for the same\n`target_version` within `AUTO_UPGRADE_ATTEMPT_WINDOW` (24h), the gate\nstops queuing and logs a `warning` for operator follow-up. Brakes **all\nthree** modes at the source — independent of plugin self-detection.\n\n- **New repo method** `count_recent_deploys_for_target(node_id,\ntarget_version, since)` — counts ALL statuses (the nastiest mode is\n`status=done` with no version progress; a status filter would miss it).\nJSONB `payload->>'target_version'` filter excludes manual/non-auto\ndeploys.\n- **New gate branch** placed *after* the in-flight check (rarest path)\nso the count query only runs on outdated-eligible-and-not-in-flight\nheartbeats. **Fail-open on DB error**, matching the in-flight check.\n\n### Why it's invisible to healthy upgrades\nA legitimate upgrade converges in **one** attempt — the next heartbeat\nreports the new version and the gate exits at the `_semver_lt` check\n*before* the budget is ever consulted. Keying on `target_version` means\na **new release (bumped target) gets a fresh budget** automatically;\nonly a non-advancing node accumulates >1 row for a given target.\n\n## Performance / load (asked during review)\n\n- **Agent turn path:** untouched — zero latency impact.\n- **Steady-state (converged fleet):** zero — the gate short-circuits at\n`_semver_lt` before any DB work.\n- **Wedged node:** large load **reduction** — ~1,440 command-inserts +\nrestart cycles/day collapse to 5.\n\nThe new query is one indexed SELECT, only on outdated-eligible\nheartbeats; `has_recent_in_flight_deploy` is left untouched (lower blast\nradius than folding the two into one query).\n\n## Production context\n\nValidated read-only on the customer prod box: the gap is **currently\nlatent** there — `MIN_RECOMMENDED` == served manifest == `2.9.0`, **0\ndeploy churn in 48h**, fleet converged. This lands as **preventive\nhardening** before the next release bump, where a manifest/target drift\non an on-prem image would re-activate the loop. (The earlier\n1,381-stuck-deploy incident was the pre-#305/#306 ack-storm — already\nresolved, not recurring.)\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new unit tests mirroring the in-flight gate tests:\n- skip-when-exhausted (+ asserts budget is keyed on target_version)\n- allow-under-cap\n- fresh-target-gets-fresh-budget\n- fail-open-on-repo-error\n- constants-are-sane\n\n56/56 in `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`; **126/126** across the\nfleet/heartbeat/repository sweep. `ruff` clean. JSONB query\ncompile-verified to `payload ->> 'target_version'`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **L1 only**, per the agreed gradual plan. L2 (full `nodes.metadata`\nstuck-stamp + UI), L3 (version-consistency guard), L4 (plugin-side\ncooldown on un-braked exits) are deferred. The exhaustion\n`logger.warning` here delivers the cheap ~80% of L2's observability.\n- No plugin change, no version bump, no migration.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 56/56 auto-upgrade unit tests\n- [x] 126/126 fleet/heartbeat/repository sweep\n- [x] ruff check + format clean\n- [x] JSONB query compiles to correct SQL\n- [x] DCO sign-off\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7425a8e285cef2688da36c2275d58cdfde66fb64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7425a8e285cef2688da36c2275d58cdfde66fb64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLpk4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvW4QAGo6WLoRAlocm2IoJzFqqn34\nziIi/OCjvtFCzXnLyA0L1v03ucJ0dlOMnN/5a4G6t8XuQwghbQyyJRTdbm5U5kmw\n0zCI27yb56JpcoOe0xuiZw7HBR7weEZRclz/QzdXg0L9Zi4HYF4a+HW7CD/UtFFF\nndkDGjhI1NMbLhjYq3MsFTFXY2dQwmYNaFzBA4ojI4x/auhbi/nlAMLj5wsVa/f0\nA0q4uvUisvsJJOBblgg85ZNbaTymT/MK1M5ssrO2q/nFWt4J2GiBlDQ8FhItphtv\nFJ9FfNqqz4eTsgtgmCFD68E8K2Lnn6xe2XSGEL/X4GeGSMzmdDAfA4afz6Yim77d\nEfe6wu1D3Nz5QXiGVRO/HBmshKISJMWUQqMTWgFNvKRNCLvEx7XZsA7nhHyFX4ze\nAfye8FA33NtpmNiAUTqCHnvkZfDyLecjQ4Opo0okdf9UWCrCxEz6g5Jw3RBOfURj\nWQeVR92b6KXzCDVgHV+ue3WAUPYxNt4BX4NJ0DOjaDZq2pwRAKFui9IwP5aOFZEn\nM+O+GEogJq/hdJBt2a2US6PvO1DSSZqKtz8rVGQ34loopSaHNtXTNxb+45I6mqVl\nQOrjK646xSYWGLJ25wRrbUvh1dBu5Yam9LG3Ahshu1xhywWZafk+hxMmtxQbOpK4\n3HmTFIlCml2krjoXLnMp\n=cEUe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7425a8e285cef2688da36c2275d58cdfde66fb64\nparent d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781438776 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781438776 +0300\n\nfix(fleet): cap auto-upgrade re-queue with a per-(node,target) attempt budget (CAURA-000) (#351)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements **L1** from the auto-upgrade re-queue bug investigation: a\nbackend-side attempt budget that stops the gate from re-queuing deploys\nindefinitely against a node that never converges to the target version.\n\nToday `_maybe_queue_auto_upgrade` has no attempt budget. Its only brakes\nare the 10-min in-flight window (stops *concurrent* storms only), the\nplugin-signalled `deploy_blocked_until` cooldown, and the hardcoded\n`KNOWN_BROKEN` set. A node that never converges is re-queued **every\nheartbeat (~60s ≈ 1,440/day)** with no brake and no operator-visible\nsignal — for any failure mode the plugin can't self-detect.\n\n## Validated failure modes (all un-braked today)\n\n| Mode | Plugin writes cooldown? |\n|---|---|\n| Persistent `/plugin-source` fetch error (`fetchOk=false`) | **No** —\n`status=failed`, no cooldown |\n| Unsafe-filename manifest abort | **No** |\n| **\"Succeeds but never advances\"** — served manifest version < gate's\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED` | **No** — every deploy builds, restarts,\npost-restart-verifies OK (clears cooldown), yet backend still sees\n`plugin_version < target` → re-queues forever, each attempt reporting\n*success* |\n\nThe plugin's 24h cooldown only covers its *own* self-detected failures\n(`build-failed`, `post-restart-version-mismatch`). `command_result`\nrecords failed deploys but feeds nothing back into the gate. Confirmed:\nno per-(node,target) counter anywhere.\n\n## Fix (backend-only)\n\nAfter `AUTO_UPGRADE_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (5) deploys for the same\n`target_version` within `AUTO_UPGRADE_ATTEMPT_WINDOW` (24h), the gate\nstops queuing and logs a `warning` for operator follow-up. Brakes **all\nthree** modes at the source — independent of plugin self-detection.\n\n- **New repo method** `count_recent_deploys_for_target(node_id,\ntarget_version, since)` — counts ALL statuses (the nastiest mode is\n`status=done` with no version progress; a status filter would miss it).\nJSONB `payload->>'target_version'` filter excludes manual/non-auto\ndeploys.\n- **New gate branch** placed *after* the in-flight check (rarest path)\nso the count query only runs on outdated-eligible-and-not-in-flight\nheartbeats. **Fail-open on DB error**, matching the in-flight check.\n\n### Why it's invisible to healthy upgrades\nA legitimate upgrade converges in **one** attempt — the next heartbeat\nreports the new version and the gate exits at the `_semver_lt` check\n*before* the budget is ever consulted. Keying on `target_version` means\na **new release (bumped target) gets a fresh budget** automatically;\nonly a non-advancing node accumulates >1 row for a given target.\n\n## Performance / load (asked during review)\n\n- **Agent turn path:** untouched — zero latency impact.\n- **Steady-state (converged fleet):** zero — the gate short-circuits at\n`_semver_lt` before any DB work.\n- **Wedged node:** large load **reduction** — ~1,440 command-inserts +\nrestart cycles/day collapse to 5.\n\nThe new query is one indexed SELECT, only on outdated-eligible\nheartbeats; `has_recent_in_flight_deploy` is left untouched (lower blast\nradius than folding the two into one query).\n\n## Production context\n\nValidated read-only on the customer prod box: the gap is **currently\nlatent** there — `MIN_RECOMMENDED` == served manifest == `2.9.0`, **0\ndeploy churn in 48h**, fleet converged. This lands as **preventive\nhardening** before the next release bump, where a manifest/target drift\non an on-prem image would re-activate the loop. (The earlier\n1,381-stuck-deploy incident was the pre-#305/#306 ack-storm — already\nresolved, not recurring.)\n\n## Tests\n\n5 new unit tests mirroring the in-flight gate tests:\n- skip-when-exhausted (+ asserts budget is keyed on target_version)\n- allow-under-cap\n- fresh-target-gets-fresh-budget\n- fail-open-on-repo-error\n- constants-are-sane\n\n56/56 in `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`; **126/126** across the\nfleet/heartbeat/repository sweep. `ruff` clean. JSONB query\ncompile-verified to `payload ->> 'target_version'`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **L1 only**, per the agreed gradual plan. L2 (full `nodes.metadata`\nstuck-stamp + UI), L3 (version-consistency guard), L4 (plugin-side\ncooldown on un-braked exits) are deferred. The exhaustion\n`logger.warning` here delivers the cheap ~80% of L2's observability.\n- No plugin change, no version bump, no migration.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 56/56 auto-upgrade unit tests\n- [x] 126/126 fleet/heartbeat/repository sweep\n- [x] ruff check + format clean\n- [x] JSONB query compiles to correct SQL\n- [x] DCO sign-off\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T12:06:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/22a3ac064ecafc912180767890399a2ce93ac531/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1"}]},{"sha":"d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQ2MmMzNmE5ZmE5MDA0MjZkNzAyNzZmMDk1MGRlMzE4ZDFiZGZmYjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T11:17:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T11:17:06Z"},"message":"fix(keystones): let the standalone operator author keystones out-of-the-box (F-7) (#354)\n\n## Summary (audit finding F-7)\n\nOn a fresh **standalone** install, authoring a keystone over REST 403s:\n```\nPOST /api/v1/memclaw/keystones   (X-API-Key: standalone, no X-Agent-ID)\n→ 403 \"Agent 'rest-admin' is not registered. Register the agent by writing one memory first.\"\n```\nA bare standalone request has no caller agent identity, so\n`_resolve_caller_identity` falls back to the synthetic **`rest-admin`**,\nwhich has no agent row → `_require_trust` not_found → 403 with a\nmisleading message. The flagship governance feature looks broken on\nfirst contact.\n\nThe trust gate is **correct and necessary for multi-tenant / gateway**\ndeployments — it's the anti-spoof defense (`_effective_min_for_caller`\nfloor-bump + X-Agent-ID mismatch rejection). But under `IS_STANDALONE`\nthe API-key holder *is* the admin and there's nobody to impersonate, so\nthe gate is pure friction.\n\n## Change (REST keystone route only)\n- **`_is_standalone_admin(auth, x_agent_id)`** — true **only** when\n`IS_STANDALONE` *and* the caller asserts no identity at all (no\nagent-scoped credential, no `X-Agent-ID`). The `upsert`/`delete`\nhandlers skip the caller-trust gate for that caller; storage-side shape\nvalidation (scope/fleet_id/agent_id) still applies.\n- **Reworded the not_found 403** to name the real cause: register the\nagent, or pass `X-Agent-ID` / an agent-scoped credential for an agent at\ntrust ≥ 2.\n\n## Why it's safe (validated against code + tests)\n- **No-op off standalone** — the bypass requires `IS_STANDALONE` *and*\nthe no-identity fallback, so the multi-tenant/gateway anti-spoof\ndefenses are fully intact.\n- **Doesn't disturb existing tests** — audited every keystone endpoint\ncall in `test_api_keystones.py`: all authenticate via the\n`_author_headers` helper (`X-Agent-ID` set), so they hit the\n`x_agent_id` branch, never the `rest-admin` fallback the bypass keys on.\n`test_set_rejected_when_agent_unknown` (X-Agent-ID=`ghost`) still 403s.\n- **No test pins the reworded string** — keystone tests assert only\n`status_code`; the `\"is not registered\"` assertions live on the MCP path\n+ `trust_service`, neither touched.\n- **MCP keystone path unaffected** — it resolves the caller to\n`mcp-agent`, not `rest-admin`.\n\n## Tests\nAdds `test_set_allowed_for_standalone_admin_without_agent_id` — bare\nstandalone admin (no X-Agent-ID) can now author a keystone (200),\nlocking the fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"beb16278548e39175e905cea502b93bd348994c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/beb16278548e39175e905cea502b93bd348994c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLo2yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6fQQAAJU5DwLMwQ3c36o7I9QtwLx\nvcwhAy8L2kpDhAU1J3BWwHLvzu5iI2nDHSQlbWIuXvExDQdpacNdpxtXxFR5gwic\nlAzxLJGMmym37RQsit1SbkF3VTiPfW3ektJ5ftj84ulFU/vGGeE3RLfsv3AsVc2A\nN9+atwSNofCIGZTunnbkHmzbWPRVT++RML4f+bYg3pK0OGtsnNjmePWqzyEtLsly\nPF/d6u7f/G2dGnJVxgLJaN70liKXNvT3+nBzy0HLtSq7eKtVOqO3G2WMaf//Tze0\nWecTvUHesfl1wfPakCV77a9d4YIMqU2MfsjDBrwJ2Y+X7JRFaHi5PjutemrDAYdN\nDWUtnsexLcTlfAUREP+JmSlokl7IVZwGXY8ycPW6Gs+fWHy+sLBGoac5JiepyvGQ\nXLmPkI9vnOXd2dUIruamVmQovBPO7vnKTg6omcnkvFBTvTpy1J7PKUQOmOMqfLkV\nxphsKvPHY9rCseWjgAzkOO3wFp1ZY6AxFVW8NEKpBDhbBAwh0r71KucP6P2ueKCj\nVK3+ztPmI18Ncz9KN7iUpiwnmjYr3fwcsSYA92vuXgUeB6bKrEEUTjuIe+Y84+DQ\n82P3zKD51IKHGqLxD0yaCp8lbvrRxZKL4E7FTVKQEqTbFuHNWyRnGzHSjb+ZEbkd\nZBTjDCB8q6G8+yElXBsW\n=BD2J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree beb16278548e39175e905cea502b93bd348994c0\nparent 0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781435826 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781435826 +0300\n\nfix(keystones): let the standalone operator author keystones out-of-the-box (F-7) (#354)\n\n## Summary (audit finding F-7)\n\nOn a fresh **standalone** install, authoring a keystone over REST 403s:\n```\nPOST /api/v1/memclaw/keystones   (X-API-Key: standalone, no X-Agent-ID)\n→ 403 \"Agent 'rest-admin' is not registered. Register the agent by writing one memory first.\"\n```\nA bare standalone request has no caller agent identity, so\n`_resolve_caller_identity` falls back to the synthetic **`rest-admin`**,\nwhich has no agent row → `_require_trust` not_found → 403 with a\nmisleading message. The flagship governance feature looks broken on\nfirst contact.\n\nThe trust gate is **correct and necessary for multi-tenant / gateway**\ndeployments — it's the anti-spoof defense (`_effective_min_for_caller`\nfloor-bump + X-Agent-ID mismatch rejection). But under `IS_STANDALONE`\nthe API-key holder *is* the admin and there's nobody to impersonate, so\nthe gate is pure friction.\n\n## Change (REST keystone route only)\n- **`_is_standalone_admin(auth, x_agent_id)`** — true **only** when\n`IS_STANDALONE` *and* the caller asserts no identity at all (no\nagent-scoped credential, no `X-Agent-ID`). The `upsert`/`delete`\nhandlers skip the caller-trust gate for that caller; storage-side shape\nvalidation (scope/fleet_id/agent_id) still applies.\n- **Reworded the not_found 403** to name the real cause: register the\nagent, or pass `X-Agent-ID` / an agent-scoped credential for an agent at\ntrust ≥ 2.\n\n## Why it's safe (validated against code + tests)\n- **No-op off standalone** — the bypass requires `IS_STANDALONE` *and*\nthe no-identity fallback, so the multi-tenant/gateway anti-spoof\ndefenses are fully intact.\n- **Doesn't disturb existing tests** — audited every keystone endpoint\ncall in `test_api_keystones.py`: all authenticate via the\n`_author_headers` helper (`X-Agent-ID` set), so they hit the\n`x_agent_id` branch, never the `rest-admin` fallback the bypass keys on.\n`test_set_rejected_when_agent_unknown` (X-Agent-ID=`ghost`) still 403s.\n- **No test pins the reworded string** — keystone tests assert only\n`status_code`; the `\"is not registered\"` assertions live on the MCP path\n+ `trust_service`, neither touched.\n- **MCP keystone path unaffected** — it resolves the caller to\n`mcp-agent`, not `rest-admin`.\n\n## Tests\nAdds `test_set_allowed_for_standalone_admin_without_agent_id` — bare\nstandalone admin (no X-Agent-ID) can now author a keystone (200),\nlocking the fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T11:17:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d62c36a9fa900426d70276f0950de318d1bdffb1/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75"}]},{"sha":"0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA0MjFjZWIwYWRkYWRkNzE4MzNmMmRkY2U0MmNmOTczZWRkOWZkNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T11:05:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T11:05:16Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): capability-usage adoption counters (MCP + REST) (#353)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a lightweight **capability-usage** signal: which product\ncapabilities (recall, write, search, doc, keystones, …) get used, broken\ndown by access path (MCP vs REST) and attributable per org, persisted to\na queryable table.\n\n### How\n\n- **`capability_usage` table** (migration `023` +\n`common.models.CapabilityUsage`) — append-only aggregate counters. No\nunique constraint and no upsert: each instance appends its own rows and\nconsumers `SUM` at query time (contention-free). Deliberately\ncross-tenant analytics, so no RLS.\n- **In-process aggregator** (`services/capability_usage.py`) folds each\noperation into per-`(tenant, capability, op, transport, minute-bucket)`\ncounters and flushes on a short interval (default 15s; final flush on\nshutdown). The request hot path pays only a dict update — never a DB\nwrite. `record_usage()` is a no-op when unwired and never raises into a\nrequest.\n- **MCP emitter**: `call_tool` is overridden on the FastMCP instance —\nthe single dispatch point every `tools/call` routes through — so the\ntool name (capability) and `op` argument are captured without touching\nany handler's signature (generated input schemas are unchanged).\n- **REST emitter**: `RequestObservationMiddleware` maps the matched\nroute template → `(capability, op)` and records `transport=rest`. It\nalso emits one structured `http.request` log line per request (route\ntemplate, method, status, duration). Registered innermost so the route\ntemplate is reliably readable.\n- `get_auth_context` stashes the resolved `tenant_id` on `request.state`\nso emitters can attribute usage to an org.\n\nGated by `capability_usage_enabled` (default on). No new dependencies.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The middleware is registered **innermost** on purpose:\n`SlowAPIMiddleware` is a `BaseHTTPMiddleware`, which runs the downstream\napp in a separate task, so `scope[\"route\"]` set by the router does not\nreliably propagate to a middleware outside it. Sitting innermost\nguarantees the template resolves. Trade-off: it does not observe 504/429\nfrom the outer middlewares (those requests didn't execute a capability\nanyway).\n- On Cloud Logging deployments the `http.request` events can also back a\nlog-based metric; on file-logging deployments they land in the JSON log\nfile. The capability counters are independent of log level.\n\n### Testing\n\n- Unit tests for the aggregator (folding, non-tenant filtering, drain,\ninterval flush) and both emitters (`tests/test_capability_usage.py`,\n`tests/test_request_observation.py`).\n- Verified end-to-end against a live stack: migration applies in the\nfull chain; REST and MCP both record correct\ncapability/op/transport/duration; the transport `CHECK` constraint and\nthe adoption `GROUP BY capability, transport` query work against\nPostgres.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6b1fbb7c6ff1911802d755df6d3e505340f90cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d6b1fbb7c6ff1911802d755df6d3e505340f90cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLortCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO0gQABNylbYJcHXDOzNDOz2ppyCl\nTbmgdvObc0lK9sTCZhhv3R72FWR1z7ladv79/cQ0+QFT43NpknlKGsHJGfPgUHHC\nXDbfNpP7SECNXsJdzZJbZi8V+u9qxcThQgavDLodKJTrVh/pwIpc9CVTd37+PuC9\nuEHylncw4fYyw7vGg0dvmgnUGvycPWX8JCYyKG3VnN9GCNVkBGMiJ/MLcXEcxLKy\nzCqTO6zR+U6mE/K38j0w4d8fZwgYfsGgCUgQemI9uNWfQBpE3MTHHR5gGysmZomN\nk6ANqYs63unRPfP8pG0XIoJ8T7A7Ng58Ej/wyGfzl0gJCDOfgBQDvf4DoMqKh6wa\nmgY+ubLut6NwrEfAqfwYOHUfUsFrHNi40rY/7aQhO8VFMHRd2x1wCEqWjnIldF1q\n6zsnvWhU629AmOf96W1uFNLIvEjsayr2HVtXHrw0/9HOaCitCq/bJXj07qK/ln1B\nDD3r/Asm0C4ncyzAuIlMWNJi+TWUsRPG3bKlxa6BpmwNHKcmCyqSO19TCQNbo0k6\n25FojxF3Yi1+KsUFc+VGucd/65Fhm0A2KHoFvncnaTFbdb0v2shF2I2G9ChIg9R9\nppVk8YigxtAL2TBi3PKsPlF95oLLOFW5e3dJzenv3O6+6bBn0utB3GPhlmrvj2Kl\nedKwO77Atst4cX10KNJJ\n=cvR8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d6b1fbb7c6ff1911802d755df6d3e505340f90cd\nparent bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1781435116 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781435116 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): capability-usage adoption counters (MCP + REST) (#353)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a lightweight **capability-usage** signal: which product\ncapabilities (recall, write, search, doc, keystones, …) get used, broken\ndown by access path (MCP vs REST) and attributable per org, persisted to\na queryable table.\n\n### How\n\n- **`capability_usage` table** (migration `023` +\n`common.models.CapabilityUsage`) — append-only aggregate counters. No\nunique constraint and no upsert: each instance appends its own rows and\nconsumers `SUM` at query time (contention-free). Deliberately\ncross-tenant analytics, so no RLS.\n- **In-process aggregator** (`services/capability_usage.py`) folds each\noperation into per-`(tenant, capability, op, transport, minute-bucket)`\ncounters and flushes on a short interval (default 15s; final flush on\nshutdown). The request hot path pays only a dict update — never a DB\nwrite. `record_usage()` is a no-op when unwired and never raises into a\nrequest.\n- **MCP emitter**: `call_tool` is overridden on the FastMCP instance —\nthe single dispatch point every `tools/call` routes through — so the\ntool name (capability) and `op` argument are captured without touching\nany handler's signature (generated input schemas are unchanged).\n- **REST emitter**: `RequestObservationMiddleware` maps the matched\nroute template → `(capability, op)` and records `transport=rest`. It\nalso emits one structured `http.request` log line per request (route\ntemplate, method, status, duration). Registered innermost so the route\ntemplate is reliably readable.\n- `get_auth_context` stashes the resolved `tenant_id` on `request.state`\nso emitters can attribute usage to an org.\n\nGated by `capability_usage_enabled` (default on). No new dependencies.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The middleware is registered **innermost** on purpose:\n`SlowAPIMiddleware` is a `BaseHTTPMiddleware`, which runs the downstream\napp in a separate task, so `scope[\"route\"]` set by the router does not\nreliably propagate to a middleware outside it. Sitting innermost\nguarantees the template resolves. Trade-off: it does not observe 504/429\nfrom the outer middlewares (those requests didn't execute a capability\nanyway).\n- On Cloud Logging deployments the `http.request` events can also back a\nlog-based metric; on file-logging deployments they land in the JSON log\nfile. The capability counters are independent of log level.\n\n### Testing\n\n- Unit tests for the aggregator (folding, non-tenant filtering, drain,\ninterval flush) and both emitters (`tests/test_capability_usage.py`,\n`tests/test_request_observation.py`).\n- Verified end-to-end against a live stack: migration applies in the\nfull chain; REST and MCP both record correct\ncapability/op/transport/duration; the transport `CHECK` constraint and\nthe adoption `GROUP BY capability, transport` query work against\nPostgres.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T11:05:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0421ceb0addadd71833f2ddce42cf973edd9fd75/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492"}]},{"sha":"bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJiZTQ3MWI0ODhiMmZjMmU0NzRjZDIzNTlmZjcwZTllMmFkNTI0OTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:56:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:56:42Z"},"message":"feat: add @caura/memclaw-client TypeScript SDK (#356)\n\n## What\n\nThe TypeScript/JavaScript client for MemClaw, in `clients/typescript/` —\na faithful port of the [Python\nclient](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/tree/main/clients/python).\n\n```ts\nimport { MemClaw } from \"@caura/memclaw-client\";\nconst mc = new MemClaw(\"mc_xxx\", { tenantId: \"my-team\", agentId: \"my-agent\" });\nawait mc.write(\"Q3 revenue target is $4M.\");\nconsole.log((await mc.recall(\"Q3 revenue target\")).summary);\n```\n\n- `write`/`search`/`recall`/`health`, typed interfaces, typed errors\n(`AuthError`/`NotFoundError`/`MemClawApiError`), `.raw` on every result.\n- **Zero runtime deps** — native `fetch` (Node 18+), ESM, built with\n`tsc` (repo convention).\n- Rich `package.json` metadata; README funnel gains a TypeScript\nsnippet.\n\n## Name\n\nShips as **`@caura/memclaw-client`**: the `plugin/` package already owns\n`@caura/memclaw`, and unscoped `memclaw` is taken on npm by an unrelated\nproject. (Parallels PyPI `memclaw-client`.)\n\n## CI / verification\n\n- New **Client (TypeScript) CI** workflow: `npm test` (= `tsc` build +\n`node --test`) on changes under `clients/typescript/`. Tests mock\n`fetch` (no network). **Verified locally: 9/9 pass, build clean.**\n- **Wet-tested against a live local stack** (core-api): `health()` and\n`write()` round-tripped successfully (real 201 + memory id); a 503/401\nfrom the server mapped correctly to typed errors. `search`/`recall`\nreached the endpoint with valid auth but the local stack's embedding\nservice was down (503) — a server/env condition, not a client issue;\ntheir response parsing is covered by the unit tests.\n- Root CI untouched (root pytest only runs `tests/`).\n\n## Publishing (maintainer action — not done here)\n\nAdds `publish-npm-client.yml` (npm publish on a `memclaw-client-ts-v*`\ntag or manual dispatch, with provenance). One-time setup (`@caura` scope\naccess + `NPM_TOKEN`) is documented in the workflow header. I did\n**not** publish.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9850a7ec1d58174f5c794ecf81049bcb756402a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a9850a7ec1d58174f5c794ecf81049bcb756402a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLojqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA39gQAA8B+S8d67EAeBMRa44jr3WK\nbLi4cd6EOeiFljFkiOIpVvKwDvwgfiKb2A06qCrQR2gjWgLEXiAJKJyt8C47ZEHV\nbNHGaQDjqiYRw4Ypb60xRcetk+yToW9AQHh7Dazi9xoo0T7OCHksthQtUTZjci/u\npGjaA9IBOBIXPyta0xCtT7FG9MQ5ry08Uu4QDSZmVWh6wbe19YWWCpfE/aiS2VS9\nNKVoIWDfSB8eucI0RJGmXmRpnDNsToiS8h3aqZb57khDxwm2hhKWK58CtqM0pGZ2\nsehcn2xSJiIeMRAoR0ReJjT+9od72Z/5dKZH5+k8kp/l7+G+LeKPTQnGTgDZ+jMy\nGYW4n18f27WThXfOMwWmOZMDTgOvFVVGEnvKdEqZaOQ5wbOyLA2PpUPEhpzvXEzs\nKfFIXxgKApEbtquxS+U/XnEb687yNYeMrGMFflmTjXnbtjq4dN3hYgcfoRCrSN28\nmiIUj9hX8XmYFYA0U740JE/EmGs/GG+eu/RJMN4Kfq9bZjisKuAbMmxYzuFWPTFg\ngK6D4Uv5KueeqD1geFysVeS8OB1nr/TKykV0r0c/evjrpRWaWCECRuPuM8Qfs+Pi\nenkY4BnZqe5f1b7Ult2gukA9wC/+vqTnLSAclg9lmf5z3py15E7lH+HzJRzopZ0Z\nIs//tKdtYAzOJ5Ky4F4V\n=frgx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9850a7ec1d58174f5c794ecf81049bcb756402a\nparent a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781434602 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781434602 +0300\n\nfeat: add @caura/memclaw-client TypeScript SDK (#356)\n\n## What\n\nThe TypeScript/JavaScript client for MemClaw, in `clients/typescript/` —\na faithful port of the [Python\nclient](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/tree/main/clients/python).\n\n```ts\nimport { MemClaw } from \"@caura/memclaw-client\";\nconst mc = new MemClaw(\"mc_xxx\", { tenantId: \"my-team\", agentId: \"my-agent\" });\nawait mc.write(\"Q3 revenue target is $4M.\");\nconsole.log((await mc.recall(\"Q3 revenue target\")).summary);\n```\n\n- `write`/`search`/`recall`/`health`, typed interfaces, typed errors\n(`AuthError`/`NotFoundError`/`MemClawApiError`), `.raw` on every result.\n- **Zero runtime deps** — native `fetch` (Node 18+), ESM, built with\n`tsc` (repo convention).\n- Rich `package.json` metadata; README funnel gains a TypeScript\nsnippet.\n\n## Name\n\nShips as **`@caura/memclaw-client`**: the `plugin/` package already owns\n`@caura/memclaw`, and unscoped `memclaw` is taken on npm by an unrelated\nproject. (Parallels PyPI `memclaw-client`.)\n\n## CI / verification\n\n- New **Client (TypeScript) CI** workflow: `npm test` (= `tsc` build +\n`node --test`) on changes under `clients/typescript/`. Tests mock\n`fetch` (no network). **Verified locally: 9/9 pass, build clean.**\n- **Wet-tested against a live local stack** (core-api): `health()` and\n`write()` round-tripped successfully (real 201 + memory id); a 503/401\nfrom the server mapped correctly to typed errors. `search`/`recall`\nreached the endpoint with valid auth but the local stack's embedding\nservice was down (503) — a server/env condition, not a client issue;\ntheir response parsing is covered by the unit tests.\n- Root CI untouched (root pytest only runs `tests/`).\n\n## Publishing (maintainer action — not done here)\n\nAdds `publish-npm-client.yml` (npm publish on a `memclaw-client-ts-v*`\ntag or manual dispatch, with provenance). One-time setup (`@caura` scope\naccess + `NPM_TOKEN`) is documented in the workflow header. I did\n**not** publish.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T10:56:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bbe471b488b2fc2e474cd2359ff70e9e2ad52492/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934"}]},{"sha":"a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGE0NTE1ZWQxZTVmNWY3Njc5ZGFlYTM2Yzk5ZTU4ZDFkMzMxYjM5MzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:52:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:52:07Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): send X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header on bulk memory writes (#355)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe OpenClaw MemClaw plugin's `memclaw_write` tool sends batch writes\n(when an `items` array is provided) to `POST /memories/bulk`, but\n**never sends the `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id` header that endpoint has required\nsince CAURA-602**. The server rejects the request with **HTTP 400\n`\"Missing required X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"`**, so every agent-driven\n*batch* write fails outright. Single-item writes (`POST /memories`) are\nunaffected.\n\nThis is impactful because models frequently route a single fact through\nthe batch path (passing `items` rather than `content`), so in practice\n`memclaw_write` can fail on the very first write attempt.\n\n## How it was found\n\nWet-testing the plugin against **memclaw.net** from an OpenClaw agent:\nevery `memclaw_write` via the batch path returned `HTTP 400 \"Missing\nrequired X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"`. Reproduced directly:\n\n```\nPOST /api/v1/memories/bulk          (no header)            → 400 \"Missing required X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"\nPOST /api/v1/memories/bulk          (+ X-Bulk-Attempt-Id)  → 200\nPOST /api/v1/memories  (single)     (no header)            → 201\n```\n\nThen **confirmed on a freshly-rebuilt local `core-api`** (same result,\nbyte-identical error) — so this is the server's intended contract, not a\nprod-only quirk. The bug is entirely on the **client/plugin** side.\n\n## Root cause\n\nServer (`core-api/src/core_api/routes/memories.py:1089-1097`) requires\nthe header for non-`install_credential` callers:\n\n```python\nif not bulk_attempt_id:\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=400,\n        detail=f\"Missing required {BULK_ATTEMPT_ID_HEADER} header\")\n```\n\nIt's the **per-attempt idempotency key** (CAURA-602): the server derives\neach row's `client_request_id` from `${X-Bulk-Attempt-Id}:${index}`, so\na retry with the same id resolves committed rows as `duplicate_attempt`\ninstead of duplicating them.\n\nNotably the server's **MCP path is immune** —\n`core-api/.../mcp_server.py` auto-generates\n`bulk_attempt_id=f\"mcp:{uuid4()}\"`. Only the **REST** bulk path requires\nthe caller to supply it, and the plugin writes via REST:\n\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.ts` → `memclaw_write` batch branch →\n`apiCall(\"POST\", \"/memories/bulk\", …)`\n- `plugin/src/transport.ts` → `apiCall` only ever set `Content-Type` +\n`X-API-Key`; no mechanism to add the header.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **`transport.ts`** — add an optional `extraHeaders` arg to `apiCall`,\nmerged into the request headers after the defaults. It is also\n**forwarded on the internal 401-retry**, so the retry reuses the same\nattempt id (a fresh id would defeat the server's bulk de-dup).\n2. **`tool-definitions.ts`** — in the `memclaw_write` batch branch,\ngenerate **one `randomUUID()` per tool invocation** and pass it as\n`X-Bulk-Attempt-Id`. One id per call (not per HTTP attempt) keeps the\nidempotency semantics intact, mirroring the server's own MCP path.\n\nSingle-item writes (`POST /memories`) are left unchanged — they never\nrequired the header.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds two cases to `plugin/src/transport.test.ts`:\n- `extraHeaders` are merged into the outgoing request headers (and the\ndefault `X-API-Key` / `Content-Type` still ride along).\n- omitting `extraHeaders` sends no `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id`.\n\nVerified locally: `transport.test.js` 13/13 pass,\n`tool-definitions.test.js` 24/24 pass, `tsc` clean.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Versioning/CHANGELOG are owned by release-please; intentionally not\nbumped here. The `fix:` type drives the patch release.\n- `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id` is validated server-side against\n`^[A-Za-z0-9._:\\-]{1,128}$`; a bare `randomUUID()` (36 chars, hex +\nhyphens) satisfies this.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"055b9ccc0b642752ebc7f9a3efe4f0b2bf57ac60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/055b9ccc0b642752ebc7f9a3efe4f0b2bf57ac60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLofXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWxoQAEwwYJJArIrPzYZzScyS4/Sb\nXkJOmnMk/oJouaoobCVJmXpkpyTXufxITchEI6yTCGZPPk7l5BPDaj+23joSel41\n9rN1mRmEacUXU/d2hB77f2zs9XPwgDti2W2Ec0WnT9JsZ/nwyLXoQfgRWotONU2H\nyfxdYiWDuaehkOjEFAPXRlUOlHVNtQ/4CMSwmBJi0WBevqGDHR89McXRFoo8K4Ma\nWRWlsih5gAkCfFVP8T10e+eMW3bthM3K192Bo84//qXLLPa5gDld8Ig309gy5TVI\nwAy3MpNs7Z6o+mVE2D5j3RTw0E+LZamr2nQyhsQJHqkPZeg8yNrwHha3TUtImKvo\naW8huO2pF4jvNXvrxwBwcKc2Gfz6tGVPnMeuwkhzI+3u5l9Ql52RxC501aUY2PaQ\ncfhyjjaFcpYgF/KJQ1XA7ESZDOznzqf/4hH9vgBw+8u3fn0nMaaqxj5YR+UUDRJ+\npPIcXKoQJUV3tsbgEGMlXs58AS7OYAsU1nN8Vdp4U1/GFO0JVDo+Kvrz4FHOlL+i\n0lDvxkEn74G2whCnexMKAB18I2UbyQi1JQ9EJk43Vk29JZ1dlS6TlKmukpAJXc0A\n98vSCowQtVHFX5jx0u+PPu8Xcn0d0jUdZubWv4VfiMzCeYGsNjIlJknYLdohkZeh\nAbFv3uZY40lnc5eOU2dN\n=tyLe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 055b9ccc0b642752ebc7f9a3efe4f0b2bf57ac60\nparent 3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781434327 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781434327 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): send X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header on bulk memory writes (#355)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe OpenClaw MemClaw plugin's `memclaw_write` tool sends batch writes\n(when an `items` array is provided) to `POST /memories/bulk`, but\n**never sends the `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id` header that endpoint has required\nsince CAURA-602**. The server rejects the request with **HTTP 400\n`\"Missing required X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"`**, so every agent-driven\n*batch* write fails outright. Single-item writes (`POST /memories`) are\nunaffected.\n\nThis is impactful because models frequently route a single fact through\nthe batch path (passing `items` rather than `content`), so in practice\n`memclaw_write` can fail on the very first write attempt.\n\n## How it was found\n\nWet-testing the plugin against **memclaw.net** from an OpenClaw agent:\nevery `memclaw_write` via the batch path returned `HTTP 400 \"Missing\nrequired X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"`. Reproduced directly:\n\n```\nPOST /api/v1/memories/bulk          (no header)            → 400 \"Missing required X-Bulk-Attempt-Id header\"\nPOST /api/v1/memories/bulk          (+ X-Bulk-Attempt-Id)  → 200\nPOST /api/v1/memories  (single)     (no header)            → 201\n```\n\nThen **confirmed on a freshly-rebuilt local `core-api`** (same result,\nbyte-identical error) — so this is the server's intended contract, not a\nprod-only quirk. The bug is entirely on the **client/plugin** side.\n\n## Root cause\n\nServer (`core-api/src/core_api/routes/memories.py:1089-1097`) requires\nthe header for non-`install_credential` callers:\n\n```python\nif not bulk_attempt_id:\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=400,\n        detail=f\"Missing required {BULK_ATTEMPT_ID_HEADER} header\")\n```\n\nIt's the **per-attempt idempotency key** (CAURA-602): the server derives\neach row's `client_request_id` from `${X-Bulk-Attempt-Id}:${index}`, so\na retry with the same id resolves committed rows as `duplicate_attempt`\ninstead of duplicating them.\n\nNotably the server's **MCP path is immune** —\n`core-api/.../mcp_server.py` auto-generates\n`bulk_attempt_id=f\"mcp:{uuid4()}\"`. Only the **REST** bulk path requires\nthe caller to supply it, and the plugin writes via REST:\n\n- `plugin/src/tool-definitions.ts` → `memclaw_write` batch branch →\n`apiCall(\"POST\", \"/memories/bulk\", …)`\n- `plugin/src/transport.ts` → `apiCall` only ever set `Content-Type` +\n`X-API-Key`; no mechanism to add the header.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **`transport.ts`** — add an optional `extraHeaders` arg to `apiCall`,\nmerged into the request headers after the defaults. It is also\n**forwarded on the internal 401-retry**, so the retry reuses the same\nattempt id (a fresh id would defeat the server's bulk de-dup).\n2. **`tool-definitions.ts`** — in the `memclaw_write` batch branch,\ngenerate **one `randomUUID()` per tool invocation** and pass it as\n`X-Bulk-Attempt-Id`. One id per call (not per HTTP attempt) keeps the\nidempotency semantics intact, mirroring the server's own MCP path.\n\nSingle-item writes (`POST /memories`) are left unchanged — they never\nrequired the header.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds two cases to `plugin/src/transport.test.ts`:\n- `extraHeaders` are merged into the outgoing request headers (and the\ndefault `X-API-Key` / `Content-Type` still ride along).\n- omitting `extraHeaders` sends no `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id`.\n\nVerified locally: `transport.test.js` 13/13 pass,\n`tool-definitions.test.js` 24/24 pass, `tsc` clean.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Versioning/CHANGELOG are owned by release-please; intentionally not\nbumped here. The `fix:` type drives the patch release.\n- `X-Bulk-Attempt-Id` is validated server-side against\n`^[A-Za-z0-9._:\\-]{1,128}$`; a bare `randomUUID()` (36 chars, hex +\nhyphens) satisfies this.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T10:52:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a4515ed1e5f5f7679daea36c99e58d1d331b3934/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b"}]},{"sha":"3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNhYzBmMzcyZThkNDU0YTkxYjhkYzNjNWFmMTk1MmE2YzI5NTcyOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:10:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T10:10:39Z"},"message":"feat: add memclaw-client Python SDK (#352)\n\n## What\n\nA thin Python client SDK for MemClaw, packaged as **`memclaw-client`**\nfor PyPI. Lives in `clients/python/`.\n\n```python\nfrom memclaw_client import MemClaw\nmc = MemClaw(\"mc_xxx\", tenant_id=\"my-team\", agent_id=\"my-agent\")\nmc.write(\"Q3 revenue target is $4M.\")\nprint(mc.recall(\"Q3 revenue target\").summary)\n```\n\n- `write` → `POST /api/v1/memories`, `search` → `POST /api/v1/search`,\n`recall` → `POST /api/v1/recall`, `health` → `GET /api/v1/health`.\n- Single dependency (`httpx`), typed (ships `py.typed`),\ncontext-manager, typed exceptions\n(`AuthError`/`NotFoundError`/`MemClawAPIError`), `.raw` on every result.\n- Rich PyPI metadata (description, keywords, classifiers, project URLs).\n- README gains a **Python client** quickstart funnel (`pip install\nmemclaw-client`).\n\n## Why\n\nFrom the OSS SEO/adoption review (Gap 1 — install funnel): evaluating\nMemClaw previously meant `git clone` + Docker, with no `pip install`\none-liner. Competitors' growth is built on exactly that. This gives the\nlowest-friction path for talking to a deployment.\n\n## Naming\n\n`memclaw` is already taken on PyPI **and** npm by unrelated projects, so\nthe package ships as **`memclaw-client`** (import `memclaw_client`). The\nTS/npm client (`@caura/memclaw`) is a planned follow-up.\n\n## CI / verification\n\n- New **Client (Python) CI** workflow runs `ruff` + `pytest` on changes\nunder `clients/python/`. Tests are fully mocked with\n`httpx.MockTransport` (no network/DB). **Verified locally: 10 passed,\nruff clean.**\n- The root CI (core services) is untouched — root pytest only runs\n`tests/`, so this doesn't affect the backend suite.\n\n## Publishing (maintainer action — not done here)\n\nAdds a `publish-python-client.yml` workflow using PyPI **trusted\npublishing** (OIDC, no token), triggered by a `memclaw-client-v*` tag or\nmanual dispatch. One-time setup (create the PyPI project +\ntrusted-publisher + `pypi` environment) is documented in the workflow\nheader. I did **not** publish — that's a maintainer action requiring the\norg's PyPI access.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"99e18149c8b5ead7cb7d44ec774b05651e2ad660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/99e18149c8b5ead7cb7d44ec774b05651e2ad660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLn4fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk7gQAEGGczFSudSTblAH9xOaQLbi\n3IxZug4ccKy0NklfwkPFrRevJGpxA6MyiNisYP5vB8dfxBKy/Oa3jMsIkHQnxGnI\n8A2UW2HhD4Bwb0baf1cmt3rHuvz4rcTPUhggc5/zfgbxeC/WEAKyVfE8uFJQyLBJ\nX1t6TznbQQ1M04CmJ1/Jc65+bIQ0Fr3SQ/7E7x/2IN/jX2kJxgZi1c6p+ov4q0/+\nmdRnp711uMNwm2it4mvusKpIVv41F+8Oj8UxM2ck6q6GiCImVnGftuX0oVSuoUen\nIQwmdFgtMKWpYFefevxg+T+90GmO8waNdVUAMh5GNa5W9m0+GpYZY7LvAak2NThf\ndSyHt2wJyuP2+6FMSu5klUnTbW28V676rJ+GMAxmyYeP4WA7qJCpzRs1hH1hL26H\ne+rYkWmnWIzaIZbuea7M/IUl3wrEs78ay4KM0xKMZ14bSjNLIVfuR8IgaLcsaeSo\naHPj43wkZG3kDp1/YuCvVM4w026A2E9N4oiJRhoBAAJtPFrHZdN0RUQ4CPE05Mhh\nwQD3njGf2QyFmm7DYeP184a/uK97ZJ2Les485GZke2LR/NAfKOXB25O60pAJIQTO\nXewVsdAcYxa2XkzVLW+ZfGr/aH5a3sBDzShI8Eo+gfcKRNhlL/9FuWl40JNgf00D\noVz20bVKEP80JwlM1gjB\n=PfCv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 99e18149c8b5ead7cb7d44ec774b05651e2ad660\nparent 8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781431839 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781431839 +0300\n\nfeat: add memclaw-client Python SDK (#352)\n\n## What\n\nA thin Python client SDK for MemClaw, packaged as **`memclaw-client`**\nfor PyPI. Lives in `clients/python/`.\n\n```python\nfrom memclaw_client import MemClaw\nmc = MemClaw(\"mc_xxx\", tenant_id=\"my-team\", agent_id=\"my-agent\")\nmc.write(\"Q3 revenue target is $4M.\")\nprint(mc.recall(\"Q3 revenue target\").summary)\n```\n\n- `write` → `POST /api/v1/memories`, `search` → `POST /api/v1/search`,\n`recall` → `POST /api/v1/recall`, `health` → `GET /api/v1/health`.\n- Single dependency (`httpx`), typed (ships `py.typed`),\ncontext-manager, typed exceptions\n(`AuthError`/`NotFoundError`/`MemClawAPIError`), `.raw` on every result.\n- Rich PyPI metadata (description, keywords, classifiers, project URLs).\n- README gains a **Python client** quickstart funnel (`pip install\nmemclaw-client`).\n\n## Why\n\nFrom the OSS SEO/adoption review (Gap 1 — install funnel): evaluating\nMemClaw previously meant `git clone` + Docker, with no `pip install`\none-liner. Competitors' growth is built on exactly that. This gives the\nlowest-friction path for talking to a deployment.\n\n## Naming\n\n`memclaw` is already taken on PyPI **and** npm by unrelated projects, so\nthe package ships as **`memclaw-client`** (import `memclaw_client`). The\nTS/npm client (`@caura/memclaw`) is a planned follow-up.\n\n## CI / verification\n\n- New **Client (Python) CI** workflow runs `ruff` + `pytest` on changes\nunder `clients/python/`. Tests are fully mocked with\n`httpx.MockTransport` (no network/DB). **Verified locally: 10 passed,\nruff clean.**\n- The root CI (core services) is untouched — root pytest only runs\n`tests/`, so this doesn't affect the backend suite.\n\n## Publishing (maintainer action — not done here)\n\nAdds a `publish-python-client.yml` workflow using PyPI **trusted\npublishing** (OIDC, no token), triggered by a `memclaw-client-v*` tag or\nmanual dispatch. One-time setup (create the PyPI project +\ntrusted-publisher + `pypi` environment) is documented in the workflow\nheader. I did **not** publish — that's a maintainer action requiring the\norg's PyPI access.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T10:10:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ac0f372e8d454a91b8dc3c5af1952a6c295728b/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1"}]},{"sha":"8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhhYjk1ZDhlNDE2ODYyMTUzNDEwOTQyYmRmMWJmY2Y1MWZjYWQyYzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T08:42:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T08:42:20Z"},"message":"fix(compose): stop shadowing .env provider keys with empty \"${VAR:-}\" passthroughs (#346)\n\n## Summary\n\n`core-api` already loads `.env` through `env_file`, but the\n`environment:` block re-declared the provider/embedding vars as\n`\"${VAR:-}\"`. Docker Compose resolves `${...}` from the operator's\n**shell** with precedence over `.env`, which causes two real failures:\n\n1. **Empty-string injection.** When a var is set only in `.env`, the\n`${VAR:-}` passthrough injects an empty string that *overrides* it. This\nis the class behind the `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` → `400 \"you must\nprovide a model parameter\"` break (the code's `os.environ.get(...) or\ndefault` is defeated because the key is present-but-empty). #336\nhardened the model read, but the same trap applied to every\nempty-default passthrough.\n2. **Stale-shell shadow.** A value exported in the operator's shell\nsilently shadows the value they just set in `.env`. Observed in the\nfield: a dead shell `OPENAI_API_KEY` beat a funded `.env` key → `429\ninsufficient_quota` on every embedding/enrichment call, with a `curl` of\nthe `.env` key succeeding — baffling until you inspect the container\nenv.\n\n## Change\n\nDrop the empty-default passthroughs and let `env_file` (`.env`) supply\nthem directly — `env_file` values are **not** shell-shadowed:\n\n- removed: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`,\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL`, `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL`,\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_TRUNCATE_TO_DIM`, `EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`\n- **kept**: `POSTGRES_HOST` / `CORE_STORAGE_API_URL` / `REDIS_URL`\n(literal Docker-network overrides), and\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_SEND_DIMENSIONS` — it needs a non-empty default\n(`true`) that the code does **not** supply when the var is absent\n(`common/embedding/_platform.py:89` → `false` if unset). Removing it\nwould flip the hosted-OpenAI default.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `env.dev` sets none of the removed vars → `.env` is the sole source,\nso nothing is lost.\n- `docker compose config` resolves cleanly.\n\n## Known follow-up\n`SEND_DIMENSIONS` still has the same shell-shadow for local-embedder\nusers who set it to `false` in `.env`. Fixing that cleanly means giving\nthe code a `true` default when unset and then dropping this last\npassthrough too — left out here to keep the change scoped and low-risk.\n\nThis is the top remaining item (F-2) from the self-host dry-run audit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec717e613e399cd22259794c3d3045a65d4707f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ec717e613e399cd22259794c3d3045a65d4707f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLmlsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4aUQADiITXfM0J39Gz3NQrBgj4L+\nsG4PAfgF5FEHg1F66wIQsHrvtKg2ewE7VXgoupRZbQV+oU7q85B0h43qqxyTzrp+\nA+Eo8Kuhnd7Lsv0QjLqPBZ2A7W2R0ZM7ipDNhcWq2bKWOjo7qp2xDClFjhnQ+sqL\nRg241lzSa3W3LHrOk+KXm513J1AicUoBSlOs1snHyQwVgnAe1G8seuPWU4alBZMs\nlP1oxoZz9+Rr14jSuiagXSpPSC1bc2XGhuwQfyZ4NrjmQmPPw32XFDupiwM+q+0Y\nPMNqDW3/OOY59ZRpZQo406AT6oAuwlJJMczKxq50usZRZEw8sZA2jk3XH77KYOCE\ntHfXec54RdjhjL4xk76Q42+3lU9djQlE1qkhZkRuWLR1/q73byo7W6VpWE36sN2r\n/QJsrAXhRuTp7HBoCamtihMgNTkQw+CvkDsl2GZKQvNtO2njtWyUqDBbkaGD4YE6\nc1MVDuxJUqLeqEK5F5+AiQeTtzgrmbuBBhuaxqJatZmuzqH+//dJn71Snckx/tLQ\nS9QTIC5FGdEhEWgoqYOAhH9mpyVk60Levh1UzH90KgBNrlMm4N0U6TVXCE30o/AB\nvDp5+8qkAmscEx5+BaqTH2wMY1Hy9cmitqv9eVZfr+COxG24exyoOeTDSk4nBkh5\nUTsZ39fqQSaWxmGsmoqB\n=gWK4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ec717e613e399cd22259794c3d3045a65d4707f7\nparent 57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781426540 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781426540 +0300\n\nfix(compose): stop shadowing .env provider keys with empty \"${VAR:-}\" passthroughs (#346)\n\n## Summary\n\n`core-api` already loads `.env` through `env_file`, but the\n`environment:` block re-declared the provider/embedding vars as\n`\"${VAR:-}\"`. Docker Compose resolves `${...}` from the operator's\n**shell** with precedence over `.env`, which causes two real failures:\n\n1. **Empty-string injection.** When a var is set only in `.env`, the\n`${VAR:-}` passthrough injects an empty string that *overrides* it. This\nis the class behind the `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` → `400 \"you must\nprovide a model parameter\"` break (the code's `os.environ.get(...) or\ndefault` is defeated because the key is present-but-empty). #336\nhardened the model read, but the same trap applied to every\nempty-default passthrough.\n2. **Stale-shell shadow.** A value exported in the operator's shell\nsilently shadows the value they just set in `.env`. Observed in the\nfield: a dead shell `OPENAI_API_KEY` beat a funded `.env` key → `429\ninsufficient_quota` on every embedding/enrichment call, with a `curl` of\nthe `.env` key succeeding — baffling until you inspect the container\nenv.\n\n## Change\n\nDrop the empty-default passthroughs and let `env_file` (`.env`) supply\nthem directly — `env_file` values are **not** shell-shadowed:\n\n- removed: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`,\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL`, `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL`,\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_TRUNCATE_TO_DIM`, `EMBEDDING_QUERY_INSTRUCTION`\n- **kept**: `POSTGRES_HOST` / `CORE_STORAGE_API_URL` / `REDIS_URL`\n(literal Docker-network overrides), and\n`OPENAI_EMBEDDING_SEND_DIMENSIONS` — it needs a non-empty default\n(`true`) that the code does **not** supply when the var is absent\n(`common/embedding/_platform.py:89` → `false` if unset). Removing it\nwould flip the hosted-OpenAI default.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `env.dev` sets none of the removed vars → `.env` is the sole source,\nso nothing is lost.\n- `docker compose config` resolves cleanly.\n\n## Known follow-up\n`SEND_DIMENSIONS` still has the same shell-shadow for local-embedder\nusers who set it to `false` in `.env`. Fixing that cleanly means giving\nthe code a `true` default when unset and then dropping this last\npassthrough too — left out here to keep the change scoped and low-risk.\n\nThis is the top remaining item (F-2) from the self-host dry-run audit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T08:42:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8ab95d8e416862153410942bdf1bfcf51fcad2c1/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7"}]},{"sha":"57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU3YjI5ZDE5NWIzNDFmOWNlYTFjN2YwNGQwZTAxNGQzOTczZjdmYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-06-14T08:28:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T08:28:28Z"},"message":"docs+fix: audit low-severity cluster (F-6 search sample, F-9 weight mapping, F-10 keystone error, F-11 embedding lag) (#350)\n\n## Summary\n\nBundles the four **Low**-severity items from the self-host dry-run\naudit. Each was validated against current `main` before writing.\n\n### F-6 — no `POST /search` response sample (docs)\nAdded a sample showing the `items[]` envelope (`SearchResponse.items:\nlist[MemoryOut]`) with `similarity` + key fields, so readers know the\nsuccess shape.\n\n### F-11 — async recall lag undocumented (docs)\nDocumented that embedding is asynchronous: a brand-new memory may not\nappear in semantic `search` for a moment (`metadata.embedding_pending`),\nwhile `GET /memories` shows it immediately.\n\n### F-9 — keystone `weight` string-in / int-out (docs)\nDocumented the bucket mapping `low=25 / med=50 / high=100`. The integer\nform is **intentional** (`KEYSTONE_WEIGHT_BUCKETS`, *\"keep ranking\npredictable\"*) and **test-locked** (`assert weight == 100`), so changing\nthe output would break the contract — this is a docs clarification.\nPlaced in README prose rather than the `memclaw_keystones_set` tool\n`_DESCRIPTION`, which is snapshot-pinned in three baseline fixtures.\n\n### F-10 — `scope=fleet/tenant` + `agent_id` error clarity (code)\nReplaced the terse `scope=fleet must not include agent_id` with a\nmessage that explains *why* (fleet/tenant keystones aren't\nagent-specific; `agent_id` is only valid for `scope=agent`). Fixed in\n`core-storage-api` because core-api deliberately lets the storage 422\npropagate (`routes/keystones.py`), so it surfaces to both REST and MCP\ncallers. No test pins the string.\n\n## Validation\n- `py_compile` + `ruff` (format + check) pass on the storage file.\n- README code-fences balanced; sample fields match `MemoryOut`.\n- Confirmed no test asserts the old F-10 string, and the\ntool-description baselines are untouched (F-9 went to README, not the\ntool desc).\n\nRemaining audit item after this: **F-7** (keystones 403 on fresh\nstandalone) — the one Medium, to be handled separately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54443f642bd553bc6ead6fccb7d7d0aeb234837d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/54443f642bd553bc6ead6fccb7d7d0aeb234837d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLmYsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqFwQAEQFU9evsoA3gTuBWtzFvF3A\nvsNxz3fmKqfdo3qpXSwajHgkA9oZlno5htXBhia/ovaLQC/dkiW8zvLOioZuWPg1\ncLQB2lKrPiUTkuwSHCUZsC9QxUJ2HVuiPb5Rdkf7k/Cg5vC41VXr8IZSKxao3xNP\na4ayu82UARc9HgHEPr0aQHzFtxOw//XqDqUIGbEBR+jkXBESWqgKpXhpNZVBBUEk\nHSr4h9kVDVZoFR12EJeJu7NlR4xd5w1tb0kSP82uWUfj9zAn2Wl5eNP3AAhwO4Y1\ny9v6eQc8Ra1p0NTpXGksVV0JvEinufZ+zysO2pGhmFxd939miN/+Z1DYc9+zsPtV\ntcrfP6U9rtzKffy00ApNsRuxKdT+Q/nyTr/HTYEFDCh202Il6gZLCdJc23WXVMKF\nGEuIDEkmYsLQXMj2gEi1k7SoZ/ZazTYpz+iSLhGvRPR8fHlrQpPsV+sFzdODFXhq\nMjuoNTVIcsdzlv8pPZWhzg0Sbz34NDyfuIJTciK/I+zFISu0LZ431ycvNCGzOAQj\nVlKgQQkU/uJ9c54Uy15fbdhWMdtqHOtpesQtj7pSgzxGtgkQNiSoOsnMZD5gBJ5h\nTnmZcllCKslFLfUs9rhBT9ddOTE3Az8B/mznf37706lkoFrtVuht6U09HiMFjhE/\nmDdwZcwHhGTLnZUsRd5E\n=+J2V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 54443f642bd553bc6ead6fccb7d7d0aeb234837d\nparent fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1781425708 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781425708 +0300\n\ndocs+fix: audit low-severity cluster (F-6 search sample, F-9 weight mapping, F-10 keystone error, F-11 embedding lag) (#350)\n\n## Summary\n\nBundles the four **Low**-severity items from the self-host dry-run\naudit. Each was validated against current `main` before writing.\n\n### F-6 — no `POST /search` response sample (docs)\nAdded a sample showing the `items[]` envelope (`SearchResponse.items:\nlist[MemoryOut]`) with `similarity` + key fields, so readers know the\nsuccess shape.\n\n### F-11 — async recall lag undocumented (docs)\nDocumented that embedding is asynchronous: a brand-new memory may not\nappear in semantic `search` for a moment (`metadata.embedding_pending`),\nwhile `GET /memories` shows it immediately.\n\n### F-9 — keystone `weight` string-in / int-out (docs)\nDocumented the bucket mapping `low=25 / med=50 / high=100`. The integer\nform is **intentional** (`KEYSTONE_WEIGHT_BUCKETS`, *\"keep ranking\npredictable\"*) and **test-locked** (`assert weight == 100`), so changing\nthe output would break the contract — this is a docs clarification.\nPlaced in README prose rather than the `memclaw_keystones_set` tool\n`_DESCRIPTION`, which is snapshot-pinned in three baseline fixtures.\n\n### F-10 — `scope=fleet/tenant` + `agent_id` error clarity (code)\nReplaced the terse `scope=fleet must not include agent_id` with a\nmessage that explains *why* (fleet/tenant keystones aren't\nagent-specific; `agent_id` is only valid for `scope=agent`). Fixed in\n`core-storage-api` because core-api deliberately lets the storage 422\npropagate (`routes/keystones.py`), so it surfaces to both REST and MCP\ncallers. No test pins the string.\n\n## Validation\n- `py_compile` + `ruff` (format + check) pass on the storage file.\n- README code-fences balanced; sample fields match `MemoryOut`.\n- Confirmed no test asserts the old F-10 string, and the\ntool-description baselines are untouched (F-9 went to README, not the\ntool desc).\n\nRemaining audit item after this: **F-7** (keystones 403 on fresh\nstandalone) — the one Medium, to be handled separately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T08:28:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/57b29d195b341f9cea1c7f04d0e014d3973f7fa7/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a"}]},{"sha":"fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZjNmQ1NjNiMTcxMjY0ZmMyYmMxNTc4YTcwOGZjOWFkMzEwNGNjNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T08:02:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T08:02:07Z"},"message":"docs: add top-level BENCHMARKS.md as a citable benchmark asset (#349)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a root-level **`BENCHMARKS.md`** — the LoCoMo / LongMemEval results\ntable, what we measure and how, the fleet-shape dimensions single-agent\nbenchmarks can't capture, and a step-by-step reproduction recipe against\nthe **public** datasets + the OSS local stack.\n\n- Cross-links it from the README **Performance** section.\n- Repoints `docs/performance.md` at `BENCHMARKS.md` for\nmethodology/reproduction (it previously pointed readers to the\n**private**, different-purpose `keystone-benchmark` repo — that's a\npolicy-enforcement benchmark, not the memory benchmark these numbers\ncome from, so the old link would 404 for the public).\n\n## Why\n\nFrom the OSS SEO/GEO review: a reproducible, in-repo benchmark is our\nmost citation-worthy asset, but it was only reachable via a blog link\nand a buried `docs/performance.md`. `BENCHMARKS.md` at the repo root is\nthe conventional, citable location evaluators and AI engines look for.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Numbers are unchanged — reused verbatim from `docs/performance.md` /\nthe blog (point-in-time, last run 2026-04-19; blog remains canonical).\n- No turnkey runner is bundled (datasets are large + public; the\ninternal runner isn't open yet). The doc is explicit about that and\ndescribes the exact methodology instead — chosen over shipping an\nunverifiable script.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"91e251e92d7b86e306fea923da95b8551f524018","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/91e251e92d7b86e306fea923da95b8551f524018"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLl//CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8AcQAKJhKSVOz6nwTpaQP7VJth4N\nUAenHtEesTAagkBV4uqjN6XZdQrdy0oMV2XsfxS/c9AITTm+5AIdCVrNxzvQ6nNh\nyKFU1nvFrcokl1DpdwiAohBfT/GGhSmEw5jjxTHlfCrngMUiZg4HR6MB0evCeczd\n5Pl8f6QqanTAE7zg3gfAcO8pVkMERZuGzXHuAkfeESSk5vjuJIutYxdXlzTsE9/m\n+l595QjlnOEfPupQGdbT0jtVR1DcUSaO1wvok136GgfoS8U/hW5WYS2wpXXnuEUc\nTZVr+NXiOmv9+C+bifsgUy0HiRJcgFgJ3nY2/SKtylT17jhLdaecpLxxNBCHFuw9\nQdz/6ozYSgWmyKR63shf0dPOfl/VdyNUBARs7zvAOwefWgjvisoBT+vBfW8by74n\nsMktW6PXy6r0IdZd90VpN9gM97mkugVS2qRip28l9z9Kcb/ia3h0/ilhJJ62CFhd\nErRGZ4fCpj/JHEbj6UoCihfv9ODJm3O6fhq9l4+/zAygnIPsbVawURhqFH849tKo\nUtvikbdiuc7eK4s5aJ6ENIWgMMbFF71mrmh+uS58rAs22VcRxi8WUQBkyPXCDeTk\nLu9+Odk3WjyN9D2v1MspBFAjz8V4w/Jpkjm7ww11I2azeFcn0iyIn7GWUhan11BM\n5ho7yp1cmJxIGa/gdDE7\n=HzR5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 91e251e92d7b86e306fea923da95b8551f524018\nparent 91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781424127 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781424127 +0300\n\ndocs: add top-level BENCHMARKS.md as a citable benchmark asset (#349)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a root-level **`BENCHMARKS.md`** — the LoCoMo / LongMemEval results\ntable, what we measure and how, the fleet-shape dimensions single-agent\nbenchmarks can't capture, and a step-by-step reproduction recipe against\nthe **public** datasets + the OSS local stack.\n\n- Cross-links it from the README **Performance** section.\n- Repoints `docs/performance.md` at `BENCHMARKS.md` for\nmethodology/reproduction (it previously pointed readers to the\n**private**, different-purpose `keystone-benchmark` repo — that's a\npolicy-enforcement benchmark, not the memory benchmark these numbers\ncome from, so the old link would 404 for the public).\n\n## Why\n\nFrom the OSS SEO/GEO review: a reproducible, in-repo benchmark is our\nmost citation-worthy asset, but it was only reachable via a blog link\nand a buried `docs/performance.md`. `BENCHMARKS.md` at the repo root is\nthe conventional, citable location evaluators and AI engines look for.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Numbers are unchanged — reused verbatim from `docs/performance.md` /\nthe blog (point-in-time, last run 2026-04-19; blog remains canonical).\n- No turnkey runner is bundled (datasets are large + public; the\ninternal runner isn't open yet). The doc is explicit about that and\ndescribes the exact methodology instead — chosen over shipping an\nunverifiable script.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T08:02:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fc6d563b171264fc2bc1578a708fc9ad3104cc4a/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a"}]},{"sha":"91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDkxZWU2MTNjNDZjZGY5ZTBmODFjNzI0OWFiMmIzYzc1NjAxYzExMGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-14T07:51:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T07:51:07Z"},"message":"docs: lead Quick Start with a no-key, no-signup local quickstart (#348)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a **no-key, no-signup local quickstart** as the first thing in the\nQuick Start section — clone, `IS_STANDALONE=true`, `docker compose up\n-d`, then a copy-paste write + search. The detailed three paths (Managed\n/ Self-Hosted / OpenClaw) follow unchanged.\n\n## Why\n\nThe OSS README leads with the Managed Platform (signup + API key) and\nburies the only credential-free runnable example at step 4 of\nSelf-Hosted, after prerequisites, env config, and provider tables. A\ndeveloper evaluating the open-source edition can't copy-paste their way\nto a first memory before hitting credential/governance nuance.\n\nThis surfaces the lowest-friction path first — a dev sees a memory\nwritten and recalled in four commands, no account, no keys — then routes\nthem to the full paths for semantic recall, multi-tenant, managed, or\nOpenClaw. From the OSS SEO/activation review (reduce activation\nfriction).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Purely additive — the managed-first funnel ordering below is\nuntouched.\n- Commands are the repo's own documented standalone setup\n(`IS_STANDALONE=true`) + the existing verified write/search example,\nhoisted to the top.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"069034f38365e4a842f3f65d06e60bd150a1a99c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/069034f38365e4a842f3f65d06e60bd150a1a99c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLl1rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0kkQABzZqXy+dZk7Xlw/slFEWrNj\nbaKvg90FoVMhDPsQLdsuL8XWEUdYwtOsdI3fWLt5k98BVlxh1Pp1ODxu6DtHLSML\ny7OIjze7S2rqyF7eB+i6VtBOArIanrqOmcjeq7+fjABfKMKOIRUQSN3NG0EbvgSg\nuLAtlInwt9RnJe8BCq9AQKvv/QWpJQgaJhonSXwBbti6anXIzBeJB8l6OGafyD6t\nJa+PTLiI7Kt0LnsDypv3J6HgHnbuIiTQupKAmaoPWPyB2YjVKnyZiIM0XTRHDiIf\n3SX+Jd+0zOi3s7C4GjMhNfV7vnMUUnhTzzklcfclN+UBXiTimLeD/+Bmvc22gyeI\nXSP9e4CHdxZpPVgTqYOQ6bmR2ILNHBv+zEYSgUm3Nnn/WXytzSLmT23gTNtY0ZMf\nztCFJUukRPCASdsYVIIeWMwQ7+m/PRX3Pyr+TeZigHq2owgVUoaDE/Du8I9lLyRM\neY2voPYOIkACPYDWf1AQ+xy1mnezziDztNRtbT/hxN7GzhizCTitffNL0Zth/38g\n6UN8kVlrZ/91Gs1aNFRchURpCbMR43MyDRO3KliJmGqLMLPInNRLVZgtnAlEsNaK\nJF89w0A4ziB6vSaxjBaj3YCOE0NuLaDVZgfNkcmcTJnp7Quh8uDOc9G73oSjEPOG\nZnGQhpgCRMMOBanOvtcv\n=MBE6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 069034f38365e4a842f3f65d06e60bd150a1a99c\nparent 3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1781423467 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781423467 +0300\n\ndocs: lead Quick Start with a no-key, no-signup local quickstart (#348)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a **no-key, no-signup local quickstart** as the first thing in the\nQuick Start section — clone, `IS_STANDALONE=true`, `docker compose up\n-d`, then a copy-paste write + search. The detailed three paths (Managed\n/ Self-Hosted / OpenClaw) follow unchanged.\n\n## Why\n\nThe OSS README leads with the Managed Platform (signup + API key) and\nburies the only credential-free runnable example at step 4 of\nSelf-Hosted, after prerequisites, env config, and provider tables. A\ndeveloper evaluating the open-source edition can't copy-paste their way\nto a first memory before hitting credential/governance nuance.\n\nThis surfaces the lowest-friction path first — a dev sees a memory\nwritten and recalled in four commands, no account, no keys — then routes\nthem to the full paths for semantic recall, multi-tenant, managed, or\nOpenClaw. From the OSS SEO/activation review (reduce activation\nfriction).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Purely additive — the managed-first funnel ordering below is\nuntouched.\n- Commands are the repo's own documented standalone setup\n(`IS_STANDALONE=true`) + the existing verified write/search example,\nhoisted to the top.\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T07:51:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/91ee613c46cdf9e0f81c7249ab2b3c75601c110a/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3bb7b1c8903e90b77630324222956eb9d83fc4b9"}]}]